-- BSB verses (4808). Requires books and chapters first.
insert into public.verses (chapter_id, number, osis_ref, text)
select c.id, x.verse, x.ref, x.body
from (values
('1KI', 15, 20, '1KI.15.20', 'And Ben-hadad listened to King Asa and sent the commanders of his armies against the cities of Israel, conquering Ijon, Dan, Abel-beth-maacah, and the whole land of Naphtali, including the region of Chinnereth.'),
('1KI', 15, 21, '1KI.15.21', 'When Baasha learned of this, he stopped fortifying Ramah and withdrew to Tirzah.'),
('1KI', 15, 22, '1KI.15.22', 'Then King Asa summoned all the men of Judah, with no exceptions, and they carried away the stones of Ramah and the timbers Baasha had used for building. And with these materials King Asa built up Geba of Benjamin, as well as Mizpah.'),
('1KI', 15, 23, '1KI.15.23', 'Now the rest of the acts of Asa, along with all his might, all his accomplishments, and the cities he built, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah? In his old age, however, he became diseased in his feet.'),
('1KI', 15, 24, '1KI.15.24', 'And Asa rested with his fathers and was buried with them in the city of his father David, and his son Jehoshaphat reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 15, 25, '1KI.15.25', 'In the second year of Asa’s reign over Judah, Nadab son of Jeroboam became king of Israel, and he reigned two years.'),
('1KI', 15, 26, '1KI.15.26', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD and walked in the way of his father and in his sin, which he had caused Israel to commit.'),
('1KI', 15, 27, '1KI.15.27', 'Then Baasha son of Ahijah of the house of Issachar conspired against Nadab, and Baasha struck him down at Gibbethon of the Philistines while Nadab and all Israel were besieging the city.'),
('1KI', 15, 28, '1KI.15.28', 'In the third year of Asa’s reign over Judah, Baasha killed Nadab and reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 15, 29, '1KI.15.29', 'As soon as Baasha became king, he struck down the entire household of Jeroboam. He did not leave to Jeroboam anyone who breathed, but destroyed them all according to the word that the LORD had spoken through His servant Ahijah the Shilonite,'),
('1KI', 15, 30, '1KI.15.30', 'because of the sins Jeroboam had committed and had caused Israel to commit, and because he had provoked the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger.'),
('1KI', 15, 31, '1KI.15.31', 'As for the rest of the acts of Nadab, along with all his accomplishments, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 15, 32, '1KI.15.32', 'And there was war between Asa and Baasha king of Israel throughout their days.'),
('1KI', 15, 33, '1KI.15.33', 'In the third year of Asa’s reign over Judah, Baasha son of Ahijah became king of all Israel, and he reigned in Tirzah twenty-four years.'),
('1KI', 15, 34, '1KI.15.34', 'And Baasha did evil in the sight of the LORD and walked in the way of Jeroboam and in his sin, which he had caused Israel to commit.'),
('1KI', 16, 1, '1KI.16.1', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Jehu son of Hanani against Baasha, saying:'),
('1KI', 16, 2, '1KI.16.2', '“Even though I lifted you out of the dust and made you ruler over My people Israel, you have walked in the way of Jeroboam and have caused My people Israel to sin and to provoke Me to anger by their sins.'),
('1KI', 16, 3, '1KI.16.3', 'So now I will consume Baasha and his house, and I will make your house like that of Jeroboam son of Nebat:'),
('1KI', 16, 4, '1KI.16.4', 'Anyone belonging to Baasha who dies in the city will be eaten by dogs, and anyone who dies in the field will be eaten by the birds of the air.”'),
('1KI', 16, 5, '1KI.16.5', 'As for the rest of the acts of Baasha, along with his accomplishments and might, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 16, 6, '1KI.16.6', 'And Baasha rested with his fathers and was buried in Tirzah, and his son Elah reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 16, 7, '1KI.16.7', 'Moreover, the word of the LORD came through the prophet Jehu son of Hanani against Baasha and his house, because of all the evil he had done in the sight of the LORD, provoking Him to anger with the work of his hands and becoming like the house of Jeroboam, and also because Baasha had struck down the house of Jeroboam.'),
('1KI', 16, 8, '1KI.16.8', 'In the twenty-sixth year of Asa’s reign over Judah, Elah son of Baasha became king of Israel, and he reigned in Tirzah two years.'),
('1KI', 16, 9, '1KI.16.9', 'However, while Elah was in Tirzah getting drunk in the house of Arza the steward of his household there, Elah’s servant Zimri, the commander of half his chariots, conspired against him.'),
('1KI', 16, 10, '1KI.16.10', 'So in the twenty-seventh year of Asa’s reign over Judah, Zimri went in, struck Elah down, and killed him. And Zimri reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 16, 11, '1KI.16.11', 'As soon as Zimri began to reign and was seated on the throne, he struck down the entire household of Baasha. He did not leave a single male, whether a kinsman or friend.'),
('1KI', 16, 12, '1KI.16.12', 'So Zimri destroyed the entire household of Baasha, according to the word that the LORD had spoken against Baasha through Jehu the prophet.'),
('1KI', 16, 13, '1KI.16.13', 'This happened because of all the sins Baasha and his son Elah had committed and had caused Israel to commit, provoking the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger with their worthless idols.'),
('1KI', 16, 14, '1KI.16.14', 'As for the rest of the acts of Elah, along with all his accomplishments, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 16, 15, '1KI.16.15', 'In the twenty-seventh year of Asa’s reign over Judah, Zimri reigned in Tirzah for seven days. Now the troops were encamped against Gibbethon of the Philistines,'),
('1KI', 16, 16, '1KI.16.16', 'and the people in the camp heard that Zimri had conspired against the king and struck him down. So there in the camp that very day, all Israel proclaimed Omri, the commander of the army, king over Israel.'),
('1KI', 16, 17, '1KI.16.17', 'Then Omri and all the Israelites marched up from Gibbethon and besieged Tirzah.'),
('1KI', 16, 18, '1KI.16.18', 'When Zimri saw that the city was captured, he entered the citadel of the royal palace and burned it down upon himself. So he died'),
('1KI', 16, 19, '1KI.16.19', 'because of the sins he had committed, doing evil in the sight of the LORD and following the example of Jeroboam and the sin he had committed and had caused Israel to commit.'),
('1KI', 16, 20, '1KI.16.20', 'As for the rest of the acts of Zimri and the treason he committed, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 16, 21, '1KI.16.21', 'At that time the people of Israel were divided: Half of the people supported Tibni son of Ginath as king, and half supported Omri.'),
('1KI', 16, 22, '1KI.16.22', 'But the followers of Omri proved stronger than those of Tibni son of Ginath. So Tibni died and Omri became king.'),
('1KI', 16, 23, '1KI.16.23', 'In the thirty-first year of Asa’s reign over Judah, Omri became king of Israel, and he reigned twelve years, six of them in Tirzah.'),
('1KI', 16, 24, '1KI.16.24', 'He bought the hill of Samaria from Shemer for two talents of silver and built a city there, calling it Samaria after the name of Shemer, who had owned the hill.'),
('1KI', 16, 25, '1KI.16.25', 'But Omri did evil in the sight of the LORD and acted more wickedly than all who were before him.'),
('1KI', 16, 26, '1KI.16.26', 'For he walked in all the ways of Jeroboam son of Nebat and in his sins, which he caused Israel to commit, provoking the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger with their worthless idols.'),
('1KI', 16, 27, '1KI.16.27', 'As for the rest of the acts of Omri, along with his accomplishments and the might he exercised, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 16, 28, '1KI.16.28', 'And Omri rested with his fathers and was buried in Samaria, and his son Ahab reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 16, 29, '1KI.16.29', 'In the thirty-eighth year of Asa’s reign over Judah, Ahab son of Omri became king of Israel, and he reigned in Samaria twenty-two years.'),
('1KI', 16, 30, '1KI.16.30', 'However, Ahab son of Omri did evil in the sight of the LORD, more than all who were before him.'),
('1KI', 16, 31, '1KI.16.31', 'And as if it were not enough for him to walk in the sins of Jeroboam son of Nebat, he even married Jezebel the daughter of Ethbaal king of the Sidonians, and he then proceeded to serve and worship Baal.'),
('1KI', 16, 32, '1KI.16.32', 'First, Ahab set up an altar for Baal in the temple of Baal that he had built in Samaria.'),
('1KI', 16, 33, '1KI.16.33', 'Then he set up an Asherah pole. Thus Ahab did more to provoke the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger than all the kings of Israel before him.'),
('1KI', 16, 34, '1KI.16.34', 'In Ahab’s days, Hiel the Bethelite rebuilt Jericho. At the cost of Abiram his firstborn he laid its foundation, and at the cost of Segub his youngest he set up its gates, according to the word that the LORD had spoken through Joshua son of Nun.'),
('1KI', 17, 1, '1KI.17.1', 'Now Elijah the Tishbite, who was among the settlers of Gilead, said to Ahab, “As surely as the LORD, the God of Israel, lives, before whom I stand, there will be neither dew nor rain in these years except at my word!”'),
('1KI', 17, 2, '1KI.17.2', 'Then a revelation from the LORD came to Elijah:'),
('1KI', 17, 3, '1KI.17.3', '“Leave here, turn eastward, and hide yourself by the Brook of Cherith, east of the Jordan.'),
('1KI', 17, 4, '1KI.17.4', 'And you are to drink from the brook, and I have commanded the ravens to feed you there.”'),
('1KI', 17, 5, '1KI.17.5', 'So Elijah did what the LORD had told him, and he went and lived by the Brook of Cherith, east of the Jordan.'),
('1KI', 17, 6, '1KI.17.6', 'The ravens would bring him bread and meat in the morning and evening, and he would drink from the brook.'),
('1KI', 17, 7, '1KI.17.7', 'Some time later, however, the brook dried up because there had been no rain in the land.'),
('1KI', 17, 8, '1KI.17.8', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Elijah:'),
('1KI', 17, 9, '1KI.17.9', '“Get up and go to Zarephath of Sidon, and stay there. Behold, I have commanded a widow there to provide for you.”'),
('1KI', 17, 10, '1KI.17.10', 'So Elijah got up and went to Zarephath. When he arrived at the city gate, there was a widow gathering sticks. Elijah called to her and said, “Please bring me a little water in a cup, so that I may drink.”'),
('1KI', 17, 11, '1KI.17.11', 'And as she was going to get it, he called to her and said, “Please bring me a piece of bread.”'),
('1KI', 17, 12, '1KI.17.12', 'But she replied, “As surely as the LORD your God lives, I have no bread—only a handful of flour in a jar and a little oil in a jug. Look, I am gathering a couple of sticks to take home and prepare a meal for myself and my son, so that we may eat it and die.”'),
('1KI', 17, 13, '1KI.17.13', '“Do not be afraid,” Elijah said to her. “Go and do as you have said. But first make me a small cake of bread from what you have, and bring it out to me. Afterward, make some for yourself and your son,'),
('1KI', 17, 14, '1KI.17.14', 'for this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘The jar of flour will not be exhausted and the jug of oil will not run dry until the day the LORD sends rain upon the face of the earth.’”'),
('1KI', 17, 15, '1KI.17.15', 'So she went and did according to the word of Elijah, and there was food every day for Elijah and the woman and her household.'),
('1KI', 17, 16, '1KI.17.16', 'The jar of flour was not exhausted and the jug of oil did not run dry, according to the word that the LORD had spoken through Elijah.'),
('1KI', 17, 17, '1KI.17.17', 'Later, the son of the woman who owned the house became ill, and his sickness grew worse and worse, until no breath remained in him.'),
('1KI', 17, 18, '1KI.17.18', '“O man of God,” said the woman to Elijah, “what have you done to me? Have you come to remind me of my iniquity and cause the death of my son?”'),
('1KI', 17, 19, '1KI.17.19', 'But Elijah said to her, “Give me your son.” So he took him from her arms, carried him to the upper room where he was staying, and laid him on his own bed.'),
('1KI', 17, 20, '1KI.17.20', 'Then he cried out to the LORD, “O LORD my God, have You also brought tragedy on this widow who has opened her home to me, by causing her son to die?”'),
('1KI', 17, 21, '1KI.17.21', 'Then he stretched himself out over the child three times and cried out to the LORD, “O LORD my God, please let this boy’s life return to him!”'),
('1KI', 17, 22, '1KI.17.22', 'And the LORD listened to the voice of Elijah, and the child’s life returned to him, and he lived.'),
('1KI', 17, 23, '1KI.17.23', 'Then Elijah took the child, brought him down from the upper room into the house, and gave him to his mother. “Look, your son is alive,” Elijah declared.'),
('1KI', 17, 24, '1KI.17.24', 'Then the woman said to Elijah, “Now I know that you are a man of God and that the word of the LORD from your mouth is truth.”'),
('1KI', 18, 1, '1KI.18.1', 'After a long time, in the third year of the drought, the word of the LORD came to Elijah: “Go and present yourself to Ahab, and I will send rain upon the face of the earth.”'),
('1KI', 18, 2, '1KI.18.2', 'So Elijah went to present himself to Ahab. The famine was severe in Samaria,'),
('1KI', 18, 3, '1KI.18.3', 'and Ahab summoned Obadiah, who was in charge of the palace. (Now Obadiah greatly feared the LORD,'),
('1KI', 18, 4, '1KI.18.4', 'for when Jezebel had slaughtered the prophets of the LORD, Obadiah had taken a hundred prophets and hidden them, fifty men per cave, providing them with food and water.)'),
('1KI', 18, 5, '1KI.18.5', 'Then Ahab said to Obadiah, “Go throughout the land to every spring and every valley. Perhaps we will find grass to keep the horses and mules alive so that we will not have to destroy any livestock.”'),
('1KI', 18, 6, '1KI.18.6', 'So they divided the land to explore. Ahab went one way by himself, and Obadiah went the other way by himself.'),
('1KI', 18, 7, '1KI.18.7', 'Now as Obadiah went on his way, Elijah suddenly met him. When Obadiah recognized him, he fell facedown and said, “Is it you, my lord Elijah?”'),
('1KI', 18, 8, '1KI.18.8', '“It is I,” he answered. “Go tell your master, ‘Elijah is here!’”'),
('1KI', 18, 9, '1KI.18.9', 'But Obadiah replied, “How have I sinned, that you are handing your servant over to Ahab to put me to death?'),
('1KI', 18, 10, '1KI.18.10', 'As surely as the LORD your God lives, there is no nation or kingdom where my lord has not sent someone to search for you. When they said, ‘He is not here,’ he made that kingdom or nation swear that they had not found you.'),
('1KI', 18, 11, '1KI.18.11', 'And now you say, ‘Go tell your master that Elijah is here!’'),
('1KI', 18, 12, '1KI.18.12', 'I do not know where the Spirit of the LORD may carry you off when I leave you. Then when I go and tell Ahab and he does not find you, he will kill me. But I, your servant, have feared the LORD from my youth.'),
('1KI', 18, 13, '1KI.18.13', 'Was it not reported to my lord what I did when Jezebel slaughtered the prophets of the LORD? I hid a hundred prophets of the LORD, fifty men per cave, and I provided them with food and water.'),
('1KI', 18, 14, '1KI.18.14', 'And now you say, ‘Go tell your lord that Elijah is here!’ He will kill me!”'),
('1KI', 18, 15, '1KI.18.15', 'Then Elijah said, “As surely as the LORD of Hosts lives, before whom I stand, I will present myself to Ahab today.”'),
('1KI', 18, 16, '1KI.18.16', 'So Obadiah went to inform Ahab, who went to meet Elijah.'),
('1KI', 18, 17, '1KI.18.17', 'When Ahab saw Elijah, he said to him, “Is that you, O troubler of Israel?”'),
('1KI', 18, 18, '1KI.18.18', '“I have not troubled Israel,” Elijah replied, “but you and your father’s house have, for you have forsaken the commandments of the LORD and have followed the Baals.'),
('1KI', 18, 19, '1KI.18.19', 'Now summon all Israel to meet me on Mount Carmel, along with the four hundred and fifty prophets of Baal and the four hundred prophets of Asherah who eat at Jezebel’s table.”'),
('1KI', 18, 20, '1KI.18.20', 'So Ahab summoned all the Israelites and assembled the prophets on Mount Carmel.'),
('1KI', 18, 21, '1KI.18.21', 'Then Elijah approached all the people and said, “How long will you waver between two opinions? If the LORD is God, follow Him. But if Baal is God, follow him.” But the people did not answer a word.'),
('1KI', 18, 22, '1KI.18.22', 'Then Elijah said to the people, “I am the only remaining prophet of the LORD, but Baal has four hundred and fifty prophets.'),
('1KI', 18, 23, '1KI.18.23', 'Get two bulls for us. Let the prophets of Baal choose one bull for themselves, cut it into pieces, and place it on the wood but not light the fire. And I will prepare the other bull and place it on the wood but not light the fire.'),
('1KI', 18, 24, '1KI.18.24', 'Then you may call on the name of your god, and I will call on the name of the LORD. The God who answers by fire, He is God.” And all the people answered, “What you say is good.”'),
('1KI', 18, 25, '1KI.18.25', 'Then Elijah said to the prophets of Baal, “Since you are so numerous, choose for yourselves one bull and prepare it first. Then call on the name of your god, but do not light the fire.”'),
('1KI', 18, 26, '1KI.18.26', 'And they took the bull that was given them, prepared it, and called on the name of Baal from morning until noon, shouting, “O Baal, answer us!” But there was no sound, and no one answered as they leaped around the altar they had made.'),
('1KI', 18, 27, '1KI.18.27', 'At noon Elijah began to taunt them, saying, “Shout louder, for he is a god! Perhaps he is deep in thought, or occupied, or on a journey. Perhaps he is sleeping and must be awakened!”'),
('1KI', 18, 28, '1KI.18.28', 'So they shouted louder and cut themselves with knives and lances, as was their custom, until the blood gushed over them.'),
('1KI', 18, 29, '1KI.18.29', 'Midday passed, and they kept on raving until the time of the evening sacrifice. But there was no response; no one answered, no one paid attention.'),
('1KI', 18, 30, '1KI.18.30', 'Then Elijah said to all the people, “Come near to me.” So all the people approached him, and he repaired the altar of the LORD that had been torn down.'),
('1KI', 18, 31, '1KI.18.31', 'And Elijah took twelve stones, one for each tribe of the sons of Jacob, to whom the word of the LORD had come and said, “Israel shall be your name.”'),
('1KI', 18, 32, '1KI.18.32', 'And with the stones, Elijah built an altar in the name of the LORD. Then he dug a trench around the altar large enough to hold two seahs of seed.'),
('1KI', 18, 33, '1KI.18.33', 'Next, he arranged the wood, cut up the bull, placed it on the wood,'),
('1KI', 18, 34, '1KI.18.34', 'and said, “Fill four waterpots and pour the water on the offering and on the wood.” “Do it a second time,” he said, and they did it a second time. “Do it a third time,” he said, and they did it a third time.'),
('1KI', 18, 35, '1KI.18.35', 'So the water ran down around the altar and even filled the trench.'),
('1KI', 18, 36, '1KI.18.36', 'At the time of the evening sacrifice, Elijah the prophet approached the altar and said, “O LORD, God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, let it be known this day that You are God in Israel and that I am Your servant and have done all these things at Your command.'),
('1KI', 18, 37, '1KI.18.37', 'Answer me, O LORD! Answer me, so that this people will know that You, the LORD, are God, and that You have turned their hearts back again.”'),
('1KI', 18, 38, '1KI.18.38', 'Then the fire of the LORD fell and consumed the sacrifice, the wood, the stones, and the dust, and it licked up the water in the trench.'),
('1KI', 18, 39, '1KI.18.39', 'When all the people saw this, they fell facedown and said, “The LORD, He is God! The LORD, He is God!”'),
('1KI', 18, 40, '1KI.18.40', 'Then Elijah ordered them, “Seize the prophets of Baal! Do not let a single one escape.” So they seized them, and Elijah brought them down to the Kishon Valley and slaughtered them there.'),
('1KI', 18, 41, '1KI.18.41', 'And Elijah said to Ahab, “Go up, eat and drink, for there is the sound of a heavy rain.”'),
('1KI', 18, 42, '1KI.18.42', 'So Ahab went up to eat and drink. But Elijah climbed to the summit of Carmel, bent down on the ground, and put his face between his knees.'),
('1KI', 18, 43, '1KI.18.43', '“Go and look toward the sea,” he said to his servant. So the servant went and looked, and he said, “There is nothing there.” Seven times Elijah said, “Go back.”'),
('1KI', 18, 44, '1KI.18.44', 'On the seventh time the servant reported, “There is a cloud as small as a man’s hand rising from the sea.” And Elijah replied, “Go and tell Ahab, ‘Prepare your chariot and go down before the rain stops you.’”'),
('1KI', 18, 45, '1KI.18.45', 'Meanwhile, the sky grew dark with clouds and wind, and a heavy rain began to fall. So Ahab rode away and went to Jezreel.'),
('1KI', 18, 46, '1KI.18.46', 'And the hand of the LORD came upon Elijah, and he tucked his cloak into his belt and ran ahead of Ahab all the way to Jezreel.'),
('1KI', 19, 1, '1KI.19.1', 'Now Ahab told Jezebel everything that Elijah had done and how he had killed all the prophets with the sword.'),
('1KI', 19, 2, '1KI.19.2', 'So Jezebel sent a messenger to Elijah, saying, “May the gods deal with me, and ever so severely, if by this time tomorrow I have not made your life like the lives of those you killed!”'),
('1KI', 19, 3, '1KI.19.3', 'And Elijah was afraid and ran for his life. When he came to Beersheba in Judah, he left his servant there,'),
('1KI', 19, 4, '1KI.19.4', 'while he himself went a day’s journey into the wilderness. He sat down under a broom tree and prayed that he might die. “I have had enough, LORD,” he said. “Take my life, for I am no better than my fathers.”'),
('1KI', 19, 5, '1KI.19.5', 'Then he lay down under the broom tree and fell asleep. Suddenly an angel touched him and said, “Get up and eat.”'),
('1KI', 19, 6, '1KI.19.6', 'And he looked around, and there by his head was a cake of bread baked over hot coals, and a jar of water. So he ate and drank and lay down again.'),
('1KI', 19, 7, '1KI.19.7', 'A second time the angel of the LORD returned and touched him, saying, “Get up and eat, or the journey will be too much for you.”'),
('1KI', 19, 8, '1KI.19.8', 'So he got up and ate and drank. And strengthened by that food, he walked forty days and forty nights until he reached Horeb, the mountain of God.'),
('1KI', 19, 9, '1KI.19.9', 'There Elijah entered a cave and spent the night. And the word of the LORD came to him, saying, “What are you doing here, Elijah?”'),
('1KI', 19, 10, '1KI.19.10', '“I have been very zealous for the LORD, the God of Hosts,” he replied, “but the Israelites have forsaken Your covenant, torn down Your altars, and killed Your prophets with the sword. I am the only one left, and they are seeking my life as well.”'),
('1KI', 19, 11, '1KI.19.11', 'Then the LORD said, “Go out and stand on the mountain before the LORD. Behold, the LORD is about to pass by.” And a great and mighty wind tore into the mountains and shattered the rocks before the LORD, but the LORD was not in the wind. After the wind there was an earthquake, but the LORD was not in the earthquake.'),
('1KI', 19, 12, '1KI.19.12', 'After the earthquake there was a fire, but the LORD was not in the fire. And after the fire came a still, small voice.'),
('1KI', 19, 13, '1KI.19.13', 'When Elijah heard it, he wrapped his face in his cloak and went out and stood at the mouth of the cave. Suddenly a voice came to him and said, “What are you doing here, Elijah?”'),
('1KI', 19, 14, '1KI.19.14', '“I have been very zealous for the LORD, the God of Hosts,” he replied, “but the Israelites have forsaken Your covenant, torn down Your altars, and killed Your prophets with the sword. I am the only one left, and they are seeking my life as well.”'),
('1KI', 19, 15, '1KI.19.15', 'Then the LORD said to him, “Go back by the way you came, and go to the Desert of Damascus. When you arrive, you are to anoint Hazael as king over Aram.'),
('1KI', 19, 16, '1KI.19.16', 'You are also to anoint Jehu son of Nimshi as king over Israel and Elisha son of Shaphat from Abel-meholah to succeed you as prophet.'),
('1KI', 19, 17, '1KI.19.17', 'Then Jehu will put to death whoever escapes the sword of Hazael, and Elisha will put to death whoever escapes the sword of Jehu.'),
('1KI', 19, 18, '1KI.19.18', 'Nevertheless, I have reserved seven thousand in Israel—all whose knees have not bowed to Baal and whose mouths have not kissed him.”'),
('1KI', 19, 19, '1KI.19.19', 'So Elijah departed and found Elisha son of Shaphat. He was plowing with twelve teams of oxen, and he was with the twelfth team. Elijah passed by him and threw his cloak around him.'),
('1KI', 19, 20, '1KI.19.20', 'So Elisha left the oxen, ran after Elijah, and said, “Please let me kiss my father and mother goodbye, and then I will follow you.” “Go on back,” Elijah replied, “for what have I done to you?”'),
('1KI', 19, 21, '1KI.19.21', 'So Elisha turned back from him, took his pair of oxen, and slaughtered them. Using the oxen’s equipment for fuel, he cooked the meat and gave it to the people, and they ate. Then he set out to follow and serve Elijah.'),
('1KI', 20, 1, '1KI.20.1', 'Now Ben-hadad king of Aram assembled his entire army. Accompanied by thirty-two kings with their horses and chariots, he marched up, besieged Samaria, and waged war against it.'),
('1KI', 20, 2, '1KI.20.2', 'Then he sent messengers into the city to Ahab king of Israel,'),
('1KI', 20, 3, '1KI.20.3', 'saying, “This is what Ben-hadad says: ‘Your silver and gold are mine, and your best wives and children are mine!’”'),
('1KI', 20, 4, '1KI.20.4', 'And the king of Israel replied, “Just as you say, my lord the king: I am yours, along with all that I have.”'),
('1KI', 20, 5, '1KI.20.5', 'The messengers came back and said, “This is what Ben-hadad says: ‘I have sent to you to demand your silver, your gold, your wives, and your children.'),
('1KI', 20, 6, '1KI.20.6', 'But about this time tomorrow I will send my servants to search your palace and the houses of your servants. They will seize and carry away all that is precious to you.’”'),
('1KI', 20, 7, '1KI.20.7', 'Then the king of Israel summoned all the elders of the land and said, “Please take note and see that this man is looking for trouble, for when he demanded my wives, my children, my silver, and my gold, I did not deny him.”'),
('1KI', 20, 8, '1KI.20.8', 'And the elders and the people all said, “Do not listen to him or consent to his terms.”'),
('1KI', 20, 9, '1KI.20.9', 'So Ahab answered the messengers of Ben-hadad, “Tell my lord the king, ‘All that you demanded of your servant the first time I will do, but this thing I cannot do.’” So the messengers departed and relayed the message to Ben-hadad.'),
('1KI', 20, 10, '1KI.20.10', 'Then Ben-hadad sent another message to Ahab: “May the gods deal with me, and ever so severely, if enough dust remains of Samaria for each of my men to have a handful.”'),
('1KI', 20, 11, '1KI.20.11', 'And the king of Israel replied, “Tell him: ‘The one putting on his armor should not boast like one taking it off.’”'),
('1KI', 20, 12, '1KI.20.12', 'Ben-hadad received this message while he and the kings were drinking in their tents, and he said to his servants, “Take your positions.” So they stationed themselves against the city.'),
('1KI', 20, 13, '1KI.20.13', 'Meanwhile a prophet approached Ahab king of Israel and declared, “This is what the LORD says: ‘Do you see this entire great army? Behold, I will deliver it into your hand this very day, and you will know that I am the LORD.’”'),
('1KI', 20, 14, '1KI.20.14', '“By whom?” Ahab asked. And the prophet replied, “This is what the LORD says: ‘By the young officers of the district governors.’” “Who will start the battle?” asked Ahab. “You will,” answered the prophet.'),
('1KI', 20, 15, '1KI.20.15', 'So Ahab assembled the young officers of the district governors, and there were 232 men. And after them, he assembled the rest of the Israelite troops, 7,000 in all.'),
('1KI', 20, 16, '1KI.20.16', 'They marched out at noon while Ben-hadad and the 32 kings allied with him were in their tents getting drunk.'),
('1KI', 20, 17, '1KI.20.17', 'And the young officers of the district governors marched out first. Now Ben-hadad had sent out scouts, who reported to him, “Men are marching out of Samaria.”'),
('1KI', 20, 18, '1KI.20.18', '“If they have marched out in peace,” he said, “take them alive. Even if they have marched out for war, take them alive.”'),
('1KI', 20, 19, '1KI.20.19', 'Meanwhile, these young officers of the district governors marched out of the city, with the army behind them,'),
('1KI', 20, 20, '1KI.20.20', 'and each one struck down his opponent. So the Arameans fled, with the Israelites in pursuit. But Ben-hadad king of Aram escaped on horseback with the cavalry.'),
('1KI', 20, 21, '1KI.20.21', 'Then the king of Israel marched out and attacked the horses and chariots, inflicting a great slaughter on the Arameans.'),
('1KI', 20, 22, '1KI.20.22', 'Afterward, the prophet approached the king of Israel and said, “Go and strengthen your position, and take note what you must do, for in the spring the king of Aram will come up against you.”'),
('1KI', 20, 23, '1KI.20.23', 'Meanwhile, the servants of the king of Aram said to him, “Their gods are gods of the hills. That is why they prevailed over us. Instead, we should fight them on the plains; surely then we will prevail.'),
('1KI', 20, 24, '1KI.20.24', 'So do this: Dismiss all the kings from their positions and replace them with other officers.'),
('1KI', 20, 25, '1KI.20.25', 'And you must raise an army like the one you have lost—horse for horse and chariot for chariot—so we can fight the Israelites on the plain, where we will surely prevail.” And the king approved their plan and acted accordingly.'),
('1KI', 20, 26, '1KI.20.26', 'In the spring, Ben-hadad mobilized the Arameans and went up to Aphek to fight against Israel.'),
('1KI', 20, 27, '1KI.20.27', 'The Israelites also mobilized, gathered supplies, and marched out to meet them. The Israelites camped before them like two small flocks of goats, while the Arameans covered the countryside.'),
('1KI', 20, 28, '1KI.20.28', 'Then the man of God approached the king of Israel and said, “This is what the LORD says: ‘Because the Arameans have said that the LORD is a god of the hills and not of the valleys, I will deliver all this great army into your hand. Then you will know that I am the LORD.’”'),
('1KI', 20, 29, '1KI.20.29', 'For seven days the armies camped opposite each other, and on the seventh day the battle ensued, and the Israelites struck down the Arameans—a hundred thousand foot soldiers in one day.'),
('1KI', 20, 30, '1KI.20.30', 'The rest of them fled into the city of Aphek, where the wall fell on twenty-seven thousand of the remaining men. Ben-hadad also fled to the city and hid in an inner room.'),
('1KI', 20, 31, '1KI.20.31', 'Then the servants of Ben-hadad said to him, “Look now, we have heard that the kings of the house of Israel are merciful. Let us go out to the king of Israel with sackcloth around our waists and ropes around our heads. Perhaps he will spare your life.”'),
('1KI', 20, 32, '1KI.20.32', 'So with sackcloth around their waists and ropes around their heads, they went to the king of Israel and said, “Your servant Ben-hadad says, ‘Please spare my life.’” And the king answered, “Is he still alive? He is my brother.”'),
('1KI', 20, 33, '1KI.20.33', 'Now the men were looking for a sign of hope, and they quickly grasped at this word and replied, “Yes, your brother Ben-hadad.” “Go and get him!” said the king. Then Ben-hadad came out, and Ahab had him come up into his chariot.'),
('1KI', 20, 34, '1KI.20.34', 'Ben-hadad said to him, “I will restore the cities my father took from your father; you may set up your own marketplaces in Damascus, as my father did in Samaria.” “By this treaty I release you,” Ahab replied. So he made a treaty with him and sent him away.'),
('1KI', 20, 35, '1KI.20.35', 'Meanwhile, by the word of the LORD, one of the sons of the prophets said to his companion, “Strike me, please!” But the man refused to strike him.'),
('1KI', 20, 36, '1KI.20.36', 'Then the prophet said to him, “Because you have not obeyed the voice of the LORD, as soon as you depart from me a lion will kill you.” And when he left, a lion found him and killed him.'),
('1KI', 20, 37, '1KI.20.37', 'Then the prophet found another man and said, “Strike me, please!” So the man struck him and wounded him,'),
('1KI', 20, 38, '1KI.20.38', 'and the prophet went and waited on the road for the king, disguising himself with a bandage over his eyes.'),
('1KI', 20, 39, '1KI.20.39', 'As the king passed by, he cried out to the king: “Your servant had marched out into the middle of the battle, when suddenly a man came over with a captive and told me, ‘Guard this man! If he goes missing for any reason, your life will be exchanged for his life, or you will weigh out a talent of silver.’'),
('1KI', 20, 40, '1KI.20.40', 'But while your servant was busy here and there, the man disappeared.” And the king of Israel said to him, “So shall your judgment be; you have pronounced it on yourself.”'),
('1KI', 20, 41, '1KI.20.41', 'Then the prophet quickly removed the bandage from his eyes, and the king of Israel recognized him as one of the prophets.'),
('1KI', 20, 42, '1KI.20.42', 'And the prophet said to the king, “This is what the LORD says: ‘Because you have let slip from your hand the man I had devoted to destruction, your life will be exchanged for his life, and your people for his people.’”'),
('1KI', 20, 43, '1KI.20.43', 'Sullen and angry, the king of Israel went home to Samaria.'),
('1KI', 21, 1, '1KI.21.1', 'Some time after these events, Naboth the Jezreelite owned a vineyard in Jezreel next to the palace of Ahab king of Samaria.'),
('1KI', 21, 2, '1KI.21.2', 'So Ahab said to Naboth, “Give me your vineyard to use as a vegetable garden, since it is next to my palace. I will give you a better vineyard in its place—or if you prefer, I will give you its value in silver.”'),
('1KI', 21, 3, '1KI.21.3', 'But Naboth replied, “The LORD forbid that I should give you the inheritance of my fathers.”'),
('1KI', 21, 4, '1KI.21.4', 'So Ahab went to his palace, sullen and angry because Naboth the Jezreelite had told him, “I will not give you the inheritance of my fathers.” He lay down on his bed, turned his face away, and refused to eat.'),
('1KI', 21, 5, '1KI.21.5', 'Soon his wife Jezebel came in and asked, “Why are you so sullen that you refuse to eat?”'),
('1KI', 21, 6, '1KI.21.6', 'Ahab answered, “Because I spoke to Naboth the Jezreelite and told him, ‘Give me your vineyard for silver, or if you wish, I will give you another vineyard in its place.’ And he replied, ‘I will not give you my vineyard!’”'),
('1KI', 21, 7, '1KI.21.7', 'But his wife Jezebel said to him, “Do you not reign over Israel? Get up, eat some food, and be cheerful, for I will get you the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite.”'),
('1KI', 21, 8, '1KI.21.8', 'Then Jezebel wrote letters in Ahab’s name, sealed them with his seal, and sent them to the elders and nobles who lived with Naboth in his city.'),
('1KI', 21, 9, '1KI.21.9', 'In the letters she wrote: “Proclaim a fast and give Naboth a seat of honor among the people.'),
('1KI', 21, 10, '1KI.21.10', 'But seat two scoundrels opposite him and have them testify, ‘You have cursed both God and the king!’ Then take him out and stone him to death.”'),
('1KI', 21, 11, '1KI.21.11', 'So the elders and nobles who lived in Naboth’s city did as Jezebel had instructed in the letters she had written to them.'),
('1KI', 21, 12, '1KI.21.12', 'They proclaimed a fast and gave Naboth a seat of honor among the people.'),
('1KI', 21, 13, '1KI.21.13', 'And the two scoundrels came in and sat opposite Naboth, and these men testified against him before the people, saying, “Naboth has cursed both God and the king!” So they took him outside the city and stoned him to death.'),
('1KI', 21, 14, '1KI.21.14', 'Then they sent word to Jezebel: “Naboth has been stoned to death.”'),
('1KI', 21, 15, '1KI.21.15', 'When Jezebel heard that Naboth had been stoned to death, she said to Ahab, “Get up and take possession of the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite, who refused to give it to you for silver. For Naboth is no longer alive, but dead.”'),
('1KI', 21, 16, '1KI.21.16', 'And when Ahab heard that Naboth was dead, he got up and went down to take possession of the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite.'),
('1KI', 21, 17, '1KI.21.17', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Elijah the Tishbite, saying,'),
('1KI', 21, 18, '1KI.21.18', '“Get up and go down to meet Ahab king of Israel, who is in Samaria. See, he is in the vineyard of Naboth, where he has gone to take possession of it.'),
('1KI', 21, 19, '1KI.21.19', 'Tell him that this is what the LORD says: ‘Have you not murdered a man and seized his land?’ Then tell him that this is also what the LORD says: ‘In the place where the dogs licked up the blood of Naboth, there also the dogs will lick up your blood—yes, yours!’”'),
('1KI', 21, 20, '1KI.21.20', 'When Elijah arrived, Ahab said to him, “So you have found me out, my enemy.” He replied, “I have found you out because you have sold yourself to do evil in the sight of the LORD.'),
('1KI', 21, 21, '1KI.21.21', 'This is what the LORD says: ‘I will bring calamity on you and consume your descendants; I will cut off from Ahab every male in Israel, both slave and free.'),
('1KI', 21, 22, '1KI.21.22', 'I will make your house like that of Jeroboam son of Nebat and like that of Baasha son of Ahijah, because you have provoked My anger and caused Israel to sin.’'),
('1KI', 21, 23, '1KI.21.23', 'And the LORD also speaks concerning Jezebel: ‘The dogs will devour Jezebel by the wall of Jezreel.’'),
('1KI', 21, 24, '1KI.21.24', 'Anyone belonging to Ahab who dies in the city will be eaten by dogs, and anyone who dies in the field will be eaten by the birds of the air.”'),
('1KI', 21, 25, '1KI.21.25', '(Surely there was never one like Ahab, who sold himself to do evil in the sight of the LORD, incited by his wife Jezebel.'),
('1KI', 21, 26, '1KI.21.26', 'He committed the most detestable acts by going after idols, just like the Amorites whom the LORD had driven out before the Israelites.)'),
('1KI', 21, 27, '1KI.21.27', 'When Ahab heard these words, he tore his clothes, put on sackcloth, and fasted. He lay down in sackcloth and walked around meekly.'),
('1KI', 21, 28, '1KI.21.28', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Elijah the Tishbite, saying:'),
('1KI', 21, 29, '1KI.21.29', '“Have you seen how Ahab has humbled himself before Me? Because he has humbled himself before Me, I will not bring the calamity during his days, but I will bring it upon his house in the days of his son.”'),
('1KI', 22, 1, '1KI.22.1', 'Then three years passed without war between Aram and Israel.'),
('1KI', 22, 2, '1KI.22.2', 'However, in the third year, Jehoshaphat king of Judah went down to visit the king of Israel,'),
('1KI', 22, 3, '1KI.22.3', 'who said to his servants, “Do you not know that Ramoth-gilead is ours, but we have failed to take it from the hand of the king of Aram?”'),
('1KI', 22, 4, '1KI.22.4', 'So he asked Jehoshaphat, “Will you go with me to fight against Ramoth-gilead?” Jehoshaphat answered the king of Israel, “I am as you are, my people are your people, and my horses are your horses.”'),
('1KI', 22, 5, '1KI.22.5', 'But Jehoshaphat also said to the king of Israel, “Please inquire first for the word of the LORD.”'),
('1KI', 22, 6, '1KI.22.6', 'So the king of Israel assembled the prophets, about four hundred men, and asked them, “Should I go to war against Ramoth-gilead, or should I refrain?” “Go up,” they replied, “and the Lord will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
('1KI', 22, 7, '1KI.22.7', 'But Jehoshaphat asked, “Is there not still a prophet of the LORD here of whom we can inquire?”'),
('1KI', 22, 8, '1KI.22.8', 'The king of Israel answered, “There is still one man through whom we can inquire of the LORD, but I hate him because he never prophesies anything good for me, but only bad. He is Micaiah son of Imlah.” “The king should not say that!” Jehoshaphat replied.'),
('1KI', 22, 9, '1KI.22.9', 'So the king of Israel called one of his officials and said, “Bring Micaiah son of Imlah at once.”'),
('1KI', 22, 10, '1KI.22.10', 'Dressed in royal attire, the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat king of Judah were sitting on their thrones at the threshing floor by the entrance of the gate of Samaria, with all the prophets prophesying before them.'),
('1KI', 22, 11, '1KI.22.11', 'Now Zedekiah son of Chenaanah had made for himself iron horns and declared, “This is what the LORD says: ‘With these you shall gore the Arameans until they are finished off.’”'),
('1KI', 22, 12, '1KI.22.12', 'And all the prophets were prophesying the same, saying, “Go up to Ramoth-gilead and triumph, for the LORD will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
('1KI', 22, 13, '1KI.22.13', 'Then the messenger who had gone to call Micaiah instructed him, “Behold now, with one accord the words of the prophets are favorable to the king. So please let your words be like theirs, and speak favorably.”'),
('1KI', 22, 14, '1KI.22.14', 'But Micaiah said, “As surely as the LORD lives, I will speak whatever the LORD tells me.”'),
('1KI', 22, 15, '1KI.22.15', 'When Micaiah arrived, the king asked him, “Micaiah, should we go to war against Ramoth-gilead, or should we refrain?” “Go up and triumph,” Micaiah replied, “for the LORD will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
('1KI', 22, 16, '1KI.22.16', 'But the king said to him, “How many times must I make you swear not to tell me anything but the truth in the name of the LORD?”'),
('1KI', 22, 17, '1KI.22.17', 'So Micaiah declared: “I saw all Israel scattered on the hills like sheep without a shepherd. And the LORD said, ‘These people have no master; let each one return home in peace.’”'),
('1KI', 22, 18, '1KI.22.18', 'Then the king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “Did I not tell you that he never prophesies good for me, but only bad?”'),
('1KI', 22, 19, '1KI.22.19', 'Micaiah continued, “Therefore hear the word of the LORD: I saw the LORD sitting on His throne, and all the host of heaven standing by Him on His right and on His left.'),
('1KI', 22, 20, '1KI.22.20', 'And the LORD said, ‘Who will entice Ahab to march up and fall at Ramoth-gilead?’ And one suggested this, and another that.'),
('1KI', 22, 21, '1KI.22.21', 'Then a spirit came forward, stood before the LORD, and said, ‘I will entice him.’ ‘By what means?’ asked the LORD.'),
('1KI', 22, 22, '1KI.22.22', 'And he replied, ‘I will go out and be a lying spirit in the mouths of all his prophets.’ ‘You will surely entice him and prevail,’ said the LORD. ‘Go and do it.’'),
('1KI', 22, 23, '1KI.22.23', 'So you see, the LORD has put a lying spirit in the mouths of all these prophets of yours, and the LORD has pronounced disaster against you.”'),
('1KI', 22, 24, '1KI.22.24', 'Then Zedekiah son of Chenaanah went up, struck Micaiah in the face, and demanded, “Which way did the Spirit of the LORD go when He departed from me to speak with you?”'),
('1KI', 22, 25, '1KI.22.25', 'Micaiah replied, “You will soon see, on that day when you go and hide in an inner room.”'),
('1KI', 22, 26, '1KI.22.26', 'And the king of Israel declared, “Take Micaiah and return him to Amon the governor of the city and to Joash the king’s son,'),
('1KI', 22, 27, '1KI.22.27', 'and tell them that this is what the king says: ‘Put this man in prison and feed him only bread and water until I return safely.’”'),
('1KI', 22, 28, '1KI.22.28', 'But Micaiah replied, “If you ever return safely, the LORD has not spoken through me.” Then he added, “Take heed, all you people!”'),
('1KI', 22, 29, '1KI.22.29', 'So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat king of Judah went up to Ramoth-gilead.'),
('1KI', 22, 30, '1KI.22.30', 'And the king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “I will disguise myself and go into battle, but you wear your royal robes.” So the king of Israel disguised himself and went into battle.'),
('1KI', 22, 31, '1KI.22.31', 'Now the king of Aram had ordered his thirty-two chariot commanders, “Do not fight with anyone, small or great, except the king of Israel.”'),
('1KI', 22, 32, '1KI.22.32', 'When the chariot commanders saw Jehoshaphat, they said, “Surely this is the king of Israel!” So they turned to fight against him, but Jehoshaphat cried out.'),
('1KI', 22, 33, '1KI.22.33', 'And when the chariot commanders saw that he was not the king of Israel, they turned back from pursuing him.'),
('1KI', 22, 34, '1KI.22.34', 'However, a certain man drew his bow without taking special aim, and he struck the king of Israel between the joints of his armor. So the king said to his charioteer, “Turn around and take me out of the battle, for I am badly wounded!”'),
('1KI', 22, 35, '1KI.22.35', 'The battle raged throughout that day, and the king was propped up in his chariot facing the Arameans. And the blood from his wound ran out onto the floor of the chariot, and that evening he died.'),
('1KI', 22, 36, '1KI.22.36', 'As the sun was setting, the cry rang out in the army: “Every man to his own city, and every man to his own land!”'),
('1KI', 22, 37, '1KI.22.37', 'So the king died and was brought to Samaria, where they buried him.'),
('1KI', 22, 38, '1KI.22.38', 'And the chariot was washed at the pool of Samaria where the prostitutes bathed, and the dogs licked up Ahab’s blood, according to the word that the LORD had spoken.'),
('1KI', 22, 39, '1KI.22.39', 'As for the rest of the acts of Ahab, along with all his accomplishments and the ivory palace and all the cities he built, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('1KI', 22, 40, '1KI.22.40', 'And Ahab rested with his fathers, and his son Ahaziah reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 22, 41, '1KI.22.41', 'In the fourth year of Ahab’s reign over Israel, Jehoshaphat son of Asa became king of Judah.'),
('1KI', 22, 42, '1KI.22.42', 'Jehoshaphat was thirty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem twenty-five years. His mother’s name was Azubah daughter of Shilhi.'),
('1KI', 22, 43, '1KI.22.43', 'And Jehoshaphat walked in all the ways of his father Asa; he did not turn away from them, but did what was right in the eyes of the LORD. The high places, however, were not removed; the people still sacrificed and burned incense on the high places.'),
('1KI', 22, 44, '1KI.22.44', 'Jehoshaphat also made peace with the king of Israel.'),
('1KI', 22, 45, '1KI.22.45', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, along with the might he exercised and how he waged war, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('1KI', 22, 46, '1KI.22.46', 'He banished from the land the male shrine prostitutes who remained from the days of his father Asa.'),
('1KI', 22, 47, '1KI.22.47', 'And there was no king in Edom; a deputy served as king.'),
('1KI', 22, 48, '1KI.22.48', 'Jehoshaphat built ships of Tarshish to go to Ophir for gold, but they never set sail, because they were wrecked at Ezion-geber.'),
('1KI', 22, 49, '1KI.22.49', 'At that time Ahaziah son of Ahab said to Jehoshaphat, “Let my servants sail with your servants,” but Jehoshaphat refused.'),
('1KI', 22, 50, '1KI.22.50', 'And Jehoshaphat rested with his fathers and was buried with them in the city of his father David. And his son Jehoram reigned in his place.'),
('1KI', 22, 51, '1KI.22.51', 'In the seventeenth year of Jehoshaphat’s reign over Judah, Ahaziah son of Ahab became king of Israel, and he reigned in Samaria two years.'),
('1KI', 22, 52, '1KI.22.52', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD and walked in the ways of his father and mother and of Jeroboam son of Nebat, who had caused Israel to sin.'),
('1KI', 22, 53, '1KI.22.53', 'Ahaziah served and worshiped Baal, provoking the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger, just as his father had done.'),
('2KI', 1, 1, '2KI.1.1', 'After the death of Ahab, Moab rebelled against Israel.'),
('2KI', 1, 2, '2KI.1.2', 'Now Ahaziah had fallen through the lattice of his upper room in Samaria and injured himself. So he sent messengers and instructed them: “Go inquire of Baal-zebub, the god of Ekron, whether I will recover from this injury.”'),
('2KI', 1, 3, '2KI.1.3', 'But the angel of the LORD said to Elijah the Tishbite, “Go up to meet the messengers of the king of Samaria and ask them, ‘Is it because there is no God in Israel that you are on your way to inquire of Baal-zebub, the god of Ekron?’'),
('2KI', 1, 4, '2KI.1.4', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: ‘You will not get up from the bed on which you are lying. You will surely die.’” So Elijah departed.'),
('2KI', 1, 5, '2KI.1.5', 'When the messengers returned to the king, he asked them, “Why have you returned?”'),
('2KI', 1, 6, '2KI.1.6', 'They replied, “A man came up to meet us and said, ‘Go back to the king who sent you and tell him that this is what the LORD says: Is it because there is no God in Israel that you are sending these men to inquire of Baal-zebub, the god of Ekron? Therefore you will not get up from the bed on which you are lying. You will surely die.’”'),
('2KI', 1, 7, '2KI.1.7', 'The king asked them, “What sort of man came up to meet you and spoke these words to you?”'),
('2KI', 1, 8, '2KI.1.8', '“He was a hairy man,” they answered, “with a leather belt around his waist.” “It was Elijah the Tishbite,” said the king.'),
('2KI', 1, 9, '2KI.1.9', 'Then King Ahaziah sent to Elijah a captain with his company of fifty men. So the captain went up to Elijah, who was sitting on top of a hill, and said to him, “Man of God, the king declares, ‘Come down!’”'),
('2KI', 1, 10, '2KI.1.10', 'Elijah answered the captain, “If I am a man of God, may fire come down from heaven and consume you and your fifty men.” And fire came down from heaven and consumed the captain and his fifty men.'),
('2KI', 1, 11, '2KI.1.11', 'So the king sent to Elijah another captain with his fifty men. And the captain said to Elijah, “Man of God, the king declares, ‘Come down at once!’”'),
('2KI', 1, 12, '2KI.1.12', 'Again Elijah replied, “If I am a man of God, may fire come down from heaven and consume you and your fifty men.” And the fire of God came down from heaven and consumed the captain and his fifty men.'),
('2KI', 1, 13, '2KI.1.13', 'So the king sent a third captain with his fifty men. And the third captain went up, fell on his knees before Elijah, and begged him, “Man of God, may my life and the lives of these fifty servants of yours please be precious in your sight.'),
('2KI', 1, 14, '2KI.1.14', 'Behold, fire has come down from heaven and consumed the first two captains of fifty, with all their men. But now may my life be precious in your sight.”'),
('2KI', 1, 15, '2KI.1.15', 'Then the angel of the LORD said to Elijah, “Go down with him. Do not be afraid of him.” So Elijah got up and went down with him to the king.'),
('2KI', 1, 16, '2KI.1.16', 'And Elijah said to King Ahaziah, “This is what the LORD says: Is there really no God in Israel for you to inquire of His word? Is that why you have sent messengers to inquire of Baal-zebub, the god of Ekron? Therefore you will not get up from the bed on which you are lying. You will surely die.”'),
('2KI', 1, 17, '2KI.1.17', 'So Ahaziah died according to the word of the LORD that Elijah had spoken. And since he had no son, Jehoram succeeded him in the second year of the reign of Jehoram son of Jehoshaphat over Judah.'),
('2KI', 1, 18, '2KI.1.18', 'As for the rest of the acts of Ahaziah, along with his accomplishments, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 2, 1, '2KI.2.1', 'Shortly before the LORD took Elijah up to heaven in a whirlwind, Elijah and Elisha were on their way from Gilgal,'),
('2KI', 2, 2, '2KI.2.2', 'and Elijah said to Elisha, “Please stay here, for the LORD has sent me on to Bethel.” But Elisha replied, “As surely as the LORD lives and as you yourself live, I will not leave you.” So they went down to Bethel.'),
('2KI', 2, 3, '2KI.2.3', 'Then the sons of the prophets at Bethel came out to Elisha and said, “Do you know that the LORD will take your master away from you today?” “Yes, I know,” he replied. “Do not speak of it.”'),
('2KI', 2, 4, '2KI.2.4', 'And Elijah said to Elisha, “Please stay here, for the LORD has sent me on to Jericho.” But Elisha replied, “As surely as the LORD lives and as you yourself live, I will not leave you.” So they went to Jericho.'),
('2KI', 2, 5, '2KI.2.5', 'Then the sons of the prophets at Jericho came up to Elisha and said, “Do you know that the LORD will take your master away from you today?” “Yes, I know,” he replied. “Do not speak of it.”'),
('2KI', 2, 6, '2KI.2.6', 'And Elijah said to Elisha, “Please stay here, for the LORD has sent me on to the Jordan.” But Elisha replied, “As surely as the LORD lives and as you yourself live, I will not leave you.” So the two of them went on.'),
('2KI', 2, 7, '2KI.2.7', 'Then a company of fifty of the sons of the prophets went and stood at a distance, facing Elijah and Elisha as the two of them stood by the Jordan.'),
('2KI', 2, 8, '2KI.2.8', 'And Elijah took his cloak, rolled it up, and struck the waters, which parted to the right and to the left, so that the two of them crossed over on dry ground.'),
('2KI', 2, 9, '2KI.2.9', 'After they had crossed over, Elijah said to Elisha, “Tell me, what can I do for you before I am taken away from you?” “Please, let me inherit a double portion of your spirit,” Elisha replied.'),
('2KI', 2, 10, '2KI.2.10', '“You have requested a difficult thing,” said Elijah. “Nevertheless, if you see me as I am taken from you, it will be yours. But if not, then it will not be so.”'),
('2KI', 2, 11, '2KI.2.11', 'As they were walking along and talking together, suddenly a chariot of fire with horses of fire appeared and separated the two of them, and Elijah went up into heaven in a whirlwind.'),
('2KI', 2, 12, '2KI.2.12', 'As Elisha watched, he cried out, “My father, my father, the chariots and horsemen of Israel!” And he saw Elijah no more. So taking hold of his own clothes, he tore them in two.'),
('2KI', 2, 13, '2KI.2.13', 'Elisha also picked up the cloak that had fallen from Elijah, and he went back and stood on the bank of the Jordan.'),
('2KI', 2, 14, '2KI.2.14', 'Then he took the cloak of Elijah that had fallen from him and struck the waters. “Where now is the LORD, the God of Elijah?” he asked. And when he had struck the waters, they parted to the right and to the left, and Elisha crossed over.'),
('2KI', 2, 15, '2KI.2.15', 'When the sons of the prophets who were watching him from Jericho saw what had happened, they said, “The spirit of Elijah rests on Elisha.” And they went to meet him and bowed down to the ground before him.'),
('2KI', 2, 16, '2KI.2.16', '“Look now,” they said to Elisha, “we your servants have fifty valiant men. Please let them go and search for your master. Perhaps the Spirit of the LORD has taken him up and put him on one of the mountains or in one of the valleys.” “Do not send them,” Elisha replied.'),
('2KI', 2, 17, '2KI.2.17', 'But when they pressed him to the point of embarrassment, he said, “Send them.” And they sent fifty men, who searched for three days but did not find Elijah.'),
('2KI', 2, 18, '2KI.2.18', 'When they returned to Elisha, who was staying in Jericho, he said to them, “Didn’t I tell you not to go?”'),
('2KI', 2, 19, '2KI.2.19', 'Then the men of the city said to Elisha, “Please note, our lord, that the city’s location is good, as you can see. But the water is bad and the land is unfruitful.”'),
('2KI', 2, 20, '2KI.2.20', '“Bring me a new bowl,” he replied, “and put some salt in it.” So they brought it to him,'),
('2KI', 2, 21, '2KI.2.21', 'and Elisha went out to the spring, cast the salt into it, and said, “This is what the LORD says: ‘I have healed this water. No longer will it cause death or unfruitfulness.’”'),
('2KI', 2, 22, '2KI.2.22', 'And the waters there have been healthy to this day, according to the word spoken by Elisha.'),
('2KI', 2, 23, '2KI.2.23', 'From there, Elisha went up to Bethel, and as he was walking up the road, a group of boys came out of the city and jeered at him, chanting, “Go up, you baldhead! Go up, you baldhead!”'),
('2KI', 2, 24, '2KI.2.24', 'Then he turned around, looked at them, and called down a curse on them in the name of the LORD. Suddenly two female bears came out of the woods and mauled forty-two of the boys.'),
('2KI', 2, 25, '2KI.2.25', 'And Elisha went on to Mount Carmel, and from there he returned to Samaria.'),
('2KI', 3, 1, '2KI.3.1', 'In the eighteenth year of Jehoshaphat’s reign over Judah, Jehoram son of Ahab became king of Israel, and he reigned in Samaria twelve years.'),
('2KI', 3, 2, '2KI.3.2', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, but not as his father and mother had done. He removed the sacred pillar of Baal that his father had made.'),
('2KI', 3, 3, '2KI.3.3', 'Nevertheless, he clung to the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit; he did not turn away from them.'),
('2KI', 3, 4, '2KI.3.4', 'Now Mesha king of Moab was a sheep breeder, and he would render to the king of Israel a hundred thousand lambs and the wool of a hundred thousand rams.'),
('2KI', 3, 5, '2KI.3.5', 'But after the death of Ahab, the king of Moab rebelled against the king of Israel.'),
('2KI', 3, 6, '2KI.3.6', 'So at that time King Jehoram set out from Samaria and mobilized all Israel.'),
('2KI', 3, 7, '2KI.3.7', 'And he sent a message to Jehoshaphat king of Judah: “The king of Moab has rebelled against me. Will you go with me to fight against Moab?” “I will go,” replied Jehoshaphat. “I am as you are, my people are your people, and my horses are your horses.”'),
('2KI', 3, 8, '2KI.3.8', 'Then he asked, “Which way shall we go up?” “By way of the Desert of Edom,” replied Joram.'),
('2KI', 3, 9, '2KI.3.9', 'So the king of Israel, the king of Judah, and the king of Edom set out, and after they had traveled a roundabout route for seven days, they had no water for their army or for their animals.'),
('2KI', 3, 10, '2KI.3.10', '“Alas,” said the king of Israel, “for the LORD has summoned these three kings to deliver them into the hand of Moab!”'),
('2KI', 3, 11, '2KI.3.11', 'But Jehoshaphat asked, “Is there no prophet of the LORD here? Let us inquire of the LORD through him.” And one of the servants of the king of Israel answered, “Elisha son of Shaphat is here. He used to pour water on the hands of Elijah.”'),
('2KI', 3, 12, '2KI.3.12', 'Jehoshaphat affirmed, “The word of the LORD is with him.” So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat and the king of Edom went down to him.'),
('2KI', 3, 13, '2KI.3.13', 'Elisha, however, said to the king of Israel, “What have we to do with each other? Go to the prophets of your father and of your mother!” “No,” replied the king of Israel, “for it is the LORD who has summoned these three kings to deliver them into the hand of Moab.”'),
('2KI', 3, 14, '2KI.3.14', 'Then Elisha said, “As surely as the LORD of Hosts lives, before whom I stand, were it not for my regard for the presence of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, I would not look at you or acknowledge you.'),
('2KI', 3, 15, '2KI.3.15', 'But now, bring me a harpist.” And while the harpist played, the hand of the LORD came upon Elisha'),
('2KI', 3, 16, '2KI.3.16', 'and he said, “This is what the LORD says: ‘Dig this valley full of ditches.’'),
('2KI', 3, 17, '2KI.3.17', 'For the LORD says, ‘You will not see wind or rain, but the valley will be filled with water, and you will drink—you and your cattle and your animals.’'),
('2KI', 3, 18, '2KI.3.18', 'This is a simple matter in the sight of the LORD, and He will also deliver the Moabites into your hand.'),
('2KI', 3, 19, '2KI.3.19', 'And you shall attack every fortified city and every city of importance. You shall cut down every good tree, stop up every spring, and ruin every good field with stones.”'),
('2KI', 3, 20, '2KI.3.20', 'The next morning, at the time of the morning sacrifice, water suddenly flowed from the direction of Edom and filled the land.'),
('2KI', 3, 21, '2KI.3.21', 'Now all the Moabites had heard that the kings had come up to fight against them. So all who could bear arms, young and old, were summoned and stationed at the border.'),
('2KI', 3, 22, '2KI.3.22', 'When they got up early in the morning, the sun was shining on the water, and it looked as red as blood to the Moabites across the way.'),
('2KI', 3, 23, '2KI.3.23', '“This is blood!” they exclaimed. “The kings have clashed swords and slaughtered one another. Now to the plunder, Moab!”'),
('2KI', 3, 24, '2KI.3.24', 'But when the Moabites came to the camp of Israel, the Israelites rose up and attacked them, and they fled before them. So the Israelites invaded their land and struck down the Moabites.'),
('2KI', 3, 25, '2KI.3.25', 'They destroyed the cities, and each man threw stones on every good field until it was covered. They stopped up every spring and cut down every good tree. Only Kir-haraseth was left with stones in place, but men with slings surrounded it and attacked it as well.'),
('2KI', 3, 26, '2KI.3.26', 'When the king of Moab saw that the battle was too fierce for him, he took with him seven hundred swordsmen to break through to the king of Edom, but they could not prevail.'),
('2KI', 3, 27, '2KI.3.27', 'So he took his firstborn son, who was to succeed him, and offered him as a burnt offering on the city wall. And there was great fury against the Israelites, so they withdrew and returned to their own land.'),
('2KI', 4, 1, '2KI.4.1', 'Now the wife of one of the sons of the prophets cried out to Elisha, “Your servant, my husband, is dead, and you know that your servant feared the LORD. And now his creditor is coming to take my two children as his slaves!”'),
('2KI', 4, 2, '2KI.4.2', '“How can I help you?” asked Elisha. “Tell me, what do you have in the house?” She answered, “Your servant has nothing in the house but a jar of oil.”'),
('2KI', 4, 3, '2KI.4.3', '“Go,” said Elisha, “borrow empty jars from all your neighbors. Do not gather just a few.'),
('2KI', 4, 4, '2KI.4.4', 'Then go inside, shut the door behind you and your sons, and pour oil into all these jars, setting the full ones aside.”'),
('2KI', 4, 5, '2KI.4.5', 'So she left him, and after she had shut the door behind her and her sons, they kept bringing jars to her, and she kept pouring.'),
('2KI', 4, 6, '2KI.4.6', 'When all the jars were full, she said to her son, “Bring me another.” But he replied, “There are no more jars.” Then the oil stopped flowing.'),
('2KI', 4, 7, '2KI.4.7', 'She went and told the man of God, and he said, “Go, sell the oil, and pay your debt. Then you and your sons can live on the remainder.”'),
('2KI', 4, 8, '2KI.4.8', 'One day Elisha went to Shunem, and a prominent woman who lived there persuaded him to have a meal. So whenever he would pass by, he would stop there to eat.'),
('2KI', 4, 9, '2KI.4.9', 'Then the woman said to her husband, “Behold, now I know that the one who often comes our way is a holy man of God.'),
('2KI', 4, 10, '2KI.4.10', 'Please let us make a small room upstairs and put in it a bed, a table, a chair, and a lamp for him. Then when he comes to us, he can stay there.”'),
('2KI', 4, 11, '2KI.4.11', 'One day Elisha came to visit and went to his upper room to lie down.'),
('2KI', 4, 12, '2KI.4.12', 'And he said to Gehazi his servant, “Call the Shunammite woman.” And when he had called her, she stood before him,'),
('2KI', 4, 13, '2KI.4.13', 'and Elisha said to Gehazi, “Now tell her, ‘Look, you have gone to all this trouble for us. What can we do for you? Can we speak on your behalf to the king or the commander of the army?’” “I have a home among my own people,” she replied.'),
('2KI', 4, 14, '2KI.4.14', 'So he asked, “Then what should be done for her?” “Well, she has no son,” Gehazi replied, “and her husband is old.”'),
('2KI', 4, 15, '2KI.4.15', '“Call her,” said Elisha. So Gehazi called her, and she stood in the doorway.'),
('2KI', 4, 16, '2KI.4.16', 'And Elisha declared, “At this time next year, you will hold a son in your arms.” “No, my lord,” she said. “Do not lie to your maidservant, O man of God.”'),
('2KI', 4, 17, '2KI.4.17', 'But the woman did conceive, and at that time the next year she gave birth to a son, just as Elisha had told her.'),
('2KI', 4, 18, '2KI.4.18', 'And the child grew, and one day he went out to his father, who was with the harvesters.'),
('2KI', 4, 19, '2KI.4.19', '“My head! My head!” he complained to his father. So his father told a servant, “Carry him to his mother.”'),
('2KI', 4, 20, '2KI.4.20', 'After the servant had picked him up and carried him to his mother, the boy sat on her lap until noon, and then he died.'),
('2KI', 4, 21, '2KI.4.21', 'And she went up and laid him on the bed of the man of God. Then she shut the door and went out.'),
('2KI', 4, 22, '2KI.4.22', 'And the woman called her husband and said, “Please send me one of the servants and one of the donkeys, that I may go quickly to the man of God and return.”'),
('2KI', 4, 23, '2KI.4.23', '“Why would you go to him today?” he replied. “It is not a New Moon or a Sabbath.” “Everything is all right,” she said.'),
('2KI', 4, 24, '2KI.4.24', 'Then she saddled the donkey and told her servant, “Drive onward; do not slow the pace for me unless I tell you.”'),
('2KI', 4, 25, '2KI.4.25', 'So she set out and went to the man of God at Mount Carmel. When the man of God saw her at a distance, he said to his servant Gehazi, “Look, there is the Shunammite woman.'),
('2KI', 4, 26, '2KI.4.26', 'Please run out now to meet her and ask, ‘Are you all right? Is your husband all right? Is your child all right?’” And she answered, “Everything is all right.”'),
('2KI', 4, 27, '2KI.4.27', 'When she reached the man of God at the mountain, she clung to his feet. Gehazi came over to push her away, but the man of God said, “Leave her alone, for her soul is in deep distress, and the LORD has hidden it from me and has not told me.”'),
('2KI', 4, 28, '2KI.4.28', 'Then she said, “Did I ask you for a son, my lord? Didn’t I say, ‘Do not deceive me?’”'),
('2KI', 4, 29, '2KI.4.29', 'So Elisha said to Gehazi, “Tie up your garment, take my staff in your hand, and go! If you meet anyone, do not greet him, and if anyone greets you, do not answer him. Then lay my staff on the boy’s face.”'),
('2KI', 4, 30, '2KI.4.30', 'And the mother of the boy said, “As surely as the LORD lives and as you yourself live, I will not leave you.” So he got up and followed her.'),
('2KI', 4, 31, '2KI.4.31', 'Gehazi went on ahead of them and laid the staff on the boy’s face, but there was no sound or response. So he went back to meet Elisha and told him, “The boy has not awakened.”'),
('2KI', 4, 32, '2KI.4.32', 'When Elisha reached the house, there was the boy lying dead on his bed.'),
('2KI', 4, 33, '2KI.4.33', 'So he went in, closed the door behind the two of them, and prayed to the LORD.'),
('2KI', 4, 34, '2KI.4.34', 'Then Elisha got on the bed and lay on the boy, mouth to mouth, eye to eye, and hand to hand. As he stretched himself out over him, the boy’s body became warm.'),
('2KI', 4, 35, '2KI.4.35', 'Elisha turned away and paced back and forth across the room. Then he got on the bed and stretched himself out over the boy again, and the boy sneezed seven times and opened his eyes.'),
('2KI', 4, 36, '2KI.4.36', 'Elisha summoned Gehazi and said, “Call the Shunammite woman.” So he called her and she came. Then Elisha said, “Pick up your son.”'),
('2KI', 4, 37, '2KI.4.37', 'She came in, fell at his feet, and bowed to the ground. Then she picked up her son and went out.'),
('2KI', 4, 38, '2KI.4.38', 'When Elisha returned to Gilgal, there was a famine in the land. As the sons of the prophets were sitting at his feet, he said to his attendant, “Put on the large pot and boil some stew for the sons of the prophets.”'),
('2KI', 4, 39, '2KI.4.39', 'One of them went out to the field to gather herbs, and he found a wild vine from which he gathered as many wild gourds as his garment could hold. Then he came back and cut them up into the pot of stew, though no one knew what they were.'),
('2KI', 4, 40, '2KI.4.40', 'And they poured it out for the men to eat, but when they tasted the stew they cried out, “There is death in the pot, O man of God!” And they could not eat it.'),
('2KI', 4, 41, '2KI.4.41', 'Then Elisha said, “Get some flour.” He threw it into the pot and said, “Pour it out for the people to eat.” And there was nothing harmful in the pot.'),
('2KI', 4, 42, '2KI.4.42', 'Now a man from Baal-shalishah came to the man of God with a sack of twenty loaves of barley bread from the first ripe grain. “Give it to the people to eat,” said Elisha.'),
('2KI', 4, 43, '2KI.4.43', 'But his servant asked, “How am I to set twenty loaves before a hundred men?” “Give it to the people to eat,” said Elisha, “for this is what the LORD says: ‘They will eat and have some left over.’”'),
('2KI', 4, 44, '2KI.4.44', 'So he set it before them, and they ate and had some left over, according to the word of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 5, 1, '2KI.5.1', 'Now Naaman, the commander of the army of the king of Aram, was a great man in his master’s sight and highly regarded, for through him the LORD had given victory to Aram. And he was a mighty man of valor, but he was a leper.'),
('2KI', 5, 2, '2KI.5.2', 'At this time the Arameans had gone out in bands and had taken a young girl from the land of Israel, and she was serving Naaman’s wife.'),
('2KI', 5, 3, '2KI.5.3', 'She said to her mistress, “If only my master would go to the prophet who is in Samaria, he would cure him of his leprosy.”'),
('2KI', 5, 4, '2KI.5.4', 'And Naaman went and told his master what the girl from the land of Israel had said.'),
('2KI', 5, 5, '2KI.5.5', '“Go now,” said the king of Aram, “and I will send you with a letter to the king of Israel.” So Naaman departed, taking with him ten talents of silver, six thousand shekels of gold, and ten sets of clothing.'),
('2KI', 5, 6, '2KI.5.6', 'And the letter that he took to the king of Israel stated: “With this letter I am sending my servant Naaman, so that you may cure him of his leprosy.”'),
('2KI', 5, 7, '2KI.5.7', 'When the king of Israel read the letter, he tore his clothes and asked, “Am I God, killing and giving life, that this man expects me to cure a leper? Surely you can see that he is seeking a quarrel with me!”'),
('2KI', 5, 8, '2KI.5.8', 'Now when Elisha the man of God heard that the king of Israel had torn his clothes, he sent a message to the king: “Why have you torn your clothes? Please let the man come to me, and he will know that there is a prophet in Israel.”'),
('2KI', 5, 9, '2KI.5.9', 'So Naaman came with his horses and chariots and stood at the door of Elisha’s house.'),
('2KI', 5, 10, '2KI.5.10', 'Then Elisha sent him a messenger, who said, “Go and wash yourself seven times in the Jordan, and your flesh will be restored, and you will be clean.”'),
('2KI', 5, 11, '2KI.5.11', 'But Naaman went away angry, saying, “I thought that he would surely come out, stand and call on the name of the LORD his God, and wave his hand over the spot to cure my leprosy.'),
('2KI', 5, 12, '2KI.5.12', 'Are not the Abanah and Pharpar, the rivers of Damascus, better than all the waters of Israel? Could I not have washed in them and been cleansed?” So he turned and went away in a rage.'),
('2KI', 5, 13, '2KI.5.13', 'Naaman’s servants, however, approached him and said, “My father, if the prophet had told you to do some great thing, would you not have done it? How much more, then, when he tells you, ‘Wash and be cleansed’?”'),
('2KI', 5, 14, '2KI.5.14', 'So Naaman went down and dipped himself in the Jordan seven times, according to the word of the man of God, and his flesh was restored and became like that of a little child, and he was clean.'),
('2KI', 5, 15, '2KI.5.15', 'Then Naaman and all his attendants went back to the man of God, stood before him, and declared, “Now I know for sure that there is no God in all the earth except in Israel. So please accept a gift from your servant.”'),
('2KI', 5, 16, '2KI.5.16', 'But Elisha replied, “As surely as the LORD lives, before whom I stand, I will not accept it.” And although Naaman urged him to accept it, he refused.'),
('2KI', 5, 17, '2KI.5.17', '“If you will not,” said Naaman, “please let me, your servant, be given as much soil as a pair of mules can carry. For your servant will never again make a burnt offering or a sacrifice to any other god but the LORD.'),
('2KI', 5, 18, '2KI.5.18', 'Yet may the LORD forgive your servant this one thing: When my master goes into the temple of Rimmon to worship there, and he leans on my arm, and I bow down in the temple of Rimmon, may the LORD forgive your servant in this matter.”'),
('2KI', 5, 19, '2KI.5.19', '“Go in peace,” said Elisha. But after Naaman had traveled a short distance,'),
('2KI', 5, 20, '2KI.5.20', 'Gehazi, the servant of Elisha the man of God, said, “Look, my master has spared this Aramean, Naaman, by not accepting what he brought. As surely as the LORD lives, I will run after him and get something from him.”'),
('2KI', 5, 21, '2KI.5.21', 'So Gehazi pursued Naaman. And when Naaman saw him running toward him, he got down from the chariot to meet him and asked, “Is everything all right?”'),
('2KI', 5, 22, '2KI.5.22', '“Everything is all right,” Gehazi replied. “My master has sent me to say, ‘Look, two young men from the sons of the prophets have just now come to me from the hill country of Ephraim. Please give them a talent of silver and two sets of clothing.’”'),
('2KI', 5, 23, '2KI.5.23', 'But Naaman insisted, “Please, take two talents.” And he urged Gehazi to accept them. Then he tied up two talents of silver in two bags along with two sets of clothing and gave them to two of his servants, who carried them ahead of Gehazi.'),
('2KI', 5, 24, '2KI.5.24', 'When Gehazi came to the hill, he took the gifts from the servants and stored them in the house. Then he dismissed the men, and they departed.'),
('2KI', 5, 25, '2KI.5.25', 'When Gehazi went in and stood before his master, Elisha asked him, “Gehazi, where have you been?” “Your servant did not go anywhere,” he replied.'),
('2KI', 5, 26, '2KI.5.26', 'But Elisha questioned him, “Did not my spirit go with you when the man got down from his chariot to meet you? Is this the time to accept money and clothing, olive groves and vineyards, sheep and oxen, menservants and maidservants?'),
('2KI', 5, 27, '2KI.5.27', 'Therefore, the leprosy of Naaman will cling to you and your descendants forever!” And as Gehazi left his presence, he was leprous—as white as snow.'),
('2KI', 6, 1, '2KI.6.1', 'Now the sons of the prophets said to Elisha, “Please take note that the place where we meet with you is too small for us.'),
('2KI', 6, 2, '2KI.6.2', 'Please let us go to the Jordan, where each of us can get a log so we can build ourselves a place to live there.” “Go,” said Elisha.'),
('2KI', 6, 3, '2KI.6.3', 'Then one of them said, “Please come with your servants.” “I will come,” he replied.'),
('2KI', 6, 4, '2KI.6.4', 'So Elisha went with them, and when they came to the Jordan, they began to cut down some trees.'),
('2KI', 6, 5, '2KI.6.5', 'As one of them was cutting down a tree, the iron axe head fell into the water. “Oh, my master,” he cried out, “it was borrowed!”'),
('2KI', 6, 6, '2KI.6.6', '“Where did it fall?” asked the man of God. And when he showed him the place, the man of God cut a stick, threw it there, and made the iron float.'),
('2KI', 6, 7, '2KI.6.7', '“Lift it out,” he said, and the man reached out his hand and took it.'),
('2KI', 6, 8, '2KI.6.8', 'Now the king of Aram was at war against Israel. After consulting with his servants, he said, “My camp will be in such and such a place.”'),
('2KI', 6, 9, '2KI.6.9', 'Then the man of God sent word to the king of Israel: “Be careful not to pass by this place, for the Arameans are going down there.”'),
('2KI', 6, 10, '2KI.6.10', 'So the king of Israel sent word to the place the man of God had pointed out. Time and again Elisha warned the king, so that he was on his guard in such places.'),
('2KI', 6, 11, '2KI.6.11', 'For this reason the king of Aram became enraged and called his servants to demand of them, “Tell me, which one of us is on the side of the king of Israel?”'),
('2KI', 6, 12, '2KI.6.12', 'But one of his servants replied, “No one, my lord the king. For Elisha, the prophet in Israel, tells the king of Israel the very words you speak in your bedroom.”'),
('2KI', 6, 13, '2KI.6.13', 'So the king said, “Go and see where he is, that I may send men to capture him.” On receiving the report, “Elisha is in Dothan,”'),
('2KI', 6, 14, '2KI.6.14', 'the king of Aram sent horses, chariots, and a great army. They went there by night and surrounded the city.'),
('2KI', 6, 15, '2KI.6.15', 'When the servant of the man of God got up and went out early in the morning, behold, an army with horses and chariots had surrounded the city. So he asked Elisha, “Oh, my master, what are we to do?”'),
('2KI', 6, 16, '2KI.6.16', '“Do not be afraid,” Elisha answered, “for those who are with us are more than those who are with them.”'),
('2KI', 6, 17, '2KI.6.17', 'Then Elisha prayed, “O LORD, please open his eyes that he may see.” And the LORD opened the eyes of the young man, and he saw that the hills were full of horses and chariots of fire all around Elisha.'),
('2KI', 6, 18, '2KI.6.18', 'As the Arameans came down against him, Elisha prayed to the LORD, “Please strike these people with blindness.” So He struck them with blindness, according to the word of Elisha.'),
('2KI', 6, 19, '2KI.6.19', 'And Elisha told them, “This is not the way, and this is not the city. Follow me, and I will take you to the man you are seeking.” And he led them to Samaria.'),
('2KI', 6, 20, '2KI.6.20', 'When they had entered Samaria, Elisha said, “O LORD, open the eyes of these men that they may see.” Then the LORD opened their eyes, and they looked around and discovered that they were in Samaria.'),
('2KI', 6, 21, '2KI.6.21', 'And when the king of Israel saw them, he asked Elisha, “My father, shall I kill them? Shall I kill them?”'),
('2KI', 6, 22, '2KI.6.22', '“Do not kill them,” he replied. “Would you kill those you have captured with your own sword or bow? Set food and water before them, that they may eat and drink and then return to their master.”'),
('2KI', 6, 23, '2KI.6.23', 'So the king prepared a great feast for them, and after they had finished eating and drinking, he sent them away, and they returned to their master. And the Aramean raiders did not come into the land of Israel again.'),
('2KI', 6, 24, '2KI.6.24', 'Some time later, Ben-hadad king of Aram assembled his entire army and marched up to besiege Samaria.'),
('2KI', 6, 25, '2KI.6.25', 'So there was a great famine in Samaria. Indeed, they besieged the city so long that a donkey’s head sold for eighty shekels of silver, and a quarter cab of dove’s dung sold for five shekels of silver.'),
('2KI', 6, 26, '2KI.6.26', 'As the king of Israel was passing by on the wall, a woman cried out to him, “Help me, my lord the king!”'),
('2KI', 6, 27, '2KI.6.27', 'He answered, “If the LORD does not help you, where can I find help for you? From the threshing floor or the winepress?”'),
('2KI', 6, 28, '2KI.6.28', 'Then the king asked her, “What is the matter?” And she answered, “This woman said to me, ‘Give up your son, that we may eat him, and tomorrow we will eat my son.’'),
('2KI', 6, 29, '2KI.6.29', 'So we boiled my son and ate him, and the next day I said to her, ‘Give up your son, that we may eat him.’ But she had hidden her son.”'),
('2KI', 6, 30, '2KI.6.30', 'When the king heard the words of the woman, he tore his clothes. And as he passed by on the wall, the people saw the sackcloth under his clothes next to his skin.'),
('2KI', 6, 31, '2KI.6.31', 'He announced, “May God punish me, and ever so severely, if the head of Elisha son of Shaphat remains on his shoulders through this day!”'),
('2KI', 6, 32, '2KI.6.32', 'Now Elisha was sitting in his house, and the elders were sitting with him. The king sent a messenger ahead, but before he arrived, Elisha said to the elders, “Do you see how this murderer has sent someone to cut off my head? Look, when the messenger comes, shut the door to keep him out. Is not the sound of his master’s footsteps behind him?”'),
('2KI', 6, 33, '2KI.6.33', 'While Elisha was still speaking with them, the messenger came down to him. And the king said, “This calamity is from the LORD. Why should I wait for the LORD any longer?”'),
('2KI', 7, 1, '2KI.7.1', 'Then Elisha said, “Hear the word of the LORD! This is what the LORD says: ‘About this time tomorrow at the gate of Samaria, a seah of fine flour will sell for a shekel, and two seahs of barley will sell for a shekel.’”'),
('2KI', 7, 2, '2KI.7.2', 'But the officer on whose arm the king leaned answered the man of God, “Look, even if the LORD were to make windows in heaven, could this really happen?” “You will see it with your own eyes,” replied Elisha, “but you will not eat any of it.”'),
('2KI', 7, 3, '2KI.7.3', 'Now there were four men with leprosy at the entrance of the city gate, and they said to one another, “Why just sit here until we die?'),
('2KI', 7, 4, '2KI.7.4', 'If we say, ‘Let us go into the city,’ we will die there from the famine in the city; but if we sit here, we will also die. So come now, let us go over to the camp of the Arameans. If they let us live, we will live; if they kill us, we will die.”'),
('2KI', 7, 5, '2KI.7.5', 'So they arose at twilight and went to the camp of the Arameans. But when they came to the outskirts of the camp, there was not a man to be found.'),
('2KI', 7, 6, '2KI.7.6', 'For the Lord had caused the Arameans to hear the sound of chariots, horses, and a great army, so that they said to one another, “Look, the king of Israel must have hired the kings of the Hittites and Egyptians to attack us.”'),
('2KI', 7, 7, '2KI.7.7', 'Thus the Arameans had arisen and fled at twilight, abandoning their tents and horses and donkeys. The camp was intact, and they had run for their lives.'),
('2KI', 7, 8, '2KI.7.8', 'When the lepers reached the edge of the camp, they went into a tent to eat and drink. Then they carried off the silver, gold, and clothing, and went and hid them. On returning, they entered another tent, carried off some items from there, and hid them.'),
('2KI', 7, 9, '2KI.7.9', 'Finally, they said to one another, “We are not doing what is right. Today is a day of good news. If we are silent and wait until morning light, our sin will overtake us. Now, therefore, let us go and tell the king’s household.”'),
('2KI', 7, 10, '2KI.7.10', 'So they went and called out to the gatekeepers of the city, saying, “We went to the Aramean camp and no one was there—not a trace—only tethered horses and donkeys, and the tents were intact.”'),
('2KI', 7, 11, '2KI.7.11', 'The gatekeepers shouted the news, and it was reported to the king’s household.'),
('2KI', 7, 12, '2KI.7.12', 'So the king got up in the night and said to his servants, “Let me tell you what the Arameans have done to us. They know we are starving, so they have left the camp to hide in the field, thinking, ‘When they come out of the city, we will take them alive and enter the city.’”'),
('2KI', 7, 13, '2KI.7.13', 'But one of his servants replied, “Please, have scouts take five of the horses that remain in the city. Their plight will be no worse than all the Israelites who are left here. You can see that all the Israelites here are doomed. So let us send them and find out.”'),
('2KI', 7, 14, '2KI.7.14', 'Then the scouts took two chariots with horses, and the king sent them after the Aramean army, saying, “Go and see.”'),
('2KI', 7, 15, '2KI.7.15', 'And they tracked them as far as the Jordan, and indeed, the whole way was littered with the clothing and equipment the Arameans had thrown off in haste. So the scouts returned and told the king.'),
('2KI', 7, 16, '2KI.7.16', 'Then the people went out and plundered the camp of the Arameans. It was then that a seah of fine flour sold for a shekel, and two seahs of barley sold for a shekel, according to the word of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 7, 17, '2KI.7.17', 'Now the king had appointed the officer on whose arm he leaned to be in charge of the gate, but the people trampled him in the gateway, and he died, just as the man of God had foretold when the king had come to him.'),
('2KI', 7, 18, '2KI.7.18', 'It happened just as the man of God had told the king: “About this time tomorrow at the gate of Samaria, two seahs of barley will sell for a shekel, and a seah of fine flour will sell for a shekel.”'),
('2KI', 7, 19, '2KI.7.19', 'And the officer had answered the man of God, “Look, even if the LORD were to make windows in heaven, could this really happen?” So Elisha had replied, “You will see it with your own eyes, but you will not eat any of it!”'),
('2KI', 7, 20, '2KI.7.20', 'And that is just what happened to him. The people trampled him in the gateway, and he died.'),
('2KI', 8, 1, '2KI.8.1', 'Now Elisha had said to the woman whose son he had restored to life, “Arise, you and your household; go and live as a foreigner wherever you can. For the LORD has decreed that a seven-year famine will come to the land.”'),
('2KI', 8, 2, '2KI.8.2', 'So the woman had proceeded to do as the man of God had instructed. And she and her household lived as foreigners for seven years in the land of the Philistines.'),
('2KI', 8, 3, '2KI.8.3', 'At the end of seven years, when the woman returned from the land of the Philistines, she went to the king to appeal for her house and her land.'),
('2KI', 8, 4, '2KI.8.4', 'Now the king had been speaking to Gehazi, the servant of the man of God, saying, “Please relate to me all the great things Elisha has done.”'),
('2KI', 8, 5, '2KI.8.5', 'And Gehazi was telling the king how Elisha had brought the dead back to life. Just then the woman whose son Elisha had revived came to appeal to the king for her house and her land. So Gehazi said, “My lord the king, this is the woman, and this is the son Elisha restored to life.”'),
('2KI', 8, 6, '2KI.8.6', 'When the king asked the woman, she confirmed it. So the king appointed for her an officer, saying, “Restore all that was hers, along with all the proceeds of the field from the day that she left the country until now.”'),
('2KI', 8, 7, '2KI.8.7', 'Then Elisha came to Damascus while Ben-hadad king of Aram was sick, and the king was told, “The man of God has come here.”'),
('2KI', 8, 8, '2KI.8.8', 'So the king said to Hazael, “Take a gift in your hand, go to meet the man of God, and inquire of the LORD through him, ‘Will I recover from this illness?’”'),
('2KI', 8, 9, '2KI.8.9', 'So Hazael went to meet Elisha, taking with him a gift of forty camel loads of every good thing from Damascus. And he went in and stood before him and said, “Your son Ben-hadad king of Aram has sent me to ask, ‘Will I recover from this illness?’”'),
('2KI', 8, 10, '2KI.8.10', 'Elisha answered, “Go and tell him, ‘You will surely recover.’ But the LORD has shown me that in fact he will die.”'),
('2KI', 8, 11, '2KI.8.11', 'Elisha fixed his gaze steadily on him until Hazael became uncomfortable. Then the man of God began to weep.'),
('2KI', 8, 12, '2KI.8.12', '“Why is my lord weeping?” asked Hazael. “Because I know the evil you will do to the Israelites,” Elisha replied. “You will set fire to their fortresses, kill their young men with the sword, dash their little ones to pieces, and rip open their pregnant women.”'),
('2KI', 8, 13, '2KI.8.13', '“But how could your servant, a mere dog, do such a monstrous thing?” said Hazael. And Elisha answered, “The LORD has shown me that you will be king over Aram.”'),
('2KI', 8, 14, '2KI.8.14', 'So Hazael left Elisha and went to his master, who asked him, “What did Elisha say to you?” And he replied, “He told me that you would surely recover.”'),
('2KI', 8, 15, '2KI.8.15', 'But the next day Hazael took a thick cloth, dipped it in water, and spread it over the king’s face. So Ben-hadad died, and Hazael reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 8, 16, '2KI.8.16', 'In the fifth year of the reign of Joram son of Ahab over Israel, Jehoram son of Jehoshaphat succeeded his father as king of Judah.'),
('2KI', 8, 17, '2KI.8.17', 'Jehoram was thirty-two years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eight years.'),
('2KI', 8, 18, '2KI.8.18', 'And Jehoram walked in the ways of the kings of Israel, just as the house of Ahab had done. For he married a daughter of Ahab and did evil in the sight of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 8, 19, '2KI.8.19', 'Yet for the sake of His servant David, the LORD was unwilling to destroy Judah, since He had promised to maintain a lamp for David and his descendants forever.'),
('2KI', 8, 20, '2KI.8.20', 'In the days of Jehoram, Edom rebelled against the hand of Judah and appointed their own king.'),
('2KI', 8, 21, '2KI.8.21', 'So Jehoram crossed over to Zair with all his chariots. When the Edomites surrounded him and his chariot commanders, he rose up and attacked by night. His troops, however, fled to their homes.'),
('2KI', 8, 22, '2KI.8.22', 'So to this day Edom has been in rebellion against the hand of Judah. Likewise, Libnah rebelled at the same time.'),
('2KI', 8, 23, '2KI.8.23', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jehoram, along with all his accomplishments, are they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 8, 24, '2KI.8.24', 'And Jehoram rested with his fathers and was buried with them in the City of David. And his son Ahaziah reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 8, 25, '2KI.8.25', 'In the twelfth year of the reign of Joram son of Ahab over Israel, Ahaziah son of Jehoram became king of Judah.'),
('2KI', 8, 26, '2KI.8.26', 'Ahaziah was twenty-two years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem one year. His mother’s name was Athaliah, the granddaughter of Omri king of Israel.'),
('2KI', 8, 27, '2KI.8.27', 'And Ahaziah walked in the ways of the house of Ahab and did evil in the sight of the LORD like the house of Ahab, for he was a son-in-law of the house of Ahab.'),
('2KI', 8, 28, '2KI.8.28', 'Then Ahaziah went with Joram son of Ahab to fight against Hazael king of Aram at Ramoth-gilead, and the Arameans wounded Joram.'),
('2KI', 8, 29, '2KI.8.29', 'So King Joram returned to Jezreel to recover from the wounds that the Arameans had inflicted on him at Ramah when he fought against Hazael king of Aram. Then Ahaziah son of Jehoram king of Judah went down to Jezreel to visit Joram son of Ahab, because Joram had been wounded.'),
('2KI', 9, 1, '2KI.9.1', 'Now Elisha the prophet summoned one of the sons of the prophets and said to him, “Tuck your cloak under your belt, take this flask of oil, and go to Ramoth-gilead.'),
('2KI', 9, 2, '2KI.9.2', 'When you arrive, look for Jehu son of Jehoshaphat, the son of Nimshi. Go in, get him away from his companions, and take him to an inner room.'),
('2KI', 9, 3, '2KI.9.3', 'Then take the flask of oil, pour it on his head, and declare, ‘This is what the LORD says: I anoint you king over Israel.’ Then open the door and run. Do not delay!”'),
('2KI', 9, 4, '2KI.9.4', 'So the young prophet went to Ramoth-gilead,'),
('2KI', 9, 5, '2KI.9.5', 'and when he arrived, the army commanders were sitting there. “I have a message for you, commander,” he said. “For which of us?” asked Jehu. “For you, commander,” he replied.'),
('2KI', 9, 6, '2KI.9.6', 'So Jehu got up and went into the house, where the young prophet poured the oil on his head and declared, “This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘I anoint you king over the LORD’s people Israel.'),
('2KI', 9, 7, '2KI.9.7', 'And you are to strike down the house of your master Ahab, so that I may avenge the blood of My servants the prophets and the blood of all the servants of the LORD shed by the hand of Jezebel.'),
('2KI', 9, 8, '2KI.9.8', 'The whole house of Ahab will perish, and I will cut off from Ahab every male, both slave and free, in Israel.'),
('2KI', 9, 9, '2KI.9.9', 'I will make the house of Ahab like the houses of Jeroboam son of Nebat and Baasha son of Ahijah.'),
('2KI', 9, 10, '2KI.9.10', 'And on the plot of ground at Jezreel the dogs will devour Jezebel, and there will be no one to bury her.’” Then the young prophet opened the door and ran.'),
('2KI', 9, 11, '2KI.9.11', 'When Jehu went out to the servants of his master, they asked, “Is everything all right? Why did this madman come to you?” “You know his kind and their babble,” he replied.'),
('2KI', 9, 12, '2KI.9.12', '“That is a lie!” they said. “Tell us now!” So Jehu answered, “He talked to me about this and that, saying, ‘This is what the LORD says: I anoint you king over Israel.’”'),
('2KI', 9, 13, '2KI.9.13', 'Quickly, each man took his garment and put it under Jehu on the bare steps. Then they blew the ram’s horn and proclaimed, “Jehu is king!”'),
('2KI', 9, 14, '2KI.9.14', 'Thus Jehu son of Jehoshaphat, the son of Nimshi, conspired against Joram. (Now Joram and all Israel had been defending Ramoth-gilead against Hazael king of Aram,'),
('2KI', 9, 15, '2KI.9.15', 'but King Joram had returned to Jezreel to recover from the wounds he had suffered at the hands of the Arameans in the battle against Hazael their king.) So Jehu said, “If you commanders wish to make me king, then do not let anyone escape from the city to go and tell it in Jezreel.”'),
('2KI', 9, 16, '2KI.9.16', 'Then Jehu got into his chariot and went to Jezreel, because Joram was laid up there. And Ahaziah king of Judah had gone down to see him.'),
('2KI', 9, 17, '2KI.9.17', 'Now the watchman standing on the tower in Jezreel saw Jehu’s troops approaching, and he called out, “I see a company of troops!” “Choose a rider,” Joram commanded. “Send him out to meet them and ask, ‘Have you come in peace?’”'),
('2KI', 9, 18, '2KI.9.18', 'So a horseman rode off to meet Jehu and said, “This is what the king asks: ‘Have you come in peace?’” “What do you know about peace?” Jehu replied. “Fall in behind me.” And the watchman reported, “The messenger reached them, but he is not coming back.”'),
('2KI', 9, 19, '2KI.9.19', 'So the king sent out a second horseman, who went to them and said, “This is what the king asks: ‘Have you come in peace?’” “What do you know about peace?” Jehu replied. “Fall in behind me.”'),
('2KI', 9, 20, '2KI.9.20', 'Again the watchman reported, “He reached them, but he is not coming back. And the charioteer is driving like Jehu son of Nimshi—he is driving like a madman!”'),
('2KI', 9, 21, '2KI.9.21', '“Harness!” Joram shouted, and they harnessed his chariot. Then Joram king of Israel and Ahaziah king of Judah set out, each in his own chariot, and met Jehu on the property of Naboth the Jezreelite.'),
('2KI', 9, 22, '2KI.9.22', 'When Joram saw Jehu, he asked, “Have you come in peace, Jehu?” “How can there be peace,” he replied, “as long as the idolatry and witchcraft of your mother Jezebel abound?”'),
('2KI', 9, 23, '2KI.9.23', 'Joram turned around and fled, calling out to Ahaziah, “Treachery, Ahaziah!”'),
('2KI', 9, 24, '2KI.9.24', 'Then Jehu drew his bow and shot Joram between the shoulders. The arrow pierced his heart, and he slumped down in his chariot.'),
('2KI', 9, 25, '2KI.9.25', 'And Jehu said to Bidkar his officer, “Pick him up and throw him into the field of Naboth the Jezreelite. For remember that when you and I were riding together behind his father Ahab, the LORD lifted up this burden against him:'),
('2KI', 9, 26, '2KI.9.26', '‘As surely as I saw the blood of Naboth and the blood of his sons yesterday, declares the LORD, so will I repay you on this plot of ground, declares the LORD.’ Now then, according to the word of the LORD, pick him up and throw him on the plot of ground.”'),
('2KI', 9, 27, '2KI.9.27', 'When King Ahaziah of Judah saw this, he fled up the road toward Beth-haggan. And Jehu pursued him, shouting, “Shoot him too!” So they shot Ahaziah in his chariot on the Ascent of Gur, near Ibleam, and he fled to Megiddo and died there.'),
('2KI', 9, 28, '2KI.9.28', 'Then his servants carried him by chariot to Jerusalem and buried him with his fathers in his tomb in the City of David.'),
('2KI', 9, 29, '2KI.9.29', '(In the eleventh year of Joram son of Ahab, Ahaziah had become king over Judah.)'),
('2KI', 9, 30, '2KI.9.30', 'Now when Jehu arrived in Jezreel, Jezebel heard of it. So she painted her eyes, adorned her head, and looked down from a window.'),
('2KI', 9, 31, '2KI.9.31', 'And as Jehu entered the gate, she asked, “Have you come in peace, O Zimri, murderer of your master?”'),
('2KI', 9, 32, '2KI.9.32', 'He looked up at the window and called out, “Who is on my side? Who?” And two or three eunuchs looked down at him.'),
('2KI', 9, 33, '2KI.9.33', '“Throw her down!” yelled Jehu. So they threw her down, and her blood splattered on the wall and on the horses as they trampled her underfoot.'),
('2KI', 9, 34, '2KI.9.34', 'Then Jehu went in and ate and drank. “Take care of this cursed woman,” he said, “and bury her, for she was the daughter of a king.”'),
('2KI', 9, 35, '2KI.9.35', 'But when they went out to bury her, they found nothing but her skull, her feet, and the palms of her hands.'),
('2KI', 9, 36, '2KI.9.36', 'So they went back and told Jehu, who replied, “This is the word of the LORD, which He spoke through His servant Elijah the Tishbite: ‘On the plot of ground at Jezreel the dogs will devour the flesh of Jezebel.'),
('2KI', 9, 37, '2KI.9.37', 'And Jezebel’s body will lie like dung in the field on the plot of ground at Jezreel, so that no one can say: This is Jezebel.’”'),
('2KI', 10, 1, '2KI.10.1', 'Now Ahab had seventy sons in Samaria. So Jehu wrote letters and sent them to Samaria to the officials of Jezreel, to the elders, and to the guardians of the sons of Ahab, saying:'),
('2KI', 10, 2, '2KI.10.2', '“When this letter arrives, since your master’s sons are with you and you have chariots and horses, a fortified city and weaponry,'),
('2KI', 10, 3, '2KI.10.3', 'select the best and most worthy son of your master, set him on his father’s throne, and fight for your master’s house.”'),
('2KI', 10, 4, '2KI.10.4', 'But they were terrified and reasoned, “If two kings could not stand against him, how can we?”'),
('2KI', 10, 5, '2KI.10.5', 'So the palace administrator, the overseer of the city, the elders, and the guardians sent a message to Jehu: “We are your servants, and we will do whatever you say. We will not make anyone king. Do whatever is good in your sight.”'),
('2KI', 10, 6, '2KI.10.6', 'Then Jehu wrote them a second letter and said: “If you are on my side, and if you will obey me, then bring the heads of your master’s sons to me at Jezreel by this time tomorrow.” Now the sons of the king, seventy in all, were being brought up by the leading men of the city.'),
('2KI', 10, 7, '2KI.10.7', 'And when the letter arrived, they took the sons of the king and slaughtered all seventy of them. They put their heads in baskets and sent them to Jehu at Jezreel.'),
('2KI', 10, 8, '2KI.10.8', 'When the messenger arrived, he told Jehu, “They have brought the heads of the sons of the king.” And Jehu ordered, “Pile them in two heaps at the entrance of the gate until morning.”'),
('2KI', 10, 9, '2KI.10.9', 'The next morning, Jehu went out and stood before all the people and said, “You are innocent. It was I who conspired against my master and killed him. But who killed all these?'),
('2KI', 10, 10, '2KI.10.10', 'Know, then, that not a word the LORD has spoken against the house of Ahab will fail, for the LORD has done what He promised through His servant Elijah.”'),
('2KI', 10, 11, '2KI.10.11', 'So Jehu killed everyone in Jezreel who remained of the house of Ahab, as well as all his great men and close friends and priests, leaving him without a single survivor.'),
('2KI', 10, 12, '2KI.10.12', 'Then Jehu set out toward Samaria. At Beth-eked of the Shepherds,'),
('2KI', 10, 13, '2KI.10.13', 'Jehu met some relatives of Ahaziah king of Judah and asked, “Who are you?” “We are relatives of Ahaziah,” they answered, “and we have come down to greet the sons of the king and of the queen mother.”'),
('2KI', 10, 14, '2KI.10.14', 'Then Jehu ordered, “Take them alive.” So his men took them alive, then slaughtered them at the well of Beth-eked—forty-two men. He spared none of them.'),
('2KI', 10, 15, '2KI.10.15', 'When he left there, he found Jehonadab son of Rechab, who was coming to meet him. Jehu greeted him and asked, “Is your heart as true to mine as my heart is to yours?” “It is!” Jehonadab replied. “If it is,” said Jehu, “give me your hand.” So he gave him his hand, and Jehu helped him into his chariot,'),
('2KI', 10, 16, '2KI.10.16', 'saying, “Come with me and see my zeal for the LORD!” So he had him ride in his chariot.'),
('2KI', 10, 17, '2KI.10.17', 'When Jehu came to Samaria, he struck down everyone belonging to Ahab who remained there, until he had destroyed them, according to the word that the LORD had spoken to Elijah.'),
('2KI', 10, 18, '2KI.10.18', 'Then Jehu brought all the people together and said, “Ahab served Baal a little, but Jehu will serve him a lot.'),
('2KI', 10, 19, '2KI.10.19', 'Now, therefore, summon to me all the prophets of Baal, all his servants, and all his priests. See that no one is missing, for I have a great sacrifice for Baal. Whoever is missing will not live.” But Jehu was acting deceptively in order to destroy the servants of Baal.'),
('2KI', 10, 20, '2KI.10.20', 'And Jehu commanded, “Proclaim a solemn assembly for Baal.” So they announced it.'),
('2KI', 10, 21, '2KI.10.21', 'Then Jehu sent word throughout Israel, and all the servants of Baal came; there was not a man who failed to show. They entered the temple of Baal, and it was filled from end to end.'),
('2KI', 10, 22, '2KI.10.22', 'And Jehu said to the keeper of the wardrobe, “Bring out garments for all the servants of Baal.” So he brought out garments for them.'),
('2KI', 10, 23, '2KI.10.23', 'Next, Jehu and Jehonadab son of Rechab entered the temple of Baal, and Jehu said to the servants of Baal, “Look around to see that there are no servants of the LORD here among you—only servants of Baal.”'),
('2KI', 10, 24, '2KI.10.24', 'And they went in to offer sacrifices and burnt offerings. Now Jehu had stationed eighty men outside and warned them, “If anyone allows one of the men I am delivering into your hands to escape, he will forfeit his life for theirs.”'),
('2KI', 10, 25, '2KI.10.25', 'When he had finished making the burnt offering, Jehu said to the guards and officers, “Go in and kill them. Do not let anyone out.” So the guards and officers put them to the sword, threw the bodies out, and went into the inner room of the temple of Baal.'),
('2KI', 10, 26, '2KI.10.26', 'They brought out the sacred pillar of the temple of Baal and burned it.'),
('2KI', 10, 27, '2KI.10.27', 'They also demolished the sacred pillar of Baal. Then they tore down the temple of Baal and made it into a latrine, which it is to this day.'),
('2KI', 10, 28, '2KI.10.28', 'Thus Jehu eradicated Baal from Israel,'),
('2KI', 10, 29, '2KI.10.29', 'but he did not turn away from the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit—the worship of the golden calves at Bethel and Dan.'),
('2KI', 10, 30, '2KI.10.30', 'Nevertheless, the LORD said to Jehu, “Because you have done well in carrying out what is right in My sight and have done to the house of Ahab all that was in My heart, four generations of your sons will sit on the throne of Israel.”'),
('2KI', 10, 31, '2KI.10.31', 'Yet Jehu was not careful to follow the instruction of the LORD, the God of Israel, with all his heart. He did not turn away from the sins that Jeroboam had caused Israel to commit.'),
('2KI', 10, 32, '2KI.10.32', 'In those days the LORD began to reduce the size of Israel. Hazael defeated the Israelites throughout their territory'),
('2KI', 10, 33, '2KI.10.33', 'from the Jordan eastward through all the land of Gilead (the region of Gad, Reuben, and Manasseh), and from Aroer by the Arnon Valley through Gilead to Bashan.'),
('2KI', 10, 34, '2KI.10.34', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jehu, along with all his accomplishments and all his might, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 10, 35, '2KI.10.35', 'And Jehu rested with his fathers and was buried in Samaria, and his son Jehoahaz reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 10, 36, '2KI.10.36', 'So the duration of Jehu’s reign over Israel in Samaria was twenty-eight years.'),
('2KI', 11, 1, '2KI.11.1', 'When Athaliah the mother of Ahaziah saw that her son was dead, she proceeded to annihilate all the royal heirs.'),
('2KI', 11, 2, '2KI.11.2', 'But Jehosheba daughter of King Joram, the sister of Ahaziah, took Joash son of Ahaziah and stole him away from among the sons of the king who were being murdered. She put him and his nurse in a bedroom to hide him from Athaliah, and he was not killed.'),
('2KI', 11, 3, '2KI.11.3', 'And Joash remained hidden with his nurse in the house of the LORD for six years while Athaliah ruled the land.'),
('2KI', 11, 4, '2KI.11.4', 'Then in the seventh year, Jehoiada sent for the commanders of hundreds, the Carites, and the guards, and had them brought into the house of the LORD. There he made a covenant with them and put them under oath. He showed them the king’s son'),
('2KI', 11, 5, '2KI.11.5', 'and commanded them, “This is what you are to do: A third of you who come on duty on the Sabbath shall guard the royal palace,'),
('2KI', 11, 6, '2KI.11.6', 'a third shall be at the gate of Sur, and a third at the gate behind the guards. You are to take turns guarding the temple—'),
('2KI', 11, 7, '2KI.11.7', 'the two divisions that would go off duty on the Sabbath are to guard the house of the LORD for the king.'),
('2KI', 11, 8, '2KI.11.8', 'You must surround the king with weapons in hand, and anyone who approaches the ranks must be put to death. You must stay close to the king wherever he goes.”'),
('2KI', 11, 9, '2KI.11.9', 'So the commanders of hundreds did everything that Jehoiada the priest had ordered. Each of them took his men—those coming on duty on the Sabbath and those going off duty—and came to Jehoiada the priest.'),
('2KI', 11, 10, '2KI.11.10', 'Then the priest gave to the commanders of hundreds the spears and shields of King David from the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 11, 11, '2KI.11.11', 'And the guards stood with weapons in hand surrounding the king by the altar and the temple, from the south side to the north side of the temple.'),
('2KI', 11, 12, '2KI.11.12', 'Then Jehoiada brought out the king’s son, put the crown on him, presented him with the Testimony, and proclaimed him king. They anointed him, and the people clapped their hands and declared, “Long live the king!”'),
('2KI', 11, 13, '2KI.11.13', 'When Athaliah heard the noise from the guards and the people, she went out to the people in the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 11, 14, '2KI.11.14', 'And she looked out and saw the king standing by the pillar, according to the custom. The officers and trumpeters were beside the king, and all the people of the land were rejoicing and blowing trumpets. Then Athaliah tore her clothes and screamed, “Treason! Treason!”'),
('2KI', 11, 15, '2KI.11.15', 'And Jehoiada the priest ordered the commanders of hundreds in charge of the army, “Bring her out between the ranks, and put to the sword anyone who follows her.” For the priest had said, “She must not be put to death in the house of the LORD.”'),
('2KI', 11, 16, '2KI.11.16', 'So they seized Athaliah as she reached the horses’ entrance to the palace grounds, and there she was put to death.'),
('2KI', 11, 17, '2KI.11.17', 'Then Jehoiada made a covenant between the LORD and the king and the people that they would be the LORD’s people. He also made a covenant between the king and the people.'),
('2KI', 11, 18, '2KI.11.18', 'So all the people of the land went to the temple of Baal and tore it down. They smashed the altars and idols to pieces, and they killed Mattan the priest of Baal in front of the altars. And Jehoiada the priest posted guards for the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 11, 19, '2KI.11.19', 'He took with him the commanders of hundreds, the Carites, the guards, and all the people of the land, and they brought the king down from the house of the LORD and entered the royal palace by way of the Gate of the Guards. Then Joash took his seat on the royal throne,'),
('2KI', 11, 20, '2KI.11.20', 'and all the people of the land rejoiced. And the city was quiet, because Athaliah had been put to the sword at the royal palace.'),
('2KI', 11, 21, '2KI.11.21', 'Joash was seven years old when he became king.'),
('2KI', 12, 1, '2KI.12.1', 'In the seventh year of Jehu, Joash became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem forty years. His mother’s name was Zibiah; she was from Beersheba.'),
('2KI', 12, 2, '2KI.12.2', 'And Joash did what was right in the eyes of the LORD all the days he was instructed by Jehoiada the priest.'),
('2KI', 12, 3, '2KI.12.3', 'Nevertheless, the high places were not removed; the people continued sacrificing and burning incense there.'),
('2KI', 12, 4, '2KI.12.4', 'Then Joash said to the priests, “Collect all the money brought as sacred gifts into the house of the LORD—the census money, the money from vows, and the money brought voluntarily into the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 12, 5, '2KI.12.5', 'Let every priest receive it from his constituency, and let it be used to repair any damage found in the temple.”'),
('2KI', 12, 6, '2KI.12.6', 'By the twenty-third year of the reign of Joash, however, the priests had not yet repaired the damage to the temple.'),
('2KI', 12, 7, '2KI.12.7', 'So King Joash called Jehoiada and the other priests and said, “Why have you not repaired the damage to the temple? Now, therefore, take no more money from your constituency, but hand it over for the repair of the temple.”'),
('2KI', 12, 8, '2KI.12.8', 'So the priests agreed that they would not receive money from the people and that they would not repair the temple themselves.'),
('2KI', 12, 9, '2KI.12.9', 'Then Jehoiada the priest took a chest, bored a hole in its lid, and set it beside the altar on the right side as one enters the house of the LORD. There the priests who guarded the threshold put all the money brought into the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 12, 10, '2KI.12.10', 'Whenever they saw that there was a large amount of money in the chest, the royal scribe and the high priest would go up, count the money brought into the house of the LORD, and tie it up in bags.'),
('2KI', 12, 11, '2KI.12.11', 'Then they would put the counted money into the hands of those who supervised the work on the house of the LORD, who in turn would pay those doing the work—the carpenters, builders,'),
('2KI', 12, 12, '2KI.12.12', 'masons, and stonecutters. They also purchased timber and dressed stone to repair the damage to the house of the LORD, and they paid the other expenses of the temple repairs.'),
('2KI', 12, 13, '2KI.12.13', 'However, the money brought into the house of the LORD was not used for making silver basins, wick trimmers, sprinkling bowls, trumpets, or any articles of gold or silver for the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 12, 14, '2KI.12.14', 'Instead, it was paid to those doing the work, and with it they repaired the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 12, 15, '2KI.12.15', 'No accounting was required from the men who received the money to pay the workmen, because they acted with integrity.'),
('2KI', 12, 16, '2KI.12.16', 'The money from the guilt offerings and sin offerings was not brought into the house of the LORD; it belonged to the priests.'),
('2KI', 12, 17, '2KI.12.17', 'At that time Hazael king of Aram marched up and fought against Gath and captured it. Then he decided to attack Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 12, 18, '2KI.12.18', 'So King Joash of Judah took all the sacred objects dedicated by his fathers—Jehoshaphat, Jehoram, and Ahaziah, the kings of Judah—along with his own consecrated items and all the gold found in the treasuries of the house of the LORD and the royal palace, and he sent them to Hazael king of Aram. So Hazael withdrew from Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 12, 19, '2KI.12.19', 'As for the rest of the acts of Joash, along with all his accomplishments, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 12, 20, '2KI.12.20', 'And the servants of Joash rose up and formed a conspiracy and killed him at Beth-millo, on the road down to Silla.'),
('2KI', 12, 21, '2KI.12.21', 'His servants Jozabad son of Shimeath and Jehozabad son of Shomer struck him down, and he died. And they buried him with his fathers in the City of David, and his son Amaziah reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 13, 1, '2KI.13.1', 'In the twenty-third year of the reign of Joash son of Ahaziah over Judah, Jehoahaz son of Jehu became king of Israel, and he reigned in Samaria seventeen years.'),
('2KI', 13, 2, '2KI.13.2', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD and followed the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit; he did not turn away from them.'),
('2KI', 13, 3, '2KI.13.3', 'So the anger of the LORD burned against Israel, and He delivered them continually into the hands of Hazael king of Aram and his son Ben-hadad.'),
('2KI', 13, 4, '2KI.13.4', 'Then Jehoahaz sought the favor of the LORD, and the LORD listened to him because He saw the oppression that the king of Aram had inflicted on Israel.'),
('2KI', 13, 5, '2KI.13.5', 'So the LORD gave Israel a deliverer, and they escaped the power of the Arameans. Then the people of Israel lived in their own homes as they had before.'),
('2KI', 13, 6, '2KI.13.6', 'Nevertheless, they did not turn away from the sins that the house of Jeroboam had caused Israel to commit, but they continued to walk in them. The Asherah pole even remained standing in Samaria.'),
('2KI', 13, 7, '2KI.13.7', 'Jehoahaz had no army left, except fifty horsemen, ten chariots, and ten thousand foot soldiers, because the king of Aram had destroyed them and made them like the dust at threshing.'),
('2KI', 13, 8, '2KI.13.8', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jehoahaz, along with all his accomplishments and his might, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 13, 9, '2KI.13.9', 'And Jehoahaz rested with his fathers and was buried in Samaria. And his son Jehoash reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 13, 10, '2KI.13.10', 'In the thirty-seventh year of the reign of Joash over Judah, Jehoash son of Jehoahaz became king of Israel in Samaria, and he reigned sixteen years.'),
('2KI', 13, 11, '2KI.13.11', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD and did not turn away from all the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit, but he walked in them.'),
('2KI', 13, 12, '2KI.13.12', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jehoash, along with all his accomplishments and his might, including his war against Amaziah king of Judah, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 13, 13, '2KI.13.13', 'And Jehoash rested with his fathers, and Jeroboam succeeded him on the throne. Jehoash was buried in Samaria with the kings of Israel.'),
('2KI', 13, 14, '2KI.13.14', 'When Elisha had fallen sick with the illness from which he would die, Jehoash king of Israel came down to him and wept over him, saying, “My father, my father, the chariots and horsemen of Israel!”'),
('2KI', 13, 15, '2KI.13.15', 'Elisha told him, “Take a bow and some arrows.” So Jehoash took a bow and some arrows.'),
('2KI', 13, 16, '2KI.13.16', 'Then Elisha said to the king of Israel, “Put your hand on the bow.” So the king put his hand on the bow, and Elisha put his hands on the king’s hands.'),
('2KI', 13, 17, '2KI.13.17', '“Open the east window,” said Elisha. So he opened it and Elisha said, “Shoot!” So he shot. And Elisha declared: “This is the LORD’s arrow of victory, the arrow of victory over Aram, for you shall strike the Arameans in Aphek until you have put an end to them.”'),
('2KI', 13, 18, '2KI.13.18', 'Then Elisha said, “Take the arrows!” So he took them, and Elisha said to the king of Israel, “Strike the ground!” So he struck the ground three times and stopped.'),
('2KI', 13, 19, '2KI.13.19', 'But the man of God was angry with him and said, “You should have struck the ground five or six times. Then you would have struck down Aram until you had put an end to it. But now you will strike down Aram only three times.”'),
('2KI', 13, 20, '2KI.13.20', 'And Elisha died and was buried. Now the Moabite raiders used to come into the land every spring.'),
('2KI', 13, 21, '2KI.13.21', 'Once, as the Israelites were burying a man, suddenly they saw a band of raiders, so they threw the man’s body into Elisha’s tomb. And as soon as his body touched the bones of Elisha, the man was revived and stood up on his feet.'),
('2KI', 13, 22, '2KI.13.22', 'And Hazael king of Aram oppressed Israel throughout the reign of Jehoahaz.'),
('2KI', 13, 23, '2KI.13.23', 'But the LORD was gracious to Israel and had compassion on them, and He turned toward them because of His covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. And to this day, the LORD has been unwilling to destroy them or cast them from His presence.'),
('2KI', 13, 24, '2KI.13.24', 'When Hazael king of Aram died, his son Ben-hadad reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 13, 25, '2KI.13.25', 'Then Jehoash son of Jehoahaz took back from Ben-hadad son of Hazael the cities that Hazael had taken in battle from his father Jehoahaz. Jehoash defeated Ben-hadad three times, and so recovered the cities of Israel.'),
('2KI', 14, 1, '2KI.14.1', 'In the second year of the reign of Jehoash son of Jehoahaz over Israel, Amaziah son of Joash became king of Judah.'),
('2KI', 14, 2, '2KI.14.2', 'He was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem twenty-nine years. His mother’s name was Jehoaddan; she was from Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 14, 3, '2KI.14.3', 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, but not as his father David had done. He did everything as his father Joash had done.'),
('2KI', 14, 4, '2KI.14.4', 'Nevertheless, the high places were not taken away, and the people continued sacrificing and burning incense on the high places.'),
('2KI', 14, 5, '2KI.14.5', 'As soon as the kingdom was firmly in his grasp, Amaziah executed the servants who had murdered his father the king.'),
('2KI', 14, 6, '2KI.14.6', 'Yet he did not put the sons of the murderers to death, but acted according to what is written in the Book of the Law of Moses, where the LORD commanded: “Fathers must not be put to death for their children, and children must not be put to death for their fathers; each is to die for his own sin.”'),
('2KI', 14, 7, '2KI.14.7', 'Amaziah struck down 10,000 Edomites in the Valley of Salt. He took Sela in battle and called it Joktheel, which is its name to this very day.'),
('2KI', 14, 8, '2KI.14.8', 'Then Amaziah sent messengers to the king of Israel Jehoash son of Jehoahaz, the son of Jehu. “Come, let us meet face to face,” he said.'),
('2KI', 14, 9, '2KI.14.9', 'But Jehoash king of Israel replied to Amaziah king of Judah: “A thistle in Lebanon sent a message to a cedar in Lebanon, saying, ‘Give your daughter to my son in marriage.’ Then a wild beast in Lebanon came along and trampled the thistle.'),
('2KI', 14, 10, '2KI.14.10', 'You have indeed defeated Edom, and your heart has become proud. Glory in that and stay at home. Why should you stir up trouble so that you fall—you and Judah with you?”'),
('2KI', 14, 11, '2KI.14.11', 'But Amaziah would not listen, so Jehoash king of Israel advanced. He and King Amaziah of Judah faced each other at Beth-shemesh in Judah.'),
('2KI', 14, 12, '2KI.14.12', 'And Judah was routed before Israel, and every man fled to his home.'),
('2KI', 14, 13, '2KI.14.13', 'There at Beth-shemesh, Jehoash king of Israel captured Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Joash, the son of Ahaziah. Then Jehoash went to Jerusalem and broke down the wall of Jerusalem from the Ephraim Gate to the Corner Gate—a section of four hundred cubits.'),
('2KI', 14, 14, '2KI.14.14', 'He took all the gold and silver and all the articles found in the house of the LORD and in the treasuries of the royal palace, as well as some hostages. Then he returned to Samaria.'),
('2KI', 14, 15, '2KI.14.15', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jehoash, along with his accomplishments, his might, and how he waged war against Amaziah king of Judah, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 14, 16, '2KI.14.16', 'And Jehoash rested with his fathers and was buried in Samaria with the kings of Israel. And his son Jeroboam reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 14, 17, '2KI.14.17', 'Amaziah son of Joash king of Judah lived for fifteen years after the death of Jehoash son of Jehoahaz king of Israel.'),
('2KI', 14, 18, '2KI.14.18', 'As for the rest of the acts of Amaziah, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 14, 19, '2KI.14.19', 'And conspirators plotted against Amaziah in Jerusalem, and he fled to Lachish. But men were sent after him to Lachish, and they killed him there.'),
('2KI', 14, 20, '2KI.14.20', 'They carried him back on horses and buried him in Jerusalem with his fathers in the City of David.'),
('2KI', 14, 21, '2KI.14.21', 'Then all the people of Judah took Azariah, who was sixteen years old, and made him king in place of his father Amaziah.'),
('2KI', 14, 22, '2KI.14.22', 'Azariah was the one who rebuilt Elath and restored it to Judah after King Amaziah rested with his fathers.'),
('2KI', 14, 23, '2KI.14.23', 'In the fifteenth year of the reign of Amaziah son of Joash over Judah, Jeroboam son of Jehoash became king of Israel, and he reigned in Samaria forty-one years.'),
('2KI', 14, 24, '2KI.14.24', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD and did not turn away from all the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit.'),
('2KI', 14, 25, '2KI.14.25', 'This Jeroboam restored the boundary of Israel from Lebo-hamath to the Sea of the Arabah, according to the word that the LORD, the God of Israel, had spoken through His servant Jonah son of Amittai, the prophet from Gath-hepher.'),
('2KI', 14, 26, '2KI.14.26', 'For the LORD saw that the affliction of the Israelites, both slave and free, was very bitter. There was no one to help Israel,'),
('2KI', 14, 27, '2KI.14.27', 'and since the LORD had said that He would not blot out the name of Israel from under heaven, He saved them by the hand of Jeroboam son of Jehoash.'),
('2KI', 14, 28, '2KI.14.28', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jeroboam, along with all his accomplishments and might, and how he waged war and recovered both Damascus and Hamath for Israel from Judah, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 14, 29, '2KI.14.29', 'And Jeroboam rested with his fathers, the kings of Israel. And his son Zechariah reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 1, '2KI.15.1', 'In the twenty-seventh year of Jeroboam’s reign over Israel, Azariah son of Amaziah became king of Judah.'),
('2KI', 15, 2, '2KI.15.2', 'He was sixteen years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem fifty-two years. His mother’s name was Jecoliah; she was from Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 15, 3, '2KI.15.3', 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, just as his father Amaziah had done.'),
('2KI', 15, 4, '2KI.15.4', 'Nevertheless, the high places were not taken away; the people continued sacrificing and burning incense there.'),
('2KI', 15, 5, '2KI.15.5', 'And the LORD afflicted the king with leprosy until the day he died, so that he lived in a separate house while his son Jotham had charge of the palace and governed the people of the land.'),
('2KI', 15, 6, '2KI.15.6', 'As for the rest of the acts of Azariah, along with all his accomplishments, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 15, 7, '2KI.15.7', 'And Azariah rested with his fathers and was buried near them in the City of David. And his son Jotham reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 8, '2KI.15.8', 'In the thirty-eighth year of Azariah’s reign over Judah, Zechariah son of Jeroboam became king of Israel, and he reigned in Samaria six months.'),
('2KI', 15, 9, '2KI.15.9', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, as his fathers had done. He did not turn away from the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit.'),
('2KI', 15, 10, '2KI.15.10', 'Then Shallum son of Jabesh conspired against Zechariah, struck him down and killed him in front of the people, and reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 11, '2KI.15.11', 'As for the rest of the acts of Zechariah, they are indeed written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.'),
('2KI', 15, 12, '2KI.15.12', 'So the word of the LORD spoken to Jehu was fulfilled: “Four generations of your sons will sit on the throne of Israel.”'),
('2KI', 15, 13, '2KI.15.13', 'In the thirty-ninth year of Uzziah’s reign over Judah, Shallum son of Jabesh became king, and he reigned in Samaria one full month.'),
('2KI', 15, 14, '2KI.15.14', 'Then Menahem son of Gadi went up from Tirzah to Samaria, struck down and killed Shallum son of Jabesh, and reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 15, '2KI.15.15', 'As for the rest of the acts of Shallum, along with the conspiracy he led, they are indeed written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.'),
('2KI', 15, 16, '2KI.15.16', 'At that time Menahem, starting from Tirzah, attacked Tiphsah and everyone in its vicinity, because they would not open their gates. So he attacked Tiphsah and ripped open all the pregnant women.'),
('2KI', 15, 17, '2KI.15.17', 'In the thirty-ninth year of Azariah’s reign over Judah, Menahem son of Gadi became king of Israel, and he reigned in Samaria ten years.'),
('2KI', 15, 18, '2KI.15.18', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, and throughout his reign he did not turn away from the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit.'),
('2KI', 15, 19, '2KI.15.19', 'Then Pul king of Assyria invaded the land, and Menahem gave Pul a thousand talents of silver in order to gain his support and strengthen his own grip on the kingdom.'),
('2KI', 15, 20, '2KI.15.20', 'Menahem exacted this money from each of the wealthy men of Israel—fifty shekels of silver from each man—to give to the king of Assyria. So the king of Assyria withdrew and did not remain in the land.'),
('2KI', 15, 21, '2KI.15.21', 'As for the rest of the acts of Menahem, along with all his accomplishments, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?'),
('2KI', 15, 22, '2KI.15.22', 'And Menahem rested with his fathers, and his son Pekahiah reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 23, '2KI.15.23', 'In the fiftieth year of Azariah’s reign over Judah, Pekahiah son of Menahem became king of Israel and reigned in Samaria two years.'),
('2KI', 15, 24, '2KI.15.24', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD and did not turn away from the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit.'),
('2KI', 15, 25, '2KI.15.25', 'Then his officer, Pekah son of Remaliah, conspired against him along with Argob, Arieh, and fifty men of Gilead. And at the citadel of the king’s palace in Samaria, Pekah struck down and killed Pekahiah and reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 26, '2KI.15.26', 'As for the rest of the acts of Pekahiah, along with all his accomplishments, they are indeed written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.'),
('2KI', 15, 27, '2KI.15.27', 'In the fifty-second year of Azariah’s reign over Judah, Pekah son of Remaliah became king of Israel, and he reigned in Samaria twenty years.'),
('2KI', 15, 28, '2KI.15.28', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD and did not turn away from the sins that Jeroboam son of Nebat had caused Israel to commit.'),
('2KI', 15, 29, '2KI.15.29', 'In the days of Pekah king of Israel, Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria came and captured Ijon, Abel-beth-maacah, Janoah, Kedesh, Hazor, Gilead, and Galilee, including all the land of Naphtali, and he took the people as captives to Assyria.'),
('2KI', 15, 30, '2KI.15.30', 'Then Hoshea son of Elah led a conspiracy against Pekah son of Remaliah. In the twentieth year of Jotham son of Uzziah, Hoshea attacked Pekah, killed him, and reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 15, 31, '2KI.15.31', 'As for the rest of the acts of Pekah, along with all his accomplishments, they are indeed written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.'),
('2KI', 15, 32, '2KI.15.32', 'In the second year of the reign of Pekah son of Remaliah over Israel, Jotham son of Uzziah became king of Judah.'),
('2KI', 15, 33, '2KI.15.33', 'He was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem sixteen years. His mother’s name was Jerusha daughter of Zadok.'),
('2KI', 15, 34, '2KI.15.34', 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, just as his father Uzziah had done.'),
('2KI', 15, 35, '2KI.15.35', 'Nevertheless, the high places were not taken away; the people continued sacrificing and burning incense there. Jotham rebuilt the Upper Gate of the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 15, 36, '2KI.15.36', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jotham, along with his accomplishments, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 15, 37, '2KI.15.37', '(In those days the LORD began to send Rezin king of Aram and Pekah son of Remaliah against Judah.)'),
('2KI', 15, 38, '2KI.15.38', 'And Jotham rested with his fathers and was buried with them in the City of David his father. And his son Ahaz reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 16, 1, '2KI.16.1', 'In the seventeenth year of Pekah son of Remaliah, Ahaz son of Jotham became king of Judah.'),
('2KI', 16, 2, '2KI.16.2', 'Ahaz was twenty years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem sixteen years. And unlike David his father, he did not do what was right in the eyes of the LORD his God.'),
('2KI', 16, 3, '2KI.16.3', 'Instead, he walked in the ways of the kings of Israel and even sacrificed his son in the fire, according to the abominations of the nations that the LORD had driven out before the Israelites.'),
('2KI', 16, 4, '2KI.16.4', 'And he sacrificed and burned incense on the high places, on the hills, and under every green tree.'),
('2KI', 16, 5, '2KI.16.5', 'Then Rezin king of Aram and Pekah son of Remaliah king of Israel came up to wage war against Jerusalem. They besieged Ahaz but could not overcome him.'),
('2KI', 16, 6, '2KI.16.6', 'At that time Rezin king of Aram recovered Elath for Aram, drove out the men of Judah, and sent the Edomites into Elath, where they live to this day.'),
('2KI', 16, 7, '2KI.16.7', 'So Ahaz sent messengers to Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria, saying, “I am your servant and your son. Come up and save me from the hands of the kings of Aram and Israel, who are rising up against me.”'),
('2KI', 16, 8, '2KI.16.8', 'Ahaz also took the silver and gold found in the house of the LORD and in the treasuries of the king’s palace, and he sent it as a gift to the king of Assyria.'),
('2KI', 16, 9, '2KI.16.9', 'So the king of Assyria responded to him, marched up to Damascus, and captured it. He took its people to Kir as captives and put Rezin to death.'),
('2KI', 16, 10, '2KI.16.10', 'Then King Ahaz went to Damascus to meet Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria. On seeing the altar in Damascus, King Ahaz sent Uriah the priest a model of the altar and complete plans for its construction.'),
('2KI', 16, 11, '2KI.16.11', 'And Uriah the priest built the altar according to all the instructions King Ahaz had sent from Damascus, and he completed it before King Ahaz returned.'),
('2KI', 16, 12, '2KI.16.12', 'When the king came back from Damascus and saw the altar, he approached it and presented offerings on it.'),
('2KI', 16, 13, '2KI.16.13', 'He offered his burnt offering and his grain offering, poured out his drink offering, and splattered the blood of his peace offerings on the altar.'),
('2KI', 16, 14, '2KI.16.14', 'He also took the bronze altar that stood before the LORD from the front of the temple (between the new altar and the house of the LORD) and he put it on the north side of the new altar.'),
('2KI', 16, 15, '2KI.16.15', 'Then King Ahaz commanded Uriah the priest, “Offer on the great altar the morning burnt offering, the evening grain offering, and the king’s burnt offering and grain offering, as well as the burnt offerings, grain offerings, and drink offerings of all the people of the land. Splatter on the altar all the blood of the burnt offerings and sacrifices. But I will use the bronze altar to seek guidance.”'),
('2KI', 16, 16, '2KI.16.16', 'So Uriah the priest did just as King Ahaz had commanded.'),
('2KI', 16, 17, '2KI.16.17', 'King Ahaz also cut off the frames of the movable stands and removed the bronze basin from each of them. He took down the Sea from the bronze oxen that were under it and put it on a stone base.'),
('2KI', 16, 18, '2KI.16.18', 'And on account of the king of Assyria, he removed the Sabbath canopy they had built in the temple and closed the royal entryway outside the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 16, 19, '2KI.16.19', 'As for the rest of the acts of Ahaz, along with his accomplishments, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 16, 20, '2KI.16.20', 'And Ahaz rested with his fathers and was buried with them in the City of David, and his son Hezekiah reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 17, 1, '2KI.17.1', 'In the twelfth year of the reign of Ahaz over Judah, Hoshea son of Elah became king of Israel, and he reigned in Samaria nine years.'),
('2KI', 17, 2, '2KI.17.2', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, but not like the kings of Israel who preceded him.'),
('2KI', 17, 3, '2KI.17.3', 'Shalmaneser king of Assyria attacked him, and Hoshea became his vassal and paid him tribute.'),
('2KI', 17, 4, '2KI.17.4', 'But the king of Assyria discovered that Hoshea had conspired to send envoys to King So of Egypt, and that he had not paid tribute to the king of Assyria as in previous years. Therefore the king of Assyria arrested Hoshea and put him in prison.'),
('2KI', 17, 5, '2KI.17.5', 'Then the king of Assyria invaded the whole land, marched up to Samaria, and besieged it for three years.'),
('2KI', 17, 6, '2KI.17.6', 'In the ninth year of Hoshea, the king of Assyria captured Samaria and carried away the Israelites to Assyria, where he settled them in Halah, in Gozan by the Habor River, and in the cities of the Medes.'),
('2KI', 17, 7, '2KI.17.7', 'All this happened because the people of Israel had sinned against the LORD their God, who had brought them out of the land of Egypt from under the hand of Pharaoh king of Egypt. They had worshiped other gods'),
('2KI', 17, 8, '2KI.17.8', 'and walked in the customs of the nations that the LORD had driven out before the Israelites, as well as in the practices introduced by the kings of Israel.'),
('2KI', 17, 9, '2KI.17.9', 'The Israelites secretly did things against the LORD their God that were not right. From watchtower to fortified city, they built high places in all their cities.'),
('2KI', 17, 10, '2KI.17.10', 'They set up for themselves sacred pillars and Asherah poles on every high hill and under every green tree.'),
('2KI', 17, 11, '2KI.17.11', 'They burned incense on all the high places like the nations that the LORD had driven out before them. They did wicked things, provoking the LORD to anger.'),
('2KI', 17, 12, '2KI.17.12', 'They served idols, although the LORD had told them, “You shall not do this thing.”'),
('2KI', 17, 13, '2KI.17.13', 'Yet through all His prophets and seers, the LORD warned Israel and Judah, saying, “Turn from your wicked ways and keep My commandments and statutes, according to the entire Law that I commanded your fathers and delivered to you through My servants the prophets.”'),
('2KI', 17, 14, '2KI.17.14', 'But they would not listen, and they stiffened their necks like their fathers, who did not believe the LORD their God.'),
('2KI', 17, 15, '2KI.17.15', 'They rejected His statutes and the covenant He had made with their fathers, as well as the decrees He had given them. They pursued worthless idols and became worthless themselves, going after the surrounding nations that the LORD had commanded them not to imitate.'),
('2KI', 17, 16, '2KI.17.16', 'They abandoned all the commandments of the LORD their God and made for themselves two cast idols of calves and an Asherah pole. They bowed down to all the host of heaven and served Baal.'),
('2KI', 17, 17, '2KI.17.17', 'They sacrificed their sons and daughters in the fire and practiced divination and soothsaying. They devoted themselves to doing evil in the sight of the LORD, provoking Him to anger.'),
('2KI', 17, 18, '2KI.17.18', 'So the LORD was very angry with Israel, and He removed them from His presence. Only the tribe of Judah remained,'),
('2KI', 17, 19, '2KI.17.19', 'and even Judah did not keep the commandments of the LORD their God, but lived according to the customs Israel had introduced.'),
('2KI', 17, 20, '2KI.17.20', 'So the LORD rejected all the descendants of Israel. He afflicted them and delivered them into the hands of plunderers, until He had banished them from His presence.'),
('2KI', 17, 21, '2KI.17.21', 'When the LORD had torn Israel away from the house of David, they made Jeroboam son of Nebat king, and Jeroboam led Israel away from following the LORD and caused them to commit a great sin.'),
('2KI', 17, 22, '2KI.17.22', 'The Israelites persisted in all the sins that Jeroboam had committed and did not turn away from them.'),
('2KI', 17, 23, '2KI.17.23', 'Finally, the LORD removed Israel from His presence, as He had declared through all His servants the prophets. So Israel was exiled from their homeland into Assyria, where they are to this day.'),
('2KI', 17, 24, '2KI.17.24', 'Then the king of Assyria brought people from Babylon, Cuthah, Avva, Hamath, and Sepharvaim and settled them in the towns of Samaria to replace the Israelites. They took possession of Samaria and lived in its towns.'),
('2KI', 17, 25, '2KI.17.25', 'Now when the settlers first lived there, they did not worship the LORD, so He sent lions among them, which killed some of them.'),
('2KI', 17, 26, '2KI.17.26', 'So they spoke to the king of Assyria, saying, “The peoples that you have removed and placed in the cities of Samaria do not know the requirements of the God of the land. Because of this, He has sent lions among them, which are indeed killing them off.”'),
('2KI', 17, 27, '2KI.17.27', 'Then the king of Assyria commanded: “Send back one of the priests you carried off from Samaria, and have him go back to live there and teach the requirements of the God of the land.”'),
('2KI', 17, 28, '2KI.17.28', 'Thus one of the priests they had carried away came and lived in Bethel, and he began to teach them how they should worship the LORD.'),
('2KI', 17, 29, '2KI.17.29', 'Nevertheless, the people of each nation continued to make their own gods in the cities where they had settled, and they set them up in the shrines that the people of Samaria had made on the high places.'),
('2KI', 17, 30, '2KI.17.30', 'The men of Babylon made Succoth-benoth, the men of Cuth made Nergal, the men of Hamath made Ashima,'),
('2KI', 17, 31, '2KI.17.31', 'the Avvites made Nibhaz and Tartak, and the Sepharvites burned their children in the fire to Adrammelech and Anammelech the gods of Sepharvaim.'),
('2KI', 17, 32, '2KI.17.32', 'So the new residents worshiped the LORD, but they also appointed for themselves priests of all sorts to serve in the shrines of the high places.'),
('2KI', 17, 33, '2KI.17.33', 'They worshiped the LORD, but they also served their own gods according to the customs of the nations from which they had been carried away.'),
('2KI', 17, 34, '2KI.17.34', 'To this day they are still practicing their former customs. None of them worship the LORD or observe the statutes, ordinances, laws, and commandments that the LORD gave the descendants of Jacob, whom He named Israel.'),
('2KI', 17, 35, '2KI.17.35', 'For the LORD had made a covenant with the Israelites and commanded them, “Do not worship other gods or bow down to them; do not serve them or sacrifice to them.'),
('2KI', 17, 36, '2KI.17.36', 'Instead, worship the LORD, who brought you out of the land of Egypt with great power and an outstretched arm. You are to bow down to Him and offer sacrifices to Him.'),
('2KI', 17, 37, '2KI.17.37', 'And you must always be careful to observe the statutes, ordinances, laws, and commandments He wrote for you. Do not worship other gods.'),
('2KI', 17, 38, '2KI.17.38', 'Do not forget the covenant I have made with you. Do not worship other gods,'),
('2KI', 17, 39, '2KI.17.39', 'but worship the LORD your God, and He will deliver you from the hands of all your enemies.”'),
('2KI', 17, 40, '2KI.17.40', 'But they would not listen, and they persisted in their former customs.'),
('2KI', 17, 41, '2KI.17.41', 'So these nations worshiped the LORD but also served their idols, and to this day their children and grandchildren continue to do as their fathers did.'),
('2KI', 18, 1, '2KI.18.1', 'In the third year of the reign of Hoshea son of Elah over Israel, Hezekiah son of Ahaz became king of Judah.'),
('2KI', 18, 2, '2KI.18.2', 'He was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem twenty-nine years. His mother’s name was Abi, the daughter of Zechariah.'),
('2KI', 18, 3, '2KI.18.3', 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, just as his father David had done.'),
('2KI', 18, 4, '2KI.18.4', 'He removed the high places, shattered the sacred pillars, and cut down the Asherah poles. He also demolished the bronze snake called Nehushtan that Moses had made, for up to that time the Israelites had burned incense to it.'),
('2KI', 18, 5, '2KI.18.5', 'Hezekiah trusted in the LORD, the God of Israel. No king of Judah was like him, either before him or after him.'),
('2KI', 18, 6, '2KI.18.6', 'He remained faithful to the LORD and did not turn from following Him; he kept the commandments that the LORD had given Moses.'),
('2KI', 18, 7, '2KI.18.7', 'And the LORD was with Hezekiah, and he prospered wherever he went. He rebelled against the king of Assyria and refused to serve him.'),
('2KI', 18, 8, '2KI.18.8', 'He defeated the Philistines as far as Gaza and its borders, from watchtower to fortified city.'),
('2KI', 18, 9, '2KI.18.9', 'In the fourth year of Hezekiah’s reign, which was the seventh year of the reign of Hoshea son of Elah over Israel, Shalmaneser king of Assyria marched against Samaria and besieged it.'),
('2KI', 18, 10, '2KI.18.10', 'And at the end of three years, the Assyrians captured it. So Samaria was captured in the sixth year of Hezekiah, which was the ninth year of Hoshea king of Israel.'),
('2KI', 18, 11, '2KI.18.11', 'The king of Assyria exiled the Israelites to Assyria and settled them in Halah, in Gozan by the Habor River, and in the cities of the Medes.'),
('2KI', 18, 12, '2KI.18.12', 'This happened because they did not listen to the voice of the LORD their God, but violated His covenant—all that Moses the servant of the LORD had commanded—and would neither listen nor obey.'),
('2KI', 18, 13, '2KI.18.13', 'In the fourteenth year of Hezekiah’s reign, Sennacherib king of Assyria attacked and captured all the fortified cities of Judah.'),
('2KI', 18, 14, '2KI.18.14', 'So Hezekiah king of Judah sent word to the king of Assyria at Lachish, saying, “I have done wrong; withdraw from me, and I will pay whatever you demand from me.” And the king of Assyria exacted from Hezekiah king of Judah three hundred talents of silver and thirty talents of gold.'),
('2KI', 18, 15, '2KI.18.15', 'Hezekiah gave him all the silver that was found in the house of the LORD and in the treasuries of the royal palace.'),
('2KI', 18, 16, '2KI.18.16', 'At that time Hezekiah stripped the gold with which he had plated the doors and doorposts of the temple of the LORD, and he gave it to the king of Assyria.'),
('2KI', 18, 17, '2KI.18.17', 'Nevertheless, the king of Assyria sent the Tartan, the Rabsaris, and the Rabshakeh, along with a great army, from Lachish to King Hezekiah at Jerusalem. They advanced up to Jerusalem and stationed themselves by the aqueduct of the upper pool, on the road to the Launderer’s Field.'),
('2KI', 18, 18, '2KI.18.18', 'Then they called for the king. And Eliakim son of Hilkiah the palace administrator, Shebnah the scribe, and Joah son of Asaph the recorder, went out to them.'),
('2KI', 18, 19, '2KI.18.19', 'The Rabshakeh said to them, “Tell Hezekiah that this is what the great king, the king of Assyria, says: What is the basis of this confidence of yours?'),
('2KI', 18, 20, '2KI.18.20', 'You claim to have a strategy and strength for war, but these are empty words. In whom are you now trusting, that you have rebelled against me?'),
('2KI', 18, 21, '2KI.18.21', 'Look now, you are trusting in Egypt, that splintered reed of a staff that will pierce the hand of anyone who leans on it. Such is Pharaoh king of Egypt to all who trust in him.'),
('2KI', 18, 22, '2KI.18.22', 'But if you say to me, ‘We trust in the LORD our God,’ is He not the One whose high places and altars Hezekiah has removed, saying to Judah and Jerusalem: ‘You must worship before this altar in Jerusalem’?'),
('2KI', 18, 23, '2KI.18.23', 'Now, therefore, make a bargain with my master, the king of Assyria. I will give you two thousand horses—if you can put riders on them!'),
('2KI', 18, 24, '2KI.18.24', 'For how can you repel a single officer among the least of my master’s servants when you depend on Egypt for chariots and horsemen?'),
('2KI', 18, 25, '2KI.18.25', 'So now, was it apart from the LORD that I have come up against this place to destroy it? The LORD Himself said to me, ‘Go up against this land and destroy it.’”'),
('2KI', 18, 26, '2KI.18.26', 'Then Eliakim son of Hilkiah, along with Shebnah and Joah, said to the Rabshakeh, “Please speak to your servants in Aramaic, since we understand it. Do not speak with us in Hebrew in the hearing of the people on the wall.”'),
('2KI', 18, 27, '2KI.18.27', 'But the Rabshakeh replied, “Has my master sent me to speak these words only to you and your master, and not to the men sitting on the wall, who are destined with you to eat their own dung and drink their own urine?”'),
('2KI', 18, 28, '2KI.18.28', 'Then the Rabshakeh stood and called out loudly in Hebrew: “Hear the word of the great king, the king of Assyria!'),
('2KI', 18, 29, '2KI.18.29', 'This is what the king says: Do not let Hezekiah deceive you; he cannot deliver you from my hand.'),
('2KI', 18, 30, '2KI.18.30', 'Do not let Hezekiah persuade you to trust in the LORD when he says, ‘The LORD will surely deliver us; this city will not be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.’'),
('2KI', 18, 31, '2KI.18.31', 'Do not listen to Hezekiah, for this is what the king of Assyria says: Make peace with me and come out to me. Then every one of you will eat from his own vine and his own fig tree and drink water from his own cistern,'),
('2KI', 18, 32, '2KI.18.32', 'until I come and take you away to a land like your own—a land of grain and new wine, a land of bread and vineyards, a land of olive trees and honey—so that you may live and not die. But do not listen to Hezekiah, for he misleads you when he says, ‘The LORD will deliver us.’'),
('2KI', 18, 33, '2KI.18.33', 'Has the god of any nation ever delivered his land from the hand of the king of Assyria?'),
('2KI', 18, 34, '2KI.18.34', 'Where are the gods of Hamath and Arpad? Where are the gods of Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivvah? Have they delivered Samaria from my hand?'),
('2KI', 18, 35, '2KI.18.35', 'Who among all the gods of these lands has delivered his land from my hand? How then can the LORD deliver Jerusalem from my hand?”'),
('2KI', 18, 36, '2KI.18.36', 'But the people remained silent and did not answer a word, for Hezekiah had commanded, “Do not answer him.”'),
('2KI', 18, 37, '2KI.18.37', 'Then Hilkiah’s son Eliakim the palace administrator, Shebna the scribe, and Asaph’s son Joah the recorder came to Hezekiah with their clothes torn, and they relayed to him the words of the Rabshakeh.'),
('2KI', 19, 1, '2KI.19.1', 'On hearing this report, King Hezekiah tore his clothes, put on sackcloth, and entered the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 19, 2, '2KI.19.2', 'And he sent Eliakim the palace administrator, Shebna the scribe, and the leading priests, all wearing sackcloth, to the prophet Isaiah son of Amoz'),
('2KI', 19, 3, '2KI.19.3', 'to tell him, “This is what Hezekiah says: Today is a day of distress, rebuke, and disgrace; for children have come to the point of birth, but there is no strength to deliver them.'),
('2KI', 19, 4, '2KI.19.4', 'Perhaps the LORD your God will hear all the words of the Rabshakeh, whom his master the king of Assyria has sent to defy the living God, and He will rebuke him for the words that the LORD your God has heard. Therefore lift up a prayer for the remnant that still survives.”'),
('2KI', 19, 5, '2KI.19.5', 'So the servants of King Hezekiah went to Isaiah,'),
('2KI', 19, 6, '2KI.19.6', 'who replied, “Tell your master that this is what the LORD says: ‘Do not be afraid of the words you have heard, with which the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed Me.'),
('2KI', 19, 7, '2KI.19.7', 'Behold, I will put a spirit in him so that he will hear a rumor and return to his own land, where I will cause him to fall by the sword.’”'),
('2KI', 19, 8, '2KI.19.8', 'When the Rabshakeh heard that the king of Assyria had left Lachish, he withdrew and found the king fighting against Libnah.'),
('2KI', 19, 9, '2KI.19.9', 'Now Sennacherib had been warned about Tirhakah king of Cush: “Look, he has set out to fight against you.” So Sennacherib again sent messengers to Hezekiah, saying,'),
('2KI', 19, 10, '2KI.19.10', '“Give this message to Hezekiah king of Judah: ‘Do not let your God, in whom you trust, deceive you by saying that Jerusalem will not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria.'),
('2KI', 19, 11, '2KI.19.11', 'Surely you have heard what the kings of Assyria have done to all the other countries, devoting them to destruction. Will you then be spared?'),
('2KI', 19, 12, '2KI.19.12', 'Did the gods of the nations destroyed by my fathers rescue those nations—the gods of Gozan, Haran, and Rezeph, and of the people of Eden in Telassar?'),
('2KI', 19, 13, '2KI.19.13', 'Where are the kings of Hamath, Arpad, Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivvah?’”'),
('2KI', 19, 14, '2KI.19.14', 'So Hezekiah received the letter from the messengers, read it, and went up to the house of the LORD and spread it out before the LORD.'),
('2KI', 19, 15, '2KI.19.15', 'And Hezekiah prayed before the LORD: “O LORD, God of Israel, enthroned between the cherubim, You alone are God over all the kingdoms of the earth. You made the heavens and the earth.'),
('2KI', 19, 16, '2KI.19.16', 'Incline Your ear, O LORD, and hear; open Your eyes, O LORD, and see. Listen to the words that Sennacherib has sent to defy the living God.'),
('2KI', 19, 17, '2KI.19.17', 'Truly, O LORD, the kings of Assyria have laid waste these nations and their lands.'),
('2KI', 19, 18, '2KI.19.18', 'They have cast their gods into the fire and destroyed them, for they were not gods, but only wood and stone—the work of human hands.'),
('2KI', 19, 19, '2KI.19.19', 'And now, O LORD our God, please save us from his hand, so that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that You alone, O LORD, are God.”'),
('2KI', 19, 20, '2KI.19.20', 'Then Isaiah son of Amoz sent a message to Hezekiah: “This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: I have heard your prayer concerning Sennacherib king of Assyria.'),
('2KI', 19, 21, '2KI.19.21', 'This is the word that the LORD has spoken against him: ‘The Virgin Daughter of Zion despises you and mocks you; the Daughter of Jerusalem shakes her head behind you.'),
('2KI', 19, 22, '2KI.19.22', 'Whom have you taunted and blasphemed? Against whom have you raised your voice and lifted your eyes in pride? Against the Holy One of Israel!'),
('2KI', 19, 23, '2KI.19.23', 'Through your servants you have taunted the Lord, and you have said: “With my many chariots I have ascended to the heights of the mountains, to the remote peaks of Lebanon. I have cut down its tallest cedars, the finest of its cypresses. I have reached its farthest outposts, the densest of its forests.'),
('2KI', 19, 24, '2KI.19.24', 'I have dug wells and drunk foreign waters. With the soles of my feet I have dried up all the streams of Egypt.”'),
('2KI', 19, 25, '2KI.19.25', 'Have you not heard? Long ago I ordained it; in days of old I planned it. Now I have brought it to pass, that you should crush fortified cities into piles of rubble.'),
('2KI', 19, 26, '2KI.19.26', 'Therefore their inhabitants, devoid of power, are dismayed and ashamed. They are like plants in the field, tender green shoots, grass on the rooftops, scorched before it is grown.'),
('2KI', 19, 27, '2KI.19.27', 'But I know your sitting down, your going out and coming in, and your raging against Me.'),
('2KI', 19, 28, '2KI.19.28', 'Because your rage and arrogance against Me have reached My ears, I will put My hook in your nose and My bit in your mouth; I will send you back the way you came.’'),
('2KI', 19, 29, '2KI.19.29', 'And this will be a sign to you, O Hezekiah: This year you will eat what grows on its own, and in the second year what springs from the same. But in the third year you will sow and reap; you will plant vineyards and eat their fruit.'),
('2KI', 19, 30, '2KI.19.30', 'And the surviving remnant of the house of Judah will again take root below and bear fruit above.'),
('2KI', 19, 31, '2KI.19.31', 'For a remnant will go forth from Jerusalem, and survivors from Mount Zion. The zeal of the LORD of Hosts will accomplish this.'),
('2KI', 19, 32, '2KI.19.32', 'So this is what the LORD says about the king of Assyria: ‘He will not enter this city or shoot an arrow into it. He will not come before it with a shield or build up a siege ramp against it.'),
('2KI', 19, 33, '2KI.19.33', 'He will go back the way he came, and he will not enter this city, declares the LORD.'),
('2KI', 19, 34, '2KI.19.34', 'I will defend this city and save it for My own sake and for the sake of My servant David.’”'),
('2KI', 19, 35, '2KI.19.35', 'And that very night the angel of the LORD went out and struck down 185,000 men in the camp of the Assyrians. When the people got up the next morning, there were all the dead bodies!'),
('2KI', 19, 36, '2KI.19.36', 'So Sennacherib king of Assyria broke camp and withdrew. He returned to Nineveh and stayed there.'),
('2KI', 19, 37, '2KI.19.37', 'One day, while he was worshiping in the temple of his god Nisroch, his sons Adrammelech and Sharezer put him to the sword and escaped to the land of Ararat. And his son Esar-haddon reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 20, 1, '2KI.20.1', 'In those days Hezekiah became mortally ill. The prophet Isaiah son of Amoz came to him and said, “This is what the LORD says: ‘Put your house in order, for you are about to die; you will not recover.’”'),
('2KI', 20, 2, '2KI.20.2', 'Then Hezekiah turned his face to the wall and prayed to the LORD, saying,'),
('2KI', 20, 3, '2KI.20.3', '“Please, O LORD, remember how I have walked before You faithfully and with wholehearted devotion; I have done what is good in Your sight.” And Hezekiah wept bitterly.'),
('2KI', 20, 4, '2KI.20.4', 'Before Isaiah had left the middle courtyard, the word of the LORD came to him, saying,'),
('2KI', 20, 5, '2KI.20.5', '“Go back and tell Hezekiah the leader of My people that this is what the LORD, the God of your father David, says: ‘I have heard your prayer; I have seen your tears. I will surely heal you. On the third day from now you will go up to the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 20, 6, '2KI.20.6', 'I will add fifteen years to your life. And I will deliver you and this city from the hand of the king of Assyria. I will defend this city for My sake and for the sake of My servant David.’”'),
('2KI', 20, 7, '2KI.20.7', 'Then Isaiah said, “Prepare a poultice of figs.” So they brought it and applied it to the boil, and Hezekiah recovered.'),
('2KI', 20, 8, '2KI.20.8', 'Now Hezekiah had asked Isaiah, “What will be the sign that the LORD will heal me and that I will go up to the house of the LORD on the third day?”'),
('2KI', 20, 9, '2KI.20.9', 'And Isaiah had replied, “This will be a sign to you from the LORD that He will do what He has promised: Would you like the shadow to go forward ten steps, or back ten steps?”'),
('2KI', 20, 10, '2KI.20.10', '“It is easy for the shadow to lengthen ten steps,” answered Hezekiah, “but not for it to go back ten steps.”'),
('2KI', 20, 11, '2KI.20.11', 'So Isaiah the prophet called out to the LORD, and He brought the shadow back the ten steps it had descended on the stairway of Ahaz.'),
('2KI', 20, 12, '2KI.20.12', 'At that time Merodach-baladan son of Baladan king of Babylon sent letters and a gift to Hezekiah, for he had heard about Hezekiah’s illness.'),
('2KI', 20, 13, '2KI.20.13', 'And Hezekiah received the envoys and showed them all that was in his treasure house—the silver, the gold, the spices, and the precious oil, as well as his armory—all that was found in his storehouses. There was nothing in his palace or in all his dominion that Hezekiah did not show them.'),
('2KI', 20, 14, '2KI.20.14', 'Then the prophet Isaiah went to King Hezekiah and asked, “Where did those men come from, and what did they say to you?” “They came from a distant land,” Hezekiah replied, “from Babylon.”'),
('2KI', 20, 15, '2KI.20.15', '“What have they seen in your palace?” Isaiah asked. “They have seen everything in my palace,” answered Hezekiah. “There is nothing among my treasures that I did not show them.”'),
('2KI', 20, 16, '2KI.20.16', 'Then Isaiah said to Hezekiah, “Hear the word of the LORD:'),
('2KI', 20, 17, '2KI.20.17', 'The time will surely come when everything in your palace and all that your fathers have stored up until this day will be carried off to Babylon. Nothing will be left, says the LORD.'),
('2KI', 20, 18, '2KI.20.18', 'And some of your descendants, your own flesh and blood, will be taken away to be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon.”'),
('2KI', 20, 19, '2KI.20.19', 'But Hezekiah said to Isaiah, “The word of the LORD that you have spoken is good.” For he thought, “Will there not at least be peace and security in my lifetime?”'),
('2KI', 20, 20, '2KI.20.20', 'As for the rest of the acts of Hezekiah, along with all his might and how he constructed the pool and the tunnel to bring water into the city, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 20, 21, '2KI.20.21', 'And Hezekiah rested with his fathers, and his son Manasseh reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 21, 1, '2KI.21.1', 'Manasseh was twelve years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem fifty-five years. His mother’s name was Hephzibah.'),
('2KI', 21, 2, '2KI.21.2', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD by following the abominations of the nations that the LORD had driven out before the Israelites.'),
('2KI', 21, 3, '2KI.21.3', 'For he rebuilt the high places that his father Hezekiah had destroyed, and he raised up altars for Baal. He made an Asherah pole, as King Ahab of Israel had done, and he worshiped and served all the host of heaven.'),
('2KI', 21, 4, '2KI.21.4', 'Manasseh also built altars in the house of the LORD, of which the LORD had said, “In Jerusalem I will put My Name.”'),
('2KI', 21, 5, '2KI.21.5', 'In both courtyards of the house of the LORD, he built altars to all the host of heaven.'),
('2KI', 21, 6, '2KI.21.6', 'He sacrificed his own son in the fire, practiced sorcery and divination, and consulted mediums and spiritists. He did great evil in the sight of the LORD, provoking Him to anger.'),
('2KI', 21, 7, '2KI.21.7', 'Manasseh even took the carved Asherah pole he had made and set it up in the temple, of which the LORD had said to David and his son Solomon, “In this temple and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, I will establish My Name forever.'),
('2KI', 21, 8, '2KI.21.8', 'I will never again cause the feet of the Israelites to wander from the land that I gave to their fathers, if only they are careful to do all I have commanded them—the whole Law that My servant Moses commanded them.”'),
('2KI', 21, 9, '2KI.21.9', 'But the people did not listen and Manasseh led them astray, so that they did greater evil than the nations that the LORD had destroyed before the Israelites.'),
('2KI', 21, 10, '2KI.21.10', 'And the LORD spoke through His servants the prophets, saying,'),
('2KI', 21, 11, '2KI.21.11', '“Since Manasseh king of Judah has committed all these abominations, acting more wickedly than the Amorites who preceded him, and with his idols has caused Judah to sin,'),
('2KI', 21, 12, '2KI.21.12', 'this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Behold, I am bringing such calamity upon Jerusalem and Judah that the news will reverberate in the ears of all who hear it.'),
('2KI', 21, 13, '2KI.21.13', 'I will stretch out over Jerusalem the measuring line used against Samaria and the plumb line used against the house of Ahab, and I will wipe out Jerusalem as one wipes out a bowl—wiping it and turning it upside down.'),
('2KI', 21, 14, '2KI.21.14', 'So I will forsake the remnant of My inheritance and deliver them into the hands of their enemies. And they will become plunder and spoil to all their enemies,'),
('2KI', 21, 15, '2KI.21.15', 'because they have done evil in My sight and have provoked Me to anger from the day their fathers came out of Egypt until this day.’”'),
('2KI', 21, 16, '2KI.21.16', 'Moreover, Manasseh shed so much innocent blood that he filled Jerusalem from end to end, in addition to the sin that he had caused Judah to commit, doing evil in the sight of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 21, 17, '2KI.21.17', 'As for the rest of the acts of Manasseh, along with all his accomplishments and the sin that he committed, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 21, 18, '2KI.21.18', 'And Manasseh rested with his fathers and was buried in his palace garden, the garden of Uzza. And his son Amon reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 21, 19, '2KI.21.19', 'Amon was twenty-two years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem two years. His mother’s name was Meshullemeth daughter of Haruz; she was from Jotbah.'),
('2KI', 21, 20, '2KI.21.20', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, as his father Manasseh had done.'),
('2KI', 21, 21, '2KI.21.21', 'He walked in all the ways of his father, and he served and worshiped the idols his father had served.'),
('2KI', 21, 22, '2KI.21.22', 'He abandoned the LORD, the God of his fathers, and did not walk in the way of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 21, 23, '2KI.21.23', 'Then the servants of Amon conspired against him and killed the king in his palace.'),
('2KI', 21, 24, '2KI.21.24', 'But the people of the land killed all those who had conspired against King Amon, and they made his son Josiah king in his place.'),
('2KI', 21, 25, '2KI.21.25', 'As for the rest of the acts of Amon, along with his accomplishments, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 21, 26, '2KI.21.26', 'And he was buried in his tomb in the garden of Uzza, and his son Josiah reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 22, 1, '2KI.22.1', 'Josiah was eight years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem thirty-one years. His mother’s name was Jedidah daughter of Adaiah; she was from Bozkath.'),
('2KI', 22, 2, '2KI.22.2', 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD and walked in all the ways of his father David; he did not turn aside to the right or to the left.'),
('2KI', 22, 3, '2KI.22.3', 'Now in the eighteenth year of his reign, King Josiah sent the scribe, Shaphan son of Azaliah, the son of Meshullam, to the house of the LORD, saying,'),
('2KI', 22, 4, '2KI.22.4', '“Go up to Hilkiah the high priest and have him count the money that has been brought into the house of the LORD, which the doorkeepers have collected from the people.'),
('2KI', 22, 5, '2KI.22.5', 'And let them deliver it into the hands of the supervisors of those doing the work on the house of the LORD, who in turn are to give it to the workmen repairing the damages to the house of the LORD—'),
('2KI', 22, 6, '2KI.22.6', 'to the carpenters, builders, and masons—to buy timber and dressed stone to repair the temple.'),
('2KI', 22, 7, '2KI.22.7', 'But they need not account for the money put into their hands, since they work with integrity.”'),
('2KI', 22, 8, '2KI.22.8', 'Then Hilkiah the high priest said to Shaphan the scribe, “I have found the Book of the Law in the house of the LORD!” And he gave it to Shaphan, who read it.'),
('2KI', 22, 9, '2KI.22.9', 'And Shaphan the scribe went to the king and reported, “Your servants have paid out the money that was found in the temple and have put it into the hands of the workers and supervisors of the house of the LORD.”'),
('2KI', 22, 10, '2KI.22.10', 'Moreover, Shaphan the scribe told the king, “Hilkiah the priest has given me a book.” And Shaphan read it in the presence of the king.'),
('2KI', 22, 11, '2KI.22.11', 'When the king heard the words of the Book of the Law, he tore his clothes'),
('2KI', 22, 12, '2KI.22.12', 'and commanded Hilkiah the priest, Ahikam son of Shaphan, Achbor son of Micaiah, Shaphan the scribe, and Asaiah the servant of the king:'),
('2KI', 22, 13, '2KI.22.13', '“Go and inquire of the LORD for me, for the people, and for all Judah concerning the words in this book that has been found. For great is the wrath of the LORD that burns against us because our fathers have not obeyed the words of this book by doing all that is written about us.”'),
('2KI', 22, 14, '2KI.22.14', 'So Hilkiah the priest, Ahikam, Achbor, Shaphan, and Asaiah went and spoke to Huldah the prophetess, the wife of Shallum son of Tikvah, the son of Harhas, the keeper of the wardrobe. She lived in Jerusalem, in the Second District.'),
('2KI', 22, 15, '2KI.22.15', 'And Huldah said to them, “This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Tell the man who sent you'),
('2KI', 22, 16, '2KI.22.16', 'that this is what the LORD says: I am about to bring calamity on this place and on its people, according to all the words of the book that the king of Judah has read,'),
('2KI', 22, 17, '2KI.22.17', 'because they have forsaken Me and burned incense to other gods, that they might provoke Me to anger with all the works of their hands. My wrath will be kindled against this place and will not be quenched.’'),
('2KI', 22, 18, '2KI.22.18', 'But as for the king of Judah, who sent you to inquire of the LORD, tell him that this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘As for the words that you heard,'),
('2KI', 22, 19, '2KI.22.19', 'because your heart was tender and you humbled yourself before the LORD when you heard what I spoke against this place and against its people, that they would become a desolation and a curse, and because you have torn your clothes and wept before Me, I have heard you,’ declares the LORD.'),
('2KI', 22, 20, '2KI.22.20', '‘Therefore I will indeed gather you to your fathers, and you will be gathered to your grave in peace. Your eyes will not see all the calamity that I will bring on this place.’” So they brought her answer back to the king.'),
('2KI', 23, 1, '2KI.23.1', 'Then the king summoned all the elders of Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 23, 2, '2KI.23.2', 'And he went up to the house of the LORD with all the people of Judah and Jerusalem, as well as the priests and the prophets—all the people small and great—and in their hearing he read all the words of the Book of the Covenant that had been found in the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 23, 3, '2KI.23.3', 'So the king stood by the pillar and made a covenant before the LORD to follow the LORD and to keep His commandments, decrees, and statutes with all his heart and all his soul, and to carry out the words of the covenant that were written in this book. And all the people entered into the covenant.'),
('2KI', 23, 4, '2KI.23.4', 'Then the king commanded Hilkiah the high priest, the priests second in rank, and the doorkeepers to remove from the temple of the LORD all the articles made for Baal, Asherah, and all the host of heaven. And he burned them outside Jerusalem in the fields of Kidron and carried their ashes to Bethel.'),
('2KI', 23, 5, '2KI.23.5', 'Josiah also did away with the idolatrous priests ordained by the kings of Judah to burn incense on the high places of the cities of Judah and in the places all around Jerusalem—those who had burned incense to Baal, to the sun and moon, to the constellations, and to all the host of heaven.'),
('2KI', 23, 6, '2KI.23.6', 'He brought the Asherah pole from the house of the LORD to the Kidron Valley outside Jerusalem, and there he burned it, ground it to powder, and threw its dust on the graves of the common people.'),
('2KI', 23, 7, '2KI.23.7', 'He also tore down the quarters of the male shrine prostitutes that were in the house of the LORD, where the women had woven tapestries for Asherah.'),
('2KI', 23, 8, '2KI.23.8', 'Then Josiah brought all the priests from the cities of Judah and desecrated the high places, from Geba to Beersheba, where the priests had burned incense. He tore down the high places of the gates at the entrance of the gate of Joshua the governor of the city, which was to the left of the city gate.'),
('2KI', 23, 9, '2KI.23.9', 'Although the priests of the high places did not come up to the altar of the LORD in Jerusalem, they ate unleavened bread with their fellow priests.'),
('2KI', 23, 10, '2KI.23.10', 'He also desecrated Topheth in the Valley of Ben-hinnom so that no one could sacrifice his son or daughter in the fire to Molech.'),
('2KI', 23, 11, '2KI.23.11', 'And he removed from the entrance to the house of the LORD the horses that the kings of Judah had dedicated to the sun. They were in the court near the chamber of an official named Nathan-melech. And Josiah burned up the chariots of the sun.'),
('2KI', 23, 12, '2KI.23.12', 'He pulled down the altars that the kings of Judah had set up on the roof near the upper chamber of Ahaz, and the altars that Manasseh had set up in the two courtyards of the house of the LORD. The king pulverized them there and threw their dust into the Kidron Valley.'),
('2KI', 23, 13, '2KI.23.13', 'The king also desecrated the high places east of Jerusalem, to the south of the Mount of Corruption, which King Solomon of Israel had built for Ashtoreth the abomination of the Sidonians, for Chemosh the abomination of the Moabites, and for Milcom the abomination of the Ammonites.'),
('2KI', 23, 14, '2KI.23.14', 'He smashed the sacred pillars to pieces, cut down the Asherah poles, and covered the sites with human bones.'),
('2KI', 23, 15, '2KI.23.15', 'He even pulled down the altar at Bethel, the high place set up by Jeroboam son of Nebat, who had caused Israel to sin. Then he burned the high place, ground it to powder, and burned the Asherah pole.'),
('2KI', 23, 16, '2KI.23.16', 'And as Josiah turned, he saw the tombs there on the hillside, and he sent someone to take the bones out of the tombs, and he burned them on the altar to defile it, according to the word of the LORD proclaimed by the man of God who had foretold these things.'),
('2KI', 23, 17, '2KI.23.17', 'Then the king asked, “What is this monument I see?” And the men of the city replied, “It is the tomb of the man of God who came from Judah and proclaimed these things that you have done to the altar of Bethel.”'),
('2KI', 23, 18, '2KI.23.18', '“Let him rest,” said Josiah. “Do not let anyone disturb his bones.” So they left his bones undisturbed, along with those of the prophet who had come from Samaria.'),
('2KI', 23, 19, '2KI.23.19', 'Just as Josiah had done at Bethel, so also in the cities of Samaria he removed all the shrines of the high places set up by the kings of Israel who had provoked the LORD to anger.'),
('2KI', 23, 20, '2KI.23.20', 'On the altars he slaughtered all the priests of the high places, and he burned human bones on them. Then he returned to Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 23, 21, '2KI.23.21', 'The king commanded all the people, “Keep the Passover of the LORD your God, as it is written in this Book of the Covenant.”'),
('2KI', 23, 22, '2KI.23.22', 'No such Passover had been observed from the days of the judges who had governed Israel through all the days of the kings of Israel and Judah.'),
('2KI', 23, 23, '2KI.23.23', 'But in the eighteenth year of Josiah’s reign, this Passover was observed to the LORD in Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 23, 24, '2KI.23.24', 'Furthermore, Josiah removed the mediums and spiritists, the household gods and idols, and all the abominations that were seen in the land of Judah and in Jerusalem. He did this to carry out the words of the law written in the book that Hilkiah the priest had found in the house of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 23, 25, '2KI.23.25', 'Neither before nor after Josiah was there any king like him, who turned to the LORD with all his heart and with all his soul and with all his strength, according to all the Law of Moses.'),
('2KI', 23, 26, '2KI.23.26', 'Nevertheless, the LORD did not turn away from the fury of His burning anger, which was kindled against Judah because of all that Manasseh had done to provoke Him to anger.'),
('2KI', 23, 27, '2KI.23.27', 'For the LORD had said, “I will remove Judah from My sight, just as I removed Israel. I will reject this city Jerusalem, which I chose, and the temple of which I said, ‘My Name shall be there.’”'),
('2KI', 23, 28, '2KI.23.28', 'As for the rest of the acts of Josiah and all his accomplishments, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 23, 29, '2KI.23.29', 'During Josiah’s reign, Pharaoh Neco king of Egypt marched up to help the king of Assyria at the Euphrates River. King Josiah went out to confront him, but Neco faced him and killed him at Megiddo.'),
('2KI', 23, 30, '2KI.23.30', 'From Megiddo his servants carried his body in a chariot, brought him to Jerusalem, and buried him in his own tomb. Then the people of the land took Jehoahaz son of Josiah, anointed him, and made him king in place of his father.'),
('2KI', 23, 31, '2KI.23.31', 'Jehoahaz was twenty-three years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months. His mother’s name was Hamutal daughter of Jeremiah; she was from Libnah.'),
('2KI', 23, 32, '2KI.23.32', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, just as his fathers had done.'),
('2KI', 23, 33, '2KI.23.33', 'And Pharaoh Neco imprisoned Jehoahaz at Riblah in the land of Hamath so that he could not reign in Jerusalem, and he imposed on Judah a levy of a hundred talents of silver and a talent of gold.'),
('2KI', 23, 34, '2KI.23.34', 'Then Pharaoh Neco made Eliakim son of Josiah king in place of his father Josiah, and he changed Eliakim’s name to Jehoiakim. But Neco took Jehoahaz and carried him off to Egypt, where he died.'),
('2KI', 23, 35, '2KI.23.35', 'So Jehoiakim paid the silver and gold to Pharaoh Neco, but to meet Pharaoh’s demand he taxed the land and exacted the silver and the gold from the people, each according to his wealth.'),
('2KI', 23, 36, '2KI.23.36', 'Jehoiakim was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eleven years. His mother’s name was Zebidah daughter of Pedaiah; she was from Rumah.'),
('2KI', 23, 37, '2KI.23.37', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, just as his fathers had done.'),
('2KI', 24, 1, '2KI.24.1', 'During Jehoiakim’s reign, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon invaded. So Jehoiakim became his vassal for three years, until he turned and rebelled against Nebuchadnezzar.'),
('2KI', 24, 2, '2KI.24.2', 'And the LORD sent Chaldean, Aramean, Moabite, and Ammonite raiders against Jehoiakim in order to destroy Judah, according to the word that the LORD had spoken through His servants the prophets.'),
('2KI', 24, 3, '2KI.24.3', 'Surely this happened to Judah at the LORD’s command, to remove them from His presence because of the sins of Manasseh and all that he had done,'),
('2KI', 24, 4, '2KI.24.4', 'and also for the innocent blood he had shed. For he had filled Jerusalem with innocent blood, and the LORD was unwilling to forgive.'),
('2KI', 24, 5, '2KI.24.5', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jehoiakim, along with all his accomplishments, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?'),
('2KI', 24, 6, '2KI.24.6', 'And Jehoiakim rested with his fathers, and his son Jehoiachin reigned in his place.'),
('2KI', 24, 7, '2KI.24.7', 'Now the king of Egypt did not march out of his land again, because the king of Babylon had taken all his territory, from the Brook of Egypt to the Euphrates River.'),
('2KI', 24, 8, '2KI.24.8', 'Jehoiachin was eighteen years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months. His mother’s name was Nehushta daughter of Elnathan; she was from Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 24, 9, '2KI.24.9', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, just as his father had done.'),
('2KI', 24, 10, '2KI.24.10', 'At that time the servants of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon marched up to Jerusalem, and the city came under siege.'),
('2KI', 24, 11, '2KI.24.11', 'And Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came to the city while his servants were besieging it.'),
('2KI', 24, 12, '2KI.24.12', 'Jehoiachin king of Judah, his mother, his servants, his commanders, and his officials all surrendered to the king of Babylon. So in the eighth year of his reign, the king of Babylon took him captive.'),
('2KI', 24, 13, '2KI.24.13', 'As the LORD had declared, Nebuchadnezzar also carried off all the treasures from the house of the LORD and the royal palace, and he cut into pieces all the gold articles that Solomon king of Israel had made in the temple of the LORD.'),
('2KI', 24, 14, '2KI.24.14', 'He carried into exile all Jerusalem—all the commanders and mighty men of valor, all the craftsmen and metalsmiths—ten thousand captives in all. Only the poorest people of the land remained.'),
('2KI', 24, 15, '2KI.24.15', 'Nebuchadnezzar carried away Jehoiachin to Babylon, as well as the king’s mother, his wives, his officials, and the leading men of the land. He took them into exile from Jerusalem to Babylon.'),
('2KI', 24, 16, '2KI.24.16', 'The king of Babylon also brought into exile to Babylon all seven thousand men of valor and a thousand craftsmen and metalsmiths—all strong and fit for battle.'),
('2KI', 24, 17, '2KI.24.17', 'Then the king of Babylon made Mattaniah, Jehoiachin’s uncle, king in his place and changed his name to Zedekiah.'),
('2KI', 24, 18, '2KI.24.18', 'Zedekiah was twenty-one years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eleven years. His mother’s name was Hamutal daughter of Jeremiah; she was from Libnah.'),
('2KI', 24, 19, '2KI.24.19', 'And Zedekiah did evil in the sight of the LORD, just as Jehoiakim had done.'),
('2KI', 24, 20, '2KI.24.20', 'For because of the anger of the LORD, all this happened in Jerusalem and Judah, until He finally banished them from His presence. And Zedekiah also rebelled against the king of Babylon.'),
('2KI', 25, 1, '2KI.25.1', 'So in the ninth year of Zedekiah’s reign, on the tenth day of the tenth month, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon marched against Jerusalem with his entire army. They encamped outside the city and built a siege wall all around it.'),
('2KI', 25, 2, '2KI.25.2', 'And the city was kept under siege until King Zedekiah’s eleventh year.'),
('2KI', 25, 3, '2KI.25.3', 'By the ninth day of the fourth month, the famine in the city was so severe that the people of the land had no food.'),
('2KI', 25, 4, '2KI.25.4', 'Then the city was breached; and though the Chaldeans had surrounded the city, all the men of war fled by night by way of the gate between the two walls near the king’s garden. They headed toward the Arabah,'),
('2KI', 25, 5, '2KI.25.5', 'but the army of the Chaldeans pursued the king and overtook him in the plains of Jericho, and his whole army deserted him.'),
('2KI', 25, 6, '2KI.25.6', 'The Chaldeans seized the king and brought him up to the king of Babylon at Riblah, where they pronounced judgment on him.'),
('2KI', 25, 7, '2KI.25.7', 'And they slaughtered the sons of Zedekiah before his eyes. Then they put out his eyes, bound him with bronze shackles, and took him to Babylon.'),
('2KI', 25, 8, '2KI.25.8', 'On the seventh day of the fifth month, in the nineteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar’s reign over Babylon, Nebuzaradan captain of the guard, a servant of the king of Babylon, entered Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 25, 9, '2KI.25.9', 'He burned down the house of the LORD, the royal palace, and all the houses of Jerusalem—every significant building.'),
('2KI', 25, 10, '2KI.25.10', 'And the whole army of the Chaldeans under the captain of the guard broke down the walls around Jerusalem.'),
('2KI', 25, 11, '2KI.25.11', 'Then Nebuzaradan captain of the guard carried into exile the people who remained in the city, along with the deserters who had defected to the king of Babylon and the rest of the population.'),
('2KI', 25, 12, '2KI.25.12', 'But the captain of the guard left behind some of the poorest of the land to tend the vineyards and fields.'),
('2KI', 25, 13, '2KI.25.13', 'Moreover, the Chaldeans broke up the bronze pillars and stands and the bronze Sea in the house of the LORD, and they carried the bronze to Babylon.'),
('2KI', 25, 14, '2KI.25.14', 'They also took away the pots, shovels, wick trimmers, dishes, and all the articles of bronze used in the temple service.'),
('2KI', 25, 15, '2KI.25.15', 'The captain of the guard also took away the censers and sprinkling bowls—anything made of pure gold or fine silver.'),
('2KI', 25, 16, '2KI.25.16', 'As for the two pillars, the Sea, and the movable stands that Solomon had made for the house of the LORD, the weight of the bronze from all these articles was beyond measure.'),
('2KI', 25, 17, '2KI.25.17', 'Each pillar was eighteen cubits tall. The bronze capital atop one pillar was three cubits high, with a network of bronze pomegranates all around. The second pillar, with its network, was similar.'),
('2KI', 25, 18, '2KI.25.18', 'The captain of the guard also took away Seraiah the chief priest, Zephaniah the priest of second rank, and the three doorkeepers.'),
('2KI', 25, 19, '2KI.25.19', 'Of those still in the city, he took a court official who had been appointed over the men of war, as well as five royal advisors. He also took the scribe of the captain of the army, who had enlisted the people of the land, and sixty men who were found in the city.'),
('2KI', 25, 20, '2KI.25.20', 'Nebuzaradan captain of the guard took them and brought them to the king of Babylon at Riblah.'),
('2KI', 25, 21, '2KI.25.21', 'There at Riblah in the land of Hamath, the king of Babylon struck them down and put them to death. So Judah was taken into exile, away from its own land.'),
('2KI', 25, 22, '2KI.25.22', 'Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon appointed Gedaliah son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, over the people he had left behind in the land of Judah.'),
('2KI', 25, 23, '2KI.25.23', 'When all the commanders of the armies and their men heard that the king of Babylon had appointed Gedaliah as governor, they came to Gedaliah at Mizpah—Ishmael son of Nethaniah, Johanan son of Kareah, Seraiah son of Tanhumeth the Netophathite, and Jaazaniah son of the Maacathite, as well as their men.'),
('2KI', 25, 24, '2KI.25.24', 'And Gedaliah took an oath before them and their men, assuring them, “Do not be afraid of the servants of the Chaldeans. Live in the land and serve the king of Babylon, and it will be well with you.”'),
('2KI', 25, 25, '2KI.25.25', 'In the seventh month, however, Ishmael son of Nethaniah, the son of Elishama, who was a member of the royal family, came with ten men and struck down and killed Gedaliah, along with the Judeans and Chaldeans who were with him at Mizpah.'),
('2KI', 25, 26, '2KI.25.26', 'Then all the people small and great, together with the commanders of the army, arose and fled to Egypt for fear of the Chaldeans.'),
('2KI', 25, 27, '2KI.25.27', 'On the twenty-seventh day of the twelfth month of the thirty-seventh year of the exile of Judah’s King Jehoiachin, in the year Evil-merodach became king of Babylon, he released King Jehoiachin of Judah from prison.'),
('2KI', 25, 28, '2KI.25.28', 'And he spoke kindly to Jehoiachin and set his throne above the thrones of the other kings who were with him in Babylon.'),
('2KI', 25, 29, '2KI.25.29', 'So Jehoiachin changed out of his prison clothes, and he dined regularly at the king’s table for the rest of his life.'),
('2KI', 25, 30, '2KI.25.30', 'And the king provided Jehoiachin a daily portion for the rest of his life.'),
('1CH', 1, 1, '1CH.1.1', 'Adam, Seth, Enosh,'),
('1CH', 1, 2, '1CH.1.2', 'Kenan, Mahalalel, Jared,'),
('1CH', 1, 3, '1CH.1.3', 'Enoch, Methuselah, Lamech, Noah.'),
('1CH', 1, 4, '1CH.1.4', 'The sons of Noah: Shem, Ham, and Japheth.'),
('1CH', 1, 5, '1CH.1.5', 'The sons of Japheth: Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshech, and Tiras.'),
('1CH', 1, 6, '1CH.1.6', 'The sons of Gomer: Ashkenaz, Riphath, and Togarmah.'),
('1CH', 1, 7, '1CH.1.7', 'And the sons of Javan: Elishah, Tarshish, the Kittites, and the Rodanites.'),
('1CH', 1, 8, '1CH.1.8', 'The sons of Ham: Cush, Mizraim, Put, and Canaan.'),
('1CH', 1, 9, '1CH.1.9', 'The sons of Cush: Seba, Havilah, Sabta, Raamah, and Sabteca. The sons of Raamah: Sheba and Dedan.'),
('1CH', 1, 10, '1CH.1.10', 'Cush was the father of Nimrod, who began to be a mighty one on the earth.'),
('1CH', 1, 11, '1CH.1.11', 'Mizraim was the father of the Ludites, the Anamites, the Lehabites, the Naphtuhites,'),
('1CH', 1, 12, '1CH.1.12', 'the Pathrusites, the Casluhites (from whom the Philistines came), and the Caphtorites.'),
('1CH', 1, 13, '1CH.1.13', 'And Canaan was the father of Sidon his firstborn, and of the Hittites,'),
('1CH', 1, 14, '1CH.1.14', 'the Jebusites, the Amorites, the Girgashites,'),
('1CH', 1, 15, '1CH.1.15', 'the Hivites, the Arkites, the Sinites,'),
('1CH', 1, 16, '1CH.1.16', 'the Arvadites, the Zemarites, and the Hamathites.'),
('1CH', 1, 17, '1CH.1.17', 'The sons of Shem: Elam, Asshur, Arphaxad, Lud, and Aram. The sons of Aram: Uz, Hul, Gether, and Meshech.'),
('1CH', 1, 18, '1CH.1.18', 'Arphaxad was the father of Shelah, and Shelah was the father of Eber.'),
('1CH', 1, 19, '1CH.1.19', 'Two sons were born to Eber: One was named Peleg, because in his days the earth was divided, and his brother was named Joktan.'),
('1CH', 1, 20, '1CH.1.20', 'And Joktan was the father of Almodad, Sheleph, Hazarmaveth, Jerah,'),
('1CH', 1, 21, '1CH.1.21', 'Hadoram, Uzal, Diklah,'),
('1CH', 1, 22, '1CH.1.22', 'Obal, Abimael, Sheba,'),
('1CH', 1, 23, '1CH.1.23', 'Ophir, Havilah, and Jobab. All these were sons of Joktan.'),
('1CH', 1, 24, '1CH.1.24', 'So from Shem came Arphaxad, Shelah,'),
('1CH', 1, 25, '1CH.1.25', 'Eber, Peleg, Reu,'),
('1CH', 1, 26, '1CH.1.26', 'Serug, Nahor, Terah,'),
('1CH', 1, 27, '1CH.1.27', 'and Abram (that is, Abraham).'),
('1CH', 1, 28, '1CH.1.28', 'The sons of Abraham were Isaac and Ishmael.'),
('1CH', 1, 29, '1CH.1.29', 'These are their genealogies: Nebaioth the firstborn of Ishmael, then Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam,'),
('1CH', 1, 30, '1CH.1.30', 'Mishma, Dumah, Massa, Hadad, Tema,'),
('1CH', 1, 31, '1CH.1.31', 'Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah. These were the sons of Ishmael.'),
('1CH', 1, 32, '1CH.1.32', 'The sons born to Keturah, Abraham’s concubine: Zimran, Jokshan, Medan, Midian, Ishbak, and Shuah. The sons of Jokshan: Sheba and Dedan.'),
('1CH', 1, 33, '1CH.1.33', 'The sons of Midian: Ephah, Epher, Hanoch, Abida, and Eldaah. All of these were Keturah’s sons.'),
('1CH', 1, 34, '1CH.1.34', 'Abraham was the father of Isaac. The sons of Isaac: Esau and Israel.'),
('1CH', 1, 35, '1CH.1.35', 'The sons of Esau: Eliphaz, Reuel, Jeush, Jalam, and Korah.'),
('1CH', 1, 36, '1CH.1.36', 'The sons of Eliphaz: Teman, Omar, Zepho, Gatam, and Kenaz; and by Timna, Amalek.'),
('1CH', 1, 37, '1CH.1.37', 'The sons of Reuel: Nahath, Zerah, Shammah, and Mizzah.'),
('1CH', 1, 38, '1CH.1.38', 'The sons of Seir: Lotan, Shobal, Zibeon, Anah, Dishon, Ezer, and Dishan.'),
('1CH', 1, 39, '1CH.1.39', 'The sons of Lotan: Hori and Homam. Timna was Lotan’s sister.'),
('1CH', 1, 40, '1CH.1.40', 'The sons of Shobal: Alvan, Manahath, Ebal, Shepho, and Onam. The sons of Zibeon: Aiah and Anah.'),
('1CH', 1, 41, '1CH.1.41', 'The son of Anah: Dishon. The sons of Dishon: Hemdan, Eshban, Ithran, and Cheran.'),
('1CH', 1, 42, '1CH.1.42', 'The sons of Ezer: Bilhan, Zaavan, and Akan. The sons of Dishan: Uz and Aran.'),
('1CH', 1, 43, '1CH.1.43', 'These are the kings who reigned in the land of Edom before any king reigned over the Israelites: Bela son of Beor. His city was named Dinhabah.'),
('1CH', 1, 44, '1CH.1.44', 'When Bela died, Jobab son of Zerah from Bozrah reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 1, 45, '1CH.1.45', 'When Jobab died, Husham from the land of the Temanites reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 1, 46, '1CH.1.46', 'When Husham died, Hadad son of Bedad, who defeated Midian in the country of Moab, reigned in his place. And the name of his city was Avith.'),
('1CH', 1, 47, '1CH.1.47', 'When Hadad died, Samlah from Masrekah reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 1, 48, '1CH.1.48', 'When Samlah died, Shaul from Rehoboth on the Euphrates reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 1, 49, '1CH.1.49', 'When Shaul died, Baal-hanan son of Achbor reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 1, 50, '1CH.1.50', 'When Baal-hanan died, Hadad reigned in his place. His city was named Pau, and his wife’s name was Mehetabel daughter of Matred, the daughter of Me-zahab.'),
('1CH', 1, 51, '1CH.1.51', 'Then Hadad died. Now the chiefs of Edom were Timna, Alvah, Jetheth,'),
('1CH', 1, 52, '1CH.1.52', 'Oholibamah, Elah, Pinon,'),
('1CH', 1, 53, '1CH.1.53', 'Kenaz, Teman, Mibzar,'),
('1CH', 1, 54, '1CH.1.54', 'Magdiel, and Iram. These were the chiefs of Edom.'),
('1CH', 2, 1, '1CH.2.1', 'These were the sons of Israel: Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, Zebulun,'),
('1CH', 2, 2, '1CH.2.2', 'Dan, Joseph, Benjamin, Naphtali, Gad, and Asher.'),
('1CH', 2, 3, '1CH.2.3', 'The sons of Judah: Er, Onan, and Shelah. These three were born to him by Bath-shua the Canaanite. Er, Judah’s firstborn, was wicked in the sight of the LORD. So the LORD put him to death.'),
('1CH', 2, 4, '1CH.2.4', 'Tamar, Judah’s daughter-in-law, bore to him Perez and Zerah. Judah had five sons in all.'),
('1CH', 2, 5, '1CH.2.5', 'The sons of Perez: Hezron and Hamul.'),
('1CH', 2, 6, '1CH.2.6', 'The sons of Zerah: Zimri, Ethan, Heman, Calcol, and Dara—five in all.'),
('1CH', 2, 7, '1CH.2.7', 'The son of Carmi: Achar, who brought trouble upon Israel by violating the ban on devoted things.'),
('1CH', 2, 8, '1CH.2.8', 'The son of Ethan: Azariah.'),
('1CH', 2, 9, '1CH.2.9', 'The sons who were born to Hezron: Jerahmeel, Ram, and Caleb.'),
('1CH', 2, 10, '1CH.2.10', 'Ram was the father of Amminadab, and Amminadab was the father of Nahshon, a leader of the descendants of Judah.'),
('1CH', 2, 11, '1CH.2.11', 'Nahshon was the father of Salmon, and Salmon was the father of Boaz.'),
('1CH', 2, 12, '1CH.2.12', 'Boaz was the father of Obed, and Obed was the father of Jesse.'),
('1CH', 2, 13, '1CH.2.13', 'Jesse was the father of Eliab his firstborn; Abinadab was born second, Shimea third,'),
('1CH', 2, 14, '1CH.2.14', 'Nethanel fourth, Raddai fifth,'),
('1CH', 2, 15, '1CH.2.15', 'Ozem sixth, and David seventh.'),
('1CH', 2, 16, '1CH.2.16', 'Their sisters were Zeruiah and Abigail. And the three sons of Zeruiah were Abishai, Joab, and Asahel.'),
('1CH', 2, 17, '1CH.2.17', 'Abigail was the mother of Amasa, whose father was Jether the Ishmaelite.'),
('1CH', 2, 18, '1CH.2.18', 'Caleb son of Hezron had children by his wife Azubah and by Jerioth. These were the sons of Azubah: Jesher, Shobab, and Ardon.'),
('1CH', 2, 19, '1CH.2.19', 'When Azubah died, Caleb married Ephrath, who bore to him Hur.'),
('1CH', 2, 20, '1CH.2.20', 'Hur was the father of Uri, and Uri was the father of Bezalel.'),
('1CH', 2, 21, '1CH.2.21', 'Later, Hezron slept with the daughter of Machir the father of Gilead. He had married her when he was sixty years old, and she bore to him Segub.'),
('1CH', 2, 22, '1CH.2.22', 'Segub was the father of Jair, who had twenty-three cities in the land of Gilead.'),
('1CH', 2, 23, '1CH.2.23', 'But Geshur and Aram captured Havvoth-jair, along with Kenath and its sixty surrounding villages. All these were descendants of Machir the father of Gilead.'),
('1CH', 2, 24, '1CH.2.24', 'After Hezron died in Caleb-ephrathah, his wife Abijah bore to him Ashhur the father of Tekoa.'),
('1CH', 2, 25, '1CH.2.25', 'The sons of Jerahmeel the firstborn of Hezron: Ram his firstborn, Bunah, Oren, Ozem, and Ahijah.'),
('1CH', 2, 26, '1CH.2.26', 'Jerahmeel had another wife named Atarah, who was the mother of Onam.'),
('1CH', 2, 27, '1CH.2.27', 'The sons of Ram the firstborn of Jerahmeel: Maaz, Jamin, and Eker.'),
('1CH', 2, 28, '1CH.2.28', 'The sons of Onam: Shammai and Jada. The sons of Shammai: Nadab and Abishur.'),
('1CH', 2, 29, '1CH.2.29', 'Abishur’s wife was named Abihail, and she bore to him Ahban and Molid.'),
('1CH', 2, 30, '1CH.2.30', 'The sons of Nadab: Seled and Appaim. Seled died without children.'),
('1CH', 2, 31, '1CH.2.31', 'The son of Appaim: Ishi. The son of Ishi: Sheshan. The son of Sheshan: Ahlai.'),
('1CH', 2, 32, '1CH.2.32', 'The sons of Jada the brother of Shammai: Jether and Jonathan. Jether died without children.'),
('1CH', 2, 33, '1CH.2.33', 'The sons of Jonathan: Peleth and Zaza. These were the descendants of Jerahmeel.'),
('1CH', 2, 34, '1CH.2.34', 'Sheshan had no sons, but only daughters. He also had an Egyptian servant named Jarha.'),
('1CH', 2, 35, '1CH.2.35', 'Sheshan gave his daughter in marriage to his servant Jarha, and she bore to him Attai.'),
('1CH', 2, 36, '1CH.2.36', 'Attai was the father of Nathan, Nathan was the father of Zabad,'),
('1CH', 2, 37, '1CH.2.37', 'Zabad was the father of Ephlal, Ephlal was the father of Obed,'),
('1CH', 2, 38, '1CH.2.38', 'Obed was the father of Jehu, Jehu was the father of Azariah,'),
('1CH', 2, 39, '1CH.2.39', 'Azariah was the father of Helez, Helez was the father of Elasah,'),
('1CH', 2, 40, '1CH.2.40', 'Elasah was the father of Sismai, Sismai was the father of Shallum,'),
('1CH', 2, 41, '1CH.2.41', 'Shallum was the father of Jekamiah, and Jekamiah was the father of Elishama.'),
('1CH', 2, 42, '1CH.2.42', 'The sons of Caleb the brother of Jerahmeel: Mesha his firstborn, who was the father of Ziph, and Mareshah his second son, who was the father of Hebron.'),
('1CH', 2, 43, '1CH.2.43', 'The sons of Hebron: Korah, Tappuah, Rekem, and Shema.'),
('1CH', 2, 44, '1CH.2.44', 'Shema was the father of Raham the father of Jorkeam, and Rekem was the father of Shammai.'),
('1CH', 2, 45, '1CH.2.45', 'The son of Shammai was Maon, and Maon was the father of Beth-zur.'),
('1CH', 2, 46, '1CH.2.46', 'Caleb’s concubine Ephah was the mother of Haran, Moza, and Gazez. Haran was the father of Gazez.'),
('1CH', 2, 47, '1CH.2.47', 'The sons of Jahdai: Regem, Jotham, Geshan, Pelet, Ephah, and Shaaph.'),
('1CH', 2, 48, '1CH.2.48', 'Caleb’s concubine Maacah was the mother of Sheber and Tirhanah.'),
('1CH', 2, 49, '1CH.2.49', 'She was also the mother of Shaaph father of Madmannah, and of Sheva father of Machbenah and Gibea. Caleb’s daughter was Acsah.'),
('1CH', 2, 50, '1CH.2.50', 'These were the descendants of Caleb. The sons of Hur the firstborn of Ephrathah: Shobal the father of Kiriath-jearim,'),
('1CH', 2, 51, '1CH.2.51', 'Salma the father of Bethlehem, and Hareph the father of Beth-gader.'),
('1CH', 2, 52, '1CH.2.52', 'These were the descendants of Shobal the father of Kiriath-jearim: Haroeh, half the Manahathites,'),
('1CH', 2, 53, '1CH.2.53', 'and the clans of Kiriath-jearim—the Ithrites, Puthites, Shumathites, and Mishraites. From these descended the Zorathites and Eshtaolites.'),
('1CH', 2, 54, '1CH.2.54', 'The descendants of Salma: Bethlehem, the Netophathites, Atroth-beth-joab, half the Manahathites, the Zorites,'),
('1CH', 2, 55, '1CH.2.55', 'and the clans of the scribes who lived at Jabez—the Tirathites, Shimeathites, and Sucathites. These are the Kenites who came from Hammath, the father of the house of Rechab.'),
('1CH', 3, 1, '1CH.3.1', 'These were the sons of David who were born to him in Hebron: The firstborn was Amnon by Ahinoam of Jezreel; the second was Daniel by Abigail of Carmel;'),
('1CH', 3, 2, '1CH.3.2', 'the third was Absalom the son of Maacah daughter of King Talmai of Geshur; the fourth was Adonijah the son of Haggith;'),
('1CH', 3, 3, '1CH.3.3', 'the fifth was Shephatiah by Abital; and the sixth was Ithream by his wife Eglah.'),
('1CH', 3, 4, '1CH.3.4', 'These six sons were born to David in Hebron, where he reigned seven years and six months. And David reigned in Jerusalem thirty-three years,'),
('1CH', 3, 5, '1CH.3.5', 'and these sons were born to him in Jerusalem: Shimea, Shobab, Nathan, and Solomon. These four were born to him by Bathsheba daughter of Ammiel.'),
('1CH', 3, 6, '1CH.3.6', 'David’s other sons were Ibhar, Elishua, Eliphelet,'),
('1CH', 3, 7, '1CH.3.7', 'Nogah, Nepheg, Japhia,'),
('1CH', 3, 8, '1CH.3.8', 'Elishama, Eliada, and Eliphelet—nine in all.'),
('1CH', 3, 9, '1CH.3.9', 'These were all the sons of David, besides the sons by his concubines. And Tamar was their sister.'),
('1CH', 3, 10, '1CH.3.10', 'Solomon’s son was Rehoboam: Abijah was his son, Asa his son, Jehoshaphat his son,'),
('1CH', 3, 11, '1CH.3.11', 'Joram his son, Ahaziah his son, Joash his son,'),
('1CH', 3, 12, '1CH.3.12', 'Amaziah his son, Azariah his son, Jotham his son,'),
('1CH', 3, 13, '1CH.3.13', 'Ahaz his son, Hezekiah his son, Manasseh his son,'),
('1CH', 3, 14, '1CH.3.14', 'Amon his son, and Josiah his son.'),
('1CH', 3, 15, '1CH.3.15', 'The sons of Josiah: Johanan was the firstborn, Jehoiakim the second, Zedekiah the third, and Shallum the fourth.'),
('1CH', 3, 16, '1CH.3.16', 'The successors of Jehoiakim: Jeconiah his son, and Zedekiah.'),
('1CH', 3, 17, '1CH.3.17', 'The descendants of Jeconiah the captive: Shealtiel his son,'),
('1CH', 3, 18, '1CH.3.18', 'Malchiram, Pedaiah, Shenazzar, Jekamiah, Hoshama, and Nedabiah.'),
('1CH', 3, 19, '1CH.3.19', 'The sons of Pedaiah: Zerubbabel and Shimei. The children of Zerubbabel: Meshullam and Hananiah, their sister Shelomith,'),
('1CH', 3, 20, '1CH.3.20', 'and five others: Hashubah, Ohel, Berechiah, Hasadiah, and Jushab-hesed.'),
('1CH', 3, 21, '1CH.3.21', 'The descendants of Hananiah: Pelatiah, Jeshaiah, and the sons of Rephaiah, of Arnan, of Obadiah, and of Shecaniah.'),
('1CH', 3, 22, '1CH.3.22', 'The six descendants of Shecaniah were Shemaiah and his sons: Hattush, Igal, Bariah, Neariah, and Shaphat.'),
('1CH', 3, 23, '1CH.3.23', 'The sons of Neariah: Elioenai, Hizkiah, and Azrikam—three in all.'),
('1CH', 3, 24, '1CH.3.24', 'The sons of Elioenai: Hodaviah, Eliashib, Pelaiah, Akkub, Johanan, Delaiah, and Anani—seven in all.'),
('1CH', 4, 1, '1CH.4.1', 'The descendants of Judah: Perez, Hezron, Carmi, Hur, and Shobal.'),
('1CH', 4, 2, '1CH.4.2', 'Reaiah son of Shobal was the father of Jahath, and Jahath was the father of Ahumai and Lahad. These were the clans of the Zorathites.'),
('1CH', 4, 3, '1CH.4.3', 'These were the sons of Etam: Jezreel, Ishma, and Idbash. And their sister was named Hazzelelponi.'),
('1CH', 4, 4, '1CH.4.4', 'Penuel was the father of Gedor, and Ezer was the father of Hushah. These were the descendants of Hur, the firstborn of Ephrathah and the father of Bethlehem.'),
('1CH', 4, 5, '1CH.4.5', 'Ashhur the father of Tekoa had two wives, Helah and Naarah.'),
('1CH', 4, 6, '1CH.4.6', 'Naarah bore to him Ahuzzam, Hepher, Temeni, and Haahashtari. These were the descendants of Naarah.'),
('1CH', 4, 7, '1CH.4.7', 'The sons of Helah were Zereth, Zohar, Ethnan,'),
('1CH', 4, 8, '1CH.4.8', 'and Koz, who was the father of Anub and Zobebah and of the clans of Aharhel son of Harum.'),
('1CH', 4, 9, '1CH.4.9', 'Now Jabez was more honorable than his brothers. His mother had named him Jabez, saying, “Because I bore him in pain.”'),
('1CH', 4, 10, '1CH.4.10', 'And Jabez called out to the God of Israel, “If only You would bless me and enlarge my territory! May Your hand be with me and keep me from harm, so that I will be free from pain.” And God granted the request of Jabez.'),
('1CH', 4, 11, '1CH.4.11', 'Chelub the brother of Shuhah was the father of Mehir, who was the father of Eshton.'),
('1CH', 4, 12, '1CH.4.12', 'Eshton was the father of Beth-rapha, of Paseah, and of Tehinnah the father of Ir-nahash. These were the men of Recah.'),
('1CH', 4, 13, '1CH.4.13', 'The sons of Kenaz: Othniel and Seraiah. The sons of Othniel: Hathath and Meonothai.'),
('1CH', 4, 14, '1CH.4.14', 'Meonothai was the father of Ophrah, and Seraiah was the father of Joab, the father of those living in Ge-harashim, which was given this name because its people were craftsmen.'),
('1CH', 4, 15, '1CH.4.15', 'The sons of Caleb son of Jephunneh: Iru, Elah, and Naam. The son of Elah: Kenaz.'),
('1CH', 4, 16, '1CH.4.16', 'The sons of Jehallelel: Ziph, Ziphah, Tiria, and Asarel.'),
('1CH', 4, 17, '1CH.4.17', 'The sons of Ezrah: Jether, Mered, Epher, and Jalon. And Mered’s wife Bithiah gave birth to Miriam, Shammai, and Ishbah the father of Eshtemoa.'),
('1CH', 4, 18, '1CH.4.18', 'These were the children of Pharaoh’s daughter Bithiah. Mered also took a Judean wife, who gave birth to Jered the father of Gedor, Heber the father of Soco, and Jekuthiel the father of Zanoah.'),
('1CH', 4, 19, '1CH.4.19', 'The sons of Hodiah’s wife, the sister of Naham, were the fathers of Keilah the Garmite and of Eshtemoa the Maacathite.'),
('1CH', 4, 20, '1CH.4.20', 'The sons of Shimon: Amnon, Rinnah, Ben-hanan, and Tilon. The descendants of Ishi: Zoheth and Ben-zoheth.'),
('1CH', 4, 21, '1CH.4.21', 'The sons of Shelah son of Judah: Er the father of Lecah, Laadah the father of Mareshah and the clans of the linen workers at Beth-ashbea,'),
('1CH', 4, 22, '1CH.4.22', 'Jokim, the men of Cozeba, and Joash and Saraph, who ruled in Moab and Jashubi-lehem. (These names are from ancient records.)'),
('1CH', 4, 23, '1CH.4.23', 'These were the potters who lived at Netaim and Gederah. They lived there in the service of the king.'),
('1CH', 4, 24, '1CH.4.24', 'The descendants of Simeon: Nemuel, Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, and Shaul.'),
('1CH', 4, 25, '1CH.4.25', 'The sons of Shaul: Shallum, Mibsam, and Mishma.'),
('1CH', 4, 26, '1CH.4.26', 'The sons of Mishma: Hammuel, Zaccur, and Shimei.'),
('1CH', 4, 27, '1CH.4.27', 'Shimei had sixteen sons and six daughters, but his brothers did not have many children, so their whole clan did not become as numerous as the sons of Judah.'),
('1CH', 4, 28, '1CH.4.28', 'They lived in Beersheba, Moladah, Hazar-shual,'),
('1CH', 4, 29, '1CH.4.29', 'Bilhah, Ezem, Tolad,'),
('1CH', 4, 30, '1CH.4.30', 'Bethuel, Hormah, Ziklag,'),
('1CH', 4, 31, '1CH.4.31', 'Beth-marcaboth, Hazar-susim, Beth-biri, and Shaaraim. These were their cities until the reign of David.'),
('1CH', 4, 32, '1CH.4.32', 'And their villages were Etam, Ain, Rimmon, Tochen, and Ashan—five towns—'),
('1CH', 4, 33, '1CH.4.33', 'and all their surrounding villages as far as Baal. These were their settlements, and they kept a genealogical record:'),
('1CH', 4, 34, '1CH.4.34', 'Meshobab, Jamlech, Joshah son of Amaziah,'),
('1CH', 4, 35, '1CH.4.35', 'Joel, Jehu son of Joshibiah (son of Seraiah, son of Asiel),'),
('1CH', 4, 36, '1CH.4.36', 'Elioenai, Jaakobah, Jeshohaiah, Asaiah, Adiel, Jesimiel, Benaiah,'),
('1CH', 4, 37, '1CH.4.37', 'and Ziza son of Shiphi (son of Allon, son of Jedaiah, son of Shimri, son of Shemaiah).'),
('1CH', 4, 38, '1CH.4.38', 'These men listed by name were the leaders of their clans. Their families increased greatly,'),
('1CH', 4, 39, '1CH.4.39', 'and they journeyed to the entrance of Gedor, to the east side of the valley, in search of pasture for their flocks.'),
('1CH', 4, 40, '1CH.4.40', 'There they found rich, good pasture, and the land was spacious, peaceful, and quiet; for some Hamites had lived there formerly.'),
('1CH', 4, 41, '1CH.4.41', 'These who were noted by name came in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah. They attacked the Hamites in their dwellings as well as the Meunites who were there, devoting them to destruction even to this day. Then they settled in their place, because there was pasture for their flocks.'),
('1CH', 4, 42, '1CH.4.42', 'And five hundred of these Simeonites led by Pelatiah, Neariah, Rephaiah, and Uzziel, the sons of Ishi, went to Mount Seir'),
('1CH', 4, 43, '1CH.4.43', 'and struck down the remnant of the Amalekites who had escaped. And they have lived there to this day.'),
('1CH', 5, 1, '1CH.5.1', 'These were the sons of Reuben the firstborn of Israel. Though he was the firstborn, his birthright was given to the sons of Joseph son of Israel, because Reuben defiled his father’s bed. So he is not reckoned according to birthright.'),
('1CH', 5, 2, '1CH.5.2', 'And though Judah prevailed over his brothers and a ruler came from him, the birthright belonged to Joseph.'),
('1CH', 5, 3, '1CH.5.3', 'The sons of Reuben, the firstborn of Israel: Hanoch, Pallu, Hezron, and Carmi.'),
('1CH', 5, 4, '1CH.5.4', 'The descendants of Joel: Shemaiah his son, Gog his son, Shimei his son,'),
('1CH', 5, 5, '1CH.5.5', 'Micah his son, Reaiah his son, Baal his son,'),
('1CH', 5, 6, '1CH.5.6', 'and Beerah his son, whom Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria carried into exile. Beerah was a leader of the Reubenites.'),
('1CH', 5, 7, '1CH.5.7', 'His relatives by their clans are recorded in their genealogy: Jeiel the chief, Zechariah,'),
('1CH', 5, 8, '1CH.5.8', 'and Bela son of Azaz, the son of Shema, the son of Joel. They settled in Aroer and as far as Nebo and Baal-meon.'),
('1CH', 5, 9, '1CH.5.9', 'They also settled in the east as far as the edge of the desert that extends to the Euphrates River, because their livestock had increased in the land of Gilead.'),
('1CH', 5, 10, '1CH.5.10', 'During the days of Saul they waged war against the Hagrites, who were defeated at their hands, and they occupied the dwellings of the Hagrites throughout the region east of Gilead.'),
('1CH', 5, 11, '1CH.5.11', 'The descendants of Gad lived next to the Reubenites in the land of Bashan, as far as Salecah:'),
('1CH', 5, 12, '1CH.5.12', 'Joel was the chief, Shapham the second, then Jaanai and Shaphat, who lived in Bashan.'),
('1CH', 5, 13, '1CH.5.13', 'Their kinsmen by families were Michael, Meshullam, Sheba, Jorai, Jacan, Zia, and Eber—seven in all.'),
('1CH', 5, 14, '1CH.5.14', 'These were the sons of Abihail son of Huri, the son of Jaroah, the son of Gilead, the son of Michael, the son of Jeshishai, the son of Jahdo, the son of Buz.'),
('1CH', 5, 15, '1CH.5.15', 'Ahi son of Abdiel, the son of Guni, was head of their family.'),
('1CH', 5, 16, '1CH.5.16', 'They lived in Gilead, in Bashan and its towns, and throughout the pasturelands of Sharon.'),
('1CH', 5, 17, '1CH.5.17', 'All of them were recorded in the genealogies during the reigns of Jotham king of Judah and Jeroboam king of Israel.'),
('1CH', 5, 18, '1CH.5.18', 'The Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh had 44,760 warriors—valiant men who carried the shield and sword, drew the bow, and were trained for battle.'),
('1CH', 5, 19, '1CH.5.19', 'They waged war against the Hagrites, as well as Jetur, Naphish, and Nodab.'),
('1CH', 5, 20, '1CH.5.20', 'And because they cried out to God in battle, they were helped against their enemies, and the Hagrites and all their allies were delivered into their hands. Because they put their trust in God, He answered their prayers.'),
('1CH', 5, 21, '1CH.5.21', 'They seized the livestock of the Hagrites—50,000 camels, 250,000 sheep, and 2,000 donkeys. They also took 100,000 captives,'),
('1CH', 5, 22, '1CH.5.22', 'and many others fell slain, because the battle belonged to God. And they occupied the land until the exile.'),
('1CH', 5, 23, '1CH.5.23', 'Now the people of the half-tribe of Manasseh were numerous. They settled in the land from Bashan to Baal-hermon (that is, Senir, also known as Mount Hermon).'),
('1CH', 5, 24, '1CH.5.24', 'These were the heads of their families: Epher, Ishi, Eliel, Azriel, Jeremiah, Hodaviah, and Jahdiel. They were mighty men of valor, famous men, and heads of their families.'),
('1CH', 5, 25, '1CH.5.25', 'But they were unfaithful to the God of their fathers, and they prostituted themselves with the gods of the peoples of the land, whom God had destroyed before them.'),
('1CH', 5, 26, '1CH.5.26', 'So the God of Israel stirred up the spirit of Pul king of Assyria (that is, Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria) to take the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh into exile. And he brought them to Halah, Habor, Hara, and the river of Gozan, where they remain to this day.'),
('1CH', 6, 1, '1CH.6.1', 'The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.'),
('1CH', 6, 2, '1CH.6.2', 'The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel.'),
('1CH', 6, 3, '1CH.6.3', 'The children of Amram: Aaron, Moses, and Miriam. The sons of Aaron: Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.'),
('1CH', 6, 4, '1CH.6.4', 'Eleazar was the father of Phinehas, Phinehas was the father of Abishua,'),
('1CH', 6, 5, '1CH.6.5', 'Abishua was the father of Bukki, Bukki was the father of Uzzi,'),
('1CH', 6, 6, '1CH.6.6', 'Uzzi was the father of Zerahiah, Zerahiah was the father of Meraioth,'),
('1CH', 6, 7, '1CH.6.7', 'Meraioth was the father of Amariah, Amariah was the father of Ahitub,'),
('1CH', 6, 8, '1CH.6.8', 'Ahitub was the father of Zadok, Zadok was the father of Ahimaaz,'),
('1CH', 6, 9, '1CH.6.9', 'Ahimaaz was the father of Azariah, Azariah was the father of Johanan,'),
('1CH', 6, 10, '1CH.6.10', 'Johanan was the father of Azariah, who served as priest in the temple that Solomon built in Jerusalem,'),
('1CH', 6, 11, '1CH.6.11', 'Azariah was the father of Amariah, Amariah was the father of Ahitub,'),
('1CH', 6, 12, '1CH.6.12', 'Ahitub was the father of Zadok, Zadok was the father of Shallum,'),
('1CH', 6, 13, '1CH.6.13', 'Shallum was the father of Hilkiah, Hilkiah was the father of Azariah,'),
('1CH', 6, 14, '1CH.6.14', 'Azariah was the father of Seraiah, and Seraiah was the father of Jehozadak.'),
('1CH', 6, 15, '1CH.6.15', 'Jehozadak went into captivity when the LORD sent Judah and Jerusalem into exile by the hand of Nebuchadnezzar.'),
('1CH', 6, 16, '1CH.6.16', 'The sons of Levi: Gershom, Kohath, and Merari.'),
('1CH', 6, 17, '1CH.6.17', 'These are the names of the sons of Gershom: Libni and Shimei.'),
('1CH', 6, 18, '1CH.6.18', 'The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel.'),
('1CH', 6, 19, '1CH.6.19', 'The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. These are the clans of the Levites listed according to their fathers:'),
('1CH', 6, 20, '1CH.6.20', 'Of Gershom: Libni his son, Jahath his son, Zimmah his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 21, '1CH.6.21', 'Joah his son, Iddo his son, Zerah his son, and Jeatherai his son.'),
('1CH', 6, 22, '1CH.6.22', 'The descendants of Kohath: Amminadab his son, Korah his son, Assir his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 23, '1CH.6.23', 'Elkanah his son, Ebiasaph his son, Assir his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 24, '1CH.6.24', 'Tahath his son, Uriel his son, Uzziah his son, and Shaul his son.'),
('1CH', 6, 25, '1CH.6.25', 'The descendants of Elkanah: Amasai, Ahimoth,'),
('1CH', 6, 26, '1CH.6.26', 'Elkanah his son, Zophai his son, Nahath his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 27, '1CH.6.27', 'Eliab his son, Jeroham his son, and Elkanah his son.'),
('1CH', 6, 28, '1CH.6.28', 'The sons of Samuel: Joel his firstborn and Abijah his second son.'),
('1CH', 6, 29, '1CH.6.29', 'The descendants of Merari: Mahli, Libni his son, Shimei his son, Uzzah his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 30, '1CH.6.30', 'Shimea his son, Haggiah his son, and Asaiah his son.'),
('1CH', 6, 31, '1CH.6.31', 'These are the men David put in charge of the music in the house of the LORD after the ark rested there.'),
('1CH', 6, 32, '1CH.6.32', 'They ministered with song before the tabernacle, the Tent of Meeting, until Solomon built the house of the LORD in Jerusalem. And they performed their duties according to the regulations given them.'),
('1CH', 6, 33, '1CH.6.33', 'These are the men who served, together with their sons. From the Kohathites: Heman the singer, the son of Joel, the son of Samuel,'),
('1CH', 6, 34, '1CH.6.34', 'the son of Elkanah, the son of Jeroham, the son of Eliel, the son of Toah,'),
('1CH', 6, 35, '1CH.6.35', 'the son of Zuph, the son of Elkanah, the son of Mahath, the son of Amasai,'),
('1CH', 6, 36, '1CH.6.36', 'the son of Elkanah, the son of Joel, the son of Azariah, the son of Zephaniah,'),
('1CH', 6, 37, '1CH.6.37', 'the son of Tahath, the son of Assir, the son of Ebiasaph, the son of Korah,'),
('1CH', 6, 38, '1CH.6.38', 'the son of Izhar, the son of Kohath, the son of Levi, the son of Israel.'),
('1CH', 6, 39, '1CH.6.39', 'Heman’s kinsman was Asaph, who served at his right hand: Asaph the son of Berechiah, the son of Shimea,'),
('1CH', 6, 40, '1CH.6.40', 'the son of Michael, the son of Baaseiah, the son of Malchijah,'),
('1CH', 6, 41, '1CH.6.41', 'the son of Ethni, the son of Zerah, the son of Adaiah,'),
('1CH', 6, 42, '1CH.6.42', 'the son of Ethan, the son of Zimmah, the son of Shimei,'),
('1CH', 6, 43, '1CH.6.43', 'the son of Jahath, the son of Gershom, the son of Levi.'),
('1CH', 6, 44, '1CH.6.44', 'On the left were their kinsmen, the sons of Merari: Ethan the son of Kishi, the son of Abdi, the son of Malluch,'),
('1CH', 6, 45, '1CH.6.45', 'the son of Hashabiah, the son of Amaziah, the son of Hilkiah,'),
('1CH', 6, 46, '1CH.6.46', 'the son of Amzi, the son of Bani, the son of Shemer,'),
('1CH', 6, 47, '1CH.6.47', 'the son of Mahli, the son of Mushi, the son of Merari, the son of Levi.'),
('1CH', 6, 48, '1CH.6.48', 'Their fellow Levites were assigned to every kind of service of the tabernacle, the house of God.'),
('1CH', 6, 49, '1CH.6.49', 'But Aaron and his sons did all the work of the Most Holy Place. They presented the offerings on the altar of burnt offering and on the altar of incense to make atonement for Israel, according to all that Moses the servant of God had commanded.'),
('1CH', 6, 50, '1CH.6.50', 'These were the descendants of Aaron: Eleazar his son, Phinehas his son, Abishua his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 51, '1CH.6.51', 'Bukki his son, Uzzi his son, Zerahiah his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 52, '1CH.6.52', 'Meraioth his son, Amariah his son, Ahitub his son,'),
('1CH', 6, 53, '1CH.6.53', 'Zadok his son, and Ahimaaz his son.'),
('1CH', 6, 54, '1CH.6.54', 'Now these were the territories assigned to the descendants of Aaron from the Kohathite clan for their settlements, because the first lot fell to them:'),
('1CH', 6, 55, '1CH.6.55', 'They were given Hebron in the land of Judah and its surrounding pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 6, 56, '1CH.6.56', 'But the fields and villages around the city were given to Caleb son of Jephunneh.'),
('1CH', 6, 57, '1CH.6.57', 'So the descendants of Aaron were given Hebron (a city of refuge), Libnah, Jattir, Eshtemoa,'),
('1CH', 6, 58, '1CH.6.58', 'Hilen, Debir,'),
('1CH', 6, 59, '1CH.6.59', 'Ashan, Juttah, and Beth-shemesh, together with their pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 6, 60, '1CH.6.60', 'And from the tribe of Benjamin they were given Gibeon, Geba, Alemeth, and Anathoth, together with their pasturelands. So they had thirteen cities in all among their families.'),
('1CH', 6, 61, '1CH.6.61', 'To the rest of the Kohathites, ten cities were allotted from the half-tribe of Manasseh.'),
('1CH', 6, 62, '1CH.6.62', 'The Gershomites, according to their clans, were allotted thirteen cities from the tribes of Issachar, Asher, Naphtali, and Manasseh in Bashan.'),
('1CH', 6, 63, '1CH.6.63', 'The Merarites, according to their clans, were allotted twelve cities from the tribes of Reuben, Gad, and Zebulun.'),
('1CH', 6, 64, '1CH.6.64', 'So the Israelites gave to the Levites these cities and their pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 6, 65, '1CH.6.65', 'They assigned by lot the cities named above from the tribes of Judah, Simeon, and Benjamin.'),
('1CH', 6, 66, '1CH.6.66', 'And some of the clans of the Kohathites were given cities from the tribe of Ephraim for their territory:'),
('1CH', 6, 67, '1CH.6.67', 'They were given Shechem (a city of refuge) with its pasturelands in the hill country of Ephraim, and Gezer,'),
('1CH', 6, 68, '1CH.6.68', 'Jokmeam, Beth-horon,'),
('1CH', 6, 69, '1CH.6.69', 'Aijalon, and Gath-rimmon, together with their pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 6, 70, '1CH.6.70', 'And from the half-tribe of Manasseh the rest of the clans of the Kohathites were given Aner and Bileam, together with their pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 6, 71, '1CH.6.71', 'The Gershomites received the following: From the clan of the half-tribe of Manasseh they were given Golan in Bashan and also Ashtaroth, together with their pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 6, 72, '1CH.6.72', 'From the tribe of Issachar they were given Kedesh, Daberath,'),
('1CH', 6, 73, '1CH.6.73', 'Ramoth, and Anem, together with their pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 6, 74, '1CH.6.74', 'From the tribe of Asher they were given Mashal, Abdon,'),
('1CH', 6, 75, '1CH.6.75', 'Hukok, and Rehob, together with their pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 6, 76, '1CH.6.76', 'And from the tribe of Naphtali they were given Kedesh in Galilee, Hammon, and Kiriathaim, together with their pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 6, 77, '1CH.6.77', 'The Merarites (the rest of the Levites) received the following: From the tribe of Zebulun they were given Rimmono and Tabor, together with their pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 6, 78, '1CH.6.78', 'From the tribe of Reuben east of the Jordan opposite Jericho they were given Bezer in the wilderness, Jahzah,'),
('1CH', 6, 79, '1CH.6.79', 'Kedemoth, and Mephaath, together with their pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 6, 80, '1CH.6.80', 'And from the tribe of Gad they were given Ramoth in Gilead, Mahanaim,'),
('1CH', 6, 81, '1CH.6.81', 'Heshbon, and Jazer, together with their pasturelands.'),
('1CH', 7, 1, '1CH.7.1', 'The sons of Issachar: Tola, Puah, Jashub, and Shimron—four in all.'),
('1CH', 7, 2, '1CH.7.2', 'The sons of Tola: Uzzi, Rephaiah, Jeriel, Jahmai, Ibsam, and Shemuel, the heads of their families. In the days of David, 22,600 descendants of Tola were numbered in their genealogies as mighty men of valor.'),
('1CH', 7, 3, '1CH.7.3', 'The son of Uzzi: Izrahiah. The sons of Izrahiah: Michael, Obadiah, Joel, and Isshiah. All five of them were chiefs.'),
('1CH', 7, 4, '1CH.7.4', 'In addition to them, according to their genealogy, they had 36,000 troops for battle, for they had many wives and children.'),
('1CH', 7, 5, '1CH.7.5', 'Their kinsmen belonging to all the families of Issachar who were mighty men of valor totaled 87,000, as listed in their genealogies.'),
('1CH', 7, 6, '1CH.7.6', 'The three sons of Benjamin: Bela, Becher, and Jediael.'),
('1CH', 7, 7, '1CH.7.7', 'The sons of Bela: Ezbon, Uzzi, Uzziel, Jerimoth, and Iri, heads of their families—five in all. There were 22,034 mighty men of valor listed in their genealogies.'),
('1CH', 7, 8, '1CH.7.8', 'The sons of Becher: Zemirah, Joash, Eliezer, Elioenai, Omri, Jeremoth, Abijah, Anathoth, and Alemeth; all these were Becher’s sons.'),
('1CH', 7, 9, '1CH.7.9', 'Their genealogies were recorded according to the heads of their families—20,200 mighty men of valor.'),
('1CH', 7, 10, '1CH.7.10', 'The son of Jediael: Bilhan. The sons of Bilhan: Jeush, Benjamin, Ehud, Chenaanah, Zethan, Tarshish, and Ahishahar.'),
('1CH', 7, 11, '1CH.7.11', 'All these sons of Jediael were heads of their families, mighty men of valor; there were 17,200 fit for battle.'),
('1CH', 7, 12, '1CH.7.12', 'The Shuppites and Huppites were descendants of Ir, and the Hushites were descendants of Aher.'),
('1CH', 7, 13, '1CH.7.13', 'The sons of Naphtali: Jahziel, Guni, Jezer, and Shallum—the descendants of Bilhah.'),
('1CH', 7, 14, '1CH.7.14', 'The descendants of Manasseh: Asriel through his Aramean concubine. She also gave birth to Machir the father of Gilead.'),
('1CH', 7, 15, '1CH.7.15', 'Machir took a wife from among the Huppites and Shuppites. The name of his sister was Maacah. Another descendant was named Zelophehad, who had only daughters.'),
('1CH', 7, 16, '1CH.7.16', 'Machir’s wife Maacah gave birth to a son, and she named him Peresh. His brother was named Sheresh, and his sons were Ulam and Rekem.'),
('1CH', 7, 17, '1CH.7.17', 'The son of Ulam: Bedan. These were the sons of Gilead son of Machir, the son of Manasseh.'),
('1CH', 7, 18, '1CH.7.18', 'His sister Hammolecheth gave birth to Ishhod, Abiezer, and Mahlah.'),
('1CH', 7, 19, '1CH.7.19', 'And these were the sons of Shemida: Ahian, Shechem, Likhi, and Aniam.'),
('1CH', 7, 20, '1CH.7.20', 'The descendants of Ephraim: Shuthelah, Bered his son, Tahath his son, Eleadah his son, Tahath his son,'),
('1CH', 7, 21, '1CH.7.21', 'Zabad his son, and Shuthelah his son. Ezer and Elead were killed by the natives of Gath, because they went down to steal their livestock.'),
('1CH', 7, 22, '1CH.7.22', 'Their father Ephraim mourned for many days, and his relatives came to comfort him.'),
('1CH', 7, 23, '1CH.7.23', 'And again he slept with his wife, and she conceived and gave birth to a son. So he named him Beriah, because tragedy had come upon his house.'),
('1CH', 7, 24, '1CH.7.24', 'His daughter was Sheerah, who built Lower and Upper Beth-horon, as well as Uzzen-sheerah.'),
('1CH', 7, 25, '1CH.7.25', 'Additionally, Rephah was his son, Resheph his son, Telah his son, Tahan his son,'),
('1CH', 7, 26, '1CH.7.26', 'Ladan his son, Ammihud his son, Elishama his son,'),
('1CH', 7, 27, '1CH.7.27', 'Nun his son, and Joshua his son.'),
('1CH', 7, 28, '1CH.7.28', 'Their holdings and settlements included Bethel and its villages, Naaran to the east, Gezer and its villages to the west, and Shechem and its villages as far as Ayyah and its villages.'),
('1CH', 7, 29, '1CH.7.29', 'And along the borders of Manasseh were Beth-shean, Taanach, Megiddo, and Dor, together with their villages. The descendants of Joseph son of Israel lived in these towns.'),
('1CH', 7, 30, '1CH.7.30', 'The children of Asher: Imnah, Ishvah, Ishvi, Beriah, and their sister Serah.'),
('1CH', 7, 31, '1CH.7.31', 'The sons of Beriah: Heber, as well as Malchiel, who was the father of Birzaith.'),
('1CH', 7, 32, '1CH.7.32', 'Heber was the father of Japhlet, Shomer, and Hotham, and of their sister Shua.'),
('1CH', 7, 33, '1CH.7.33', 'The sons of Japhlet: Pasach, Bimhal, and Ashvath. These were Japhlet’s sons.'),
('1CH', 7, 34, '1CH.7.34', 'The sons of Shemer: Ahi, Rohgah, Hubbah, and Aram.'),
('1CH', 7, 35, '1CH.7.35', 'The sons of his brother Helem: Zophah, Imna, Shelesh, and Amal.'),
('1CH', 7, 36, '1CH.7.36', 'The sons of Zophah: Suah, Harnepher, Shual, Beri, Imrah,'),
('1CH', 7, 37, '1CH.7.37', 'Bezer, Hod, Shamma, Shilshah, Ithran, and Beera.'),
('1CH', 7, 38, '1CH.7.38', 'The sons of Jether: Jephunneh, Pispa, and Ara.'),
('1CH', 7, 39, '1CH.7.39', 'The sons of Ulla: Arah, Hanniel, and Rizia.'),
('1CH', 7, 40, '1CH.7.40', 'All these were the descendants of Asher—heads of their families, choice and mighty men of valor, and chiefs among the leaders. The number of men fit for battle, recorded in their genealogies, was 26,000.'),
('1CH', 8, 1, '1CH.8.1', 'Benjamin was the father of Bela his firstborn, Ashbel the second, Aharah the third,'),
('1CH', 8, 2, '1CH.8.2', 'Nohah the fourth, and Rapha the fifth.'),
('1CH', 8, 3, '1CH.8.3', 'The sons of Bela: Addar, Gera, Abihud,'),
('1CH', 8, 4, '1CH.8.4', 'Abishua, Naaman, Ahoah,'),
('1CH', 8, 5, '1CH.8.5', 'Gera, Shephuphan, and Huram.'),
('1CH', 8, 6, '1CH.8.6', 'These were the descendants of Ehud who were the heads of the families living in Geba and were exiled to Manahath:'),
('1CH', 8, 7, '1CH.8.7', 'Naaman, Ahijah, and Gera, who carried them into exile and who was the father of Uzza and Ahihud.'),
('1CH', 8, 8, '1CH.8.8', 'Shaharaim had sons in the country of Moab after he had divorced his wives Hushim and Baara.'),
('1CH', 8, 9, '1CH.8.9', 'His sons by his wife Hodesh: Jobab, Zibia, Mesha, Malcam,'),
('1CH', 8, 10, '1CH.8.10', 'Jeuz, Sachia, and Mirmah. These were his sons, heads of families.'),
('1CH', 8, 11, '1CH.8.11', 'He also had sons by Hushim: Abitub and Elpaal.'),
('1CH', 8, 12, '1CH.8.12', 'The sons of Elpaal: Eber, Misham, Shemed (who built Ono and Lod with its villages),'),
('1CH', 8, 13, '1CH.8.13', 'and Beriah and Shema (who were the heads of families living in Aijalon and who drove out the inhabitants of Gath).'),
('1CH', 8, 14, '1CH.8.14', 'Ahio, Shashak, Jeremoth,'),
('1CH', 8, 15, '1CH.8.15', 'Zebadiah, Arad, Eder,'),
('1CH', 8, 16, '1CH.8.16', 'Michael, Ishpah, and Joha were the sons of Beriah.'),
('1CH', 8, 17, '1CH.8.17', 'Zebadiah, Meshullam, Hizki, Heber,'),
('1CH', 8, 18, '1CH.8.18', 'Ishmerai, Izliah, and Jobab were the sons of Elpaal.'),
('1CH', 8, 19, '1CH.8.19', 'Jakim, Zichri, Zabdi,'),
('1CH', 8, 20, '1CH.8.20', 'Elienai, Zillethai, Eliel,'),
('1CH', 8, 21, '1CH.8.21', 'Adaiah, Beraiah, and Shimrath were the sons of Shimei.'),
('1CH', 8, 22, '1CH.8.22', 'Ishpan, Eber, Eliel,'),
('1CH', 8, 23, '1CH.8.23', 'Abdon, Zichri, Hanan,'),
('1CH', 8, 24, '1CH.8.24', 'Hananiah, Elam, Anthothijah,'),
('1CH', 8, 25, '1CH.8.25', 'Iphdeiah, and Penuel were the sons of Shashak.'),
('1CH', 8, 26, '1CH.8.26', 'Shamsherai, Shehariah, Athaliah,'),
('1CH', 8, 27, '1CH.8.27', 'Jaareshiah, Elijah, and Zichri were the sons of Jeroham.'),
('1CH', 8, 28, '1CH.8.28', 'All these were heads of families, the chiefs according to their genealogies, and they lived in Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 8, 29, '1CH.8.29', 'Jeiel the father of Gibeon lived in Gibeon. His wife’s name was Maacah,'),
('1CH', 8, 30, '1CH.8.30', 'and Abdon was his firstborn son, then Zur, Kish, Baal, Nadab,'),
('1CH', 8, 31, '1CH.8.31', 'Gedor, Ahio, Zecher,'),
('1CH', 8, 32, '1CH.8.32', 'and Mikloth, who was the father of Shimeah. They too lived alongside their relatives in Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 8, 33, '1CH.8.33', 'Ner was the father of Kish, Kish was the father of Saul, and Saul was the father of Jonathan, Malchishua, Abinadab, and Esh-baal.'),
('1CH', 8, 34, '1CH.8.34', 'The son of Jonathan: Merib-baal, and Merib-baal was the father of Micah.'),
('1CH', 8, 35, '1CH.8.35', 'The sons of Micah: Pithon, Melech, Tarea, and Ahaz.'),
('1CH', 8, 36, '1CH.8.36', 'Ahaz was the father of Jehoaddah, Jehoaddah was the father of Alemeth, Azmaveth, and Zimri, and Zimri was the father of Moza.'),
('1CH', 8, 37, '1CH.8.37', 'Moza was the father of Binea. Raphah was his son, Eleasah his son, and Azel his son.'),
('1CH', 8, 38, '1CH.8.38', 'Azel had six sons, and these were their names: Azrikam, Bocheru, Ishmael, Sheariah, Obadiah, and Hanan. All these were the sons of Azel.'),
('1CH', 8, 39, '1CH.8.39', 'The sons of his brother Eshek: Ulam was his firstborn, Jeush second, and Eliphelet third.'),
('1CH', 8, 40, '1CH.8.40', 'The sons of Ulam were mighty men of valor, archers, and they had many sons and grandsons—150 in all. All these were the descendants of Benjamin.'),
('1CH', 9, 1, '1CH.9.1', 'So all Israel was recorded in the genealogies written in the Book of the Kings of Israel. But Judah was exiled to Babylon because of their unfaithfulness.'),
('1CH', 9, 2, '1CH.9.2', 'Now the first to resettle their own property in their cities were Israelites, priests, Levites, and temple servants.'),
('1CH', 9, 3, '1CH.9.3', 'Some of the descendants of Judah, Benjamin, Ephraim, and Manasseh lived in Jerusalem:'),
('1CH', 9, 4, '1CH.9.4', 'Uthai son of Ammihud, the son of Omri, the son of Imri, the son of Bani, a descendant of Perez son of Judah.'),
('1CH', 9, 5, '1CH.9.5', 'From the Shilonites: Asaiah the firstborn and his sons.'),
('1CH', 9, 6, '1CH.9.6', 'From the Zerahites: Jeuel and 690 relatives.'),
('1CH', 9, 7, '1CH.9.7', 'From the Benjamites: Sallu son of Meshullam, the son of Hodaviah, the son of Hassenuah;'),
('1CH', 9, 8, '1CH.9.8', 'Ibneiah son of Jeroham; Elah son of Uzzi, the son of Michri; Meshullam son of Shephatiah, the son of Reuel, the son of Ibnijah;'),
('1CH', 9, 9, '1CH.9.9', 'and 956 of their relatives according to their genealogy. All these men were heads of their families.'),
('1CH', 9, 10, '1CH.9.10', 'From the priests: Jedaiah, Jehoiarib, and Jachin;'),
('1CH', 9, 11, '1CH.9.11', 'Azariah son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, the chief official of God’s temple;'),
('1CH', 9, 12, '1CH.9.12', 'Adaiah son of Jeroham, the son of Pashhur, the son of Malchijah; Maasai son of Adiel, the son of Jahzerah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Meshillemith, the son of Immer;'),
('1CH', 9, 13, '1CH.9.13', 'and 1,760 of their relatives, the heads of their families, able men for the work of the service of the house of God.'),
('1CH', 9, 14, '1CH.9.14', 'From the Levites: Shemaiah son of Hasshub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, a descendant of Merari;'),
('1CH', 9, 15, '1CH.9.15', 'Bakbakkar, Heresh, Galal, and Mattaniah son of Mica, the son of Zichri, the son of Asaph;'),
('1CH', 9, 16, '1CH.9.16', 'Obadiah son of Shemaiah, the son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun; and Berechiah son of Asa, the son of Elkanah, who lived in the villages of the Netophathites.'),
('1CH', 9, 17, '1CH.9.17', 'These were the gatekeepers: Shallum, Akkub, Talmon, Ahiman, and their relatives. Shallum was their chief;'),
('1CH', 9, 18, '1CH.9.18', 'he was previously stationed at the King’s Gate on the east side. These were the gatekeepers from the camp of the Levites.'),
('1CH', 9, 19, '1CH.9.19', 'Shallum son of Kore, the son of Ebiasaph, the son of Korah, and his relatives from the Korahites were assigned to guard the thresholds of the Tent, just as their fathers had been assigned to guard the entrance to the dwelling of the LORD.'),
('1CH', 9, 20, '1CH.9.20', 'In earlier times Phinehas son of Eleazar had been in charge of the gatekeepers, and the LORD was with him.'),
('1CH', 9, 21, '1CH.9.21', 'Zechariah son of Meshelemiah was the gatekeeper at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.'),
('1CH', 9, 22, '1CH.9.22', 'The number of those chosen to be gatekeepers at the thresholds was 212. They were registered by genealogy in their villages. David and Samuel the seer had appointed them to their positions of trust.'),
('1CH', 9, 23, '1CH.9.23', 'So they and their descendants were assigned to guard the gates of the house of the LORD—the house called the Tent.'),
('1CH', 9, 24, '1CH.9.24', 'The gatekeepers were stationed on the four sides: east, west, north, and south.'),
('1CH', 9, 25, '1CH.9.25', 'Their relatives came from their villages at fixed times to serve with them for seven-day periods.'),
('1CH', 9, 26, '1CH.9.26', 'But the four chief gatekeepers, who were Levites, were entrusted with the rooms and the treasuries of the house of God.'),
('1CH', 9, 27, '1CH.9.27', 'They would spend the night stationed around the house of God, because they were responsible for guarding it and opening it every morning.'),
('1CH', 9, 28, '1CH.9.28', 'Some of them were in charge of the articles used in worship, to count them whenever they were brought in or taken out.'),
('1CH', 9, 29, '1CH.9.29', 'Others were put in charge of the furnishings and other articles of the sanctuary, as well as the fine flour, wine, oil, frankincense, and spices.'),
('1CH', 9, 30, '1CH.9.30', 'And some of the sons of the priests mixed the spices.'),
('1CH', 9, 31, '1CH.9.31', 'A Levite named Mattithiah, the firstborn son of Shallum the Korahite, was entrusted with baking the bread.'),
('1CH', 9, 32, '1CH.9.32', 'Some of their Kohathite relatives were responsible for preparing the rows of the showbread every Sabbath.'),
('1CH', 9, 33, '1CH.9.33', 'Those who were musicians, the heads of Levite families, stayed in the temple chambers and were exempt from other duties because they were on duty day and night.'),
('1CH', 9, 34, '1CH.9.34', 'All these were heads of Levite families, chiefs according to their genealogies, and they lived in Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 9, 35, '1CH.9.35', 'Jeiel the father of Gibeon lived in Gibeon. His wife’s name was Maacah.'),
('1CH', 9, 36, '1CH.9.36', 'Abdon was his firstborn son, then Zur, Kish, Baal, Ner, Nadab,'),
('1CH', 9, 37, '1CH.9.37', 'Gedor, Ahio, Zechariah, and Mikloth.'),
('1CH', 9, 38, '1CH.9.38', 'Mikloth was the father of Shimeam. They too lived alongside their relatives in Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 9, 39, '1CH.9.39', 'Ner was the father of Kish, Kish was the father of Saul, and Saul was the father of Jonathan, Malchishua, Abinadab, and Esh-baal.'),
('1CH', 9, 40, '1CH.9.40', 'The son of Jonathan: Merib-baal, who was the father of Micah.'),
('1CH', 9, 41, '1CH.9.41', 'The sons of Micah: Pithon, Melech, Tahrea, and Ahaz.'),
('1CH', 9, 42, '1CH.9.42', 'Ahaz was the father of Jarah; Jarah was the father of Alemeth, Azmaveth, and Zimri; and Zimri was the father of Moza.'),
('1CH', 9, 43, '1CH.9.43', 'Moza was the father of Binea. Rephaiah was his son, Elasah his son, and Azel his son.'),
('1CH', 9, 44, '1CH.9.44', 'And Azel had six sons, and these were their names: Azrikam, Bocheru, Ishmael, Sheariah, Obadiah, and Hanan. These were the sons of Azel.'),
('1CH', 10, 1, '1CH.10.1', 'Now the Philistines fought against Israel, and the men of Israel fled before them, and many fell slain on Mount Gilboa.'),
('1CH', 10, 2, '1CH.10.2', 'The Philistines followed hard after Saul and his sons, and they killed Saul’s sons Jonathan, Abinadab, and Malchishua.'),
('1CH', 10, 3, '1CH.10.3', 'When the battle intensified against Saul, the archers overtook him and wounded him.'),
('1CH', 10, 4, '1CH.10.4', 'Then Saul said to his armor-bearer, “Draw your sword and run me through with it, or these uncircumcised men will come and torture me!” But his armor-bearer was terrified and refused to do it. So Saul took his own sword and fell on it.'),
('1CH', 10, 5, '1CH.10.5', 'When his armor-bearer saw that Saul was dead, he too fell on his own sword and died.'),
('1CH', 10, 6, '1CH.10.6', 'So Saul died together with his three sons and all his house.'),
('1CH', 10, 7, '1CH.10.7', 'When all the Israelites in the valley saw that the army had fled and that Saul and his sons had died, they abandoned their cities and ran away. So the Philistines came and occupied their cities.'),
('1CH', 10, 8, '1CH.10.8', 'The next day, when the Philistines came to strip the dead, they found Saul and his sons fallen on Mount Gilboa.'),
('1CH', 10, 9, '1CH.10.9', 'They stripped Saul, cut off his head, took his armor, and sent messengers throughout the land of the Philistines to proclaim the news in the temple of their idols and among their people.'),
('1CH', 10, 10, '1CH.10.10', 'They put his armor in the temple of their gods and hung his head in the temple of Dagon.'),
('1CH', 10, 11, '1CH.10.11', 'When all the people of Jabesh-gilead heard about everything the Philistines had done to Saul,'),
('1CH', 10, 12, '1CH.10.12', 'all their men of valor set out and retrieved the bodies of Saul and his sons and brought them to Jabesh. And they buried their bones under the oak in Jabesh and fasted seven days.'),
('1CH', 10, 13, '1CH.10.13', 'So Saul died for his unfaithfulness to the LORD, because he did not keep the word of the LORD and even consulted a medium for guidance,'),
('1CH', 10, 14, '1CH.10.14', 'and he failed to inquire of the LORD. So the LORD put him to death and turned the kingdom over to David son of Jesse.'),
('1CH', 11, 1, '1CH.11.1', 'Then all Israel came together to David at Hebron and said, “Here we are, your own flesh and blood.'),
('1CH', 11, 2, '1CH.11.2', 'Even in times past, while Saul was king, you were the one who led Israel out and brought them back. And the LORD your God said, ‘You will shepherd My people Israel, and you will be ruler over them.’”'),
('1CH', 11, 3, '1CH.11.3', 'So all the elders of Israel came to the king at Hebron, where David made a covenant with them before the LORD. And they anointed him king over Israel, according to the word of the LORD through Samuel.'),
('1CH', 11, 4, '1CH.11.4', 'Then David and all the Israelites marched to Jerusalem (that is, Jebus), where the Jebusites inhabited the land.'),
('1CH', 11, 5, '1CH.11.5', 'The people of Jebus said to David, “You will never get in here.” Nevertheless, David captured the fortress of Zion (that is, the City of David).'),
('1CH', 11, 6, '1CH.11.6', 'Now David had said, “Whoever is the first to strike down a Jebusite will become chief commander.” And Joab son of Zeruiah went up first, and he became the chief.'),
('1CH', 11, 7, '1CH.11.7', 'So David took up residence in the fortress; that is why it was called the City of David.'),
('1CH', 11, 8, '1CH.11.8', 'He built up the city around it, from the supporting terraces to the surrounding wall, while Joab restored the rest of the city.'),
('1CH', 11, 9, '1CH.11.9', 'And David became greater and greater, for the LORD of Hosts was with him.'),
('1CH', 11, 10, '1CH.11.10', 'Now these were the chiefs of David’s mighty men, who, together with all Israel, bolstered and strengthened his kingdom, according to the word of the LORD concerning Israel.'),
('1CH', 11, 11, '1CH.11.11', 'This is the list of David’s mighty men: Jashobeam son of Hachmoni was chief of the officers; he wielded his spear against three hundred men, whom he killed at one time.'),
('1CH', 11, 12, '1CH.11.12', 'Next in command was Eleazar son of Dodo the Ahohite, one of the three mighty men.'),
('1CH', 11, 13, '1CH.11.13', 'He was with David at Pas-dammim when the Philistines gathered there for battle. At a place with a field full of barley, the troops fled from the Philistines.'),
('1CH', 11, 14, '1CH.11.14', 'But Eleazar and David stationed themselves in the middle of the field and defended it. They struck down the Philistines, and the LORD brought about a great victory.'),
('1CH', 11, 15, '1CH.11.15', 'Three of the thirty chief men went down to David, to the rock at the cave of Adullam, while a company of Philistines was encamped in the Valley of Rephaim.'),
('1CH', 11, 16, '1CH.11.16', 'At that time David was in the stronghold, and the garrison of the Philistines was at Bethlehem.'),
('1CH', 11, 17, '1CH.11.17', 'David longed for water and said, “Oh, that someone would get me a drink of water from the well near the gate of Bethlehem!”'),
('1CH', 11, 18, '1CH.11.18', 'So the Three broke through the Philistine camp, drew water from the well at the gate of Bethlehem, and brought it back to David. But he refused to drink it; instead, he poured it out to the LORD,'),
('1CH', 11, 19, '1CH.11.19', 'saying, “Far be it from me, my God, to do this! How can I drink the blood of these men who risked their lives?” Because they had brought it at the risk of their lives, David refused to drink it. Such were the exploits of the three mighty men.'),
('1CH', 11, 20, '1CH.11.20', 'Now Abishai, the brother of Joab, was chief of the Three, and he wielded his spear against three hundred men, killed them, and won a name along with the Three.'),
('1CH', 11, 21, '1CH.11.21', 'He was doubly honored above the Three, and he became their commander, even though he was not included among the Three.'),
('1CH', 11, 22, '1CH.11.22', 'And Benaiah son of Jehoiada was a man of valor from Kabzeel, a man of many exploits. He struck down two champions of Moab, and on a snowy day he went down into a pit and killed a lion.'),
('1CH', 11, 23, '1CH.11.23', 'He also struck down an Egyptian, a huge man five cubits tall. Although the Egyptian had a spear like a weaver’s beam in his hand, Benaiah went against him with a club, snatched the spear from his hand, and killed the Egyptian with his own spear.'),
('1CH', 11, 24, '1CH.11.24', 'These were the exploits of Benaiah son of Jehoiada, who won a name along with the three mighty men.'),
('1CH', 11, 25, '1CH.11.25', 'He was most honored among the Thirty, but he did not become one of the Three. And David appointed him over his guard.'),
('1CH', 11, 26, '1CH.11.26', 'Now these were the mighty men: Asahel the brother of Joab, Elhanan son of Dodo of Bethlehem,'),
('1CH', 11, 27, '1CH.11.27', 'Shammoth the Harorite, Helez the Pelonite,'),
('1CH', 11, 28, '1CH.11.28', 'Ira son of Ikkesh the Tekoite, Abiezer the Anathothite,'),
('1CH', 11, 29, '1CH.11.29', 'Sibbecai the Hushathite, Ilai the Ahohite,'),
('1CH', 11, 30, '1CH.11.30', 'Maharai the Netophathite, Heled son of Baanah the Netophathite,'),
('1CH', 11, 31, '1CH.11.31', 'Ithai son of Ribai from Gibeah of the Benjamites, Benaiah the Pirathonite,'),
('1CH', 11, 32, '1CH.11.32', 'Hurai from the brooks of Gaash, Abiel the Arbathite,'),
('1CH', 11, 33, '1CH.11.33', 'Azmaveth the Baharumite, Eliahba the Shaalbonite,'),
('1CH', 11, 34, '1CH.11.34', 'the sons of Hashem the Gizonite, Jonathan son of Shagee the Hararite,'),
('1CH', 11, 35, '1CH.11.35', 'Ahiam son of Sachar the Hararite, Eliphal son of Ur,'),
('1CH', 11, 36, '1CH.11.36', 'Hepher the Mecherathite, Ahijah the Pelonite,'),
('1CH', 11, 37, '1CH.11.37', 'Hezro the Carmelite, Naarai son of Ezbai,'),
('1CH', 11, 38, '1CH.11.38', 'Joel the brother of Nathan, Mibhar son of Hagri,'),
('1CH', 11, 39, '1CH.11.39', 'Zelek the Ammonite, Naharai the Beerothite, the armor-bearer of Joab son of Zeruiah,'),
('1CH', 11, 40, '1CH.11.40', 'Ira the Ithrite, Gareb the Ithrite,'),
('1CH', 11, 41, '1CH.11.41', 'Uriah the Hittite, Zabad son of Ahlai,'),
('1CH', 11, 42, '1CH.11.42', 'Adina son of Shiza the Reubenite, chief of the Reubenites, and the thirty with him,'),
('1CH', 11, 43, '1CH.11.43', 'Hanan son of Maacah, Joshaphat the Mithnite,'),
('1CH', 11, 44, '1CH.11.44', 'Uzzia the Ashterathite, Shama and Jeiel the sons of Hotham the Aroerite,'),
('1CH', 11, 45, '1CH.11.45', 'Jediael son of Shimri and his brother Joha the Tizite,'),
('1CH', 11, 46, '1CH.11.46', 'Eliel the Mahavite, Jeribai and Joshaviah, the sons of Elnaam, Ithmah the Moabite,'),
('1CH', 11, 47, '1CH.11.47', 'Eliel, Obed, and Jaasiel the Mezobaite.'),
('1CH', 12, 1, '1CH.12.1', 'Now these were the men who came to David at Ziklag, while he was still banished from the presence of Saul son of Kish (they were among the mighty men who helped him in battle;'),
('1CH', 12, 2, '1CH.12.2', 'they were archers using both the right and left hands to sling stones and shoot arrows; and they were Saul’s kinsmen from Benjamin):'),
('1CH', 12, 3, '1CH.12.3', 'Ahiezer their chief and Joash, who were the sons of Shemaah the Gibeathite; Jeziel and Pelet, the sons of Azmaveth; Beracah; Jehu the Anathothite;'),
('1CH', 12, 4, '1CH.12.4', 'Ishmaiah the Gibeonite, a mighty man among the Thirty and a leader over the Thirty; Jeremiah, Jahaziel, Johanan, and Jozabad the Gederathite;'),
('1CH', 12, 5, '1CH.12.5', 'Eluzai, Jerimoth, Bealiah, Shemariah, and Shephatiah the Haruphite;'),
('1CH', 12, 6, '1CH.12.6', 'Elkanah, Isshiah, Azarel, Joezer, and Jashobeam, who were Korahites;'),
('1CH', 12, 7, '1CH.12.7', 'and Joelah and Zebadiah, the sons of Jeroham from Gedor.'),
('1CH', 12, 8, '1CH.12.8', 'Some Gadites defected to David at his stronghold in the wilderness. They were mighty men of valor, trained for battle, experts with the shield and spear, whose faces were like the faces of lions and who were as swift as gazelles on the mountains:'),
('1CH', 12, 9, '1CH.12.9', 'Ezer the chief, Obadiah the second in command, Eliab the third,'),
('1CH', 12, 10, '1CH.12.10', 'Mishmannah the fourth, Jeremiah the fifth,'),
('1CH', 12, 11, '1CH.12.11', 'Attai the sixth, Eliel the seventh,'),
('1CH', 12, 12, '1CH.12.12', 'Johanan the eighth, Elzabad the ninth,'),
('1CH', 12, 13, '1CH.12.13', 'Jeremiah the tenth, and Machbanai the eleventh.'),
('1CH', 12, 14, '1CH.12.14', 'These Gadites were army commanders, the least of whom was a match for a hundred, and the greatest for a thousand.'),
('1CH', 12, 15, '1CH.12.15', 'These are the ones who crossed the Jordan in the first month when it was overflowing all its banks, and they put to flight all those in the valleys, both to the east and to the west.'),
('1CH', 12, 16, '1CH.12.16', 'Other Benjamites and some men from Judah also came to David in his stronghold.'),
('1CH', 12, 17, '1CH.12.17', 'And David went out to meet them, saying, “If you have come to me in peace to help me, my heart will be united with you; but if you have come to betray me to my enemies when my hands are free of violence, may the God of our fathers see it and judge you.”'),
('1CH', 12, 18, '1CH.12.18', 'Then the Spirit came upon Amasai, the chief of the Thirty, and he said: “We are yours, O David! We are with you, O son of Jesse! Peace, peace to you, and peace to your helpers, for your God helps you.” So David received them and made them leaders of his troops.'),
('1CH', 12, 19, '1CH.12.19', 'Some from Manasseh defected to David when he went with the Philistines to fight against Saul. (They did not help the Philistines because the Philistine rulers consulted and sent David away, saying, “It will cost us our heads if he defects to his master Saul.”)'),
('1CH', 12, 20, '1CH.12.20', 'When David went to Ziklag, these men of Manasseh defected to him: Adnah, Jozabad, Jediael, Michael, Jozabad, Elihu, and Zillethai, chiefs of thousands in Manasseh.'),
('1CH', 12, 21, '1CH.12.21', 'They helped David against the raiders, for they were all mighty men of valor and commanders in the army.'),
('1CH', 12, 22, '1CH.12.22', 'For at that time men came to David day after day to help him, until he had a great army, like the army of God.'),
('1CH', 12, 23, '1CH.12.23', 'Now these are the numbers of men armed for battle who came to David at Hebron to turn Saul’s kingdom over to him, in accordance with the word of the LORD:'),
('1CH', 12, 24, '1CH.12.24', 'From Judah: 6,800 armed troops bearing shields and spears.'),
('1CH', 12, 25, '1CH.12.25', 'From Simeon: 7,100 mighty men of valor, ready for battle.'),
('1CH', 12, 26, '1CH.12.26', 'From Levi: 4,600,'),
('1CH', 12, 27, '1CH.12.27', 'including Jehoiada, leader of the house of Aaron, with 3,700 men,'),
('1CH', 12, 28, '1CH.12.28', 'and Zadok, a mighty young man of valor, with 22 commanders from his own family.'),
('1CH', 12, 29, '1CH.12.29', 'From Benjamin, the kinsmen of Saul: 3,000, most of whom had remained loyal to the house of Saul up to that time.'),
('1CH', 12, 30, '1CH.12.30', 'From Ephraim: 20,800 mighty men of valor, famous among their own clans.'),
('1CH', 12, 31, '1CH.12.31', 'From the half-tribe of Manasseh: 18,000 designated by name to come and make David king.'),
('1CH', 12, 32, '1CH.12.32', 'From Issachar, men who understood the times and knew what Israel should do: 200 chiefs with all their kinsmen at their command.'),
('1CH', 12, 33, '1CH.12.33', 'From Zebulun: 50,000 fit for service, trained for battle with all kinds of weapons of war, who with one purpose were devoted to David.'),
('1CH', 12, 34, '1CH.12.34', 'From Naphtali: 1,000 commanders, accompanied by 37,000 men with shield and spear.'),
('1CH', 12, 35, '1CH.12.35', 'From Dan: 28,600 prepared for battle.'),
('1CH', 12, 36, '1CH.12.36', 'From Asher: 40,000 fit for service, prepared for battle.'),
('1CH', 12, 37, '1CH.12.37', 'And from east of the Jordan, from Reuben, Gad, and the half-tribe of Manasseh there: 120,000 armed with every kind of weapon of war.'),
('1CH', 12, 38, '1CH.12.38', 'All these men of war, arrayed for battle, came to Hebron fully determined to make David king over all Israel. And all the rest of the Israelites were of one mind to make David king.'),
('1CH', 12, 39, '1CH.12.39', 'They spent three days there eating and drinking with David, for their relatives had provided for them.'),
('1CH', 12, 40, '1CH.12.40', 'And their neighbors from as far away as Issachar, Zebulun, and Naphtali came bringing food on donkeys, camels, mules, and oxen—abundant supplies of flour, fig cakes and raisin cakes, wine and oil, oxen and sheep. Indeed, there was joy in Israel.'),
('1CH', 13, 1, '1CH.13.1', 'Then David conferred with all his leaders, the commanders of thousands and of hundreds.'),
('1CH', 13, 2, '1CH.13.2', 'And he said to the whole assembly of Israel, “If it seems good to you, and if this is of the LORD our God, let us send word far and wide to the rest of our brothers in all the land of Israel, and also to the priests and Levites in their cities and pasturelands, so that they may join us.'),
('1CH', 13, 3, '1CH.13.3', 'Then let us bring back the ark of our God, for we did not inquire of Him in the days of Saul.”'),
('1CH', 13, 4, '1CH.13.4', 'And because this proposal seemed right to all the people, the whole assembly agreed to it.'),
('1CH', 13, 5, '1CH.13.5', 'So David assembled all Israel, from the River Shihor in Egypt to Lebo-hamath, to bring the ark of God from Kiriath-jearim.'),
('1CH', 13, 6, '1CH.13.6', 'David and all Israel went up to Baalah of Judah (that is, Kiriath-jearim) to bring up from there the ark of God the LORD, who is enthroned between the cherubim—the ark that is called by the Name.'),
('1CH', 13, 7, '1CH.13.7', 'So they carried the ark of God from the house of Abinadab on a new cart, with Uzzah and Ahio guiding the cart.'),
('1CH', 13, 8, '1CH.13.8', 'David and all the Israelites were celebrating before God with all their might, with songs and on harps and lyres, with tambourines, cymbals, and trumpets.'),
('1CH', 13, 9, '1CH.13.9', 'When they came to the threshing floor of Chidon, Uzzah reached out and took hold of the ark, because the oxen had stumbled.'),
('1CH', 13, 10, '1CH.13.10', 'And the anger of the LORD burned against Uzzah, and He struck him down because he had put his hand on the ark. So he died there before God.'),
('1CH', 13, 11, '1CH.13.11', 'Then David became angry because the LORD had burst forth against Uzzah. So he named that place Perez-uzzah, as it is called to this day.'),
('1CH', 13, 12, '1CH.13.12', 'That day David feared God and asked, “How can I ever bring the ark of God to me?”'),
('1CH', 13, 13, '1CH.13.13', 'So he did not move the ark with him to the City of David; instead, he took it aside to the house of Obed-edom the Gittite.'),
('1CH', 13, 14, '1CH.13.14', 'Thus the ark of God remained with the family of Obed-edom in his house for three months, and the LORD blessed his household and everything he owned.'),
('1CH', 14, 1, '1CH.14.1', 'Now Hiram king of Tyre sent envoys to David, along with cedar logs, stonemasons, and carpenters, to build a palace for him.'),
('1CH', 14, 2, '1CH.14.2', 'And David realized that the LORD had established him as king over Israel and had highly exalted his kingdom for the sake of His people Israel.'),
('1CH', 14, 3, '1CH.14.3', 'And David took more wives in Jerusalem and became the father of more sons and daughters.'),
('1CH', 14, 4, '1CH.14.4', 'These are the names of the children born to him in Jerusalem: Shammua, Shobab, Nathan, Solomon,'),
('1CH', 14, 5, '1CH.14.5', 'Ibhar, Elishua, Elpelet,'),
('1CH', 14, 6, '1CH.14.6', 'Nogah, Nepheg, Japhia,'),
('1CH', 14, 7, '1CH.14.7', 'Elishama, Beeliada, and Eliphelet.'),
('1CH', 14, 8, '1CH.14.8', 'When the Philistines heard that David had been anointed king over all Israel, they all went in search of him; but David learned of this and went out to face them.'),
('1CH', 14, 9, '1CH.14.9', 'Now the Philistines had come and raided the Valley of Rephaim.'),
('1CH', 14, 10, '1CH.14.10', 'So David inquired of God, “Should I go up against the Philistines? Will You deliver them into my hand?” “Go,” replied the LORD, “for I will deliver them into your hand.”'),
('1CH', 14, 11, '1CH.14.11', 'So David and his men went up to Baal-perazim, where he defeated the Philistines and said, “Like a bursting flood, God has burst out against my enemies by my hand.” So they called that place Baal-perazim.'),
('1CH', 14, 12, '1CH.14.12', 'There the Philistines abandoned their gods, and David ordered that they be burned in the fire.'),
('1CH', 14, 13, '1CH.14.13', 'Once again the Philistines raided the valley.'),
('1CH', 14, 14, '1CH.14.14', 'So David again inquired of God, who answered him, “Do not march up after them, but circle around them and attack them in front of the balsam trees.'),
('1CH', 14, 15, '1CH.14.15', 'As soon as you hear the sound of marching in the tops of the balsam trees, move out to battle, because this will mean that God has gone out before you to strike the camp of the Philistines.”'),
('1CH', 14, 16, '1CH.14.16', 'So David did as God had commanded him, and they struck down the army of the Philistines all the way from Gibeon to Gezer.'),
('1CH', 14, 17, '1CH.14.17', 'And David’s fame went out into every land, and the LORD caused all nations to fear him.'),
('1CH', 15, 1, '1CH.15.1', 'David constructed buildings for himself in the City of David, and he prepared a place for the ark of God and pitched a tent for it.'),
('1CH', 15, 2, '1CH.15.2', 'Then David said, “No one but the Levites may carry the ark of God, because the LORD has chosen them to carry the ark of the LORD and to minister before Him forever.”'),
('1CH', 15, 3, '1CH.15.3', 'And David assembled all Israel in Jerusalem to bring up the ark of the LORD to the place he had prepared for it.'),
('1CH', 15, 4, '1CH.15.4', 'Then he gathered together the descendants of Aaron and the Levites:'),
('1CH', 15, 5, '1CH.15.5', 'From the Kohathites, Uriel the chief and 120 of his relatives;'),
('1CH', 15, 6, '1CH.15.6', 'from the Merarites, Asaiah the chief and 220 of his relatives;'),
('1CH', 15, 7, '1CH.15.7', 'from the Gershomites, Joel the chief and 130 of his relatives;'),
('1CH', 15, 8, '1CH.15.8', 'from the Elizaphanites, Shemaiah the chief and 200 of his relatives;'),
('1CH', 15, 9, '1CH.15.9', 'from the Hebronites, Eliel the chief and 80 of his relatives;'),
('1CH', 15, 10, '1CH.15.10', 'and from the Uzzielites, Amminadab the chief and 112 of his relatives.'),
('1CH', 15, 11, '1CH.15.11', 'David summoned the priests Zadok and Abiathar and the Levites Uriel, Asaiah, Joel, Shemaiah, Eliel, and Amminadab.'),
('1CH', 15, 12, '1CH.15.12', 'And he said to them, “You are the heads of the Levitical families. You and your relatives must consecrate yourselves so that you may bring the ark of the LORD, the God of Israel, to the place I have prepared for it.'),
('1CH', 15, 13, '1CH.15.13', 'It was because you Levites were not with us the first time that the LORD our God burst forth in anger against us. For we did not consult Him about the proper order.”'),
('1CH', 15, 14, '1CH.15.14', 'So the priests and Levites consecrated themselves to bring up the ark of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('1CH', 15, 15, '1CH.15.15', 'And the Levites carried the ark of God on their shoulders with the poles, as Moses had commanded in accordance with the word of the LORD.'),
('1CH', 15, 16, '1CH.15.16', 'David also told the leaders of the Levites to appoint their relatives as singers to lift up their voices with joy, accompanied by musical instruments—harps, lyres, and cymbals.'),
('1CH', 15, 17, '1CH.15.17', 'So the Levites appointed Heman son of Joel; from his brothers, Asaph son of Berechiah; from their brothers the Merarites, Ethan son of Kushaiah;'),
('1CH', 15, 18, '1CH.15.18', 'and with them their brothers next in rank: Zechariah, Jaaziel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Unni, Eliab, Benaiah, Maaseiah, Mattithiah, Eliphelehu, Mikneiah, and the gatekeepers Obed-edom and Jeiel.'),
('1CH', 15, 19, '1CH.15.19', 'The musicians Heman, Asaph, and Ethan were to sound the bronze cymbals.'),
('1CH', 15, 20, '1CH.15.20', 'Zechariah, Aziel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Unni, Eliab, Maaseiah, and Benaiah were to play the harps according to Alamoth.'),
('1CH', 15, 21, '1CH.15.21', 'And Mattithiah, Eliphelehu, Mikneiah, Obed-edom, Jeiel, and Azaziah were to lead the music with lyres according to Sheminith.'),
('1CH', 15, 22, '1CH.15.22', 'Chenaniah the head Levite was the director of the music because he was highly skilled.'),
('1CH', 15, 23, '1CH.15.23', 'Berechiah and Elkanah were to be guardians of the ark.'),
('1CH', 15, 24, '1CH.15.24', 'Shebaniah, Joshaphat, Nethanel, Amasai, Zechariah, Benaiah, and Eliezer—the priests—were to blow the trumpets before the ark of God. Obed-edom and Jehiah were also to be guardians of the ark.'),
('1CH', 15, 25, '1CH.15.25', 'So David, the elders of Israel, and the commanders of thousands went with rejoicing to bring the ark of the covenant of the LORD from the house of Obed-edom.'),
('1CH', 15, 26, '1CH.15.26', 'And because God helped the Levites who were carrying the ark of the covenant of the LORD, they sacrificed seven bulls and seven rams.'),
('1CH', 15, 27, '1CH.15.27', 'Now David was dressed in a robe of fine linen, as were all the Levites who were carrying the ark, as well as the singers and Chenaniah, the director of music for the singers. David also wore a linen ephod.'),
('1CH', 15, 28, '1CH.15.28', 'So all Israel brought up the ark of the covenant of the LORD with shouting, with the sounding of rams’ horns and trumpets, and with cymbals and the music of harps and lyres.'),
('1CH', 15, 29, '1CH.15.29', 'As the ark of the covenant of the LORD was entering the City of David, Saul’s daughter Michal looked down from a window and saw King David dancing and celebrating, and she despised him in her heart.'),
('1CH', 16, 1, '1CH.16.1', 'So they brought the ark of God and placed it inside the tent that David had pitched for it. And they presented burnt offerings and peace offerings before God.'),
('1CH', 16, 2, '1CH.16.2', 'When David had finished sacrificing the burnt offerings and peace offerings, he blessed the people in the name of the LORD.'),
('1CH', 16, 3, '1CH.16.3', 'Then he distributed to every man and woman of Israel a loaf of bread, a date cake, and a raisin cake.'),
('1CH', 16, 4, '1CH.16.4', 'David appointed some of the Levites to minister before the ark of the LORD, to celebrate, to give thanks, and to praise the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('1CH', 16, 5, '1CH.16.5', 'Asaph was the chief, Zechariah was second, then Jeiel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Mattithiah, Eliab, Benaiah, Obed-edom, and Jeiel. They were to play the harps and lyres, while Asaph sounded the cymbals'),
('1CH', 16, 6, '1CH.16.6', 'and the priests Benaiah and Jahaziel blew the trumpets regularly before the ark of the covenant of God.'),
('1CH', 16, 7, '1CH.16.7', 'On that day David first committed to Asaph and his associates this song of thanksgiving to the LORD:'),
('1CH', 16, 8, '1CH.16.8', '“Give thanks to the LORD; call upon His name; make known His deeds among the nations.'),
('1CH', 16, 9, '1CH.16.9', 'Sing to Him, sing praises to Him; tell of all His wonders.'),
('1CH', 16, 10, '1CH.16.10', 'Glory in His holy name; let the hearts of those who seek the LORD rejoice.'),
('1CH', 16, 11, '1CH.16.11', 'Seek out the LORD and His strength; seek His face always.'),
('1CH', 16, 12, '1CH.16.12', 'Remember the wonders He has done, His marvels, and the judgments He has pronounced,'),
('1CH', 16, 13, '1CH.16.13', 'O offspring of His servant Israel, O sons of Jacob, His chosen ones.'),
('1CH', 16, 14, '1CH.16.14', 'He is the LORD our God; His judgments carry throughout the earth.'),
('1CH', 16, 15, '1CH.16.15', 'Remember His covenant forever, the word He ordained for a thousand generations—'),
('1CH', 16, 16, '1CH.16.16', 'the covenant He made with Abraham, and the oath He swore to Isaac.'),
('1CH', 16, 17, '1CH.16.17', 'He confirmed it to Jacob as a decree, to Israel as an everlasting covenant:'),
('1CH', 16, 18, '1CH.16.18', '‘I will give you the land of Canaan as the portion of your inheritance.’'),
('1CH', 16, 19, '1CH.16.19', 'When they were few in number, few indeed, and strangers in the land,'),
('1CH', 16, 20, '1CH.16.20', 'they wandered from nation to nation, from one kingdom to another.'),
('1CH', 16, 21, '1CH.16.21', 'He let no man oppress them; He rebuked kings on their behalf:'),
('1CH', 16, 22, '1CH.16.22', '‘Do not touch My anointed ones! Do no harm to My prophets!’'),
('1CH', 16, 23, '1CH.16.23', 'Sing to the LORD, all the earth. Proclaim His salvation day after day.'),
('1CH', 16, 24, '1CH.16.24', 'Declare His glory among the nations, His wonders among all peoples.'),
('1CH', 16, 25, '1CH.16.25', 'For great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised; He is to be feared above all gods.'),
('1CH', 16, 26, '1CH.16.26', 'For all the gods of the nations are idols, but it is the LORD who made the heavens.'),
('1CH', 16, 27, '1CH.16.27', 'Splendor and majesty are before Him; strength and joy fill His dwelling.'),
('1CH', 16, 28, '1CH.16.28', 'Ascribe to the LORD, O families of the nations, ascribe to the LORD glory and strength.'),
('1CH', 16, 29, '1CH.16.29', 'Ascribe to the LORD the glory due His name; bring an offering and come before Him. Worship the LORD in the splendor of His holiness;'),
('1CH', 16, 30, '1CH.16.30', 'tremble before Him, all the earth. The world is firmly established; it cannot be moved.'),
('1CH', 16, 31, '1CH.16.31', 'Let the heavens be glad, and the earth rejoice. Let them say among the nations, ‘The LORD reigns!’'),
('1CH', 16, 32, '1CH.16.32', 'Let the sea resound, and all that fills it; let the fields exult, and all that is in them.'),
('1CH', 16, 33, '1CH.16.33', 'Then the trees of the forest will sing for joy before the LORD, for He is coming to judge the earth.'),
('1CH', 16, 34, '1CH.16.34', 'Give thanks to the LORD, for He is good; His loving devotion endures forever.'),
('1CH', 16, 35, '1CH.16.35', 'Then cry out: ‘Save us, O God of our salvation; gather and deliver us from the nations, that we may give thanks to Your holy name, that we may glory in Your praise.’'),
('1CH', 16, 36, '1CH.16.36', 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, from everlasting to everlasting.” Then all the people said, “Amen!” and “Praise the LORD!”'),
('1CH', 16, 37, '1CH.16.37', 'So David left Asaph and his associates there before the ark of the covenant of the LORD, to minister there regularly according to the daily requirements,'),
('1CH', 16, 38, '1CH.16.38', 'along with Obed-edom and his sixty-eight relatives. Obed-edom son of Jeduthun, and also Hosah, were to be gatekeepers.'),
('1CH', 16, 39, '1CH.16.39', 'And David left Zadok the priest and his fellow priests before the tabernacle of the LORD at the high place in Gibeon'),
('1CH', 16, 40, '1CH.16.40', 'to regularly present burnt offerings to the LORD on the altar of burnt offerings, morning and evening, according to all that was written in the Law of the LORD, which He had commanded Israel to keep.'),
('1CH', 16, 41, '1CH.16.41', 'With them were Heman, Jeduthun, and the rest of those chosen and designated by name to give thanks to the LORD, for “His loving devotion endures forever.”'),
('1CH', 16, 42, '1CH.16.42', 'Heman and Jeduthun had with them trumpets and cymbals for the music and instruments for the songs of God. And the sons of Jeduthun were stationed at the gate.'),
('1CH', 16, 43, '1CH.16.43', 'Then all the people departed for their homes, and David returned home to bless his household.'),
('1CH', 17, 1, '1CH.17.1', 'After David had settled into his palace, he said to Nathan the prophet, “Here I am, living in a house of cedar, while the ark of the covenant of the LORD is under a tent.”'),
('1CH', 17, 2, '1CH.17.2', 'And Nathan replied to David, “Do all that is in your heart, for God is with you.”'),
('1CH', 17, 3, '1CH.17.3', 'But that night the word of God came to Nathan, saying,'),
('1CH', 17, 4, '1CH.17.4', '“Go and tell My servant David that this is what the LORD says: You are not the one to build Me a house in which to dwell.'),
('1CH', 17, 5, '1CH.17.5', 'For I have not dwelt in a house from the day I brought Israel up out of Egypt until this day, but I have moved from tent to tent and dwelling to dwelling.'),
('1CH', 17, 6, '1CH.17.6', 'In all My journeys with all the Israelites, have I ever asked any of the leaders I appointed to shepherd My people, ‘Why haven’t you built Me a house of cedar?’'),
('1CH', 17, 7, '1CH.17.7', 'Now then, you are to tell My servant David that this is what the LORD of Hosts says: I took you from the pasture, from following the flock, to be the ruler over My people Israel.'),
('1CH', 17, 8, '1CH.17.8', 'I have been with you wherever you have gone, and I have cut off all your enemies from before you. Now I will make for you a name like that of the greatest in the land.'),
('1CH', 17, 9, '1CH.17.9', 'And I will provide a place for My people Israel and will plant them so that they may dwell in a place of their own and be disturbed no more. No longer will the sons of wickedness oppress them as they did at the beginning'),
('1CH', 17, 10, '1CH.17.10', 'and have done since the day I appointed judges over My people Israel. And I will subdue all your enemies. Moreover, I declare to you that the LORD will build a house for you.'),
('1CH', 17, 11, '1CH.17.11', 'And when your days are fulfilled and you go to be with your fathers, I will raise up your descendant after you, one of your own sons, and I will establish his kingdom.'),
('1CH', 17, 12, '1CH.17.12', 'He will build a house for Me, and I will establish his throne forever.'),
('1CH', 17, 13, '1CH.17.13', 'I will be his Father, and he will be My son. And I will never remove My loving devotion from him as I removed it from your predecessor.'),
('1CH', 17, 14, '1CH.17.14', 'But I will set him over My house and My kingdom forever, and his throne will be established forever.”'),
('1CH', 17, 15, '1CH.17.15', 'So Nathan relayed to David all the words of this entire revelation.'),
('1CH', 17, 16, '1CH.17.16', 'Then King David went in, sat before the LORD, and said, “Who am I, O LORD God, and what is my house, that You have brought me this far?'),
('1CH', 17, 17, '1CH.17.17', 'And as if this was a small thing in Your eyes, O God, You have spoken about the future of the house of Your servant and have regarded me as a man of great distinction, O LORD God.'),
('1CH', 17, 18, '1CH.17.18', 'What more can David say to You for honoring Your servant? For You know Your servant,'),
('1CH', 17, 19, '1CH.17.19', 'O LORD. For the sake of Your servant and according to Your own heart, You have accomplished this great thing and made known all these great promises.'),
('1CH', 17, 20, '1CH.17.20', 'O LORD, there is none like You, and there is no God but You, according to everything we have heard with our own ears.'),
('1CH', 17, 21, '1CH.17.21', 'And who is like Your people Israel—the one nation on earth whom God went out to redeem as a people for Himself? You made a name for Yourself through great and awesome wonders by driving out nations from before Your people, whom You redeemed from Egypt.'),
('1CH', 17, 22, '1CH.17.22', 'For You have made Your people Israel Your very own forever, and You, O LORD, have become their God.'),
('1CH', 17, 23, '1CH.17.23', 'And now, O LORD, let the word You have spoken concerning Your servant and his house be established forever. Do as You have promised,'),
('1CH', 17, 24, '1CH.17.24', 'so that Your name will be established and magnified forever when it is said, ‘The LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, is God over Israel.’ And may the house of Your servant David be established before You.'),
('1CH', 17, 25, '1CH.17.25', 'For You, my God, have revealed to Your servant that You will build a house for him. Therefore Your servant has found the courage to pray before You.'),
('1CH', 17, 26, '1CH.17.26', 'And now, O LORD, You are God! And You have promised this goodness to Your servant.'),
('1CH', 17, 27, '1CH.17.27', 'So now You have been pleased to bless the house of Your servant, that it may continue forever before You. For You, O LORD, have blessed it, and it will be blessed forever.”'),
('1CH', 18, 1, '1CH.18.1', 'Some time later, David defeated the Philistines, subdued them, and took Gath and its villages from the hand of the Philistines.'),
('1CH', 18, 2, '1CH.18.2', 'David also defeated the Moabites, and they became subject to David and brought him tribute.'),
('1CH', 18, 3, '1CH.18.3', 'As far as Hamath, David also defeated King Hadadezer of Zobah, who had marched out to establish his dominion along the Euphrates River.'),
('1CH', 18, 4, '1CH.18.4', 'David captured from him a thousand chariots, seven thousand charioteers, and twenty thousand foot soldiers, and he hamstrung all the horses except a hundred he kept for the chariots.'),
('1CH', 18, 5, '1CH.18.5', 'When the Arameans of Damascus came to help King Hadadezer of Zobah, David struck down twenty-two thousand of their men.'),
('1CH', 18, 6, '1CH.18.6', 'Then he placed garrisons in Aram of Damascus, and the Arameans became subject to David and brought him tribute. So the LORD made David victorious wherever he went.'),
('1CH', 18, 7, '1CH.18.7', 'And David took the gold shields that belonged to the officers of Hadadezer and brought them to Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 18, 8, '1CH.18.8', 'And from Tibhath and Cun, cities of Hadadezer, David took a large amount of bronze, with which Solomon made the bronze Sea, the pillars, and various bronze articles.'),
('1CH', 18, 9, '1CH.18.9', 'When King Tou of Hamath heard that David had defeated the entire army of Hadadezer king of Zobah,'),
('1CH', 18, 10, '1CH.18.10', 'he sent his son Hadoram to greet King David and bless him for fighting and defeating Hadadezer, who had been at war with Tou. Hadoram brought all kinds of articles of gold and silver and bronze,'),
('1CH', 18, 11, '1CH.18.11', 'and King David dedicated these to the LORD, along with the silver and gold he had carried off from all these nations—from Edom and Moab, and from the Ammonites, Philistines, and Amalekites.'),
('1CH', 18, 12, '1CH.18.12', 'Moreover, Abishai son of Zeruiah struck down eighteen thousand Edomites in the Valley of Salt.'),
('1CH', 18, 13, '1CH.18.13', 'He placed garrisons in Edom, and all the Edomites were subject to David. So the LORD made David victorious wherever he went.'),
('1CH', 18, 14, '1CH.18.14', 'Thus David reigned over all Israel and administered justice and righteousness for all his people:'),
('1CH', 18, 15, '1CH.18.15', 'Joab son of Zeruiah was over the army; Jehoshaphat son of Ahilud was the recorder;'),
('1CH', 18, 16, '1CH.18.16', 'Zadok son of Ahitub and Ahimelech son of Abiathar were priests; Shavsha was the scribe;'),
('1CH', 18, 17, '1CH.18.17', 'Benaiah son of Jehoiada was over the Cherethites and Pelethites; and David’s sons were chief officials at the king’s side.'),
('1CH', 19, 1, '1CH.19.1', 'Some time later, Nahash king of the Ammonites died and was succeeded by his son.'),
('1CH', 19, 2, '1CH.19.2', 'And David said, “I will show kindness to Hanun son of Nahash, because his father showed kindness to me.” So David sent messengers to console Hanun concerning his father. But when David’s servants arrived in the land of the Ammonites to console him,'),
('1CH', 19, 3, '1CH.19.3', 'the princes of the Ammonites said to Hanun, “Just because David has sent you comforters, do you really believe he is showing respect for your father? Have not his servants come to you to explore the land, spy it out, and overthrow it?”'),
('1CH', 19, 4, '1CH.19.4', 'So Hanun took David’s servants, shaved their beards, cut off their garments at the hips, and sent them away.'),
('1CH', 19, 5, '1CH.19.5', 'When someone came and told David about his men, he sent messengers to meet them, since the men had been thoroughly humiliated. The king told them, “Stay in Jericho until your beards have grown back, and then return.”'),
('1CH', 19, 6, '1CH.19.6', 'When the Ammonites realized that they had become a stench to David, Hanun and the Ammonites sent a thousand talents of silver to hire for themselves chariots and horsemen from Aram-naharaim, Aram-maacah, and Zobah.'),
('1CH', 19, 7, '1CH.19.7', 'So they hired for themselves thirty-two thousand chariots, as well as the king of Maacah with his troops, who came and camped near Medeba while the Ammonites were mustered from their cities and marched out for battle.'),
('1CH', 19, 8, '1CH.19.8', 'On hearing this, David sent Joab and the entire army of mighty men.'),
('1CH', 19, 9, '1CH.19.9', 'The Ammonites marched out and arrayed themselves for battle at the entrance to the city, while the kings who had come stayed by themselves in the open country.'),
('1CH', 19, 10, '1CH.19.10', 'When Joab saw the battle lines before him and behind him, he selected some of the best men of Israel and arrayed them against the Arameans.'),
('1CH', 19, 11, '1CH.19.11', 'And he placed the rest of the troops under the command of his brother Abishai, who arrayed them against the Ammonites.'),
('1CH', 19, 12, '1CH.19.12', '“If the Arameans are too strong for me,” said Joab, “then you will come to my rescue. And if the Ammonites are too strong for you, then I will come to your rescue.'),
('1CH', 19, 13, '1CH.19.13', 'Be strong and let us fight bravely for our people and for the cities of our God. May the LORD do what is good in His sight.”'),
('1CH', 19, 14, '1CH.19.14', 'So Joab and his troops advanced to fight the Arameans, who fled before him.'),
('1CH', 19, 15, '1CH.19.15', 'When the Ammonites saw that the Arameans had fled, they too fled before Joab’s brother Abishai, and they entered the city. So Joab went back to Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 19, 16, '1CH.19.16', 'When the Arameans saw that they had been defeated by Israel, they sent messengers to bring more Arameans from beyond the Euphrates, with Shophach the commander of Hadadezer’s army leading them.'),
('1CH', 19, 17, '1CH.19.17', 'When this was reported to David, he gathered all Israel, crossed the Jordan, advanced toward the Arameans, and arrayed for battle against them. When David lined up to engage them in battle, they fought against him.'),
('1CH', 19, 18, '1CH.19.18', 'But the Arameans fled before Israel, and David killed seven thousand of their charioteers and forty thousand foot soldiers. He also killed Shophach the commander of their army.'),
('1CH', 19, 19, '1CH.19.19', 'When Hadadezer’s subjects saw that they had been defeated by Israel, they made peace with David and became subject to him. So the Arameans were unwilling to help the Ammonites anymore.'),
('1CH', 20, 1, '1CH.20.1', 'In the spring, at the time when kings march out to war, Joab led out the army and ravaged the land of the Ammonites. He came to Rabbah and besieged it, but David remained in Jerusalem. And Joab attacked Rabbah and demolished it.'),
('1CH', 20, 2, '1CH.20.2', 'Then David took the crown from the head of their king. It was found to weigh a talent of gold and was set with precious stones, and it was placed on David’s head. And David took a great amount of plunder from the city.'),
('1CH', 20, 3, '1CH.20.3', 'David brought out the people who were there and put them to work with saws, iron picks, and axes. And he did the same to all the Ammonite cities. Then David and all his troops returned to Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 20, 4, '1CH.20.4', 'Some time later, war broke out with the Philistines at Gezer. At that time Sibbecai the Hushathite killed Sippai, a descendant of the Rephaim, and the Philistines were subdued.'),
('1CH', 20, 5, '1CH.20.5', 'Once again there was a battle with the Philistines, and Elhanan son of Jair killed Lahmi the brother of Goliath the Gittite, the shaft of whose spear was like a weaver’s beam.'),
('1CH', 20, 6, '1CH.20.6', 'And there was also a battle at Gath, where there was a man of great stature with six fingers on each hand and six toes on each foot—twenty-four in all. He too was descended from Rapha,'),
('1CH', 20, 7, '1CH.20.7', 'and when he taunted Israel, Jonathan the son of David’s brother Shimei killed him.'),
('1CH', 20, 8, '1CH.20.8', 'So these descendants of Rapha in Gath fell at the hands of David and his servants.'),
('1CH', 21, 1, '1CH.21.1', 'Then Satan rose up against Israel and incited David to take a census of Israel.'),
('1CH', 21, 2, '1CH.21.2', 'So David said to Joab and the commanders of the troops, “Go and count the Israelites from Beersheba to Dan and bring me a report, so that I may know their number.”'),
('1CH', 21, 3, '1CH.21.3', 'But Joab replied, “May the LORD multiply His troops a hundred times over. My lord the king, are they not all servants of my lord? Why does my lord want to do this? Why should he bring guilt on Israel?”'),
('1CH', 21, 4, '1CH.21.4', 'Nevertheless, the king’s word prevailed against Joab. So Joab departed and traveled throughout Israel, and then he returned to Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 21, 5, '1CH.21.5', 'And Joab reported to David the total number of the troops. In all Israel there were 1,100,000 men who drew the sword, including 470,000 in Judah.'),
('1CH', 21, 6, '1CH.21.6', 'But Joab did not include Levi and Benjamin in the count, because the king’s command was detestable to him.'),
('1CH', 21, 7, '1CH.21.7', 'This command was also evil in the sight of God; so He struck Israel.'),
('1CH', 21, 8, '1CH.21.8', 'Then David said to God, “I have sinned greatly because I have done this thing. Now I beg You to take away the iniquity of Your servant, for I have acted very foolishly.”'),
('1CH', 21, 9, '1CH.21.9', 'And the LORD instructed Gad, David’s seer,'),
('1CH', 21, 10, '1CH.21.10', '“Go and tell David that this is what the LORD says: ‘I am offering you three options. Choose one of them, and I will carry it out against you.’”'),
('1CH', 21, 11, '1CH.21.11', 'So Gad went and said to David, “This is what the LORD says: ‘You must choose'),
('1CH', 21, 12, '1CH.21.12', 'between three years of famine, three months of being swept away before your enemies and overtaken by their swords, or three days of the sword of the LORD—days of plague upon the land, with the angel of the LORD ravaging every part of Israel.’ Now then, decide how I should reply to Him who sent me.”'),
('1CH', 21, 13, '1CH.21.13', 'David answered Gad, “I am deeply distressed. Please, let me fall into the hand of the LORD, for His mercies are very great; but do not let me fall into the hands of men.”'),
('1CH', 21, 14, '1CH.21.14', 'So the LORD sent a plague upon Israel, and seventy thousand men of Israel fell dead.'),
('1CH', 21, 15, '1CH.21.15', 'Then God sent an angel to destroy Jerusalem, but as the angel was doing so, the LORD saw it and relented from the calamity, and He said to the angel who was destroying the people, “Enough! Withdraw your hand now!” At that time the angel of the LORD was standing by the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.'),
('1CH', 21, 16, '1CH.21.16', 'When David lifted up his eyes and saw the angel of the LORD standing between heaven and earth, with a drawn sword in his hand stretched out over Jerusalem, David and the elders, clothed in sackcloth, fell facedown.'),
('1CH', 21, 17, '1CH.21.17', 'And David said to God, “Was it not I who gave the order to count the people? I am the one who has sinned and acted wickedly. But these sheep, what have they done? O LORD my God, please let Your hand fall upon me and my father’s house, but do not let this plague remain upon Your people.”'),
('1CH', 21, 18, '1CH.21.18', 'Then the angel of the LORD ordered Gad to tell David to go up and build an altar to the LORD on the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.'),
('1CH', 21, 19, '1CH.21.19', 'So David went up at the word that Gad had spoken in the name of the LORD.'),
('1CH', 21, 20, '1CH.21.20', 'Now Ornan was threshing wheat when he turned and saw the angel; and his four sons who were with him hid themselves.'),
('1CH', 21, 21, '1CH.21.21', 'David came to Ornan, and when Ornan looked out and saw David, he left the threshing floor and bowed facedown before David.'),
('1CH', 21, 22, '1CH.21.22', 'Then David said to Ornan, “Grant me the site of this threshing floor, that I may build an altar to the LORD. Sell it to me for the full price, so that the plague upon the people may be halted.”'),
('1CH', 21, 23, '1CH.21.23', 'Ornan said to David, “Take it! May my lord the king do whatever seems good to him. Look, I will give the oxen for the burnt offerings, the threshing sledges for the wood, and the wheat for the grain offering—I will give it all.”'),
('1CH', 21, 24, '1CH.21.24', '“No,” replied King David, “I insist on paying the full price, for I will not take for the LORD what belongs to you, nor will I offer burnt offerings that cost me nothing.”'),
('1CH', 21, 25, '1CH.21.25', 'So David paid Ornan six hundred shekels of gold for the site.'),
('1CH', 21, 26, '1CH.21.26', 'And there he built an altar to the LORD and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings. He called upon the LORD, who answered him with fire from heaven on the altar of burnt offering.'),
('1CH', 21, 27, '1CH.21.27', 'Then the LORD spoke to the angel, who put his sword back into its sheath.'),
('1CH', 21, 28, '1CH.21.28', 'At that time, when David saw that the LORD had answered him at the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite, he offered sacrifices there.'),
('1CH', 21, 29, '1CH.21.29', 'For the tabernacle of the LORD that Moses had made in the wilderness and the altar of burnt offering were presently at the high place in Gibeon,'),
('1CH', 21, 30, '1CH.21.30', 'but David could not go before it to inquire of God, because he was afraid of the sword of the angel of the LORD.'),
('1CH', 22, 1, '1CH.22.1', 'Then David said, “Here shall be the house of the LORD God, as well as the altar of burnt offering for Israel.”'),
('1CH', 22, 2, '1CH.22.2', 'So David gave orders to gather the foreigners in the land of Israel, from whom he appointed stonecutters to prepare finished stones for building the house of God.'),
('1CH', 22, 3, '1CH.22.3', 'David provided a large quantity of iron to make the nails for the doors of the gateways and for the fittings, together with more bronze than could be weighed'),
('1CH', 22, 4, '1CH.22.4', 'and more cedar logs than could be counted; for the Sidonians and Tyrians had brought a large quantity of cedar logs to David.'),
('1CH', 22, 5, '1CH.22.5', 'And David said, “My son Solomon is young and inexperienced, and the house to be built for the LORD must be exceedingly magnificent—famous and glorious throughout all lands. Therefore I must make preparations for it.” So David made lavish preparations before his death.'),
('1CH', 22, 6, '1CH.22.6', 'Then David called for his son Solomon and instructed him to build a house for the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('1CH', 22, 7, '1CH.22.7', '“My son,” said David to Solomon, “it was in my heart to build a house for the Name of the LORD my God,'),
('1CH', 22, 8, '1CH.22.8', 'but this word of the LORD came to me: ‘You have shed much blood and waged great wars. You are not to build a house for My Name because you have shed so much blood on the ground before Me.'),
('1CH', 22, 9, '1CH.22.9', 'But a son will be born to you who will be a man of rest. I will give him rest from all his enemies on every side; for his name will be Solomon, and I will grant to Israel peace and quiet during his reign.'),
('1CH', 22, 10, '1CH.22.10', 'He is the one who will build a house for My Name. He will be My son, and I will be his Father. And I will establish the throne of his kingdom over Israel forever.’'),
('1CH', 22, 11, '1CH.22.11', 'Now, my son, may the LORD be with you, and may you succeed in building the house of the LORD your God, as He said you would.'),
('1CH', 22, 12, '1CH.22.12', 'Above all, may the LORD give you insight and understanding when He puts you in command over Israel, so that you may keep the Law of the LORD your God.'),
('1CH', 22, 13, '1CH.22.13', 'Then you will succeed, if you carefully follow the statutes and ordinances that the LORD commanded Moses for Israel. Be strong and courageous. Do not be afraid or discouraged.'),
('1CH', 22, 14, '1CH.22.14', 'Now behold, I have taken great pains to provide for the house of the LORD—100,000 talents of gold, 1,000,000 talents of silver, and bronze and iron too great to be weighed. I have also provided timber and stone, and you may add to them.'),
('1CH', 22, 15, '1CH.22.15', 'You also have many workers: stonecutters, masons, carpenters, and men skilled in every kind of work—'),
('1CH', 22, 16, '1CH.22.16', 'in gold and silver, bronze and iron—craftsmen beyond number. Now begin the work, and may the LORD be with you.”'),
('1CH', 22, 17, '1CH.22.17', 'Then David ordered all the leaders of Israel to help his son Solomon:'),
('1CH', 22, 18, '1CH.22.18', '“Is not the LORD your God with you, and has He not granted you rest on every side? For He has given the inhabitants of the land into my hand, and the land has been subdued before the LORD and His people.'),
('1CH', 22, 19, '1CH.22.19', 'Now set your heart and soul to seek the LORD your God. Begin building the sanctuary of the LORD God, so that you may bring the ark of the covenant of the LORD and the holy articles of God into the temple that will be built for the Name of the LORD.”'),
('1CH', 23, 1, '1CH.23.1', 'When David was old and full of years, he installed his son Solomon as king over Israel.'),
('1CH', 23, 2, '1CH.23.2', 'Then he gathered all the leaders of Israel, as well as the priests and Levites.'),
('1CH', 23, 3, '1CH.23.3', 'The Levites thirty years of age or older were counted, and the total number of men was 38,000.'),
('1CH', 23, 4, '1CH.23.4', '“Of these,” said David, “24,000 are to oversee the work of the house of the LORD, 6,000 are to be officers and judges,'),
('1CH', 23, 5, '1CH.23.5', '4,000 are to be gatekeepers, and 4,000 are to praise the LORD with the instruments I have made for giving praise.”'),
('1CH', 23, 6, '1CH.23.6', 'Then David divided the Levites into divisions according to the sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.'),
('1CH', 23, 7, '1CH.23.7', 'The Gershonites: Ladan and Shimei.'),
('1CH', 23, 8, '1CH.23.8', 'The sons of Ladan: Jehiel the first, Zetham, and Joel—three in all.'),
('1CH', 23, 9, '1CH.23.9', 'The sons of Shimei: Shelomoth, Haziel, and Haran—three in all. These were the heads of the families of Ladan.'),
('1CH', 23, 10, '1CH.23.10', 'And the sons of Shimei: Jahath, Zina, Jeush, and Beriah. These were the sons of Shimei—four in all.'),
('1CH', 23, 11, '1CH.23.11', 'Jahath was the first and Zizah was the second; but Jeush and Beriah did not have many sons, so they were counted as one family and received a single assignment.'),
('1CH', 23, 12, '1CH.23.12', 'The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel—four in all.'),
('1CH', 23, 13, '1CH.23.13', 'The sons of Amram: Aaron and Moses. Aaron and his descendants were set apart forever to consecrate the most holy things, to burn incense before the LORD, to minister before Him, and to pronounce blessings in His name forever.'),
('1CH', 23, 14, '1CH.23.14', 'As for Moses the man of God, his sons were named among the tribe of Levi.'),
('1CH', 23, 15, '1CH.23.15', 'The sons of Moses: Gershom and Eliezer.'),
('1CH', 23, 16, '1CH.23.16', 'The descendants of Gershom: Shebuel was the first.'),
('1CH', 23, 17, '1CH.23.17', 'The descendants of Eliezer: Rehabiah was the first. Eliezer did not have any other sons, but the sons of Rehabiah were very numerous.'),
('1CH', 23, 18, '1CH.23.18', 'The sons of Izhar: Shelomith was the first.'),
('1CH', 23, 19, '1CH.23.19', 'The sons of Hebron: Jeriah was the first, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, and Jekameam the fourth.'),
('1CH', 23, 20, '1CH.23.20', 'The sons of Uzziel: Micah was the first and Isshiah the second.'),
('1CH', 23, 21, '1CH.23.21', 'The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. The sons of Mahli: Eleazar and Kish.'),
('1CH', 23, 22, '1CH.23.22', 'Eleazar died without having any sons; he had only daughters. Their cousins, the sons of Kish, married them.'),
('1CH', 23, 23, '1CH.23.23', 'The sons of Mushi: Mahli, Eder, and Jeremoth—three in all.'),
('1CH', 23, 24, '1CH.23.24', 'These were the descendants of Levi by their families—the heads of families, registered individually by name—those twenty years of age or older who worked in the service of the house of the LORD.'),
('1CH', 23, 25, '1CH.23.25', 'For David had said, “The LORD, the God of Israel, has given rest to His people and has come to dwell in Jerusalem forever.'),
('1CH', 23, 26, '1CH.23.26', 'So now the Levites no longer need to carry the tabernacle or any of the articles for its service.”'),
('1CH', 23, 27, '1CH.23.27', 'For according to the final instructions of David, the Levites twenty years of age or older were counted,'),
('1CH', 23, 28, '1CH.23.28', 'but their duty was to assist the descendants of Aaron with the service of the house of the LORD, being responsible for the courts and chambers, the purification of all the holy things, and the work of the service of the house of God,'),
('1CH', 23, 29, '1CH.23.29', 'as well as for the rows of the showbread, the fine flour for the grain offering, the wafers of unleavened bread, the baking, the mixing, and all measurements of quantity and size.'),
('1CH', 23, 30, '1CH.23.30', 'They were also to stand every morning to give thanks and praise to the LORD, and likewise in the evening.'),
('1CH', 23, 31, '1CH.23.31', 'Whenever burnt offerings were presented to the LORD on the Sabbaths, New Moons, and appointed feasts, they were to serve regularly before the LORD in the numbers prescribed for them.'),
('1CH', 23, 32, '1CH.23.32', 'So the Levites were to carry out the responsibilities for the Tent of Meeting and the Holy Place, and, under their brothers the descendants of Aaron, the service of the house of the LORD.'),
('1CH', 24, 1, '1CH.24.1', 'These were the divisions of the descendants of Aaron. The sons of Aaron were Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.'),
('1CH', 24, 2, '1CH.24.2', 'But Nadab and Abihu died before their father did, and they had no sons; so Eleazar and Ithamar served as priests.'),
('1CH', 24, 3, '1CH.24.3', 'With the help of Eleazar’s descendant Zadok and Ithamar’s descendant Ahimelech, David divided them according to the offices of their service.'),
('1CH', 24, 4, '1CH.24.4', 'Since more leaders were found among Eleazar’s descendants than those of Ithamar, they were divided accordingly. There were sixteen heads of families from the descendants of Eleazar and eight from the descendants of Ithamar.'),
('1CH', 24, 5, '1CH.24.5', 'Thus they were divided by lot, for there were officers of the sanctuary and officers of God among both Eleazar’s and Ithamar’s descendants.'),
('1CH', 24, 6, '1CH.24.6', 'The scribe, Shemaiah son of Nethanel, a Levite, recorded their names in the presence of the king and of the officers: Zadok the priest, Ahimelech son of Abiathar, and the heads of families of the priests and the Levites—one family being taken from Eleazar, and then one from Ithamar.'),
('1CH', 24, 7, '1CH.24.7', 'The first lot fell to Jehoiarib, the second to Jedaiah,'),
('1CH', 24, 8, '1CH.24.8', 'the third to Harim, the fourth to Seorim,'),
('1CH', 24, 9, '1CH.24.9', 'the fifth to Malchijah, the sixth to Mijamin,'),
('1CH', 24, 10, '1CH.24.10', 'the seventh to Hakkoz, the eighth to Abijah,'),
('1CH', 24, 11, '1CH.24.11', 'the ninth to Jeshua, the tenth to Shecaniah,'),
('1CH', 24, 12, '1CH.24.12', 'the eleventh to Eliashib, the twelfth to Jakim,'),
('1CH', 24, 13, '1CH.24.13', 'the thirteenth to Huppah, the fourteenth to Jeshebeab,'),
('1CH', 24, 14, '1CH.24.14', 'the fifteenth to Bilgah, the sixteenth to Immer,'),
('1CH', 24, 15, '1CH.24.15', 'the seventeenth to Hezir, the eighteenth to Happizzez,'),
('1CH', 24, 16, '1CH.24.16', 'the nineteenth to Pethahiah, the twentieth to Jehezkel,'),
('1CH', 24, 17, '1CH.24.17', 'the twenty-first to Jachin, the twenty-second to Gamul,'),
('1CH', 24, 18, '1CH.24.18', 'the twenty-third to Delaiah, and the twenty-fourth to Maaziah.'),
('1CH', 24, 19, '1CH.24.19', 'This was their appointed order for service when they entered the house of the LORD, according to the regulations prescribed for them by their forefather Aaron, as the LORD, the God of Israel, had commanded him.'),
('1CH', 24, 20, '1CH.24.20', 'Now these were the rest of the descendants of Levi: From the sons of Amram: Shubael; from the sons of Shubael: Jehdeiah.'),
('1CH', 24, 21, '1CH.24.21', 'As for Rehabiah, from his sons: The first was Isshiah.'),
('1CH', 24, 22, '1CH.24.22', 'From the Izharites: Shelomoth; from the sons of Shelomoth: Jahath.'),
('1CH', 24, 23, '1CH.24.23', 'From the sons of Hebron: Jeriah was the first, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, and Jekameam the fourth.'),
('1CH', 24, 24, '1CH.24.24', 'From the sons of Uzziel: Micah; from the sons of Micah: Shamir.'),
('1CH', 24, 25, '1CH.24.25', 'The brother of Micah: Isshiah; from the sons of Isshiah: Zechariah.'),
('1CH', 24, 26, '1CH.24.26', 'The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. The son of Jaaziah: Beno.'),
('1CH', 24, 27, '1CH.24.27', 'The descendants of Merari from Jaaziah: Beno, Shoham, Zaccur, and Ibri.'),
('1CH', 24, 28, '1CH.24.28', 'From Mahli: Eleazar, who had no sons.'),
('1CH', 24, 29, '1CH.24.29', 'From Kish: Jerahmeel the son of Kish.'),
('1CH', 24, 30, '1CH.24.30', 'And the sons of Mushi: Mahli, Eder, and Jerimoth. These were the sons of the Levites, according to their families.'),
('1CH', 24, 31, '1CH.24.31', 'As their brothers the descendants of Aaron did, they also cast lots in the presence of King David and of Zadok, Ahimelech, and the heads of the families of the priests and Levites—the family heads and their younger brothers alike.'),
('1CH', 25, 1, '1CH.25.1', 'Additionally, David and the commanders of the army set apart some of the sons of Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun to prophesy with the accompaniment of lyres, harps, and cymbals. The following is the list of the men who performed this service:'),
('1CH', 25, 2, '1CH.25.2', 'From the sons of Asaph: Zaccur, Joseph, Nethaniah, and Asarelah. These sons of Asaph were under the direction of Asaph, who prophesied under the direction of the king.'),
('1CH', 25, 3, '1CH.25.3', 'From the sons of Jeduthun: Gedaliah, Zeri, Jeshaiah, Shimei, Hashabiah, and Mattithiah—six in all—under the direction of their father Jeduthun, who prophesied with the harp, giving thanks and praise to the LORD.'),
('1CH', 25, 4, '1CH.25.4', 'From the sons of Heman: Bukkiah, Mattaniah, Uzziel, Shebuel, Jerimoth, Hananiah, Hanani, Eliathah, Giddalti, Romamti-ezer, Joshbekashah, Mallothi, Hothir, and Mahazioth.'),
('1CH', 25, 5, '1CH.25.5', 'All these sons of Heman the king’s seer were given him through the promises of God to exalt him, for God had given Heman fourteen sons and three daughters.'),
('1CH', 25, 6, '1CH.25.6', 'All these were under the direction of their fathers for the music of the house of the LORD with cymbals, harps, and lyres, for the service of the house of God. Asaph, Jeduthun, and Heman were under the direction of the king.'),
('1CH', 25, 7, '1CH.25.7', 'Together with their relatives, who were all trained and skillful in the songs of the LORD, they numbered 288.'),
('1CH', 25, 8, '1CH.25.8', 'They cast lots for their duties, young and old alike, teacher as well as pupil.'),
('1CH', 25, 9, '1CH.25.9', 'The first lot, which was for Asaph, fell to Joseph, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all; the second to Gedaliah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 10, '1CH.25.10', 'the third to Zaccur, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 11, '1CH.25.11', 'the fourth to Izri, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 12, '1CH.25.12', 'the fifth to Nethaniah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 13, '1CH.25.13', 'the sixth to Bukkiah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 14, '1CH.25.14', 'the seventh to Jesarelah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 15, '1CH.25.15', 'the eighth to Jeshaiah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 16, '1CH.25.16', 'the ninth to Mattaniah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 17, '1CH.25.17', 'the tenth to Shimei, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 18, '1CH.25.18', 'the eleventh to Azarel, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 19, '1CH.25.19', 'the twelfth to Hashabiah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 20, '1CH.25.20', 'the thirteenth to Shubael, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 21, '1CH.25.21', 'the fourteenth to Mattithiah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 22, '1CH.25.22', 'the fifteenth to Jeremoth, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 23, '1CH.25.23', 'the sixteenth to Hananiah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 24, '1CH.25.24', 'the seventeenth to Joshbekashah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 25, '1CH.25.25', 'the eighteenth to Hanani, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 26, '1CH.25.26', 'the nineteenth to Mallothi, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 27, '1CH.25.27', 'the twentieth to Eliathah, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 28, '1CH.25.28', 'the twenty-first to Hothir, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 29, '1CH.25.29', 'the twenty-second to Giddalti, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 30, '1CH.25.30', 'the twenty-third to Mahazioth, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all;'),
('1CH', 25, 31, '1CH.25.31', 'and the twenty-fourth to Romamti-ezer, his sons, and his brothers—12 in all.'),
('1CH', 26, 1, '1CH.26.1', 'These were the divisions of the gatekeepers: From the Korahites: Meshelemiah son of Kore, one of the sons of Asaph.'),
('1CH', 26, 2, '1CH.26.2', 'Meshelemiah had sons: Zechariah the firstborn, Jediael the second, Zebadiah the third, Jathniel the fourth,'),
('1CH', 26, 3, '1CH.26.3', 'Elam the fifth, Jehohanan the sixth, and Eliehoenai the seventh.'),
('1CH', 26, 4, '1CH.26.4', 'And Obed-edom also had sons: Shemaiah the firstborn, Jehozabad the second, Joah the third, Sachar the fourth, Nethanel the fifth,'),
('1CH', 26, 5, '1CH.26.5', 'Ammiel the sixth, Issachar the seventh, and Peullethai the eighth. For God had blessed Obed-edom.'),
('1CH', 26, 6, '1CH.26.6', 'Also to his son Shemaiah were born sons who ruled over their families because they were strong, capable men.'),
('1CH', 26, 7, '1CH.26.7', 'Shemaiah’s sons were Othni, Rephael, Obed, and Elzabad; his brothers were Elihu and Semachiah, also capable men.'),
('1CH', 26, 8, '1CH.26.8', 'All these were descendants of Obed-edom; they and their sons and brothers were capable men with strength to do the work—62 in all from Obed-edom.'),
('1CH', 26, 9, '1CH.26.9', 'Meshelemiah also had sons and brothers who were capable men—18 in all.'),
('1CH', 26, 10, '1CH.26.10', 'Hosah the Merarite also had sons: Shimri the first (although he was not the firstborn, his father had appointed him as the first),'),
('1CH', 26, 11, '1CH.26.11', 'Hilkiah the second, Tebaliah the third, and Zechariah the fourth. The sons and brothers of Hosah numbered 13 in all.'),
('1CH', 26, 12, '1CH.26.12', 'These divisions of the gatekeepers, through their chief men, had duties for ministering in the house of the LORD, just as their relatives did.'),
('1CH', 26, 13, '1CH.26.13', 'They cast lots for each gate, according to their families, young and old alike.'),
('1CH', 26, 14, '1CH.26.14', 'The lot for the East Gate fell to Shelemiah. Then lots were cast for his son Zechariah, a wise counselor, and the lot for the North Gate fell to him.'),
('1CH', 26, 15, '1CH.26.15', 'The lot for the South Gate fell to Obed-edom, and the lot for the storehouses to his sons.'),
('1CH', 26, 16, '1CH.26.16', 'The lots for the West Gate and the Shallecheth Gate on the ascending highway fell to Shuppim and Hosah. There were guards stationed at every watch.'),
('1CH', 26, 17, '1CH.26.17', 'Each day there were six Levites on the east, four on the north, four on the south, and two pairs at the storehouse.'),
('1CH', 26, 18, '1CH.26.18', 'As for the court on the west, there were four at the highway and two at the court.'),
('1CH', 26, 19, '1CH.26.19', 'These were the divisions of the gatekeepers who were descendants of Korah and Merari.'),
('1CH', 26, 20, '1CH.26.20', 'Now their fellow Levites were in charge of the treasuries of the house of God and the treasuries of the dedicated things.'),
('1CH', 26, 21, '1CH.26.21', 'From the descendants of Ladan, who were Gershonites through Ladan and heads of the families of Ladan the Gershonite, were Jehieli,'),
('1CH', 26, 22, '1CH.26.22', 'the sons of Jehieli, Zetham, and his brother Joel. They were in charge of the treasuries of the house of the LORD.'),
('1CH', 26, 23, '1CH.26.23', 'From the Amramites, the Izharites, the Hebronites, and the Uzzielites:'),
('1CH', 26, 24, '1CH.26.24', 'Shebuel, a descendant of Gershom son of Moses, was the officer in charge of the treasuries.'),
('1CH', 26, 25, '1CH.26.25', 'His relatives through Eliezer included Rehabiah his son, Jeshaiah his son, Joram his son, Zichri his son, and Shelomith his son.'),
('1CH', 26, 26, '1CH.26.26', 'This Shelomith and his brothers were in charge of all the treasuries for the things dedicated by King David, by the heads of families who were the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and by the army commanders.'),
('1CH', 26, 27, '1CH.26.27', 'They had dedicated some of the plunder from their battles to the repair of the house of the LORD.'),
('1CH', 26, 28, '1CH.26.28', 'Everything that had been dedicated by Samuel the seer, Saul son of Kish, Abner son of Ner, and Joab son of Zeruiah, along with everything else that was dedicated, was under the care of Shelomith and his brothers.'),
('1CH', 26, 29, '1CH.26.29', 'From the Izharites, Chenaniah and his sons had the outside duties as officers and judges over Israel.'),
('1CH', 26, 30, '1CH.26.30', 'From the Hebronites, Hashabiah and his relatives, 1,700 capable men, had charge of the affairs of Israel west of the Jordan for all the work of the LORD and for the service of the king.'),
('1CH', 26, 31, '1CH.26.31', 'As for the Hebronites, Jerijah was the chief of the Hebronites, according to the genealogies of his ancestors. In the fortieth year of David’s reign the records were searched, and strong, capable men were found among the Hebronites at Jazer in Gilead.'),
('1CH', 26, 32, '1CH.26.32', 'Among Jerijah’s relatives there were 2,700 capable men who were heads of families. King David appointed them over the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh for every matter pertaining to God and for the affairs of the king.'),
('1CH', 27, 1, '1CH.27.1', 'This is the list of the Israelites—the heads of families, the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and their officers who served the king in every matter concerning the divisions on rotating military duty each month throughout the year. There were 24,000 men in each division:'),
('1CH', 27, 2, '1CH.27.2', 'Jashobeam son of Zabdiel was in charge of the first division, which was assigned the first month. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 3, '1CH.27.3', 'He was a descendant of Perez and chief of all the army commanders for the first month.'),
('1CH', 27, 4, '1CH.27.4', 'Dodai the Ahohite was in charge of the division for the second month, and Mikloth was the leader. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 5, '1CH.27.5', 'The third army commander, as chief for the third month, was Benaiah son of Jehoiada the priest. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 6, '1CH.27.6', 'This Benaiah was mighty among the Thirty and was over the Thirty, and his son Ammizabad was in charge of his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 7, '1CH.27.7', 'The fourth, for the fourth month, was Joab’s brother Asahel, and his son Zebadiah was commander after him. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 8, '1CH.27.8', 'The fifth, for the fifth month, was the commander Shamhuth the Izrahite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 9, '1CH.27.9', 'The sixth, for the sixth month, was Ira son of Ikkesh the Tekoite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 10, '1CH.27.10', 'The seventh, for the seventh month, was Helez the Pelonite, an Ephraimite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 11, '1CH.27.11', 'The eighth, for the eighth month, was Sibbecai the Hushathite, a Zerahite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 12, '1CH.27.12', 'The ninth, for the ninth month, was Abiezer the Anathothite, a Benjamite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 13, '1CH.27.13', 'The tenth, for the tenth month, was Maharai the Netophathite, a Zerahite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 14, '1CH.27.14', 'The eleventh, for the eleventh month, was Benaiah the Pirathonite, an Ephraimite. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 15, '1CH.27.15', 'The twelfth, for the twelfth month, was Heldai the Netophathite, from the family of Othniel. There were 24,000 men in his division.'),
('1CH', 27, 16, '1CH.27.16', 'These officers were in charge of the tribes of Israel: Over the Reubenites was Eliezer son of Zichri; over the Simeonites was Shephatiah son of Maacah;'),
('1CH', 27, 17, '1CH.27.17', 'over Levi was Hashabiah son of Kemuel; over Aaron was Zadok;'),
('1CH', 27, 18, '1CH.27.18', 'over Judah was Elihu, one of David’s brothers; over Issachar was Omri son of Michael;'),
('1CH', 27, 19, '1CH.27.19', 'over Zebulun was Ishmaiah son of Obadiah; over Naphtali was Jerimoth son of Azriel;'),
('1CH', 27, 20, '1CH.27.20', 'over the Ephraimites was Hoshea son of Azaziah; over one of the half-tribes of Manasseh was Joel son of Pedaiah;'),
('1CH', 27, 21, '1CH.27.21', 'over the half-tribe of Manasseh in Gilead was Iddo son of Zechariah; over Benjamin was Jaasiel son of Abner;'),
('1CH', 27, 22, '1CH.27.22', 'and over Dan was Azarel son of Jeroham. These were the leaders of the tribes of Israel.'),
('1CH', 27, 23, '1CH.27.23', 'David did not count the men aged twenty or under, because the LORD had said that He would make Israel as numerous as the stars of the sky.'),
('1CH', 27, 24, '1CH.27.24', 'Joab son of Zeruiah began to count the men but did not finish. For because of this census wrath came upon Israel, and the number was not entered in the Book of the Chronicles of King David.'),
('1CH', 27, 25, '1CH.27.25', 'Azmaveth son of Adiel was in charge of the royal storehouses. Jonathan son of Uzziah was in charge of the storehouses in the country, in the cities, in the villages, and in the fortresses.'),
('1CH', 27, 26, '1CH.27.26', 'Ezri son of Chelub was in charge of the workers in the fields who tilled the soil.'),
('1CH', 27, 27, '1CH.27.27', 'Shimei the Ramathite was in charge of the vineyards. Zabdi the Shiphmite was in charge of the produce of the vineyards for the wine vats.'),
('1CH', 27, 28, '1CH.27.28', 'Baal-hanan the Gederite was in charge of the olive and sycamore trees in the foothills. Joash was in charge of the stores of olive oil.'),
('1CH', 27, 29, '1CH.27.29', 'Shitrai the Sharonite was in charge of the herds grazing in Sharon. Shaphat son of Adlai was in charge of the herds in the valleys.'),
('1CH', 27, 30, '1CH.27.30', 'Obil the Ishmaelite was in charge of the camels. Jehdeiah the Meronothite was in charge of the donkeys.'),
('1CH', 27, 31, '1CH.27.31', 'Jaziz the Hagrite was in charge of the flocks. All these officials were in charge of King David’s property.'),
('1CH', 27, 32, '1CH.27.32', 'David’s uncle Jonathan was a counselor; he was a man of insight and a scribe. Jehiel son of Hachmoni attended to the sons of the king.'),
('1CH', 27, 33, '1CH.27.33', 'Ahithophel was the king’s counselor. Hushai the Archite was the king’s friend.'),
('1CH', 27, 34, '1CH.27.34', 'Ahithophel was succeeded by Jehoiada son of Benaiah, then by Abiathar. Joab was the commander of the king’s army.'),
('1CH', 28, 1, '1CH.28.1', 'Now David summoned all the leaders of Israel to Jerusalem: the leaders of the tribes, the leaders of the divisions in the king’s service, the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and the officials in charge of all the property and cattle of the king and his sons, along with the court officials and mighty men—every mighty man of valor.'),
('1CH', 28, 2, '1CH.28.2', 'Then King David rose to his feet and said, “Listen to me, my brothers and my people. It was in my heart to build a house as a resting place for the ark of the covenant of the LORD and as a footstool for our God. I had made preparations to build it,'),
('1CH', 28, 3, '1CH.28.3', 'but God said to me, ‘You are not to build a house for My Name, because you are a man of war who has shed blood.’'),
('1CH', 28, 4, '1CH.28.4', 'Yet the LORD, the God of Israel, chose me out of all my father’s house to be king over Israel forever. For He chose Judah as leader, and from the house of Judah He chose my father’s household, and from my father’s sons He was pleased to make me king over all Israel.'),
('1CH', 28, 5, '1CH.28.5', 'And of all my sons—for the LORD has given me many sons—He has chosen Solomon my son to sit on the throne of the kingdom of the LORD over Israel.'),
('1CH', 28, 6, '1CH.28.6', 'And He said to me, ‘Solomon your son is the one who will build My house and My courts, for I have chosen him as My son, and I will be his Father.'),
('1CH', 28, 7, '1CH.28.7', 'I will establish his kingdom forever, if he resolutely carries out My commandments and ordinances, as is being done this day.’'),
('1CH', 28, 8, '1CH.28.8', 'So now in the sight of all Israel, the assembly of the LORD, and in the hearing of our God, keep and seek out all the commandments of the LORD your God, so that you may possess this good land and leave it as an inheritance to your descendants forever.'),
('1CH', 28, 9, '1CH.28.9', 'As for you, Solomon my son, know the God of your father and serve Him wholeheartedly and with a willing mind, for the LORD searches every heart and understands the intent of every thought. If you seek Him, He will be found by you; but if you forsake Him, He will reject you forever.'),
('1CH', 28, 10, '1CH.28.10', 'Consider now that the LORD has chosen you to build a house for the sanctuary. Be strong and do it.”'),
('1CH', 28, 11, '1CH.28.11', 'Then David gave his son Solomon the plans for the portico of the temple, its buildings, storehouses, upper rooms, inner rooms, and the room for the mercy seat.'),
('1CH', 28, 12, '1CH.28.12', 'The plans contained everything David had in mind for the courts of the house of the LORD, for all the surrounding rooms, for the treasuries of the house of God and of the dedicated things,'),
('1CH', 28, 13, '1CH.28.13', 'for the divisions of the priests and Levites, for all the work of service in the house of the LORD, and for all the articles of service in the house of the LORD:'),
('1CH', 28, 14, '1CH.28.14', 'the weight of all the gold articles for every kind of service; the weight of all the silver articles for every kind of service;'),
('1CH', 28, 15, '1CH.28.15', 'the weight of the gold lampstands and their lamps, including the weight of each lampstand and its lamps; the weight of each silver lampstand and its lamps, according to the use of each lampstand;'),
('1CH', 28, 16, '1CH.28.16', 'the weight of gold for each table of showbread, and of silver for the silver tables;'),
('1CH', 28, 17, '1CH.28.17', 'the weight of the pure gold for the forks, sprinkling bowls, and pitchers; the weight of each gold dish; the weight of each silver bowl;'),
('1CH', 28, 18, '1CH.28.18', 'the weight of the refined gold for the altar of incense; and the plans for the chariot of the gold cherubim that spread their wings and overshadowed the ark of the covenant of the LORD.'),
('1CH', 28, 19, '1CH.28.19', '“All this,” said David, “all the details of this plan, the LORD has made clear to me in writing by His hand upon me.”'),
('1CH', 28, 20, '1CH.28.20', 'David also said to Solomon his son, “Be strong and courageous, and do it. Do not be afraid or discouraged, for the LORD God, my God, is with you. He will neither fail you nor forsake you before all the work for the service of the house of the LORD is finished.'),
('1CH', 28, 21, '1CH.28.21', 'The divisions of the priests and Levites are ready for all the service of the house of God, and every willing man of every skill will be at your disposal for the work. The officials and all the people are fully at your command.”'),
('1CH', 29, 1, '1CH.29.1', 'Then King David said to the whole assembly, “My son Solomon, the one whom God has chosen, is young and inexperienced. The task is great because this palace is not for man, but for the LORD God.'),
('1CH', 29, 2, '1CH.29.2', 'Now with all my ability I have made provision for the house of my God—gold for the gold articles, silver for the silver, bronze for the bronze, iron for the iron, and wood for the wood, as well as onyx for the settings, turquoise, stones of various colors, all kinds of precious stones, and slabs of marble—all in abundance.'),
('1CH', 29, 3, '1CH.29.3', 'Moreover, because of my delight in the house of my God, I now give for it my personal treasures of gold and silver, over and above all that I have provided for this holy temple:'),
('1CH', 29, 4, '1CH.29.4', 'three thousand talents of gold (the gold of Ophir) and seven thousand talents of refined silver, to overlay the walls of the buildings,'),
('1CH', 29, 5, '1CH.29.5', 'for the gold work and the silver work, and for all the work to be done by the craftsmen. Now who is willing to consecrate himself to the LORD today?”'),
('1CH', 29, 6, '1CH.29.6', 'Then the leaders of the families, the officers of the tribes of Israel, the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and the officials in charge of the king’s work gave willingly.'),
('1CH', 29, 7, '1CH.29.7', 'Toward the service of God’s house they gave 5,000 talents and 10,000 darics of gold, 10,000 talents of silver, 18,000 talents of bronze, and 100,000 talents of iron.'),
('1CH', 29, 8, '1CH.29.8', 'Whoever had precious stones gave them to the treasury of the house of the LORD, under the care of Jehiel the Gershonite.'),
('1CH', 29, 9, '1CH.29.9', 'And the people rejoiced at the willing response of their leaders, for they had given to the LORD freely and wholeheartedly. And King David also rejoiced greatly.'),
('1CH', 29, 10, '1CH.29.10', 'Then David blessed the LORD in the sight of all the assembly and said: “May You be blessed, O LORD, God of our father Israel, from everlasting to everlasting.'),
('1CH', 29, 11, '1CH.29.11', 'Yours, O LORD, is the greatness and the power and the glory and the splendor and the majesty, for everything in heaven and on earth belongs to You. Yours, O LORD, is the kingdom, and You are exalted as head over all.'),
('1CH', 29, 12, '1CH.29.12', 'Both riches and honor come from You, and You are the ruler over all. In Your hands are power and might to exalt and give strength to all.'),
('1CH', 29, 13, '1CH.29.13', 'Now therefore, our God, we give You thanks, and we praise Your glorious name.'),
('1CH', 29, 14, '1CH.29.14', 'But who am I, and who are my people, that we should be able to give as generously as this? For everything comes from You, and from Your own hand we have given to You.'),
('1CH', 29, 15, '1CH.29.15', 'For we are foreigners and strangers in Your presence, as were all our forefathers. Our days on earth are like a shadow, without hope.'),
('1CH', 29, 16, '1CH.29.16', 'O LORD our God, from Your hand comes all this abundance that we have provided to build You a house for Your holy Name, and all of it belongs to You.'),
('1CH', 29, 17, '1CH.29.17', 'I know, my God, that You test the heart and delight in uprightness. All these things I have given willingly and with an upright heart, and now I have seen Your people who are present here giving joyfully and willingly to You.'),
('1CH', 29, 18, '1CH.29.18', 'O LORD, God of our fathers Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, keep this desire forever in the intentions of the hearts of Your people, and direct their hearts toward You.'),
('1CH', 29, 19, '1CH.29.19', 'And give my son Solomon a whole heart to keep and carry out all Your commandments, decrees, and statutes, and to build Your palace for which I have made provision.”'),
('1CH', 29, 20, '1CH.29.20', 'Then David said to the whole assembly, “Bless the LORD your God.” So the whole assembly blessed the LORD, the God of their fathers. They bowed down and paid homage to the LORD and to the king.'),
('1CH', 29, 21, '1CH.29.21', 'The next day they offered sacrifices and presented burnt offerings to the LORD: a thousand bulls, a thousand rams, and a thousand lambs, along with their drink offerings, and other sacrifices in abundance for all Israel.'),
('1CH', 29, 22, '1CH.29.22', 'That day they ate and drank with great joy in the presence of the LORD. Then, for a second time, they designated David’s son Solomon as king, anointing him before the LORD as ruler, and Zadok as the priest.'),
('1CH', 29, 23, '1CH.29.23', 'So Solomon sat on the throne of the LORD as king in place of his father David. He prospered, and all Israel obeyed him.'),
('1CH', 29, 24, '1CH.29.24', 'All the officials and mighty men, as well as all of King David’s sons, pledged their allegiance to King Solomon.'),
('1CH', 29, 25, '1CH.29.25', 'The LORD highly exalted Solomon in the sight of all Israel and bestowed on him royal majesty such as had not been bestowed on any king in Israel before him.'),
('1CH', 29, 26, '1CH.29.26', 'David son of Jesse was king over all Israel.'),
('1CH', 29, 27, '1CH.29.27', 'The length of David’s reign over Israel was forty years—seven years in Hebron and thirty-three years in Jerusalem.'),
('1CH', 29, 28, '1CH.29.28', 'He died at a ripe old age, full of years, riches, and honor, and his son Solomon reigned in his place.'),
('1CH', 29, 29, '1CH.29.29', 'Now the acts of King David, from first to last, are indeed written in the Chronicles of Samuel the Seer, the Chronicles of Nathan the Prophet, and the Chronicles of Gad the Seer,'),
('1CH', 29, 30, '1CH.29.30', 'together with all the details of his reign, his might, and the circumstances that came upon him and Israel and all the kingdoms of the lands.'),
('2CH', 1, 1, '2CH.1.1', 'Now Solomon son of David established himself securely over his kingdom, and the LORD his God was with him and highly exalted him.'),
('2CH', 1, 2, '2CH.1.2', 'Then Solomon spoke to all Israel, to the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, to the judges, and to every leader in all Israel—the heads of the families.'),
('2CH', 1, 3, '2CH.1.3', 'And Solomon and the whole assembly went to the high place at Gibeon because it was the location of God’s Tent of Meeting, which Moses the servant of the LORD had made in the wilderness.'),
('2CH', 1, 4, '2CH.1.4', 'Now David had brought the ark of God from Kiriath-jearim to the place he had prepared for it, because he had pitched a tent for it in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 1, 5, '2CH.1.5', 'But the bronze altar made by Bezalel son of Uri, the son of Hur, was in Gibeon before the tabernacle of the LORD. So Solomon and the assembly inquired of Him there.'),
('2CH', 1, 6, '2CH.1.6', 'Solomon offered sacrifices there before the LORD on the bronze altar at the Tent of Meeting, where he offered a thousand burnt offerings.'),
('2CH', 1, 7, '2CH.1.7', 'That night God appeared to Solomon and said, “Ask, and I will give it to you!”'),
('2CH', 1, 8, '2CH.1.8', 'Solomon replied to God: “You have shown much loving devotion to my father David, and You have made me king in his place.'),
('2CH', 1, 9, '2CH.1.9', 'Now, O LORD God, let Your promise to my father David be fulfilled. For You have made me king over a people as numerous as the dust of the earth.'),
('2CH', 1, 10, '2CH.1.10', 'Now grant me wisdom and knowledge, so that I may lead this people. For who is able to govern this great people of Yours?”'),
('2CH', 1, 11, '2CH.1.11', 'God said to Solomon, “Since this was in your heart instead of requesting riches or wealth or honor for yourself or death for your enemies—and since you have not even requested long life but have asked for wisdom and knowledge to govern My people over whom I have made you king—'),
('2CH', 1, 12, '2CH.1.12', 'therefore wisdom and knowledge have been granted to you. And I will also give you riches and wealth and honor unlike anything given to the kings before you or after you.”'),
('2CH', 1, 13, '2CH.1.13', 'So Solomon went to Jerusalem from the high place in Gibeon, from before the Tent of Meeting, and he reigned over Israel.'),
('2CH', 1, 14, '2CH.1.14', 'Solomon accumulated 1,400 chariots and 12,000 horses, which he stationed in the chariot cities and also with him in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 1, 15, '2CH.1.15', 'The king made silver and gold as common in Jerusalem as stones, and cedar as abundant as sycamore in the foothills.'),
('2CH', 1, 16, '2CH.1.16', 'Solomon’s horses were imported from Egypt and Kue; the royal merchants purchased them from Kue.'),
('2CH', 1, 17, '2CH.1.17', 'A chariot could be imported from Egypt for six hundred shekels of silver, and a horse for a hundred and fifty. Likewise, they exported them to all the kings of the Hittites and to the kings of Aram.'),
('2CH', 2, 1, '2CH.2.1', 'Now Solomon purposed to build a house for the Name of the LORD and a royal palace for himself.'),
('2CH', 2, 2, '2CH.2.2', 'So he conscripted 70,000 porters, 80,000 stonecutters in the mountains, and 3,600 supervisors.'),
('2CH', 2, 3, '2CH.2.3', 'Then Solomon sent word to Hiram king of Tyre: “Do for me as you did for my father David when you sent him cedars to build himself a house to live in.'),
('2CH', 2, 4, '2CH.2.4', 'Behold, I am about to build a house for the Name of the LORD my God to dedicate to Him for burning fragrant incense before Him, for displaying the showbread continuously, and for making burnt offerings every morning and evening as well as on the Sabbaths, New Moons, and appointed feasts of the LORD our God. This is ordained for Israel forever.'),
('2CH', 2, 5, '2CH.2.5', 'The house that I am building will be great, for our God is greater than all gods.'),
('2CH', 2, 6, '2CH.2.6', 'But who is able to build a house for Him, since the heavens, even the highest heavens, cannot contain Him? Who then am I, that I should build a house for Him, except as a place to burn sacrifices before Him?'),
('2CH', 2, 7, '2CH.2.7', 'Send me, therefore, a craftsman skilled in engraving to work with gold and silver, with bronze and iron, and with purple, crimson, and blue yarn. He will work with my craftsmen in Judah and Jerusalem, whom my father David provided.'),
('2CH', 2, 8, '2CH.2.8', 'Send me also cedar, cypress, and algum logs from Lebanon, for I know that your servants have skill to cut timber there. And indeed, my servants will work with yours'),
('2CH', 2, 9, '2CH.2.9', 'to prepare for me timber in abundance, because the temple I am building will be great and wonderful.'),
('2CH', 2, 10, '2CH.2.10', 'I will pay your servants, the woodcutters, 20,000 cors of ground wheat, 20,000 cors of barley, 20,000 baths of wine, and 20,000 baths of olive oil.”'),
('2CH', 2, 11, '2CH.2.11', 'Then Hiram king of Tyre wrote a letter in reply to Solomon: “Because the LORD loves His people, He has set you over them as king.”'),
('2CH', 2, 12, '2CH.2.12', 'And Hiram added: “Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, who made the heavens and the earth! He has given King David a wise son with insight and understanding, who will build a temple for the LORD and a royal palace for himself.'),
('2CH', 2, 13, '2CH.2.13', 'So now I am sending you Huram-abi, a skillful man endowed with creativity.'),
('2CH', 2, 14, '2CH.2.14', 'He is the son of a woman from the daughters of Dan, and his father is a man of Tyre. He is skilled in work with gold and silver, bronze and iron, stone and wood, purple, blue, and crimson yarn, and fine linen. He is experienced in every kind of engraving and can execute any design that is given him. He will work with your craftsmen and with those of my lord, your father David.'),
('2CH', 2, 15, '2CH.2.15', 'Now let my lord send to his servants the wheat, barley, olive oil, and wine he promised.'),
('2CH', 2, 16, '2CH.2.16', 'We will cut logs from Lebanon, as many as you need, and we will float them to you as rafts by sea down to Joppa. Then you can take them up to Jerusalem.”'),
('2CH', 2, 17, '2CH.2.17', 'Solomon numbered all the foreign men in the land of Israel following the census his father David had conducted, and there were found to be 153,600 in all.'),
('2CH', 2, 18, '2CH.2.18', 'Solomon made 70,000 of them porters, 80,000 stonecutters in the mountains, and 3,600 supervisors.'),
('2CH', 3, 1, '2CH.3.1', 'Then Solomon began to build the house of the LORD in Jerusalem on Mount Moriah, where the LORD had appeared to his father David. This was the place that David had prepared on the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.'),
('2CH', 3, 2, '2CH.3.2', 'Solomon began construction on the second day of the second month in the fourth year of his reign.'),
('2CH', 3, 3, '2CH.3.3', 'The foundation that Solomon laid for the house of God was sixty cubits long and twenty cubits wide, according to the old standard.'),
('2CH', 3, 4, '2CH.3.4', 'The portico at the front, extending across the width of the temple, was twenty cubits long and twenty cubits high. He overlaid the inside with pure gold.'),
('2CH', 3, 5, '2CH.3.5', 'He paneled the main room with cypress, which he overlaid with fine gold and decorated with palm trees and chains.'),
('2CH', 3, 6, '2CH.3.6', 'He adorned the temple with precious stones for beauty, and its gold was from Parvaim.'),
('2CH', 3, 7, '2CH.3.7', 'He overlaid its beams, thresholds, walls, and doors with gold, and he carved cherubim on the walls.'),
('2CH', 3, 8, '2CH.3.8', 'Then he made the Most Holy Place; its length corresponded to the width of the temple—twenty cubits long and twenty cubits wide. And he overlaid the inside with six hundred talents of fine gold.'),
('2CH', 3, 9, '2CH.3.9', 'The weight of the nails was fifty shekels of gold. He also overlaid the upper rooms with gold.'),
('2CH', 3, 10, '2CH.3.10', 'In the Most Holy Place he made two cherubim of sculptured work, and he overlaid them with gold.'),
('2CH', 3, 11, '2CH.3.11', 'The total wingspan of the cherubim was twenty cubits. One wing of the first cherub was five cubits long and touched the wall of the temple, and its other wing was five cubits long and touched the wing of the other cherub.'),
('2CH', 3, 12, '2CH.3.12', 'The wing of the second cherub also measured five cubits and touched the wall of the temple, while its other wing measured five cubits and touched the wing of the first cherub.'),
('2CH', 3, 13, '2CH.3.13', 'So the total wingspan of these cherubim was twenty cubits. They stood on their feet, facing the main room.'),
('2CH', 3, 14, '2CH.3.14', 'He made the veil of blue, purple, and crimson yarn and fine linen, with cherubim woven into it.'),
('2CH', 3, 15, '2CH.3.15', 'In front of the temple he made two pillars, which together were thirty-five cubits high, each with a capital on top measuring five cubits.'),
('2CH', 3, 16, '2CH.3.16', 'He made interwoven chains and put them on top of the pillars. He made a hundred pomegranates and fastened them into the chainwork.'),
('2CH', 3, 17, '2CH.3.17', 'Then he set up the pillars in front of the temple, one on the south and one on the north. The pillar on the south he named Jachin, and the pillar on the north he named Boaz.'),
('2CH', 4, 1, '2CH.4.1', 'He made a bronze altar twenty cubits long, twenty cubits wide, and ten cubits high.'),
('2CH', 4, 2, '2CH.4.2', 'He also made the Sea of cast metal. It was circular in shape, measuring ten cubits from rim to rim, five cubits in height, and thirty cubits in circumference.'),
('2CH', 4, 3, '2CH.4.3', 'Below the rim, figures of oxen encircled it, ten per cubit all the way around the Sea, cast in two rows as a part of the Sea.'),
('2CH', 4, 4, '2CH.4.4', 'The Sea stood on twelve oxen, three facing north, three facing west, three facing south, and three facing east. The Sea rested on them, with all their hindquarters toward the center.'),
('2CH', 4, 5, '2CH.4.5', 'It was a handbreadth thick, and its rim was fashioned like the brim of a cup, like a lily blossom. It could hold three thousand baths.'),
('2CH', 4, 6, '2CH.4.6', 'He also made ten basins for washing and placed five on the south side and five on the north. The parts of the burnt offering were rinsed in them, but the priests used the Sea for washing.'),
('2CH', 4, 7, '2CH.4.7', 'He made ten gold lampstands according to their specifications and placed them in the temple, five on the south side and five on the north.'),
('2CH', 4, 8, '2CH.4.8', 'Additionally, he made ten tables and placed them in the temple, five on the south side and five on the north. He also made a hundred gold bowls.'),
('2CH', 4, 9, '2CH.4.9', 'He made the courtyard of the priests and the large court with its doors, and he overlaid the doors with bronze.'),
('2CH', 4, 10, '2CH.4.10', 'He put the Sea on the south side, at the southeast corner.'),
('2CH', 4, 11, '2CH.4.11', 'Additionally, Huram made the pots, shovels, and sprinkling bowls. So Huram finished the work that he had undertaken for King Solomon in the house of God:'),
('2CH', 4, 12, '2CH.4.12', 'the two pillars; the two bowl-shaped capitals atop the pillars; the two sets of network covering both bowls of the capitals atop the pillars;'),
('2CH', 4, 13, '2CH.4.13', 'the four hundred pomegranates for the two sets of network (two rows of pomegranates for each network covering both the bowl-shaped capitals atop the pillars);'),
('2CH', 4, 14, '2CH.4.14', 'the stands; the basins on the stands;'),
('2CH', 4, 15, '2CH.4.15', 'the Sea; the twelve oxen underneath the Sea;'),
('2CH', 4, 16, '2CH.4.16', 'and the pots, shovels, meat forks, and all the other articles. All these objects that Huram-abi made for King Solomon for the house of the LORD were of polished bronze.'),
('2CH', 4, 17, '2CH.4.17', 'The king had them cast in clay molds in the plain of the Jordan between Succoth and Zeredah.'),
('2CH', 4, 18, '2CH.4.18', 'Solomon made all these articles in such great abundance that the weight of the bronze could not be determined.'),
('2CH', 4, 19, '2CH.4.19', 'Solomon also made all the furnishings for the house of God: the golden altar; the tables on which was placed the Bread of the Presence;'),
('2CH', 4, 20, '2CH.4.20', 'the lampstands of pure gold and their lamps, to burn in front of the inner sanctuary as prescribed;'),
('2CH', 4, 21, '2CH.4.21', 'the flowers, lamps, and tongs of gold—of purest gold;'),
('2CH', 4, 22, '2CH.4.22', 'the wick trimmers, sprinkling bowls, ladles, and censers of pure gold; and the gold doors of the temple: the inner doors to the Most Holy Place as well as the doors of the main hall.'),
('2CH', 5, 1, '2CH.5.1', 'So all the work that Solomon had performed for the house of the LORD was completed. Then Solomon brought in the items his father David had dedicated—the silver, the gold, and all the furnishings—and he placed them in the treasuries of the house of God.'),
('2CH', 5, 2, '2CH.5.2', 'At that time Solomon assembled in Jerusalem the elders of Israel—all the tribal heads and family leaders of the Israelites—to bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD from Zion, the City of David.'),
('2CH', 5, 3, '2CH.5.3', 'So all the men of Israel came together to the king at the feast in the seventh month.'),
('2CH', 5, 4, '2CH.5.4', 'When all the elders of Israel had arrived, the Levites took up the ark,'),
('2CH', 5, 5, '2CH.5.5', 'and they brought up the ark and the Tent of Meeting with all its sacred furnishings. The Levitical priests carried them up.'),
('2CH', 5, 6, '2CH.5.6', 'There, before the ark, King Solomon and the whole congregation of Israel who had assembled with him sacrificed so many sheep and oxen that they could not be counted or numbered.'),
('2CH', 5, 7, '2CH.5.7', 'Then the priests brought the ark of the covenant of the LORD to its place in the inner sanctuary of the temple, the Most Holy Place, beneath the wings of the cherubim.'),
('2CH', 5, 8, '2CH.5.8', 'For the cherubim spread their wings over the place of the ark and overshadowed the ark and its poles.'),
('2CH', 5, 9, '2CH.5.9', 'The poles of the ark extended far enough that their ends were visible from in front of the inner sanctuary, but not from outside the Holy Place; and they are there to this day.'),
('2CH', 5, 10, '2CH.5.10', 'There was nothing in the ark except the two tablets that Moses had placed in it at Horeb, where the LORD had made a covenant with the Israelites after they had come out of Egypt.'),
('2CH', 5, 11, '2CH.5.11', 'Now all the priests who were present had consecrated themselves regardless of their divisions. And when the priests came out of the Holy Place,'),
('2CH', 5, 12, '2CH.5.12', 'all the Levitical singers—Asaph, Heman, Jeduthun, and their sons and relatives—stood on the east side of the altar, dressed in fine linen and playing cymbals, harps, and lyres, accompanied by 120 priests sounding trumpets.'),
('2CH', 5, 13, '2CH.5.13', 'The trumpeters and singers joined together to praise and thank the LORD with one voice. They lifted up their voices, accompanied by trumpets, cymbals, and musical instruments, in praise to the LORD: “For He is good; His loving devotion endures forever.” And the temple, the house of the LORD, was filled with a cloud'),
('2CH', 5, 14, '2CH.5.14', 'so that the priests could not stand there to minister because of the cloud. For the glory of the LORD filled the house of God.'),
('2CH', 6, 1, '2CH.6.1', 'Then Solomon declared: “The LORD has said that He would dwell in the thick cloud.'),
('2CH', 6, 2, '2CH.6.2', 'But I have built You an exalted house, a place for You to dwell forever.”'),
('2CH', 6, 3, '2CH.6.3', 'And as the whole assembly of Israel stood there, the king turned around and blessed them all'),
('2CH', 6, 4, '2CH.6.4', 'and said: “Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, who has fulfilled with His own hand what He spoke with His mouth to my father David, saying,'),
('2CH', 6, 5, '2CH.6.5', '‘Since the day I brought My people out of the land of Egypt, I have not chosen a city from any tribe of Israel in which to build a house so that My Name would be there, nor have I chosen anyone to be ruler over My people Israel.'),
('2CH', 6, 6, '2CH.6.6', 'But now I have chosen Jerusalem for My Name to be there, and I have chosen David to be over My people Israel.’'),
('2CH', 6, 7, '2CH.6.7', 'Now it was in the heart of my father David to build a house for the Name of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 6, 8, '2CH.6.8', 'But the LORD said to my father David, ‘Since it was in your heart to build a house for My Name, you have done well to have this in your heart.'),
('2CH', 6, 9, '2CH.6.9', 'Nevertheless, you are not the one to build it; but your son, your own offspring, will build the house for My Name.’'),
('2CH', 6, 10, '2CH.6.10', 'Now the LORD has fulfilled the word that He spoke. I have succeeded my father David, and I sit on the throne of Israel, as the LORD promised. I have built the house for the Name of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 6, 11, '2CH.6.11', 'And there I have placed the ark, which contains the covenant of the LORD that He made with the children of Israel.”'),
('2CH', 6, 12, '2CH.6.12', 'Then Solomon stood before the altar of the LORD in front of the whole assembly of Israel and spread out his hands.'),
('2CH', 6, 13, '2CH.6.13', 'Now Solomon had made a bronze platform five cubits long, five cubits wide, and three cubits high and had placed it in the middle of the courtyard. He stood on it, knelt down before the whole assembly of Israel, spread out his hands toward heaven,'),
('2CH', 6, 14, '2CH.6.14', 'and said: “O LORD, God of Israel, there is no God like You in heaven or on earth, keeping Your covenant of loving devotion with Your servants who walk before You with all their hearts.'),
('2CH', 6, 15, '2CH.6.15', 'You have kept Your promise to Your servant, my father David. What You spoke with Your mouth You have fulfilled with Your hand this day.'),
('2CH', 6, 16, '2CH.6.16', 'Therefore now, O LORD, God of Israel, keep for Your servant, my father David, what You promised when You said: ‘You will never fail to have a man to sit before Me on the throne of Israel, if only your descendants guard their way to walk in My law as you have walked before Me.’'),
('2CH', 6, 17, '2CH.6.17', 'And now, O LORD, God of Israel, please confirm what You promised to Your servant David.'),
('2CH', 6, 18, '2CH.6.18', 'But will God indeed dwell with man upon the earth? The heavens, even the highest heavens, cannot contain You, much less this temple I have built.'),
('2CH', 6, 19, '2CH.6.19', 'Yet regard the prayer and plea of Your servant, O LORD my God, so that You may hear the cry and the prayer that Your servant is praying before You.'),
('2CH', 6, 20, '2CH.6.20', 'May Your eyes be open toward this temple day and night, toward the place where You said You would put Your Name, so that You may hear the prayer that Your servant prays toward this place.'),
('2CH', 6, 21, '2CH.6.21', 'Hear the plea of Your servant and of Your people Israel when they pray toward this place. May You hear from heaven, Your dwelling place. May You hear and forgive.'),
('2CH', 6, 22, '2CH.6.22', 'When a man sins against his neighbor and is required to take an oath, and he comes to take an oath before Your altar in this temple,'),
('2CH', 6, 23, '2CH.6.23', 'then may You hear from heaven and act. May You judge Your servants, condemning the wicked man by bringing down on his own head what he has done, and justifying the righteous man by rewarding him according to his righteousness.'),
('2CH', 6, 24, '2CH.6.24', 'When Your people Israel are defeated before an enemy because they have sinned against You, and they return to You and confess Your name, praying and pleading before You in this temple,'),
('2CH', 6, 25, '2CH.6.25', 'then may You hear from heaven and forgive the sin of Your people Israel. May You restore them to the land You gave to them and their fathers.'),
('2CH', 6, 26, '2CH.6.26', 'When the skies are shut and there is no rain because Your people have sinned against You, and they pray toward this place and confess Your name, and they turn from their sins because You have afflicted them,'),
('2CH', 6, 27, '2CH.6.27', 'then may You hear from heaven and forgive the sin of Your servants, Your people Israel, so that You may teach them the good way in which they should walk. May You send rain on the land that You gave Your people as an inheritance.'),
('2CH', 6, 28, '2CH.6.28', 'When famine or plague comes upon the land, or blight or mildew or locusts or grasshoppers, or when their enemies besiege them in their cities, whatever plague or sickness may come,'),
('2CH', 6, 29, '2CH.6.29', 'then may whatever prayer or plea Your people Israel make—each knowing his own afflictions and spreading out his hands toward this temple—'),
('2CH', 6, 30, '2CH.6.30', 'be heard by You from heaven, Your dwelling place. And may You forgive and repay each man according to all his ways, since You know his heart—for You alone know the hearts of men—'),
('2CH', 6, 31, '2CH.6.31', 'so that they may fear You and walk in Your ways all the days they live in the land that You gave to our fathers.'),
('2CH', 6, 32, '2CH.6.32', 'And as for the foreigner who is not of Your people Israel but has come from a distant land because of Your great name and Your mighty hand and outstretched arm—when he comes and prays toward this temple,'),
('2CH', 6, 33, '2CH.6.33', 'then may You hear from heaven, Your dwelling place, and do according to all for which the foreigner calls to You. Then all the peoples of the earth will know Your name and fear You, as do Your people Israel, and they will know that this house I have built is called by Your Name.'),
('2CH', 6, 34, '2CH.6.34', 'When Your people go to war against their enemies, wherever You send them, and when they pray to You in the direction of this city You have chosen and the house I have built for Your Name,'),
('2CH', 6, 35, '2CH.6.35', 'then may You hear from heaven their prayer and their plea, and may You uphold their cause.'),
('2CH', 6, 36, '2CH.6.36', 'When they sin against You—for there is no one who does not sin—and You become angry with them and deliver them to an enemy who takes them as captives to a land far or near,'),
('2CH', 6, 37, '2CH.6.37', 'and when they come to their senses in the land to which they were taken, and they repent and plead with You in the land of their captors, saying, ‘We have sinned and done wrong; we have acted wickedly,’'),
('2CH', 6, 38, '2CH.6.38', 'and when they return to You with all their heart and soul in the land of the enemies who took them captive, and when they pray in the direction of the land that You gave to their fathers, the city You have chosen, and the house I have built for Your Name,'),
('2CH', 6, 39, '2CH.6.39', 'then may You hear from heaven, Your dwelling place, their prayer and pleas, and may You uphold their cause. May You forgive Your people who sinned against You.'),
('2CH', 6, 40, '2CH.6.40', 'Now, my God, may Your eyes be open and Your ears attentive to the prayer offered in this place.'),
('2CH', 6, 41, '2CH.6.41', 'Now therefore, arise, O LORD God, and enter Your resting place, You and the ark of Your might. May Your priests, O LORD God, be clothed with salvation, and may Your godly ones rejoice in goodness.'),
('2CH', 6, 42, '2CH.6.42', 'O LORD God, do not reject Your anointed one. Remember Your loving devotion to Your servant David.”'),
('2CH', 7, 1, '2CH.7.1', 'When Solomon had finished praying, fire came down from heaven and consumed the burnt offering and the sacrifices, and the glory of the LORD filled the temple.'),
('2CH', 7, 2, '2CH.7.2', 'The priests were unable to enter the house of the LORD, because the glory of the LORD had filled it.'),
('2CH', 7, 3, '2CH.7.3', 'When all the Israelites saw the fire coming down and the glory of the LORD above the temple, they bowed down on the pavement with their faces to the ground, and they worshiped and gave thanks to the LORD: “For He is good; His loving devotion endures forever.”'),
('2CH', 7, 4, '2CH.7.4', 'Then the king and all the people offered sacrifices before the LORD.'),
('2CH', 7, 5, '2CH.7.5', 'And King Solomon offered a sacrifice of 22,000 oxen and 120,000 sheep. So the king and all the people dedicated the house of God.'),
('2CH', 7, 6, '2CH.7.6', 'The priests stood at their posts, as did the Levites with the musical instruments of the LORD, which King David had made for giving thanks to the LORD and with which David had offered praise, saying, “For His loving devotion endures forever.” Across from the Levites, the priests sounded trumpets, and all the Israelites were standing.'),
('2CH', 7, 7, '2CH.7.7', 'Then Solomon consecrated the middle of the courtyard in front of the house of the LORD, and there he offered the burnt offerings and the fat of the peace offerings, since the bronze altar he had made could not hold all these offerings.'),
('2CH', 7, 8, '2CH.7.8', 'So at that time Solomon and all Israel with him—a very great assembly of people from Lebo-hamath to the Brook of Egypt—kept the feast for seven days.'),
('2CH', 7, 9, '2CH.7.9', 'On the eighth day they held a solemn assembly, for the dedication of the altar had lasted seven days, and the feast seven days more.'),
('2CH', 7, 10, '2CH.7.10', 'On the twenty-third day of the seventh month, Solomon sent the people away to their homes, joyful and glad of heart for the good things that the LORD had done for David, for Solomon, and for His people Israel.'),
('2CH', 7, 11, '2CH.7.11', 'When Solomon had finished the house of the LORD and the royal palace, successfully carrying out all that was in his heart to do for the house of the LORD and for his own palace,'),
('2CH', 7, 12, '2CH.7.12', 'the LORD appeared to him at night and said to him: “I have heard your prayer and have chosen this place for Myself as a house of sacrifice.'),
('2CH', 7, 13, '2CH.7.13', 'If I close the sky so there is no rain, or if I command the locust to devour the land, or if I send a plague among My people,'),
('2CH', 7, 14, '2CH.7.14', 'and if My people who are called by My name humble themselves and pray and seek My face and turn from their wicked ways, then I will hear from heaven, forgive their sin, and heal their land.'),
('2CH', 7, 15, '2CH.7.15', 'Now My eyes will be open and My ears attentive to the prayers offered in this place.'),
('2CH', 7, 16, '2CH.7.16', 'For I have now chosen and consecrated this temple so that My Name may be there forever. My eyes and My heart will be there for all time.'),
('2CH', 7, 17, '2CH.7.17', 'And as for you, if you walk before Me as your father David walked, doing all I have commanded you, and if you keep My statutes and ordinances,'),
('2CH', 7, 18, '2CH.7.18', 'then I will establish your royal throne, as I covenanted with your father David when I said, ‘You will never fail to have a man to rule over Israel.’'),
('2CH', 7, 19, '2CH.7.19', 'But if you turn away and forsake the statutes and commandments I have set before you, and if you go off to serve and worship other gods,'),
('2CH', 7, 20, '2CH.7.20', 'then I will uproot Israel from the soil I have given them, and I will banish from My presence this temple I have sanctified for My Name. I will make it an object of scorn and ridicule among all the peoples.'),
('2CH', 7, 21, '2CH.7.21', 'And when this temple has become a heap of rubble, all who pass by it will be appalled and say, ‘Why has the LORD done such a thing to this land and to this temple?’'),
('2CH', 7, 22, '2CH.7.22', 'And others will answer, ‘Because they have forsaken the LORD, the God of their fathers, who brought them out of the land of Egypt, and have embraced other gods, worshiping and serving them—because of this, He has brought all this disaster upon them.’”'),
('2CH', 8, 1, '2CH.8.1', 'Now at the end of the twenty years during which Solomon had built the house of the LORD and his own palace,'),
('2CH', 8, 2, '2CH.8.2', 'Solomon rebuilt the cities Hiram had given him and settled Israelites there.'),
('2CH', 8, 3, '2CH.8.3', 'Then Solomon went to Hamath-zobah and captured it.'),
('2CH', 8, 4, '2CH.8.4', 'He built Tadmor in the wilderness, in addition to all the store cities that he had built in Hamath.'),
('2CH', 8, 5, '2CH.8.5', 'He rebuilt Upper and Lower Beth-horon as fortified cities with walls, gates, and bars,'),
('2CH', 8, 6, '2CH.8.6', 'as well as Baalath, all the store cities that belonged to Solomon, and all the cities for his chariots and horses—whatever he desired to build in Jerusalem, Lebanon, and throughout the land of his dominion.'),
('2CH', 8, 7, '2CH.8.7', 'As for all the people who remained of the Hittites, Amorites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites (these people were not Israelites)—'),
('2CH', 8, 8, '2CH.8.8', 'their descendants who remained in the land, those whom the Israelites had not destroyed—Solomon conscripted these people to be forced laborers, as they are to this day.'),
('2CH', 8, 9, '2CH.8.9', 'But Solomon did not consign any of the Israelites to slave labor, because they were his men of war, the leaders of his captains, and the commanders of his chariots and cavalry.'),
('2CH', 8, 10, '2CH.8.10', 'They were also the chief officers for King Solomon: 250 supervisors.'),
('2CH', 8, 11, '2CH.8.11', 'Solomon brought the daughter of Pharaoh up from the City of David to the palace he had built for her. For he said, “My wife must not live in the house of David king of Israel, because the places the ark of the LORD has entered are holy.”'),
('2CH', 8, 12, '2CH.8.12', 'At that time Solomon offered burnt offerings to the LORD on the altar of the LORD he had built in front of the portico.'),
('2CH', 8, 13, '2CH.8.13', 'He observed the daily requirement for offerings according to the commandment of Moses for Sabbaths, New Moons, and the three annual appointed feasts—the Feast of Unleavened Bread, the Feast of Weeks, and the Feast of Tabernacles.'),
('2CH', 8, 14, '2CH.8.14', 'In keeping with the ordinances of his father David, Solomon appointed the divisions of the priests over their service, and the Levites for their duties to offer praise and to minister before the priests according to the daily requirement. He also appointed gatekeepers by their divisions at each gate, for this had been the command of David, the man of God.'),
('2CH', 8, 15, '2CH.8.15', 'They did not turn aside from the king’s command regarding the priests or the Levites in any matter, including that of the treasuries.'),
('2CH', 8, 16, '2CH.8.16', 'Thus all the work of Solomon was carried out, from the day the foundation was laid for the house of the LORD until it was finished. So the house of the LORD was completed.'),
('2CH', 8, 17, '2CH.8.17', 'Then Solomon went to Ezion-geber and to Eloth on the coast of Edom.'),
('2CH', 8, 18, '2CH.8.18', 'So Hiram sent him ships captained by his servants, along with crews of experienced sailors. They went with Solomon’s servants to Ophir and acquired from there 450 talents of gold, which they delivered to King Solomon.'),
('2CH', 9, 1, '2CH.9.1', 'Now when the queen of Sheba heard about the fame of Solomon, she came to test him with difficult questions. She arrived in Jerusalem with a very large caravan—with camels bearing spices, gold in abundance, and precious stones. And she came to Solomon and spoke with him about all that was on her mind.'),
('2CH', 9, 2, '2CH.9.2', 'And Solomon answered all her questions; nothing was too difficult for him to explain.'),
('2CH', 9, 3, '2CH.9.3', 'When the queen of Sheba saw the wisdom of Solomon, the palace he had built,'),
('2CH', 9, 4, '2CH.9.4', 'the food at his table, the seating of his servants, the service and attire of his attendants, the attire of his cupbearers, and the burnt offerings he presented at the house of the LORD, it took her breath away.'),
('2CH', 9, 5, '2CH.9.5', 'She said to the king, “The report I heard in my own country about your words and wisdom is true.'),
('2CH', 9, 6, '2CH.9.6', 'But I did not believe the reports until I came and saw with my own eyes. Indeed, not half of the greatness of your wisdom was told to me. You have far exceeded the report I heard.'),
('2CH', 9, 7, '2CH.9.7', 'How blessed are your men! How blessed are these servants of yours who stand continually before you and hear your wisdom!'),
('2CH', 9, 8, '2CH.9.8', 'Blessed be the LORD your God, who has delighted in you to set you on His throne to be king for the LORD your God. Because your God loved Israel enough to establish them forever, He has made you king over them to carry out justice and righteousness.”'),
('2CH', 9, 9, '2CH.9.9', 'Then she gave the king 120 talents of gold, a great quantity of spices, and precious stones. There had never been such spices as those the queen of Sheba gave to King Solomon.'),
('2CH', 9, 10, '2CH.9.10', '(The servants of Hiram and of Solomon who brought gold from Ophir also brought algum wood and precious stones.'),
('2CH', 9, 11, '2CH.9.11', 'The king made the algum wood into steps for the house of the LORD and for the king’s palace, and into lyres and harps for the singers. Never before had anything like them been seen in the land of Judah.)'),
('2CH', 9, 12, '2CH.9.12', 'King Solomon gave the queen of Sheba all she desired—whatever she asked—far more than she had brought the king. Then she left and returned to her own country, along with her servants.'),
('2CH', 9, 13, '2CH.9.13', 'The weight of gold that came to Solomon each year was 666 talents,'),
('2CH', 9, 14, '2CH.9.14', 'not including the revenue from the merchants and traders. And all the Arabian kings and governors of the land also brought gold and silver to Solomon.'),
('2CH', 9, 15, '2CH.9.15', 'King Solomon made two hundred large shields of hammered gold; six hundred shekels of hammered gold went into each shield.'),
('2CH', 9, 16, '2CH.9.16', 'He also made three hundred small shields of hammered gold; three hundred shekels of gold went into each shield. And the king put them in the House of the Forest of Lebanon.'),
('2CH', 9, 17, '2CH.9.17', 'Additionally, the king made a great throne of ivory and overlaid it with pure gold.'),
('2CH', 9, 18, '2CH.9.18', 'The throne had six steps, and a footstool of gold was attached to it. There were armrests on both sides of the seat, with a lion standing beside each armrest.'),
('2CH', 9, 19, '2CH.9.19', 'Twelve lions stood on the six steps, one at either end of each step. Nothing like this had ever been made for any kingdom.'),
('2CH', 9, 20, '2CH.9.20', 'All King Solomon’s drinking cups were gold, and all the utensils of the House of the Forest of Lebanon were pure gold. There was no silver, because it was accounted as nothing in the days of Solomon.'),
('2CH', 9, 21, '2CH.9.21', 'For the king had the ships of Tarshish that went with Hiram’s servants, and once every three years the ships of Tarshish would arrive bearing gold, silver, ivory, apes, and peacocks.'),
('2CH', 9, 22, '2CH.9.22', 'So King Solomon surpassed all the kings of the earth in riches and wisdom.'),
('2CH', 9, 23, '2CH.9.23', 'All the kings of the earth sought an audience with Solomon to hear the wisdom that God had put in his heart.'),
('2CH', 9, 24, '2CH.9.24', 'Year after year, each visitor would bring his tribute: articles of silver and gold, clothing, weapons, spices, horses, and mules.'),
('2CH', 9, 25, '2CH.9.25', 'Solomon had 4,000 stalls for horses and chariots, and 12,000 horses, which he stationed in the chariot cities and also with him in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 9, 26, '2CH.9.26', 'He reigned over all the kings from the Euphrates to the land of the Philistines, as far as the border of Egypt.'),
('2CH', 9, 27, '2CH.9.27', 'The king made silver as common in Jerusalem as stones, and cedar as abundant as sycamore in the foothills.'),
('2CH', 9, 28, '2CH.9.28', 'Solomon’s horses were imported from Egypt and from all the lands.'),
('2CH', 9, 29, '2CH.9.29', 'As for the rest of the acts of Solomon, from beginning to end, are they not written in the Records of Nathan the Prophet, in the Prophecy of Ahijah the Shilonite, and in the Visions of Iddo the Seer concerning Jeroboam son of Nebat?'),
('2CH', 9, 30, '2CH.9.30', 'Solomon reigned in Jerusalem over all Israel forty years.'),
('2CH', 9, 31, '2CH.9.31', 'And Solomon rested with his fathers and was buried in the city of his father David. And his son Rehoboam reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 10, 1, '2CH.10.1', 'Then Rehoboam went to Shechem, for all Israel had gone there to make him king.'),
('2CH', 10, 2, '2CH.10.2', 'When Jeroboam son of Nebat heard about this, he returned from Egypt, where he had fled from King Solomon.'),
('2CH', 10, 3, '2CH.10.3', 'So they sent for Jeroboam, and he and all Israel came to Rehoboam and said,'),
('2CH', 10, 4, '2CH.10.4', '“Your father put a heavy yoke on us. But now you must lighten the burden of your father’s service and the heavy yoke he put on us, and we will serve you.”'),
('2CH', 10, 5, '2CH.10.5', 'Rehoboam answered, “Come back to me in three days.” So the people departed.'),
('2CH', 10, 6, '2CH.10.6', 'Then King Rehoboam consulted with the elders who had served his father Solomon during his lifetime. “How do you advise me to respond to these people?” he asked.'),
('2CH', 10, 7, '2CH.10.7', 'They replied, “If you will be kind to these people and please them by speaking kind words to them, they will be your servants forever.”'),
('2CH', 10, 8, '2CH.10.8', 'But Rehoboam rejected the advice of the elders; instead, he consulted the young men who had grown up with him and served him.'),
('2CH', 10, 9, '2CH.10.9', 'He asked them, “What message do you advise that we send back to these people who have spoken to me, saying, ‘Lighten the yoke your father put on us’?”'),
('2CH', 10, 10, '2CH.10.10', 'The young men who had grown up with him replied, “This is how you should answer these people who said to you, ‘Your father made our yoke heavy, but you must make it lighter.’ This is what you should tell them: ‘My little finger is thicker than my father’s waist!'),
('2CH', 10, 11, '2CH.10.11', 'Whereas my father burdened you with a heavy yoke, I will add to your yoke. Whereas my father scourged you with whips, I will scourge you with scorpions.’”'),
('2CH', 10, 12, '2CH.10.12', 'After three days, Jeroboam and all the people returned to Rehoboam, since the king had said, “Come back to me on the third day.”'),
('2CH', 10, 13, '2CH.10.13', 'And the king answered them harshly. King Rehoboam rejected the advice of the elders'),
('2CH', 10, 14, '2CH.10.14', 'and spoke to them as the young men had advised, saying, “Whereas my father made your yoke heavy, I will add to your yoke. Whereas my father scourged you with whips, I will scourge you with scorpions.”'),
('2CH', 10, 15, '2CH.10.15', 'So the king did not listen to the people, and indeed this turn of events was from God, in order that the LORD might fulfill the word that He had spoken through Ahijah the Shilonite to Jeroboam son of Nebat.'),
('2CH', 10, 16, '2CH.10.16', 'When all Israel saw that the king had refused to listen to them, they answered the king: “What portion do we have in David, and what inheritance in the son of Jesse? To your tents, O Israel! Look now to your own house, O David!” So all the Israelites went home,'),
('2CH', 10, 17, '2CH.10.17', 'but Rehoboam still reigned over the Israelites living in the cities of Judah.'),
('2CH', 10, 18, '2CH.10.18', 'Then King Rehoboam sent out Hadoram, who was in charge of the forced labor, but the Israelites stoned him to death. And King Rehoboam mounted his chariot in haste and escaped to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 10, 19, '2CH.10.19', 'So to this day Israel has been in rebellion against the house of David.'),
('2CH', 11, 1, '2CH.11.1', 'When Rehoboam arrived in Jerusalem, he mobilized the house of Judah and Benjamin—180,000 chosen warriors—to fight against Israel and restore the kingdom to Rehoboam.'),
('2CH', 11, 2, '2CH.11.2', 'But the word of the LORD came to Shemaiah the man of God:'),
('2CH', 11, 3, '2CH.11.3', '“Tell Rehoboam son of Solomon king of Judah and all the Israelites in Judah and Benjamin'),
('2CH', 11, 4, '2CH.11.4', 'that this is what the LORD says: ‘You are not to go up and fight against your brothers. Each of you must return home, for this is My doing.’” So they listened to the words of the LORD and turned back from going against Jeroboam.'),
('2CH', 11, 5, '2CH.11.5', 'Rehoboam lived in Jerusalem, and he built up cities for defense in Judah.'),
('2CH', 11, 6, '2CH.11.6', 'He built up Bethlehem, Etam, Tekoa,'),
('2CH', 11, 7, '2CH.11.7', 'Beth-zur, Soco, Adullam,'),
('2CH', 11, 8, '2CH.11.8', 'Gath, Mareshah, Ziph,'),
('2CH', 11, 9, '2CH.11.9', 'Adoraim, Lachish, Azekah,'),
('2CH', 11, 10, '2CH.11.10', 'Zorah, Aijalon, and Hebron, the fortified cities in Judah and Benjamin.'),
('2CH', 11, 11, '2CH.11.11', 'He strengthened their fortifications and put officers in them, with supplies of food, oil, and wine.'),
('2CH', 11, 12, '2CH.11.12', 'He also put shields and spears in all the cities and strengthened them greatly. So Judah and Benjamin belonged to him.'),
('2CH', 11, 13, '2CH.11.13', 'Moreover, the priests and Levites from all their districts throughout Israel stood with Rehoboam.'),
('2CH', 11, 14, '2CH.11.14', 'For the Levites left their pasturelands and their possessions and went to Judah and Jerusalem, because Jeroboam and his sons had rejected them as priests of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 11, 15, '2CH.11.15', 'And Jeroboam appointed his own priests for the high places and for the goat demons and calf idols he had made.'),
('2CH', 11, 16, '2CH.11.16', 'Those from every tribe of Israel who had set their hearts to seek the LORD their God followed the Levites to Jerusalem to sacrifice to the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 11, 17, '2CH.11.17', 'So they strengthened the kingdom of Judah and supported Rehoboam son of Solomon for three years, because they walked for three years in the way of David and Solomon.'),
('2CH', 11, 18, '2CH.11.18', 'And Rehoboam married Mahalath, who was the daughter of David’s son Jerimoth and of Abihail, the daughter of Jesse’s son Eliab.'),
('2CH', 11, 19, '2CH.11.19', 'She bore sons to him: Jeush, Shemariah, and Zaham.'),
('2CH', 11, 20, '2CH.11.20', 'After her, he married Maacah daughter of Absalom, and she bore to him Abijah, Attai, Ziza, and Shelomith.'),
('2CH', 11, 21, '2CH.11.21', 'Rehoboam loved Maacah daughter of Absalom more than all his wives and concubines. In all, he had eighteen wives and sixty concubines, and he was the father of twenty-eight sons and sixty daughters.'),
('2CH', 11, 22, '2CH.11.22', 'Rehoboam appointed Abijah son of Maacah as chief prince among his brothers, intending to make him king.'),
('2CH', 11, 23, '2CH.11.23', 'Rehoboam also acted wisely by dispersing some of his sons throughout the districts of Judah and Benjamin, and to all the fortified cities. He gave them abundant provisions and sought many wives for them.'),
('2CH', 12, 1, '2CH.12.1', 'After Rehoboam had established his sovereignty and royal power, he and all Israel with him forsook the Law of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 12, 2, '2CH.12.2', 'In the fifth year of Rehoboam’s reign, because they had been unfaithful to the LORD, Shishak king of Egypt attacked Jerusalem'),
('2CH', 12, 3, '2CH.12.3', 'with 1,200 chariots, 60,000 horsemen, and countless troops who came with him out of Egypt—Libyans, Sukkites, and Cushites.'),
('2CH', 12, 4, '2CH.12.4', 'He captured the fortified cities of Judah and came as far as Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 12, 5, '2CH.12.5', 'Then Shemaiah the prophet came to Rehoboam and the leaders of Judah who had gathered at Jerusalem because of Shishak, and he said to them, “This is what the LORD says: ‘You have forsaken Me; therefore, I have forsaken you into the hand of Shishak.’”'),
('2CH', 12, 6, '2CH.12.6', 'So the leaders of Israel and the king humbled themselves and said, “The LORD is righteous.”'),
('2CH', 12, 7, '2CH.12.7', 'When the LORD saw that they had humbled themselves, the word of the LORD came to Shemaiah, saying, “They have humbled themselves; I will not destroy them, but will soon grant them deliverance. My wrath will not be poured out on Jerusalem through Shishak.'),
('2CH', 12, 8, '2CH.12.8', 'Nevertheless, they will become his servants, so that they may learn the difference between serving Me and serving the kings of other lands.”'),
('2CH', 12, 9, '2CH.12.9', 'So King Shishak of Egypt attacked Jerusalem and seized the treasures of the house of the LORD and of the royal palace. He took everything, including the gold shields that Solomon had made.'),
('2CH', 12, 10, '2CH.12.10', 'Then King Rehoboam made bronze shields in their place and committed them to the care of the captains of the guard on duty at the entrance to the royal palace.'),
('2CH', 12, 11, '2CH.12.11', 'And whenever the king entered the house of the LORD, the guards would go with him, bearing the shields, and later they would return them to the guardroom.'),
('2CH', 12, 12, '2CH.12.12', 'Because Rehoboam humbled himself, the anger of the LORD turned away from him, and He did not destroy him completely. Indeed, conditions were good in Judah.'),
('2CH', 12, 13, '2CH.12.13', 'Thus King Rehoboam established himself in Jerusalem and reigned. He was forty-one years old when he became king, and he reigned seventeen years in Jerusalem, the city the LORD had chosen from all the tribes of Israel in which to put His Name. His mother’s name was Naamah the Ammonite.'),
('2CH', 12, 14, '2CH.12.14', 'And Rehoboam did evil because he did not set his heart to seek the LORD.'),
('2CH', 12, 15, '2CH.12.15', 'Now the acts of Rehoboam, from first to last, are they not written in the records of Shemaiah the Prophet and of Iddo the Seer concerning the genealogies? There was war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam throughout their days.'),
('2CH', 12, 16, '2CH.12.16', 'And Rehoboam rested with his fathers and was buried in the City of David. And his son Abijah reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 13, 1, '2CH.13.1', 'In the eighteenth year of Jeroboam’s reign, Abijah became king of Judah,'),
('2CH', 13, 2, '2CH.13.2', 'and he reigned in Jerusalem three years. His mother’s name was Micaiah daughter of Uriel; she was from Gibeah. And there was war between Abijah and Jeroboam.'),
('2CH', 13, 3, '2CH.13.3', 'Abijah went into battle with an army of 400,000 chosen men, while Jeroboam drew up in formation against him with 800,000 chosen and mighty men of valor.'),
('2CH', 13, 4, '2CH.13.4', 'Then Abijah stood on Mount Zemaraim in the hill country of Ephraim and said, “Hear me, O Jeroboam and all Israel!'),
('2CH', 13, 5, '2CH.13.5', 'Do you not know that the LORD, the God of Israel, has given the kingship of Israel to David and his descendants forever by a covenant of salt?'),
('2CH', 13, 6, '2CH.13.6', 'Yet Jeroboam son of Nebat, a servant of Solomon son of David, rose up and rebelled against his master.'),
('2CH', 13, 7, '2CH.13.7', 'Then worthless and wicked men gathered around him to resist Rehoboam son of Solomon when he was young, inexperienced, and unable to resist them.'),
('2CH', 13, 8, '2CH.13.8', 'And now you think you can resist the kingdom of the LORD, which is in the hands of David’s descendants. You are indeed a vast army, and you have with you the golden calves that Jeroboam made for you as gods.'),
('2CH', 13, 9, '2CH.13.9', 'But did you not drive out the priests of the LORD, the sons of Aaron, and the Levites? And did you not make priests for yourselves as do the peoples of other lands? Now whoever comes to consecrate himself with a young bull and seven rams can become a priest of things that are not gods.'),
('2CH', 13, 10, '2CH.13.10', 'But as for us, the LORD is our God. We have not forsaken Him; the priests who minister to the LORD are sons of Aaron, and the Levites attend to their duties.'),
('2CH', 13, 11, '2CH.13.11', 'Every morning and every evening they present burnt offerings and fragrant incense to the LORD. They set out the rows of showbread on the ceremonially clean table, and every evening they light the lamps of the gold lampstand. We are carrying out the requirements of the LORD our God, while you have forsaken Him.'),
('2CH', 13, 12, '2CH.13.12', 'Now behold, God Himself is with us as our head, and His priests with their trumpets sound the battle call against you. O children of Israel, do not fight against the LORD, the God of your fathers, for you will not succeed.”'),
('2CH', 13, 13, '2CH.13.13', 'Now Jeroboam had sent troops around to ambush from the rear, so that while he was in front of Judah, the ambush was behind them.'),
('2CH', 13, 14, '2CH.13.14', 'When Judah turned and discovered that the battle was both before and behind them, they cried out to the LORD. Then the priests blew the trumpets,'),
('2CH', 13, 15, '2CH.13.15', 'and the men of Judah raised the battle cry. And when they raised the cry, God routed Jeroboam and all Israel before Abijah and Judah.'),
('2CH', 13, 16, '2CH.13.16', 'So the Israelites fled before Judah, and God delivered them into their hands.'),
('2CH', 13, 17, '2CH.13.17', 'Then Abijah and his people struck them with a mighty blow, and 500,000 chosen men of Israel fell slain.'),
('2CH', 13, 18, '2CH.13.18', 'Thus the Israelites were subdued at that time, and the men of Judah prevailed because they relied on the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 13, 19, '2CH.13.19', 'Abijah pursued Jeroboam and captured some cities from him: Bethel, Jeshanah, and Ephron, along with their villages.'),
('2CH', 13, 20, '2CH.13.20', 'Jeroboam did not again recover his power during the days of Abijah, and the LORD struck him down and he died.'),
('2CH', 13, 21, '2CH.13.21', 'But Abijah grew strong, married fourteen wives, and became the father of twenty-two sons and sixteen daughters.'),
('2CH', 13, 22, '2CH.13.22', 'Now the rest of the acts of Abijah, along with his ways and his words, are written in the Treatise of the Prophet Iddo.'),
('2CH', 14, 1, '2CH.14.1', 'Then Abijah rested with his fathers and was buried in the City of David. And his son Asa reigned in his place, and in his days the land was at peace for ten years.'),
('2CH', 14, 2, '2CH.14.2', 'And Asa did what was good and right in the eyes of the LORD his God.'),
('2CH', 14, 3, '2CH.14.3', 'He removed the foreign altars and high places, shattered the sacred pillars, and chopped down the Asherah poles.'),
('2CH', 14, 4, '2CH.14.4', 'He commanded the people of Judah to seek the LORD, the God of their fathers, and to observe the law and the commandments.'),
('2CH', 14, 5, '2CH.14.5', 'He also removed the high places and incense altars from all the cities of Judah, and under him the kingdom was at peace.'),
('2CH', 14, 6, '2CH.14.6', 'Because the land was at peace, Asa built fortified cities in Judah. In those days no one made war with him, because the LORD had given him rest.'),
('2CH', 14, 7, '2CH.14.7', 'So he said to the people of Judah, “Let us build these cities and surround them with walls and towers, with doors and bars. The land is still ours because we have sought the LORD our God. We have sought Him, and He has given us rest on every side.” So they built and prospered.'),
('2CH', 14, 8, '2CH.14.8', 'Asa had an army of 300,000 men from Judah bearing large shields and spears, and 280,000 men from Benjamin bearing small shields and drawing the bow. All these were mighty men of valor.'),
('2CH', 14, 9, '2CH.14.9', 'Then Zerah the Cushite came against them with an army of 1,000,000 men and 300 chariots, and they advanced as far as Mareshah.'),
('2CH', 14, 10, '2CH.14.10', 'So Asa marched out against him and lined up in battle formation in the Valley of Zephathah near Mareshah.'),
('2CH', 14, 11, '2CH.14.11', 'Then Asa cried out to the LORD his God: “O LORD, there is no one besides You to help the powerless against the mighty. Help us, O LORD our God, for we rely on You, and in Your name we have come against this multitude. O LORD, You are our God. Do not let a mere mortal prevail against You.”'),
('2CH', 14, 12, '2CH.14.12', 'So the LORD struck down the Cushites before Asa and Judah, and the Cushites fled.'),
('2CH', 14, 13, '2CH.14.13', 'Then Asa and his army pursued them as far as Gerar. The Cushites fell and could not recover, for they were crushed before the LORD and His army. So the people of Judah carried off a great amount of plunder'),
('2CH', 14, 14, '2CH.14.14', 'and attacked all the cities around Gerar, because the terror of the LORD had fallen upon them. They plundered all the cities, since there was much plunder there.'),
('2CH', 14, 15, '2CH.14.15', 'They also attacked the tents of the herdsmen and carried off many sheep and camels. Then they returned to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 15, 1, '2CH.15.1', 'Now the Spirit of God came upon Azariah son of Oded.'),
('2CH', 15, 2, '2CH.15.2', 'So he went out to meet Asa and said to him, “Listen to me, Asa and all Judah and Benjamin. The LORD is with you when you are with Him. If you seek Him, He will be found by you, but if you forsake Him, He will forsake you.'),
('2CH', 15, 3, '2CH.15.3', 'For many years Israel has been without the true God, without a priest to instruct them, and without the law.'),
('2CH', 15, 4, '2CH.15.4', 'But in their distress they turned to the LORD, the God of Israel, and sought Him, and He was found by them.'),
('2CH', 15, 5, '2CH.15.5', 'In those days there was no safety for travelers, because the residents of the lands had many conflicts.'),
('2CH', 15, 6, '2CH.15.6', 'Nation was crushed by nation, and city by city, for God afflicted them with all kinds of adversity.'),
('2CH', 15, 7, '2CH.15.7', 'But as for you, be strong; do not be discouraged, for your work will be rewarded.”'),
('2CH', 15, 8, '2CH.15.8', 'When Asa heard these words and the prophecy of Azariah son of Oded the prophet, he took courage and removed the detestable idols from the whole land of Judah and Benjamin and from the cities he had captured in the hill country of Ephraim. He then restored the altar of the LORD that was in front of the portico of the LORD’s temple.'),
('2CH', 15, 9, '2CH.15.9', 'And he assembled all Judah and Benjamin, along with those from the tribes of Ephraim, Manasseh, and Simeon who had settled among them, for great numbers had come over to him from Israel when they saw that the LORD his God was with him.'),
('2CH', 15, 10, '2CH.15.10', 'So they gathered together in Jerusalem in the third month of the fifteenth year of Asa’s reign.'),
('2CH', 15, 11, '2CH.15.11', 'At that time they sacrificed to the LORD seven hundred oxen and seven thousand sheep from all the plunder they had brought back.'),
('2CH', 15, 12, '2CH.15.12', 'Then they entered into a covenant to seek the LORD, the God of their fathers, with all their heart and soul.'),
('2CH', 15, 13, '2CH.15.13', 'And whoever would not seek the LORD, the God of Israel, would be put to death, whether young or old, man or woman.'),
('2CH', 15, 14, '2CH.15.14', 'They took an oath to the LORD with a loud voice, with shouting, trumpets, and rams’ horns.'),
('2CH', 15, 15, '2CH.15.15', 'And all Judah rejoiced over the oath, for they had sworn it with all their heart. They had sought Him earnestly, and He was found by them. So the LORD gave them rest on every side.'),
('2CH', 15, 16, '2CH.15.16', 'King Asa also removed his grandmother Maacah from her position as queen mother because she had made a detestable Asherah pole. Asa chopped down the pole, crushed it, and burned it in the Kidron Valley.'),
('2CH', 15, 17, '2CH.15.17', 'The high places were not removed from Israel, but Asa’s heart was fully devoted all his days.'),
('2CH', 15, 18, '2CH.15.18', 'And he brought into the house of God the silver and gold and the articles that he and his father had dedicated.'),
('2CH', 15, 19, '2CH.15.19', 'And there was no war until the thirty-fifth year of Asa’s reign.'),
('2CH', 16, 1, '2CH.16.1', 'In the thirty-sixth year of Asa’s reign, Baasha king of Israel went up against Judah and fortified Ramah to prevent anyone from leaving or entering the territory of Asa king of Judah.'),
('2CH', 16, 2, '2CH.16.2', 'So Asa withdrew the silver and gold from the treasuries of the house of the LORD and the royal palace, and he sent it with this message to Ben-hadad king of Aram, who was ruling in Damascus:'),
('2CH', 16, 3, '2CH.16.3', '“Let there be a treaty between me and you as there was between my father and your father. See, I have sent you silver and gold. Now go and break your treaty with Baasha king of Israel, so that he will withdraw from me.”'),
('2CH', 16, 4, '2CH.16.4', 'And Ben-hadad listened to King Asa and sent the commanders of his armies against the cities of Israel, conquering Ijon, Dan, Abel-maim, and all the store cities of Naphtali.'),
('2CH', 16, 5, '2CH.16.5', 'When Baasha learned of this, he stopped fortifying Ramah and abandoned his work.'),
('2CH', 16, 6, '2CH.16.6', 'Then King Asa brought all the men of Judah, and they carried away the stones of Ramah and the timbers Baasha had used for building. And with these materials he built up Geba and Mizpah.'),
('2CH', 16, 7, '2CH.16.7', 'At that time Hanani the seer came to King Asa of Judah and told him, “Because you have relied on the king of Aram and not on the LORD your God, the army of the king of Aram has escaped from your hand.'),
('2CH', 16, 8, '2CH.16.8', 'Were not the Cushites and Libyans a vast army with many chariots and horsemen? Yet because you relied on the LORD, He delivered them into your hand.'),
('2CH', 16, 9, '2CH.16.9', 'For the eyes of the LORD roam to and fro over all the earth, to show Himself strong on behalf of those whose hearts are fully devoted to Him. You have acted foolishly in this matter. From now on, therefore, you will be at war.”'),
('2CH', 16, 10, '2CH.16.10', 'Asa was angry with the seer and became so enraged over this matter that he put the man in prison. And at the same time Asa oppressed some of the people.'),
('2CH', 16, 11, '2CH.16.11', 'Now the acts of Asa, from beginning to end, are indeed written in the Book of the Kings of Judah and Israel.'),
('2CH', 16, 12, '2CH.16.12', 'In the thirty-ninth year of his reign, Asa became diseased in his feet, and his disease became increasingly severe. Yet even in his illness he did not seek the LORD, but only the physicians.'),
('2CH', 16, 13, '2CH.16.13', 'So in the forty-first year of his reign, Asa died and rested with his fathers.'),
('2CH', 16, 14, '2CH.16.14', 'And he was buried in the tomb that he had cut out for himself in the City of David. They laid him on a bier that was full of spices and various blended perfumes; then they made a great fire in his honor.'),
('2CH', 17, 1, '2CH.17.1', 'Asa’s son Jehoshaphat reigned in his place, and he strengthened himself against Israel.'),
('2CH', 17, 2, '2CH.17.2', 'He stationed troops in every fortified city of Judah and put garrisons in the land of Judah and in the cities of Ephraim that his father Asa had captured.'),
('2CH', 17, 3, '2CH.17.3', 'Now the LORD was with Jehoshaphat because he walked in the earlier ways of his father David. He did not seek the Baals,'),
('2CH', 17, 4, '2CH.17.4', 'but he sought the God of his father and walked by His commandments rather than the practices of Israel.'),
('2CH', 17, 5, '2CH.17.5', 'So the LORD established the kingdom in his hand, and all Judah brought him tribute, so that he had an abundance of riches and honor.'),
('2CH', 17, 6, '2CH.17.6', 'And his heart took delight in the ways of the LORD; furthermore, he removed the high places and Asherah poles from Judah.'),
('2CH', 17, 7, '2CH.17.7', 'In the third year of his reign, Jehoshaphat sent his officials Ben-hail, Obadiah, Zechariah, Nethanel, and Micaiah to teach in the cities of Judah,'),
('2CH', 17, 8, '2CH.17.8', 'accompanied by certain Levites—Shemaiah, Nethaniah, Zebadiah, Asahel, Shemiramoth, Jehonathan, Adonijah, Tobijah, and Tob-adonijah—along with the priests Elishama and Jehoram.'),
('2CH', 17, 9, '2CH.17.9', 'They taught throughout Judah, taking with them the Book of the Law of the LORD. They went throughout the towns of Judah and taught the people.'),
('2CH', 17, 10, '2CH.17.10', 'And the dread of the LORD fell upon all the kingdoms of the lands that surrounded Judah, so that they did not make war against Jehoshaphat.'),
('2CH', 17, 11, '2CH.17.11', 'Some Philistines also brought gifts and silver as tribute to Jehoshaphat, and the Arabs brought him 7,700 rams and 7,700 goats from their flocks.'),
('2CH', 17, 12, '2CH.17.12', 'Jehoshaphat grew stronger and stronger, and he built fortresses and store cities in Judah'),
('2CH', 17, 13, '2CH.17.13', 'and kept vast supplies in the cities of Judah. He also had warriors in Jerusalem who were mighty men of valor.'),
('2CH', 17, 14, '2CH.17.14', 'These are their numbers according to the houses of their fathers: From Judah, the commanders of thousands: Adnah the commander, and with him 300,000 mighty men of valor;'),
('2CH', 17, 15, '2CH.17.15', 'next to him, Jehohanan the commander, and with him 280,000;'),
('2CH', 17, 16, '2CH.17.16', 'and next to him, Amasiah son of Zichri, the volunteer for the LORD, and with him 200,000 mighty men of valor.'),
('2CH', 17, 17, '2CH.17.17', 'From Benjamin: Eliada, a mighty man of valor, and with him 200,000 armed with bows and shields;'),
('2CH', 17, 18, '2CH.17.18', 'and next to him, Jehozabad, and with him 180,000 armed for battle.'),
('2CH', 17, 19, '2CH.17.19', 'These were the men who served the king, besides those he stationed in the fortified cities throughout Judah.'),
('2CH', 18, 1, '2CH.18.1', 'Now Jehoshaphat had an abundance of riches and honor, and he allied himself with Ahab by marriage.'),
('2CH', 18, 2, '2CH.18.2', 'And some years later he went down to visit Ahab in Samaria, where Ahab sacrificed many sheep and cattle for him and the people with him and urged him to march up to Ramoth-gilead.'),
('2CH', 18, 3, '2CH.18.3', 'Ahab king of Israel asked Jehoshaphat king of Judah, “Will you go with me against Ramoth-gilead?” And Jehoshaphat replied, “I am as you are, and my people are your people; we will join you in the war.”'),
('2CH', 18, 4, '2CH.18.4', 'But Jehoshaphat also said to the king of Israel, “Please inquire first for the word of the LORD.”'),
('2CH', 18, 5, '2CH.18.5', 'So the king of Israel assembled the prophets, four hundred men, and asked them, “Should we go to war against Ramoth-gilead, or should we refrain?” “Go up,” they replied, “and God will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
('2CH', 18, 6, '2CH.18.6', 'But Jehoshaphat asked, “Is there not still a prophet of the LORD here of whom we can inquire?”'),
('2CH', 18, 7, '2CH.18.7', 'The king of Israel answered, “There is still one man through whom we can inquire of the LORD, but I hate him because he never prophesies anything good for me, but only bad. He is Micaiah son of Imlah.” “The king should not say that!” Jehoshaphat replied.'),
('2CH', 18, 8, '2CH.18.8', 'So the king of Israel called one of his officials and said, “Bring Micaiah son of Imlah at once.”'),
('2CH', 18, 9, '2CH.18.9', 'Dressed in royal attire, the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat king of Judah were sitting on their thrones at the threshing floor by the entrance of the gate of Samaria, with all the prophets prophesying before them.'),
('2CH', 18, 10, '2CH.18.10', 'Now Zedekiah son of Chenaanah had made for himself iron horns and declared, “This is what the LORD says: ‘With these you shall gore the Arameans until they are finished off.’”'),
('2CH', 18, 11, '2CH.18.11', 'And all the prophets were prophesying the same, saying, “Go up to Ramoth-gilead and triumph, for the LORD will deliver it into the hand of the king.”'),
('2CH', 18, 12, '2CH.18.12', 'Then the messenger who had gone to call Micaiah instructed him, “Behold, with one accord the words of the prophets are favorable to the king. So please let your words be like theirs, and speak favorably.”'),
('2CH', 18, 13, '2CH.18.13', 'But Micaiah said, “As surely as the LORD lives, I will speak whatever my God tells me.”'),
('2CH', 18, 14, '2CH.18.14', 'When Micaiah arrived, the king asked him, “Micaiah, should we go to war against Ramoth-gilead, or should we refrain?” “Go up and triumph,” Micaiah replied, “for they will be delivered into your hand.”'),
('2CH', 18, 15, '2CH.18.15', 'But the king said to him, “How many times must I make you swear not to tell me anything but the truth in the name of the LORD?”'),
('2CH', 18, 16, '2CH.18.16', 'So Micaiah declared: “I saw all Israel scattered on the hills like sheep without a shepherd. And the LORD said, ‘These people have no master; let each one return home in peace.’”'),
('2CH', 18, 17, '2CH.18.17', 'Then the king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “Did I not tell you that he never prophesies good for me, but only bad?”'),
('2CH', 18, 18, '2CH.18.18', 'Micaiah continued, “Therefore hear the word of the LORD: I saw the LORD sitting on His throne, and all the host of heaven standing on His right and on His left.'),
('2CH', 18, 19, '2CH.18.19', 'And the LORD said, ‘Who will entice Ahab king of Israel to march up and fall at Ramoth-gilead?’ And one suggested this, and another that.'),
('2CH', 18, 20, '2CH.18.20', 'Then a spirit came forward, stood before the LORD, and said, ‘I will entice him.’ ‘By what means?’ asked the LORD.'),
('2CH', 18, 21, '2CH.18.21', 'And he replied, ‘I will go out and be a lying spirit in the mouths of all his prophets.’ ‘You will surely entice him and prevail,’ said the LORD. ‘Go and do it.’'),
('2CH', 18, 22, '2CH.18.22', 'So you see, the LORD has put a lying spirit in the mouths of these prophets of yours, and the LORD has pronounced disaster against you.”'),
('2CH', 18, 23, '2CH.18.23', 'Then Zedekiah son of Chenaanah went up, struck Micaiah in the face, and demanded, “Which way did the Spirit of the LORD go when He departed from me to speak with you?”'),
('2CH', 18, 24, '2CH.18.24', 'Micaiah replied, “You will soon see, on that day when you go and hide in an inner room.”'),
('2CH', 18, 25, '2CH.18.25', 'And the king of Israel declared, “Take Micaiah and return him to Amon the governor of the city and to Joash the king’s son,'),
('2CH', 18, 26, '2CH.18.26', 'and tell them that this is what the king says: ‘Put this man in prison and feed him only bread and water until I return safely.’”'),
('2CH', 18, 27, '2CH.18.27', 'But Micaiah replied, “If you ever return safely, the LORD has not spoken through me.” Then he added, “Take heed, all you people!”'),
('2CH', 18, 28, '2CH.18.28', 'So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat king of Judah went up to Ramoth-gilead.'),
('2CH', 18, 29, '2CH.18.29', 'And the king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, “I will disguise myself and go into battle, but you wear your royal robes.” So the king of Israel disguised himself and went into battle.'),
('2CH', 18, 30, '2CH.18.30', 'Now the king of Aram had ordered his chariot commanders, “Do not fight with anyone, small or great, except the king of Israel.”'),
('2CH', 18, 31, '2CH.18.31', 'When the chariot commanders saw Jehoshaphat, they said, “This is the king of Israel!” So they turned to fight against him, but Jehoshaphat cried out, and the LORD helped him. God drew them away from him.'),
('2CH', 18, 32, '2CH.18.32', 'And when the chariot commanders saw that he was not the king of Israel, they turned back from pursuing him.'),
('2CH', 18, 33, '2CH.18.33', 'However, a certain man drew his bow without taking special aim, and he struck the king of Israel between the joints of his armor. So the king said to his charioteer, “Turn around and take me out of the battle, for I am badly wounded!”'),
('2CH', 18, 34, '2CH.18.34', 'The battle raged throughout that day, and the king of Israel propped himself up in his chariot facing the Arameans until evening. And at sunset he died.'),
('2CH', 19, 1, '2CH.19.1', 'When Jehoshaphat king of Judah had returned safely to his home in Jerusalem,'),
('2CH', 19, 2, '2CH.19.2', 'Jehu son of Hanani the seer went out to confront him and said to King Jehoshaphat, “Should you help the wicked and love those who hate the LORD? Because of this, the wrath of the LORD is upon you.'),
('2CH', 19, 3, '2CH.19.3', 'However, some good is found in you, for you have removed the Asherah poles from the land and have set your heart on seeking God.”'),
('2CH', 19, 4, '2CH.19.4', 'Jehoshaphat lived in Jerusalem, and once again he went out among the people from Beersheba to the hill country of Ephraim and turned them back to the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 19, 5, '2CH.19.5', 'He appointed judges in the land, in each of the fortified cities of Judah.'),
('2CH', 19, 6, '2CH.19.6', 'Then he said to the judges, “Consider carefully what you do, for you are not judging for man, but for the LORD, who is with you when you render judgment.'),
('2CH', 19, 7, '2CH.19.7', 'And now, may the fear of the LORD be upon you. Be careful what you do, for with the LORD our God there is no injustice or partiality or bribery.”'),
('2CH', 19, 8, '2CH.19.8', 'Moreover, Jehoshaphat appointed in Jerusalem some of the Levites, priests, and heads of the Israelite families to judge on behalf of the LORD and to settle disputes. And they lived in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 19, 9, '2CH.19.9', 'He commanded them, saying, “You must serve faithfully and wholeheartedly in the fear of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 19, 10, '2CH.19.10', 'For every dispute that comes before you from your brothers who dwell in their cities—whether it regards bloodshed or some other violation of law, commandments, statutes, or ordinances—you are to warn them, so that they will not incur guilt before the LORD and wrath will not come upon you and your brothers. Do this, and you will not incur guilt.'),
('2CH', 19, 11, '2CH.19.11', 'Note that Amariah, the chief priest, will be over you in all that pertains to the LORD, and Zebadiah son of Ishmael, the ruler of the house of Judah, in all that pertains to the king. And the Levites will serve as officers before you. Act resolutely; may the LORD be with the upright!”'),
('2CH', 20, 1, '2CH.20.1', 'After this, the Moabites and Ammonites, together with some of the Meunites, came to make war against Jehoshaphat.'),
('2CH', 20, 2, '2CH.20.2', 'Then some men came and told Jehoshaphat, “A vast army is coming against you from Edom, from beyond the Sea; they are already in Hazazon-tamar” (that is, En-gedi).'),
('2CH', 20, 3, '2CH.20.3', 'Jehoshaphat was alarmed and set his face to seek the LORD. And he proclaimed a fast throughout Judah.'),
('2CH', 20, 4, '2CH.20.4', 'So the people of Judah gathered to seek the LORD, and indeed, they came from all the cities of Judah to seek Him.'),
('2CH', 20, 5, '2CH.20.5', 'Then Jehoshaphat stood in the assembly of Judah and Jerusalem in the house of the LORD in front of the new courtyard'),
('2CH', 20, 6, '2CH.20.6', 'and said, “O LORD, God of our fathers, are You not the God who is in heaven, and do You not rule over all the kingdoms of the nations? Power and might are in Your hand, and no one can stand against You.'),
('2CH', 20, 7, '2CH.20.7', 'Our God, did You not drive out the inhabitants of this land before Your people Israel and give it forever to the descendants of Abraham Your friend?'),
('2CH', 20, 8, '2CH.20.8', 'They have lived in the land and have built in it a sanctuary for Your Name, saying,'),
('2CH', 20, 9, '2CH.20.9', '‘If disaster comes upon us—whether sword or judgment, plague or famine—we will stand before this temple and before You, for Your Name is in this temple. We will cry out to You in our distress, and You will hear us and save us.’'),
('2CH', 20, 10, '2CH.20.10', 'And now, here are the men of Ammon, Moab, and Mount Seir, whom You did not let Israel invade when they came out of the land of Egypt. So Israel turned away from them and did not destroy them.'),
('2CH', 20, 11, '2CH.20.11', 'See how they are repaying us by coming to drive us out of the possession that You gave us as an inheritance.'),
('2CH', 20, 12, '2CH.20.12', 'Our God, will You not judge them? For we are powerless before this vast army that comes against us. We do not know what to do, but our eyes are upon You.”'),
('2CH', 20, 13, '2CH.20.13', 'Meanwhile all the men of Judah, with their wives and children and little ones, were standing before the LORD.'),
('2CH', 20, 14, '2CH.20.14', 'Then the Spirit of the LORD came upon Jahaziel son of Zechariah, the son of Benaiah, the son of Jeiel, the son of Mattaniah, a Levite from Asaph’s descendants, as he stood in the midst of the assembly.'),
('2CH', 20, 15, '2CH.20.15', 'And he said, “Listen, all you people of Judah and Jerusalem! Listen, King Jehoshaphat! This is what the LORD says: ‘Do not be afraid or discouraged because of this vast army, for the battle does not belong to you, but to God.'),
('2CH', 20, 16, '2CH.20.16', 'Tomorrow you are to march down against them. You will see them coming up the Ascent of Ziz, and you will find them at the end of the valley facing the Wilderness of Jeruel.'),
('2CH', 20, 17, '2CH.20.17', 'You need not fight this battle. Take up your positions, stand firm, and see the salvation of the LORD on your behalf, O Judah and Jerusalem. Do not be afraid or discouraged. Go out and face them tomorrow, for the LORD is with you.’”'),
('2CH', 20, 18, '2CH.20.18', 'Then Jehoshaphat bowed facedown, and all the people of Judah and Jerusalem fell down before the LORD to worship Him.'),
('2CH', 20, 19, '2CH.20.19', 'And the Levites from the Kohathites and Korahites stood up to praise the LORD, the God of Israel, shouting in a very loud voice.'),
('2CH', 20, 20, '2CH.20.20', 'Early in the morning they got up and left for the Wilderness of Tekoa. As they set out, Jehoshaphat stood up and said, “Hear me, O people of Judah and Jerusalem. Believe in the LORD your God, and you will be upheld; believe in His prophets, and you will succeed.”'),
('2CH', 20, 21, '2CH.20.21', 'Then Jehoshaphat consulted with the people and appointed those who would sing to the LORD and praise the splendor of His holiness. As they went out before the army, they were singing: “Give thanks to the LORD, for His loving devotion endures forever.”'),
('2CH', 20, 22, '2CH.20.22', 'The moment they began their shouts and praises, the LORD set ambushes against the men of Ammon, Moab, and Mount Seir who had come against Judah, and they were defeated.'),
('2CH', 20, 23, '2CH.20.23', 'The Ammonites and Moabites rose up against the inhabitants of Mount Seir, devoting them to destruction. And when they had finished off the inhabitants of Seir, they helped to destroy one another.'),
('2CH', 20, 24, '2CH.20.24', 'When the men of Judah came to a place overlooking the wilderness, they looked for the vast army, but there were only corpses lying on the ground; no one had escaped.'),
('2CH', 20, 25, '2CH.20.25', 'Then Jehoshaphat and his people went to carry off the plunder, and they found on the bodies an abundance of goods and valuables—more than they could carry away. They were gathering the plunder for three days because there was so much.'),
('2CH', 20, 26, '2CH.20.26', 'On the fourth day they assembled in the Valley of Beracah, where they blessed the LORD. Therefore that place is called the Valley of Beracah to this day.'),
('2CH', 20, 27, '2CH.20.27', 'Then all the men of Judah and Jerusalem, with Jehoshaphat at their head, returned joyfully to Jerusalem, for the LORD had made them rejoice over their enemies.'),
('2CH', 20, 28, '2CH.20.28', 'So they entered Jerusalem and went into the house of the LORD with harps, lyres, and trumpets.'),
('2CH', 20, 29, '2CH.20.29', 'And the fear of God came upon all the kingdoms of the lands when they heard that the LORD had fought against the enemies of Israel.'),
('2CH', 20, 30, '2CH.20.30', 'Then Jehoshaphat’s kingdom was at peace, for his God had given him rest on every side.'),
('2CH', 20, 31, '2CH.20.31', 'So Jehoshaphat reigned over Judah. He was thirty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem twenty-five years. His mother’s name was Azubah daughter of Shilhi.'),
('2CH', 20, 32, '2CH.20.32', 'And Jehoshaphat walked in the way of his father Asa and did not turn away from it; he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 20, 33, '2CH.20.33', 'The high places, however, were not removed; the people had not yet set their hearts on the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 20, 34, '2CH.20.34', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, from beginning to end, they are indeed written in the Chronicles of Jehu son of Hanani, which are recorded in the Book of the Kings of Israel.'),
('2CH', 20, 35, '2CH.20.35', 'Later, Jehoshaphat king of Judah made an alliance with Ahaziah king of Israel, who acted wickedly.'),
('2CH', 20, 36, '2CH.20.36', 'They agreed to make ships to go to Tarshish, and these were built in Ezion-geber.'),
('2CH', 20, 37, '2CH.20.37', 'Then Eliezer son of Dodavahu of Mareshah prophesied against Jehoshaphat, saying, “Because you have allied yourself with Ahaziah, the LORD has destroyed your works.” So the ships were wrecked and were unable to sail to Tarshish.'),
('2CH', 21, 1, '2CH.21.1', 'And Jehoshaphat rested with his fathers and was buried with them in the City of David. And his son Jehoram reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 21, 2, '2CH.21.2', 'Jehoram’s brothers, the sons of Jehoshaphat, were Azariah, Jehiel, Zechariah, Azariah, Michael, and Shephatiah; these were all sons of Jehoshaphat king of Israel.'),
('2CH', 21, 3, '2CH.21.3', 'Their father had given them many gifts of silver and gold and precious things, as well as the fortified cities in Judah; but he gave the kingdom to Jehoram because he was the firstborn.'),
('2CH', 21, 4, '2CH.21.4', 'When Jehoram had established himself over his father’s kingdom, he strengthened himself by putting to the sword all his brothers along with some of the princes of Israel.'),
('2CH', 21, 5, '2CH.21.5', 'Jehoram was thirty-two years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eight years.'),
('2CH', 21, 6, '2CH.21.6', 'And Jehoram walked in the ways of the kings of Israel, just as the house of Ahab had done. For he married a daughter of Ahab and did evil in the sight of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 21, 7, '2CH.21.7', 'Yet the LORD was unwilling to destroy the house of David, because of the covenant He had made with David, and since He had promised to maintain a lamp for David and his descendants forever.'),
('2CH', 21, 8, '2CH.21.8', 'In the days of Jehoram, Edom rebelled against the hand of Judah and appointed their own king.'),
('2CH', 21, 9, '2CH.21.9', 'So Jehoram crossed into Edom with his officers and all his chariots. When the Edomites surrounded him and his chariot commanders, he rose up and attacked by night.'),
('2CH', 21, 10, '2CH.21.10', 'So to this day Edom has been in rebellion against the hand of Judah. Likewise, Libnah rebelled against his hand at the same time, because Jehoram had forsaken the LORD, the God of his fathers.'),
('2CH', 21, 11, '2CH.21.11', 'Jehoram had also built high places on the hills of Judah; he had caused the people of Jerusalem to prostitute themselves and had led Judah astray.'),
('2CH', 21, 12, '2CH.21.12', 'Then a letter came to Jehoram from Elijah the prophet, which stated: “This is what the LORD, the God of your father David, says: ‘You have not walked in the ways of your father Jehoshaphat or of Asa king of Judah,'),
('2CH', 21, 13, '2CH.21.13', 'but you have walked in the ways of the kings of Israel and have caused Judah and the people of Jerusalem to prostitute themselves, just as the house of Ahab prostituted itself. You have also killed your brothers, your father’s family, who were better than you.'),
('2CH', 21, 14, '2CH.21.14', 'So behold, the LORD is about to strike your people, your sons, your wives, and all your possessions with a serious blow.'),
('2CH', 21, 15, '2CH.21.15', 'And day after day you yourself will suffer from a severe illness, a disease of your bowels, until it causes your bowels to come out.’”'),
('2CH', 21, 16, '2CH.21.16', 'Then the LORD stirred against Jehoram the spirit of the Philistines and Arabs who lived near the Cushites.'),
('2CH', 21, 17, '2CH.21.17', 'So they went to war against Judah, invaded it, and carried off all the possessions found in the king’s palace, along with his sons and wives; not a son was left to him except Jehoahaz, his youngest.'),
('2CH', 21, 18, '2CH.21.18', 'After all this, the LORD afflicted Jehoram with an incurable disease of the bowels.'),
('2CH', 21, 19, '2CH.21.19', 'This continued day after day until two full years had passed. Finally, his intestines came out because of his disease, and he died in severe pain. And his people did not make a fire in his honor as they had done for his fathers.'),
('2CH', 21, 20, '2CH.21.20', 'Jehoram was thirty-two years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eight years. He died, to no one’s regret, and was buried in the City of David, but not in the tombs of the kings.'),
('2CH', 22, 1, '2CH.22.1', 'Then the people of Jerusalem made Ahaziah, the youngest son of Jehoram, king in his place, since the raiders who had come into the camp with the Arabs had killed all the older sons. So Ahaziah son of Jehoram became king of Judah.'),
('2CH', 22, 2, '2CH.22.2', 'Ahaziah was twenty-two years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem one year. His mother’s name was Athaliah, the granddaughter of Omri.'),
('2CH', 22, 3, '2CH.22.3', 'Ahaziah also walked in the ways of the house of Ahab, for his mother was his counselor in wickedness.'),
('2CH', 22, 4, '2CH.22.4', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, as the house of Ahab had done, for to his destruction they were his counselors after the death of his father.'),
('2CH', 22, 5, '2CH.22.5', 'Ahaziah also followed their counsel and went with Joram son of Ahab king of Israel to fight against Hazael king of Aram at Ramoth-gilead. But the Arameans wounded Joram.'),
('2CH', 22, 6, '2CH.22.6', 'So he returned to Jezreel to recover from the wounds they had inflicted on him at Ramah when he fought against Hazael king of Aram. Then Ahaziah son of Jehoram king of Judah went down to Jezreel to visit Joram son of Ahab, because Joram had been wounded.'),
('2CH', 22, 7, '2CH.22.7', 'Ahaziah’s downfall came from God when he went to visit Joram. When Ahaziah arrived, he went out with Joram to meet Jehu son of Nimshi, whom the LORD had anointed to destroy the house of Ahab.'),
('2CH', 22, 8, '2CH.22.8', 'So while Jehu was executing judgment on the house of Ahab, he found the rulers of Judah and the sons of Ahaziah’s brothers who were serving Ahaziah, and he killed them.'),
('2CH', 22, 9, '2CH.22.9', 'Then Jehu looked for Ahaziah, and Jehu’s soldiers captured him while he was hiding in Samaria. So Ahaziah was brought to Jehu and put to death. They buried him, for they said, “He is the grandson of Jehoshaphat, who sought the LORD with all his heart.” So no one was left from the house of Ahaziah with the strength to rule the kingdom.'),
('2CH', 22, 10, '2CH.22.10', 'When Athaliah the mother of Ahaziah saw that her son was dead, she proceeded to annihilate all the royal heirs of the house of Judah.'),
('2CH', 22, 11, '2CH.22.11', 'But Jehoshabeath daughter of King Jehoram took Joash son of Ahaziah and stole him away from among the sons of the king who were being murdered, and she put him and his nurse in a bedroom. Because Jehoshabeath, the daughter of King Jehoram and the wife of Jehoiada the priest, was Ahaziah’s sister, she hid Joash from Athaliah so that she could not kill him.'),
('2CH', 22, 12, '2CH.22.12', 'And Joash remained hidden with them in the house of God for six years while Athaliah ruled the land.'),
('2CH', 23, 1, '2CH.23.1', 'Then in the seventh year, Jehoiada strengthened himself and made a covenant with the commanders of hundreds—with Azariah son of Jeroham, Ishmael son of Jehohanan, Azariah son of Obed, Maaseiah son of Adaiah, and Elishaphat son of Zichri.'),
('2CH', 23, 2, '2CH.23.2', 'So they went throughout Judah and gathered the Levites from all the cities of Judah and the heads of the families of Israel. And when they came to Jerusalem,'),
('2CH', 23, 3, '2CH.23.3', 'the whole assembly made a covenant with the king in the house of God. “Behold, the king’s son!” said Jehoiada. “He must reign, just as the LORD promised concerning the descendants of David.'),
('2CH', 23, 4, '2CH.23.4', 'This is what you are to do: A third of you priests and Levites who come on duty on the Sabbath shall keep watch at the doors,'),
('2CH', 23, 5, '2CH.23.5', 'a third shall be at the royal palace, and a third at the Foundation Gate, while all the others are to be in the courtyards of the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 23, 6, '2CH.23.6', 'No one is to enter the house of the LORD except the priests and those Levites who serve; they may enter because they are consecrated, but all the people are to obey the requirement of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 23, 7, '2CH.23.7', 'The Levites must surround the king with weapons in hand, and anyone who enters the temple must be put to death. You must stay close to the king wherever he goes.”'),
('2CH', 23, 8, '2CH.23.8', 'So the Levites and all Judah did everything that Jehoiada the priest had ordered. Each of them took his men—those coming on duty on the Sabbath and those going off duty—for Jehoiada the priest had not released any of the divisions.'),
('2CH', 23, 9, '2CH.23.9', 'Then Jehoiada the priest gave to the commanders of hundreds the spears and the large and small shields of King David that were in the house of God.'),
('2CH', 23, 10, '2CH.23.10', 'He stationed all the troops, with their weapons in hand, surrounding the king by the altar and the temple, from the south side to the north side of the temple.'),
('2CH', 23, 11, '2CH.23.11', 'Then Jehoiada and his sons brought out the king’s son, put the crown on him, presented him with the Testimony, and proclaimed him king. They anointed him and shouted, “Long live the king!”'),
('2CH', 23, 12, '2CH.23.12', 'When Athaliah heard the noise of the people running and cheering the king, she went out to them in the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 23, 13, '2CH.23.13', 'And she looked and saw the king standing by his pillar at the entrance. The officers and trumpeters were beside the king, and all the people of the land were rejoicing and blowing trumpets, while the singers with musical instruments were leading the praises. Then Athaliah tore her clothes and screamed, “Treason, treason!”'),
('2CH', 23, 14, '2CH.23.14', 'And Jehoiada the priest sent out the commanders of hundreds in charge of the army, saying, “Bring her out between the ranks, and put to the sword anyone who follows her.” For the priest had said, “She must not be put to death in the house of the LORD.”'),
('2CH', 23, 15, '2CH.23.15', 'So they seized Athaliah as she reached the entrance of the Horse Gate on the palace grounds, and there they put her to death.'),
('2CH', 23, 16, '2CH.23.16', 'Then Jehoiada made a covenant between himself and the king and the people that they would be the LORD’s people.'),
('2CH', 23, 17, '2CH.23.17', 'So all the people went to the temple of Baal and tore it down. They smashed the altars and idols to pieces and killed Mattan the priest of Baal in front of the altars.'),
('2CH', 23, 18, '2CH.23.18', 'Moreover, Jehoiada put the oversight of the house of the LORD into the hands of the Levitical priests, whom David had appointed over the house of the LORD, to offer burnt offerings to the LORD as written in the Law of Moses, with rejoicing and song, as ordained by David.'),
('2CH', 23, 19, '2CH.23.19', 'He stationed gatekeepers at the gates of the house of the LORD, so that no one who was in any way unclean could enter.'),
('2CH', 23, 20, '2CH.23.20', 'And he took with him the commanders of hundreds, the nobles, the rulers of the people, and all the people of the land, and they brought the king down from the house of the LORD and entered the royal palace through the Upper Gate. They seated King Joash on the royal throne,'),
('2CH', 23, 21, '2CH.23.21', 'and all the people of the land rejoiced. And the city was quiet, because Athaliah had been put to the sword.'),
('2CH', 24, 1, '2CH.24.1', 'Joash was seven years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem forty years. His mother’s name was Zibiah; she was from Beersheba.'),
('2CH', 24, 2, '2CH.24.2', 'And Joash did what was right in the eyes of the LORD all the days of Jehoiada the priest.'),
('2CH', 24, 3, '2CH.24.3', 'Jehoiada took for him two wives, and he had sons and daughters.'),
('2CH', 24, 4, '2CH.24.4', 'Some time later, Joash set his heart on repairing the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 24, 5, '2CH.24.5', 'So he gathered the priests and Levites and said, “Go out to the cities of Judah and collect the money due annually from all Israel, to repair the house of your God. Do it quickly.” The Levites, however, did not make haste.'),
('2CH', 24, 6, '2CH.24.6', 'So the king called Jehoiada the high priest and said, “Why have you not required the Levites to bring from Judah and Jerusalem the tax imposed by Moses the servant of the LORD and by the assembly of Israel for the Tent of the Testimony?”'),
('2CH', 24, 7, '2CH.24.7', 'For the sons of that wicked woman Athaliah had broken into the house of God and had even used the sacred objects of the house of the LORD for the Baals.'),
('2CH', 24, 8, '2CH.24.8', 'At the king’s command a chest was made and placed outside, at the gate of the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 24, 9, '2CH.24.9', 'And a proclamation was issued in Judah and Jerusalem that they were to bring to the LORD the tax imposed by Moses the servant of God on Israel in the wilderness.'),
('2CH', 24, 10, '2CH.24.10', 'All the officers and all the people rejoiced and brought their contributions, and they dropped them in the chest until it was full.'),
('2CH', 24, 11, '2CH.24.11', 'Whenever the chest was brought by the Levites to the king’s overseers and they saw that there was a large amount of money, the royal scribe and the officer of the high priest would come and empty the chest and carry it back to its place. They did this daily and gathered the money in abundance.'),
('2CH', 24, 12, '2CH.24.12', 'Then the king and Jehoiada would give the money to those who supervised the labor on the house of the LORD to hire stonecutters and carpenters to restore the house of the LORD, as well as workers in iron and bronze to repair the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 24, 13, '2CH.24.13', 'So the workmen labored, and in their hands the repair work progressed. They restored the house of God according to its specifications, and they reinforced it.'),
('2CH', 24, 14, '2CH.24.14', 'When they were finished, they brought the rest of the money to the king and Jehoiada, and with it were made articles for the house of the LORD—utensils for the service and for the burnt offerings, dishes, and other objects of gold and silver. Throughout the days of Jehoiada, burnt offerings were presented regularly in the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 24, 15, '2CH.24.15', 'When Jehoiada was old and full of years, he died at the age of 130.'),
('2CH', 24, 16, '2CH.24.16', 'And Jehoiada was buried with the kings in the City of David, because he had done what was good in Israel for God and His temple.'),
('2CH', 24, 17, '2CH.24.17', 'After the death of Jehoiada, however, the officials of Judah came and paid homage to the king, and he listened to them.'),
('2CH', 24, 18, '2CH.24.18', 'They abandoned the house of the LORD, the God of their fathers, and served the Asherah poles and idols. So wrath came upon Judah and Jerusalem for this guilt of theirs.'),
('2CH', 24, 19, '2CH.24.19', 'Nevertheless, the LORD sent prophets to bring the people back to Him and to testify against them, but they would not listen.'),
('2CH', 24, 20, '2CH.24.20', 'Then the Spirit of God came upon Zechariah son of Jehoiada the priest, who stood up before the people and said to them, “This is what God says: ‘Why do you transgress the commandments of the LORD so that you cannot prosper? Because you have forsaken the LORD, He has forsaken you.’”'),
('2CH', 24, 21, '2CH.24.21', 'But they conspired against Zechariah, and by order of the king, they stoned him in the courtyard of the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 24, 22, '2CH.24.22', 'Thus King Joash failed to remember the kindness that Zechariah’s father Jehoiada had extended to him. Instead, Joash killed Jehoiada’s son. As he lay dying, Zechariah said, “May the LORD see this and call you to account.”'),
('2CH', 24, 23, '2CH.24.23', 'In the spring, the army of Aram went to war against Joash. They entered Judah and Jerusalem and destroyed all the leaders of the people, and they sent all the plunder to their king in Damascus.'),
('2CH', 24, 24, '2CH.24.24', 'Although the Aramean army had come with only a few men, the LORD delivered into their hand a very great army. Because Judah had forsaken the LORD, the God of their fathers, judgment was executed on Joash.'),
('2CH', 24, 25, '2CH.24.25', 'And when the Arameans had withdrawn, they left Joash severely wounded. His own servants conspired against him for shedding the blood of the son of Jehoiada the priest, and they killed him on his bed. So he died and was buried in the City of David, but not in the tombs of the kings.'),
('2CH', 24, 26, '2CH.24.26', 'Those who conspired against Joash were Zabad son of Shimeath the Ammonitess and Jehozabad son of Shimrith the Moabitess.'),
('2CH', 24, 27, '2CH.24.27', 'The accounts of the sons of Joash and the many pronouncements about him, and of the restoration of the house of God, are indeed written in the Treatise of the Book of the Kings. And his son Amaziah reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 25, 1, '2CH.25.1', 'Amaziah was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem twenty-nine years. His mother’s name was Jehoaddan; she was from Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 25, 2, '2CH.25.2', 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, but not wholeheartedly.'),
('2CH', 25, 3, '2CH.25.3', 'As soon as the kingdom was firmly in his grasp, Amaziah executed the servants who had murdered his father the king.'),
('2CH', 25, 4, '2CH.25.4', 'Yet he did not put their sons to death, but acted according to what is written in the Law, in the Book of Moses, where the LORD commanded: “Fathers must not be put to death for their children, and children must not be put to death for their fathers; each is to die for his own sin.”'),
('2CH', 25, 5, '2CH.25.5', 'Then Amaziah gathered the people of Judah and assigned them according to their families to commanders of thousands and of hundreds. And he numbered those twenty years of age or older throughout Judah and Benjamin and found 300,000 chosen men able to serve in the army, bearing the spear and shield.'),
('2CH', 25, 6, '2CH.25.6', 'He also hired 100,000 mighty men of valor from Israel for a hundred talents of silver.'),
('2CH', 25, 7, '2CH.25.7', 'But a man of God came to him and said, “O king, do not let the army of Israel go with you, for the LORD is not with Israel—not with any of the Ephraimites.'),
('2CH', 25, 8, '2CH.25.8', 'Even if you go and fight bravely in battle, God will overthrow you before the enemy, for God has power to help and power to overthrow.”'),
('2CH', 25, 9, '2CH.25.9', 'Amaziah asked the man of God, “What should I do about the hundred talents I have given to the troops of Israel?” And the man of God replied, “The LORD is able to give you much more than this.”'),
('2CH', 25, 10, '2CH.25.10', 'So Amaziah dismissed the troops who had come to him from Ephraim and sent them home. And they were furious with Judah and returned home in great anger.'),
('2CH', 25, 11, '2CH.25.11', 'Amaziah, however, summoned his strength and led his troops to the Valley of Salt, where he struck down 10,000 men of Seir,'),
('2CH', 25, 12, '2CH.25.12', 'and the army of Judah also captured 10,000 men alive. They took them to the top of a cliff and threw them down so that all were dashed to pieces.'),
('2CH', 25, 13, '2CH.25.13', 'Meanwhile the troops that Amaziah had dismissed from battle raided the cities of Judah, from Samaria to Beth-horon. They struck down 3,000 people and carried off a great deal of plunder.'),
('2CH', 25, 14, '2CH.25.14', 'When Amaziah returned from the slaughter of the Edomites, he brought back the gods of the Seirites, set them up as his own gods, bowed before them, and burned sacrifices to them.'),
('2CH', 25, 15, '2CH.25.15', 'Therefore the anger of the LORD burned against Amaziah, and He sent him a prophet, who said, “Why have you sought this people’s gods, which could not deliver them from your hand?”'),
('2CH', 25, 16, '2CH.25.16', 'While he was still speaking, the king asked, “Have we made you the counselor to the king? Stop! Why be struck down?” So the prophet stopped, but he said, “I know that God has determined to destroy you, because you have done this and have not heeded my advice.”'),
('2CH', 25, 17, '2CH.25.17', 'Then Amaziah king of Judah took counsel and sent word to the king of Israel Jehoash son of Jehoahaz, the son of Jehu. “Come, let us meet face to face,” he said.'),
('2CH', 25, 18, '2CH.25.18', 'But Jehoash king of Israel replied to Amaziah king of Judah: “A thistle in Lebanon sent a message to a cedar in Lebanon, saying, ‘Give your daughter to my son in marriage.’ Then a wild beast in Lebanon came along and trampled the thistle.'),
('2CH', 25, 19, '2CH.25.19', 'You have said, ‘Look, I have defeated Edom,’ and your heart has become proud and boastful. Now stay at home. Why should you stir up trouble so that you fall—you and Judah with you?”'),
('2CH', 25, 20, '2CH.25.20', 'But Amaziah would not listen, for this had come from God in order to deliver them into the hand of Jehoash, because they had sought the gods of Edom.'),
('2CH', 25, 21, '2CH.25.21', 'So Jehoash king of Israel advanced, and he and Amaziah king of Judah faced each other at Beth-shemesh in Judah.'),
('2CH', 25, 22, '2CH.25.22', 'And Judah was routed before Israel, and every man fled to his own home.'),
('2CH', 25, 23, '2CH.25.23', 'There at Beth-shemesh, Jehoash king of Israel captured Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Joash, the son of Jehoahaz. Then Jehoash brought him to Jerusalem and broke down the wall of Jerusalem from the Ephraim Gate to the Corner Gate—a section of four hundred cubits.'),
('2CH', 25, 24, '2CH.25.24', 'He took all the gold and silver and all the articles found in the house of God with Obed-edom and in the treasuries of the royal palace, as well as some hostages. Then he returned to Samaria.'),
('2CH', 25, 25, '2CH.25.25', 'Amaziah son of Joash king of Judah lived for fifteen years after the death of Jehoash son of Jehoahaz king of Israel.'),
('2CH', 25, 26, '2CH.25.26', 'As for the rest of the acts of Amaziah, from beginning to end, are they not written in the Book of the Kings of Judah and Israel?'),
('2CH', 25, 27, '2CH.25.27', 'From the time that Amaziah turned from following the LORD, a conspiracy was formed against him in Jerusalem, and he fled to Lachish. But men were sent after him to Lachish, and they killed him there.'),
('2CH', 25, 28, '2CH.25.28', 'They carried him back on horses and buried him with his fathers in the City of Judah.'),
('2CH', 26, 1, '2CH.26.1', 'All the people of Judah took Uzziah, who was sixteen years old, and made him king in place of his father Amaziah.'),
('2CH', 26, 2, '2CH.26.2', 'Uzziah was the one who rebuilt Eloth and restored it to Judah after King Amaziah rested with his fathers.'),
('2CH', 26, 3, '2CH.26.3', 'Uzziah was sixteen years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem fifty-two years. His mother’s name was Jecoliah; she was from Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 26, 4, '2CH.26.4', 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, just as his father Amaziah had done.'),
('2CH', 26, 5, '2CH.26.5', 'He sought God throughout the days of Zechariah, who instructed him in the fear of God. And as long as he sought the LORD, God gave him success.'),
('2CH', 26, 6, '2CH.26.6', 'Uzziah went out to wage war against the Philistines, and he tore down the walls of Gath, Jabneh, and Ashdod. Then he built cities near Ashdod and among the Philistines.'),
('2CH', 26, 7, '2CH.26.7', 'God helped him against the Philistines, against the Arabs living in Gur-baal, and against the Meunites.'),
('2CH', 26, 8, '2CH.26.8', 'The Ammonites brought tribute to Uzziah, and his fame spread as far as the border of Egypt, for he had become exceedingly powerful.'),
('2CH', 26, 9, '2CH.26.9', 'Uzziah built towers in Jerusalem at the Corner Gate, the Valley Gate, and the angle in the wall, and he fortified them.'),
('2CH', 26, 10, '2CH.26.10', 'Since he had much livestock in the foothills and in the plain, he built towers in the desert and dug many cisterns. And since he was a lover of the soil, he had farmers and vinedressers in the hill country and in the fertile fields.'),
('2CH', 26, 11, '2CH.26.11', 'Uzziah had an army ready for battle that went out to war by assigned divisions, as recorded by Jeiel the scribe and Maaseiah the officer under the direction of Hananiah, one of the royal officers.'),
('2CH', 26, 12, '2CH.26.12', 'The total number of family leaders of the mighty men of valor was 2,600.'),
('2CH', 26, 13, '2CH.26.13', 'Under their authority was an army of 307,500 trained for war, a powerful force to support the king against his enemies.'),
('2CH', 26, 14, '2CH.26.14', 'Uzziah supplied the entire army with shields, spears, helmets, armor, bows, and slingstones.'),
('2CH', 26, 15, '2CH.26.15', 'And in Jerusalem he made skillfully designed devices to shoot arrows and catapult large stones from the towers and corners. So his fame spread far and wide, for he was helped tremendously until he became powerful.'),
('2CH', 26, 16, '2CH.26.16', 'But when Uzziah became powerful, his arrogance led to his own destruction. He was unfaithful to the LORD his God, for he entered the temple of the LORD to burn incense on the altar of incense.'),
('2CH', 26, 17, '2CH.26.17', 'Then Azariah the priest, along with eighty brave priests of the LORD, went in after him.'),
('2CH', 26, 18, '2CH.26.18', 'They took their stand against King Uzziah and said, “Uzziah, you have no right to offer incense to the LORD. Only the priests, the descendants of Aaron, are consecrated to burn incense. Leave the sanctuary, for you have acted unfaithfully; you will not receive honor from the LORD God.”'),
('2CH', 26, 19, '2CH.26.19', 'Uzziah, with a censer in his hand to offer incense, was enraged. But while he raged against the priests in their presence in the house of the LORD before the altar of incense, leprosy broke out on his forehead.'),
('2CH', 26, 20, '2CH.26.20', 'When Azariah the chief priest and all the priests turned to him and saw his leprous forehead, they rushed him out. Indeed, he himself hurried to get out, because the LORD had afflicted him.'),
('2CH', 26, 21, '2CH.26.21', 'So King Uzziah was a leper until the day of his death. He lived in isolation, leprous and cut off from the house of the LORD, while his son Jotham had charge of the royal palace and governed the people of the land.'),
('2CH', 26, 22, '2CH.26.22', 'As for the rest of the acts of Uzziah, from beginning to end, they are recorded by the prophet Isaiah son of Amoz.'),
('2CH', 26, 23, '2CH.26.23', 'And Uzziah rested with his fathers and was buried near them in a field of burial that belonged to the kings, for the people said, “He was a leper.” And his son Jotham reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 27, 1, '2CH.27.1', 'Jotham was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem sixteen years. His mother’s name was Jerushah daughter of Zadok.'),
('2CH', 27, 2, '2CH.27.2', 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, just as his father Uzziah had done. In addition, he did not enter the temple of the LORD. But the people still behaved corruptly.'),
('2CH', 27, 3, '2CH.27.3', 'Jotham rebuilt the Upper Gate of the house of the LORD, and he worked extensively on the wall at the hill of Ophel.'),
('2CH', 27, 4, '2CH.27.4', 'He also built cities in the hill country of Judah and fortresses and towers in the forests.'),
('2CH', 27, 5, '2CH.27.5', 'Jotham waged war against the king of the Ammonites and defeated them, and that year they gave him a hundred talents of silver, ten thousand cors of wheat, and ten thousand cors of barley. They paid him the same in the second and third years.'),
('2CH', 27, 6, '2CH.27.6', 'So Jotham grew powerful because he ordered his ways before the LORD his God.'),
('2CH', 27, 7, '2CH.27.7', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jotham, along with all his wars and his ways, they are indeed written in the Book of the Kings of Israel and Judah.'),
('2CH', 27, 8, '2CH.27.8', 'He was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem sixteen years.'),
('2CH', 27, 9, '2CH.27.9', 'And Jotham rested with his fathers and was buried in the City of David. And his son Ahaz reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 28, 1, '2CH.28.1', 'Ahaz was twenty years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem sixteen years. And unlike David his father, he did not do what was right in the eyes of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 28, 2, '2CH.28.2', 'Instead, he walked in the ways of the kings of Israel and even made cast images of the Baals.'),
('2CH', 28, 3, '2CH.28.3', 'Moreover, Ahaz burned incense in the Valley of Ben-hinnom and sacrificed his sons in the fire, according to the abominations of the nations that the LORD had driven out before the Israelites.'),
('2CH', 28, 4, '2CH.28.4', 'And he sacrificed and burned incense on the high places, on the hills, and under every green tree.'),
('2CH', 28, 5, '2CH.28.5', 'So the LORD his God delivered Ahaz into the hand of the king of Aram, who attacked him and took many captives to Damascus. Ahaz was also delivered into the hand of the king of Israel, who struck him with great force.'),
('2CH', 28, 6, '2CH.28.6', 'For in one day Pekah son of Remaliah killed 120,000 valiant men in Judah. This happened because they had forsaken the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 28, 7, '2CH.28.7', 'Zichri, a mighty man of Ephraim, killed Maaseiah the son of the king, Azrikam the governor of the palace, and Elkanah the second to the king.'),
('2CH', 28, 8, '2CH.28.8', 'Then the Israelites took 200,000 captives from their kinsmen—women, sons, and daughters. They also carried off a great deal of plunder and brought it to Samaria.'),
('2CH', 28, 9, '2CH.28.9', 'But a prophet of the LORD named Oded was there, and he went out to meet the army that returned to Samaria. “Look,” he said to them, “because of His wrath against Judah, the LORD, the God of your fathers, has delivered them into your hand. But you have slaughtered them in a rage that reaches up to heaven.'),
('2CH', 28, 10, '2CH.28.10', 'And now you intend to reduce to slavery the men and women of Judah and Jerusalem. But are you not also guilty before the LORD your God?'),
('2CH', 28, 11, '2CH.28.11', 'Now therefore, listen to me and return the captives you took from your kinsmen, for the fierce anger of the LORD is upon you.”'),
('2CH', 28, 12, '2CH.28.12', 'Then some of the leaders of the Ephraimites—Azariah son of Jehohanan, Berechiah son of Meshillemoth, Jehizkiah son of Shallum, and Amasa son of Hadlai—stood in opposition to those arriving from the war.'),
('2CH', 28, 13, '2CH.28.13', '“You must not bring the captives here,” they said, “for you are proposing to bring guilt upon us from the LORD and to add to our sins and our guilt. For our guilt is great, and fierce anger is upon Israel.”'),
('2CH', 28, 14, '2CH.28.14', 'So the armed men left the captives and the plunder before the leaders and all the assembly.'),
('2CH', 28, 15, '2CH.28.15', 'Then the men who were designated by name arose, took charge of the captives, and provided from the plunder clothing for the naked. They clothed them, gave them sandals and food and drink, anointed their wounds, and put all the feeble on donkeys. So they brought them to Jericho, the City of Palms, to their brothers. Then they returned to Samaria.'),
('2CH', 28, 16, '2CH.28.16', 'At that time King Ahaz sent for help from the king of Assyria.'),
('2CH', 28, 17, '2CH.28.17', 'The Edomites had again come and attacked Judah and carried away captives.'),
('2CH', 28, 18, '2CH.28.18', 'The Philistines had also raided the cities of the foothills and the Negev of Judah, capturing and occupying Beth-shemesh, Aijalon, and Gederoth, as well as Soco, Timnah, and Gimzo with their villages.'),
('2CH', 28, 19, '2CH.28.19', 'For the LORD humbled Judah because Ahaz king of Israel had thrown off restraint in Judah and had been most unfaithful to the LORD.'),
('2CH', 28, 20, '2CH.28.20', 'Then Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria came to Ahaz but afflicted him rather than strengthening him.'),
('2CH', 28, 21, '2CH.28.21', 'Although Ahaz had taken a portion from the house of the LORD, from the royal palace, and from the princes and had presented it to the king of Assyria, it did not help him.'),
('2CH', 28, 22, '2CH.28.22', 'In the time of his distress, King Ahaz became even more unfaithful to the LORD.'),
('2CH', 28, 23, '2CH.28.23', 'He sacrificed to the gods of Damascus, who had defeated him, and he said, “Because the gods of the kings of Aram have helped them, I will sacrifice to them that they may help me.” But these gods were the downfall of Ahaz and of all Israel.'),
('2CH', 28, 24, '2CH.28.24', 'Then Ahaz gathered up the articles of the house of God, cut them into pieces, shut the doors of the house of the LORD, and set up altars of his own on every street corner in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 28, 25, '2CH.28.25', 'In every city of Judah he built high places to offer incense to other gods, and so he provoked the LORD, the God of his fathers.'),
('2CH', 28, 26, '2CH.28.26', 'As for the rest of the acts of Ahaz and all his ways, from beginning to end, they are indeed written in the Book of the Kings of Judah and Israel.'),
('2CH', 28, 27, '2CH.28.27', 'And Ahaz rested with his fathers and was buried in the city of Jerusalem, but he was not placed in the tombs of the kings of Israel. And his son Hezekiah reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 29, 1, '2CH.29.1', 'Hezekiah was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem twenty-nine years. His mother’s name was Abijah, the daughter of Zechariah.'),
('2CH', 29, 2, '2CH.29.2', 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD, just as his father David had done.'),
('2CH', 29, 3, '2CH.29.3', 'In the first month of the first year of his reign, Hezekiah opened and repaired the doors of the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 29, 4, '2CH.29.4', 'Then he brought in the priests and Levites and gathered them in the square on the east side.'),
('2CH', 29, 5, '2CH.29.5', '“Listen to me, O Levites,” he said. “Consecrate yourselves now and consecrate the house of the LORD, the God of your fathers. Remove from the Holy Place every impurity.'),
('2CH', 29, 6, '2CH.29.6', 'For our fathers were unfaithful and did evil in the sight of the LORD our God. They abandoned Him, turned their faces away from the dwelling place of the LORD, and turned their backs on Him.'),
('2CH', 29, 7, '2CH.29.7', 'They also shut the doors of the portico and extinguished the lamps. They did not burn incense or present burnt offerings in the Holy Place of the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 29, 8, '2CH.29.8', 'Therefore, the wrath of the LORD has fallen upon Judah and Jerusalem, and He has made them an object of terror, horror, and scorn, as you can see with your own eyes.'),
('2CH', 29, 9, '2CH.29.9', 'For behold, this is why our fathers have fallen by the sword, and our sons and daughters and wives are in captivity.'),
('2CH', 29, 10, '2CH.29.10', 'Now it is in my heart to make a covenant with the LORD, the God of Israel, so that His fierce anger will turn away from us.'),
('2CH', 29, 11, '2CH.29.11', 'Now, my sons, do not be negligent, for the LORD has chosen you to stand before Him, to serve Him, to minister before Him, and to burn incense.”'),
('2CH', 29, 12, '2CH.29.12', 'Then the Levites set to work: Mahath son of Amasai and Joel son of Azariah from the Kohathites; Kish son of Abdi and Azariah son of Jehallelel from the Merarites; Joah son of Zimmah and Eden son of Joah from the Gershonites;'),
('2CH', 29, 13, '2CH.29.13', 'Shimri and Jeuel from the Elizaphanites; Zechariah and Mattaniah from the Asaphites;'),
('2CH', 29, 14, '2CH.29.14', 'Jehiel and Shimei from the Hemanites; and Shemaiah and Uzziel from the Jeduthunites.'),
('2CH', 29, 15, '2CH.29.15', 'When they had assembled their brothers and consecrated themselves, they went in to cleanse the house of the LORD, according to the command of the king by the words of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 29, 16, '2CH.29.16', 'So the priests went inside the house of the LORD to cleanse it, and they brought out to the courtyard all the unclean things that they found in the temple of the LORD. Then the Levites took these things and carried them out to the Kidron Valley.'),
('2CH', 29, 17, '2CH.29.17', 'They began the consecration on the first day of the first month, and on the eighth day of the month they reached the portico of the LORD. For eight more days they consecrated the house of the LORD itself, finishing on the sixteenth day of the first month.'),
('2CH', 29, 18, '2CH.29.18', 'Then they went in to King Hezekiah and reported, “We have cleansed the entire house of the LORD, the altar of burnt offering with all its utensils, and the table of the showbread with all its utensils.'),
('2CH', 29, 19, '2CH.29.19', 'Moreover, we have prepared and consecrated all the articles that King Ahaz in his unfaithfulness cast aside during his reign. They are now in front of the altar of the LORD.”'),
('2CH', 29, 20, '2CH.29.20', 'Early the next morning King Hezekiah gathered the city officials and went up to the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 29, 21, '2CH.29.21', 'They brought seven bulls, seven rams, seven lambs, and seven male goats as a sin offering for the kingdom, for the sanctuary, and for Judah. And the king commanded the priests, the descendants of Aaron, to offer them on the altar of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 29, 22, '2CH.29.22', 'So they slaughtered the bulls, and the priests took the blood and splattered it on the altar. They slaughtered the rams and splattered the blood on the altar. And they slaughtered the lambs and splattered the blood on the altar.'),
('2CH', 29, 23, '2CH.29.23', 'Then they brought the goats for the sin offering before the king and the assembly, who laid their hands on them.'),
('2CH', 29, 24, '2CH.29.24', 'And the priests slaughtered the goats and put their blood on the altar for a sin offering, to make atonement for all Israel, because the king had ordered the burnt offering and the sin offering for all Israel.'),
('2CH', 29, 25, '2CH.29.25', 'Hezekiah stationed the Levites in the house of the LORD with cymbals, harps, and lyres according to the command of David, of Gad the king’s seer, and of Nathan the prophet. For the command had come from the LORD through His prophets.'),
('2CH', 29, 26, '2CH.29.26', 'The Levites stood with the instruments of David, and the priests with the trumpets.'),
('2CH', 29, 27, '2CH.29.27', 'And Hezekiah ordered that the burnt offering be sacrificed on the altar. When the burnt offering began, the song of the LORD and the trumpets began as well, accompanied by the instruments of David king of Israel.'),
('2CH', 29, 28, '2CH.29.28', 'The whole assembly was worshiping, the singers were singing, and the trumpeters were playing. All this continued until the burnt offering was completed.'),
('2CH', 29, 29, '2CH.29.29', 'When the offerings were completed, the king and all those present with him bowed down and worshiped.'),
('2CH', 29, 30, '2CH.29.30', 'Then King Hezekiah and his officials ordered the Levites to sing praises to the LORD in the words of David and of Asaph the seer. So they sang praises with gladness and bowed down and worshiped.'),
('2CH', 29, 31, '2CH.29.31', 'Then Hezekiah said, “Now that you have consecrated yourselves to the LORD, come near and bring sacrifices and thank offerings to the house of the LORD.” So the assembly brought sacrifices and thank offerings, and all whose hearts were willing brought burnt offerings.'),
('2CH', 29, 32, '2CH.29.32', 'The number of burnt offerings the assembly brought was seventy bulls, a hundred rams, and two hundred lambs; all these were for a burnt offering to the LORD.'),
('2CH', 29, 33, '2CH.29.33', 'And the consecrated offerings were six hundred bulls and three thousand sheep.'),
('2CH', 29, 34, '2CH.29.34', 'However, since there were not enough priests to skin all the burnt offerings, their Levite brothers helped them until the work was finished and until the priests had consecrated themselves. For the Levites had been more diligent in consecrating themselves than the priests had been.'),
('2CH', 29, 35, '2CH.29.35', 'Furthermore, the burnt offerings were abundant, along with the fat of the peace offerings and the drink offerings for the burnt offerings. So the service of the house of the LORD was established.'),
('2CH', 29, 36, '2CH.29.36', 'Then Hezekiah and all the people rejoiced at what God had prepared for the people, because everything had been accomplished so quickly.'),
('2CH', 30, 1, '2CH.30.1', 'Then Hezekiah sent word throughout all Israel and Judah, and he also wrote letters to Ephraim and Manasseh inviting them to come to the house of the LORD in Jerusalem to keep the Passover of the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 30, 2, '2CH.30.2', 'For the king and his officials and the whole assembly in Jerusalem had decided to keep the Passover in the second month,'),
('2CH', 30, 3, '2CH.30.3', 'since they had been unable to keep it at the regular time, because not enough priests had consecrated themselves and the people had not been gathered in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 30, 4, '2CH.30.4', 'This plan pleased the king and the whole assembly.'),
('2CH', 30, 5, '2CH.30.5', 'So they established a decree to circulate a proclamation throughout Israel, from Beersheba to Dan, that the people should come to keep the Passover of the LORD, the God of Israel, in Jerusalem. For they had not observed it in great numbers as prescribed.'),
('2CH', 30, 6, '2CH.30.6', 'At the command of the king, the couriers went throughout Israel and Judah with letters from the king and his officials, which read: “Children of Israel, return to the LORD, the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, so that He may return to those of you who remain, who have escaped the grasp of the kings of Assyria.'),
('2CH', 30, 7, '2CH.30.7', 'Do not be like your fathers and brothers who were unfaithful to the LORD, the God of their fathers, so that He made them an object of horror, as you can see.'),
('2CH', 30, 8, '2CH.30.8', 'Now do not stiffen your necks as your fathers did. Submit to the LORD and come to His sanctuary, which He has consecrated forever. Serve the LORD your God, so that His fierce anger will turn away from you.'),
('2CH', 30, 9, '2CH.30.9', 'For if you return to the LORD, your brothers and sons will receive mercy in the presence of their captors and will return to this land. For the LORD your God is gracious and merciful; He will not turn His face away from you if you return to Him.”'),
('2CH', 30, 10, '2CH.30.10', 'And the couriers traveled from city to city through the land of Ephraim and Manasseh as far as Zebulun, but the people scorned and mocked them.'),
('2CH', 30, 11, '2CH.30.11', 'Nevertheless, some from Asher, Manasseh, and Zebulun humbled themselves and came to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 30, 12, '2CH.30.12', 'Moreover, the power of God was on the people in Judah to give them one heart to obey the command of the king and his officials according to the word of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 30, 13, '2CH.30.13', 'In the second month, a very great assembly gathered in Jerusalem to celebrate the Feast of Unleavened Bread.'),
('2CH', 30, 14, '2CH.30.14', 'They proceeded to remove the altars in Jerusalem and to take away the incense altars and throw them into the Kidron Valley.'),
('2CH', 30, 15, '2CH.30.15', 'And on the fourteenth day of the second month they slaughtered the Passover lamb. The priests and Levites were ashamed, and they consecrated themselves and brought burnt offerings to the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 30, 16, '2CH.30.16', 'They stood at their prescribed posts, according to the Law of Moses the man of God. The priests splattered the blood, which they received from the hand of the Levites.'),
('2CH', 30, 17, '2CH.30.17', 'Since there were many in the assembly who had not consecrated themselves, the Levites were in charge of slaughtering the Passover lambs for every unclean person to consecrate the lambs to the LORD.'),
('2CH', 30, 18, '2CH.30.18', 'A large number of the people—many from Ephraim, Manasseh, Issachar, and Zebulun—had not purified themselves, yet they ate the Passover, contrary to what was written. But Hezekiah interceded for them, saying, “May the LORD, who is good, provide atonement for everyone'),
('2CH', 30, 19, '2CH.30.19', 'who sets his heart on seeking God—the LORD, the God of his fathers—even if he is not cleansed according to the purification rules of the sanctuary.”'),
('2CH', 30, 20, '2CH.30.20', 'And the LORD heard Hezekiah and healed the people.'),
('2CH', 30, 21, '2CH.30.21', 'The Israelites who were present in Jerusalem celebrated the Feast of Unleavened Bread for seven days with great joy, and the Levites and priests praised the LORD day after day, accompanied by loud instruments of praise to the LORD.'),
('2CH', 30, 22, '2CH.30.22', 'And Hezekiah encouraged all the Levites who performed skillfully before the LORD. For seven days they ate their assigned portion, sacrificing peace offerings and giving thanks to the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 30, 23, '2CH.30.23', 'The whole assembly agreed to observe seven more days, so they observed seven days with joy.'),
('2CH', 30, 24, '2CH.30.24', 'For Hezekiah king of Judah contributed a thousand bulls and seven thousand sheep for the assembly, and the officials contributed a thousand bulls and ten thousand sheep for the assembly, and a great number of priests consecrated themselves.'),
('2CH', 30, 25, '2CH.30.25', 'Then the whole assembly of Judah rejoiced along with the priests and Levites and the whole assembly that had come from Israel, including the foreigners who had come from Israel and those who lived in Judah.'),
('2CH', 30, 26, '2CH.30.26', 'So there was great rejoicing in Jerusalem, for nothing like this had happened there since the days of Solomon son of David king of Israel.'),
('2CH', 30, 27, '2CH.30.27', 'Then the priests and the Levites stood to bless the people, and God heard their voice, and their prayer came into His holy dwelling place in heaven.'),
('2CH', 31, 1, '2CH.31.1', 'When all this had ended, the Israelites in attendance went out to the cities of Judah and broke up the sacred pillars, chopped down the Asherah poles, and tore down the high places and altars throughout Judah and Benjamin, as well as in Ephraim and Manasseh, until they had utterly destroyed them all. Then all the Israelites returned to their cities, each to his own property.'),
('2CH', 31, 2, '2CH.31.2', 'Hezekiah reestablished the divisions of the priests and Levites—each of them according to their duties as priests or Levites—for the burnt offerings and peace offerings, for ministry, for giving thanks, and for singing praises at the gates of the LORD’s dwelling.'),
('2CH', 31, 3, '2CH.31.3', 'The king contributed from his own possessions for the regular morning and evening burnt offerings and for the burnt offerings on the Sabbaths, New Moons, and appointed feasts, as written in the Law of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 31, 4, '2CH.31.4', 'Moreover, he commanded the people living in Jerusalem to make a contribution for the priests and Levites so that they could devote themselves to the Law of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 31, 5, '2CH.31.5', 'As soon as the order went out, the Israelites generously provided the firstfruits of the grain, new wine, oil, and honey, and of all the produce of the field, and they brought in an abundance—a tithe of everything.'),
('2CH', 31, 6, '2CH.31.6', 'And the Israelites and Judahites who lived in the cities of Judah also brought a tithe of their herds and flocks and a tithe of the holy things consecrated to the LORD their God, and they laid them in large heaps.'),
('2CH', 31, 7, '2CH.31.7', 'In the third month they began building up the heaps, and they finished in the seventh month.'),
('2CH', 31, 8, '2CH.31.8', 'When Hezekiah and his officials came and viewed the heaps, they blessed the LORD and His people Israel.'),
('2CH', 31, 9, '2CH.31.9', 'Then Hezekiah questioned the priests and Levites about the heaps,'),
('2CH', 31, 10, '2CH.31.10', 'and Azariah, the chief priest of the household of Zadok, answered him, “Since the people began to bring their contributions into the house of the LORD, we have had enough to eat, and there is plenty left over, because the LORD has blessed His people; this great abundance is what is left over.”'),
('2CH', 31, 11, '2CH.31.11', 'Then Hezekiah commanded them to prepare storerooms in the house of the LORD, and they did so.'),
('2CH', 31, 12, '2CH.31.12', 'And they faithfully brought in the contributions, tithes, and dedicated gifts. Conaniah the Levite was the officer in charge of them, and his brother Shimei was second.'),
('2CH', 31, 13, '2CH.31.13', 'Jehiel, Azaziah, Nahath, Asahel, Jerimoth, Jozabad, Eliel, Ismachiah, Mahath, and Benaiah were overseers under the authority of Conaniah and his brother Shimei, by appointment of King Hezekiah and of Azariah the chief official of the house of God.'),
('2CH', 31, 14, '2CH.31.14', 'Kore son of Imnah the Levite, the keeper of the East Gate, was in charge of the freewill offerings given to God, distributing the contributions to the LORD and the consecrated gifts.'),
('2CH', 31, 15, '2CH.31.15', 'Under his authority, Eden, Miniamin, Jeshua, Shemaiah, Amariah, and Shecaniah faithfully distributed portions to their fellow priests in their cities, according to their divisions, old and young alike.'),
('2CH', 31, 16, '2CH.31.16', 'In addition, they distributed portions to the males registered by genealogy who were three years of age or older—to all who would enter the house of the LORD for their daily duties for service in the responsibilities of their divisions—'),
('2CH', 31, 17, '2CH.31.17', 'and to the priests enrolled according to their families in the genealogy, as well as to the Levites twenty years of age or older, according to their responsibilities and divisions.'),
('2CH', 31, 18, '2CH.31.18', 'The genealogy included all the little ones, wives, sons, and daughters of the whole assembly. For they had faithfully consecrated themselves as holy.'),
('2CH', 31, 19, '2CH.31.19', 'As for the priests, the descendants of Aaron, who lived on the farmlands around each of their cities or in any other city, men were designated by name to distribute a portion to every male among the priests and to every Levite listed by the genealogies.'),
('2CH', 31, 20, '2CH.31.20', 'So this is what Hezekiah did throughout Judah. He did what was good and upright and true before the LORD his God.'),
('2CH', 31, 21, '2CH.31.21', 'He acted with all his heart in every work that he began in the service of the house of God, and in the law and the commandments, in order to seek his God. And so he prospered.'),
('2CH', 32, 1, '2CH.32.1', 'After all these acts of faithfulness, Sennacherib king of Assyria came and invaded Judah. He laid siege to the fortified cities, intending to conquer them for himself.'),
('2CH', 32, 2, '2CH.32.2', 'When Hezekiah saw that Sennacherib had come to make war against Jerusalem,'),
('2CH', 32, 3, '2CH.32.3', 'he consulted with his leaders and mighty men about stopping up the waters of the springs outside the city, and they helped him carry it out.'),
('2CH', 32, 4, '2CH.32.4', 'Many people assembled and stopped up all the springs and the stream that flowed through the land. “Why should the kings of Assyria come and find plenty of water?” they said.'),
('2CH', 32, 5, '2CH.32.5', 'Then Hezekiah worked resolutely to rebuild all the broken sections of the wall and to raise up towers on it. He also built an outer wall and reinforced the supporting terraces of the City of David, and he produced an abundance of weapons and shields.'),
('2CH', 32, 6, '2CH.32.6', 'Hezekiah appointed military commanders over the people and gathered the people in the square of the city gate. Then he encouraged them, saying,'),
('2CH', 32, 7, '2CH.32.7', '“Be strong and courageous! Do not be afraid or discouraged before the king of Assyria and the vast army with him, for there is a greater One with us than with him.'),
('2CH', 32, 8, '2CH.32.8', 'With him is only the arm of flesh, but with us is the LORD our God to help us and to fight our battles.” So the people were strengthened by the words of Hezekiah king of Judah.'),
('2CH', 32, 9, '2CH.32.9', 'Later, as Sennacherib king of Assyria and all his forces besieged Lachish, he sent his servants to Jerusalem with a message for King Hezekiah of Judah and all the people of Judah who were in Jerusalem:'),
('2CH', 32, 10, '2CH.32.10', '“This is what Sennacherib king of Assyria says: What is the basis of your confidence, that you remain in Jerusalem under siege?'),
('2CH', 32, 11, '2CH.32.11', 'Is not Hezekiah misleading you to give you over to death by famine and thirst when he says, ‘The LORD our God will deliver us from the hand of the king of Assyria?’'),
('2CH', 32, 12, '2CH.32.12', 'Did not Hezekiah himself remove His high places and His altars and say to Judah and Jerusalem, ‘You must worship before one altar, and on it you shall burn sacrifices’?'),
('2CH', 32, 13, '2CH.32.13', 'Do you not know what I and my fathers have done to all the peoples of the lands? Have the gods of these nations ever been able to deliver their land from my hand?'),
('2CH', 32, 14, '2CH.32.14', 'Who among all the gods of these nations that my fathers devoted to destruction has been able to deliver his people from my hand? How then can your God deliver you from my hand?'),
('2CH', 32, 15, '2CH.32.15', 'So now, do not let Hezekiah deceive you, and do not let him mislead you like this. Do not believe him, for no god of any nation or kingdom has been able to deliver his people from my hand or from the hand of my fathers. How much less will your God deliver you from my hand!”'),
('2CH', 32, 16, '2CH.32.16', 'And the servants of Sennacherib spoke further against the LORD God and against His servant Hezekiah.'),
('2CH', 32, 17, '2CH.32.17', 'He also wrote letters mocking the LORD, the God of Israel, and saying against Him: “Just as the gods of the nations did not deliver their people from my hand, so the God of Hezekiah will not deliver His people from my hand.”'),
('2CH', 32, 18, '2CH.32.18', 'Then the Assyrians called out loudly in Hebrew to the people of Jerusalem who were on the wall, to frighten and terrify them in order to capture the city.'),
('2CH', 32, 19, '2CH.32.19', 'They spoke against the God of Jerusalem as they had spoken against the gods of the peoples of the earth—the work of human hands.'),
('2CH', 32, 20, '2CH.32.20', 'In response, King Hezekiah and the prophet Isaiah son of Amoz cried out to heaven in prayer,'),
('2CH', 32, 21, '2CH.32.21', 'and the LORD sent an angel who annihilated every mighty man of valor and every leader and commander in the camp of the king of Assyria. So he withdrew to his own land in disgrace. And when he entered the temple of his god, some of his own sons struck him down with the sword.'),
('2CH', 32, 22, '2CH.32.22', 'So the LORD saved Hezekiah and the people of Jerusalem from the hands of King Sennacherib of Assyria and all others, and He gave them rest on every side.'),
('2CH', 32, 23, '2CH.32.23', 'Many brought offerings to Jerusalem for the LORD and valuable gifts for Hezekiah king of Judah, and from then on he was exalted in the eyes of all nations.'),
('2CH', 32, 24, '2CH.32.24', 'In those days Hezekiah became mortally ill. So he prayed to the LORD, who spoke to him and gave him a sign.'),
('2CH', 32, 25, '2CH.32.25', 'But because his heart was proud, Hezekiah did not repay the favor shown to him. Therefore wrath came upon him and upon Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 32, 26, '2CH.32.26', 'Then Hezekiah humbled the pride of his heart—he and the people of Jerusalem—so that the wrath of the LORD did not come upon them during the days of Hezekiah.'),
('2CH', 32, 27, '2CH.32.27', 'Hezekiah had very great riches and honor, and he made treasuries for his silver, gold, precious stones, spices, shields, and all kinds of valuable articles.'),
('2CH', 32, 28, '2CH.32.28', 'He also made storehouses for the harvest of grain and new wine and oil, stalls for all kinds of livestock, and pens for the flocks.'),
('2CH', 32, 29, '2CH.32.29', 'He made cities for himself, and he acquired herds of sheep and cattle in abundance, for God gave him very great wealth.'),
('2CH', 32, 30, '2CH.32.30', 'It was Hezekiah who blocked the upper outlet of the Spring of Gihon and channeled it down to the west side of the City of David. And Hezekiah prospered in all that he did.'),
('2CH', 32, 31, '2CH.32.31', 'And so when ambassadors of the rulers of Babylon were sent to him to inquire about the wonder that had happened in the land, God left him alone to test him, that He might know all that was in Hezekiah’s heart.'),
('2CH', 32, 32, '2CH.32.32', 'As for the rest of the acts of Hezekiah and his deeds of loving devotion, they are indeed written in the vision of the prophet Isaiah son of Amoz in the Book of the Kings of Judah and Israel.'),
('2CH', 32, 33, '2CH.32.33', 'And Hezekiah rested with his fathers and was buried in the upper tombs of David’s descendants. All Judah and the people of Jerusalem paid him honor at his death. And his son Manasseh reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 33, 1, '2CH.33.1', 'Manasseh was twelve years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem fifty-five years.'),
('2CH', 33, 2, '2CH.33.2', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD by following the abominations of the nations that the LORD had driven out before the Israelites.'),
('2CH', 33, 3, '2CH.33.3', 'For he rebuilt the high places that his father Hezekiah had torn down, and he raised up altars for the Baals and made Asherah poles. And he worshiped and served all the host of heaven.'),
('2CH', 33, 4, '2CH.33.4', 'Manasseh also built altars in the house of the LORD, of which the LORD had said, “My Name will remain in Jerusalem forever.”'),
('2CH', 33, 5, '2CH.33.5', 'In both courtyards of the house of the LORD, he built altars to all the host of heaven.'),
('2CH', 33, 6, '2CH.33.6', 'He sacrificed his sons in the fire in the Valley of Ben-hinnom. He practiced sorcery, divination, and witchcraft, and consulted mediums and spiritists. He did great evil in the sight of the LORD, provoking Him to anger.'),
('2CH', 33, 7, '2CH.33.7', 'Manasseh even took the carved image he had made and set it up in the house of God, of which God had said to David and his son Solomon, “In this temple and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, I will establish My Name forever.'),
('2CH', 33, 8, '2CH.33.8', 'I will never again cause the feet of the Israelites to leave the land that I assigned to your fathers, if only they are careful to do all that I have commanded them through Moses—all the laws, statutes, and judgments.”'),
('2CH', 33, 9, '2CH.33.9', 'So Manasseh led the people of Judah and Jerusalem astray, so that they did greater evil than the nations that the LORD had destroyed before the Israelites.'),
('2CH', 33, 10, '2CH.33.10', 'And the LORD spoke to Manasseh and his people, but they did not listen.'),
('2CH', 33, 11, '2CH.33.11', 'So the LORD brought against them the military commanders of the king of Assyria, who captured Manasseh, put a hook in his nose, bound him with bronze shackles, and took him to Babylon.'),
('2CH', 33, 12, '2CH.33.12', 'And in his distress, Manasseh sought the favor of the LORD his God and earnestly humbled himself before the God of his fathers.'),
('2CH', 33, 13, '2CH.33.13', 'And when he prayed to Him, the LORD received his plea and heard his petition. So He brought him back to Jerusalem and to his kingdom. Then Manasseh knew that the LORD is God.'),
('2CH', 33, 14, '2CH.33.14', 'After this, Manasseh rebuilt the outer wall of the City of David from west of Gihon in the valley to the entrance of the Fish Gate, and he brought it around the hill of Ophel and heightened it considerably. He also stationed military commanders in all the fortified cities of Judah.'),
('2CH', 33, 15, '2CH.33.15', 'He removed the foreign gods and the idol from the house of the LORD, along with all the altars he had built on the temple mount and in Jerusalem, and he dumped them outside the city.'),
('2CH', 33, 16, '2CH.33.16', 'Then he restored the altar of the LORD and sacrificed peace offerings and thank offerings on it, and he told Judah to serve the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 33, 17, '2CH.33.17', 'Nevertheless, the people still sacrificed at the high places, but only to the LORD their God.'),
('2CH', 33, 18, '2CH.33.18', 'As for the rest of the acts of Manasseh, along with his prayer to his God and the words of the seers who spoke to him in the name of the LORD, the God of Israel, they are indeed written in the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel.'),
('2CH', 33, 19, '2CH.33.19', 'His prayer and how God received his plea, as well as all his sin and unfaithfulness, and the sites where he built high places and set up Asherah poles and idols before he humbled himself, they are indeed written in the Records of the Seers.'),
('2CH', 33, 20, '2CH.33.20', 'And Manasseh rested with his fathers and was buried at his palace. And his son Amon reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 33, 21, '2CH.33.21', 'Amon was twenty-two years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem two years.'),
('2CH', 33, 22, '2CH.33.22', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, as his father Manasseh had done. Amon served and sacrificed to all the idols that his father Manasseh had made,'),
('2CH', 33, 23, '2CH.33.23', 'but he did not humble himself before the LORD as his father Manasseh had done; instead, Amon increased his guilt.'),
('2CH', 33, 24, '2CH.33.24', 'Then the servants of Amon conspired against him and killed him in his palace.'),
('2CH', 33, 25, '2CH.33.25', 'But the people of the land killed all those who had conspired against King Amon, and they made his son Josiah king in his place.'),
('2CH', 34, 1, '2CH.34.1', 'Josiah was eight years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem thirty-one years.'),
('2CH', 34, 2, '2CH.34.2', 'And he did what was right in the eyes of the LORD and walked in the ways of his father David; he did not turn aside to the right or to the left.'),
('2CH', 34, 3, '2CH.34.3', 'In the eighth year of his reign, while he was still young, Josiah began to seek the God of his father David, and in the twelfth year he began to cleanse Judah and Jerusalem of the high places, the Asherah poles, the carved idols, and the cast images.'),
('2CH', 34, 4, '2CH.34.4', 'Then in his presence the altars of the Baals were torn down, and he cut to pieces the incense altars that were above them. He shattered the Asherah poles, the carved idols, and the cast images, crushed them to dust, and scattered them over the graves of those who had sacrificed to them.'),
('2CH', 34, 5, '2CH.34.5', 'Then he burned the bones of the priests on their altars. So he cleansed Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 34, 6, '2CH.34.6', 'Josiah did the same in the cities of Manasseh, Ephraim, and Simeon, as far as Naphtali, and in the ruins around them.'),
('2CH', 34, 7, '2CH.34.7', 'He tore down the altars and Asherah poles, crushed the idols to powder, and cut to pieces all the incense altars throughout the land of Israel. Then he returned to Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 34, 8, '2CH.34.8', 'Now in the eighteenth year of his reign, in order to cleanse the land and the temple, Josiah sent Shaphan son of Azaliah, Maaseiah the governor of the city, and Joah son of Joahaz, the recorder, to repair the house of the LORD his God.'),
('2CH', 34, 9, '2CH.34.9', 'So they went to Hilkiah the high priest and gave him the money that had been brought into the house of God, which the Levites who guarded the doors had collected from the people of Manasseh and Ephraim, from all the remnant of Israel, from all Judah and Benjamin, and from the people of Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 34, 10, '2CH.34.10', 'They put it into the hands of those supervising the work in the house of the LORD, who in turn gave it to the workmen restoring and repairing the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 34, 11, '2CH.34.11', 'They also gave money to the carpenters and builders to buy dressed stone, as well as timbers for couplings and beams for the buildings that the kings of Judah had allowed to deteriorate.'),
('2CH', 34, 12, '2CH.34.12', 'And the men did the work faithfully. The Levites overseeing them were Jahath and Obadiah, descendants of Merari, and Zechariah and Meshullam, descendants of Kohath. Other Levites, all skilled with musical instruments,'),
('2CH', 34, 13, '2CH.34.13', 'were over the laborers and supervised all who did the work, task by task. Some of the Levites were secretaries, officers, and gatekeepers.'),
('2CH', 34, 14, '2CH.34.14', 'While they were bringing out the money that had been taken into the house of the LORD, Hilkiah the priest found the Book of the Law of the LORD given by Moses.'),
('2CH', 34, 15, '2CH.34.15', 'And Hilkiah said to Shaphan the scribe, “I have found the Book of the Law in the house of the LORD!” And he gave it to Shaphan.'),
('2CH', 34, 16, '2CH.34.16', 'Then Shaphan brought the book to the king and reported, “Your servants are doing all that has been placed in their hands.'),
('2CH', 34, 17, '2CH.34.17', 'They have paid out the money that was found in the house of the LORD and have put it into the hands of the supervisors and workers.”'),
('2CH', 34, 18, '2CH.34.18', 'Moreover, Shaphan the scribe told the king, “Hilkiah the priest has given me a book.” And Shaphan read it in the presence of the king.'),
('2CH', 34, 19, '2CH.34.19', 'When the king heard the words of the Law, he tore his clothes'),
('2CH', 34, 20, '2CH.34.20', 'and commanded Hilkiah, Ahikam son of Shaphan, Abdon son of Micah, Shaphan the scribe, and Asaiah the servant of the king:'),
('2CH', 34, 21, '2CH.34.21', '“Go and inquire of the LORD for me and for those remaining in Israel and Judah concerning the words in the book that has been found. For great is the wrath of the LORD that has been poured out on us because our fathers have not kept the word of the LORD by doing all that is written in this book.”'),
('2CH', 34, 22, '2CH.34.22', 'So Hilkiah and those the king had designated went and spoke to Huldah the prophetess, the wife of Shallum son of Tokhath, the son of Hasrah, the keeper of the wardrobe. She lived in Jerusalem, in the Second District.'),
('2CH', 34, 23, '2CH.34.23', 'And Huldah said to them, “This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Tell the man who sent you'),
('2CH', 34, 24, '2CH.34.24', 'that this is what the LORD says: I am about to bring calamity on this place and on its people, according to all the curses written in the book that has been read in the presence of the king of Judah,'),
('2CH', 34, 25, '2CH.34.25', 'because they have forsaken Me and burned incense to other gods, that they might provoke Me to anger with all the works of their hands. My wrath will be poured out upon this place and will not be quenched.’'),
('2CH', 34, 26, '2CH.34.26', 'But as for the king of Judah, who sent you to inquire of the LORD, tell him that this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘As for the words that you heard,'),
('2CH', 34, 27, '2CH.34.27', 'because your heart was tender and you humbled yourself before God when you heard His words against this place and against its people, and because you have humbled yourself before Me and have torn your clothes and wept before Me, I have heard you,’ declares the LORD.'),
('2CH', 34, 28, '2CH.34.28', '‘Now I will indeed gather you to your fathers, and you will be gathered to your grave in peace. Your eyes will not see all the calamity that I will bring on this place and on its people.’” So they brought her answer back to the king.'),
('2CH', 34, 29, '2CH.34.29', 'Then the king summoned all the elders of Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 34, 30, '2CH.34.30', 'And he went up to the house of the LORD with all the people of Judah and Jerusalem, as well as the priests and the Levites—all the people great and small—and in their hearing he read all the words of the Book of the Covenant that had been found in the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 34, 31, '2CH.34.31', 'So the king stood by the pillar and made a covenant before the LORD to follow the LORD and to keep His commandments, decrees, and statutes with all his heart and all his soul, and to carry out the words of the covenant that were written in this book.'),
('2CH', 34, 32, '2CH.34.32', 'Then he had everyone in Jerusalem and Benjamin take a stand in agreement to it. So all the people of Jerusalem carried out the covenant of God, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 34, 33, '2CH.34.33', 'And Josiah removed all the abominations from all the lands belonging to the Israelites, and he required everyone in Israel to serve the LORD their God. Throughout his reign they did not turn aside from following the LORD, the God of their fathers.'),
('2CH', 35, 1, '2CH.35.1', 'Then Josiah kept the Passover to the LORD in Jerusalem, and the Passover lamb was slaughtered on the fourteenth day of the first month.'),
('2CH', 35, 2, '2CH.35.2', 'He appointed the priests to their duties and encouraged them in the service of the house of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 35, 3, '2CH.35.3', 'To the Levites who taught all Israel and were holy to the LORD, Josiah said: “Put the holy ark in the temple built by Solomon son of David king of Israel. It is not to be carried around on your shoulders. Now serve the LORD your God and His people Israel.'),
('2CH', 35, 4, '2CH.35.4', 'Prepare yourselves by families in your divisions, according to the instructions written by David king of Israel and Solomon his son.'),
('2CH', 35, 5, '2CH.35.5', 'Moreover, stand in the Holy Place by the divisions of the families of your kinsmen the lay people, and by the divisions of the families of the Levites.'),
('2CH', 35, 6, '2CH.35.6', 'Slaughter the Passover lambs, consecrate yourselves, and make preparations for your fellow countrymen to carry out the word of the LORD given by Moses.”'),
('2CH', 35, 7, '2CH.35.7', 'From his own flocks and herds Josiah contributed 30,000 lambs and goats plus 3,000 bulls for the Passover offerings for all the people who were present.'),
('2CH', 35, 8, '2CH.35.8', 'His officials also contributed willingly to the people and priests and Levites. Hilkiah, Zechariah, and Jehiel, the chief officials of the house of God, gave the priests 2,600 Passover offerings and 300 bulls.'),
('2CH', 35, 9, '2CH.35.9', 'Additionally, Conaniah and his brothers Shemaiah and Nethanel, as well as Hashabiah, Jeiel, and Jozabad, officers of the Levites, contributed to the Levites 5,000 Passover offerings and 500 bulls.'),
('2CH', 35, 10, '2CH.35.10', 'So the service was prepared; the priests stood in their places and the Levites in their divisions according to the king’s command.'),
('2CH', 35, 11, '2CH.35.11', 'And they slaughtered the Passover lambs, while the priests splattered the blood handed to them and the Levites skinned the animals.'),
('2CH', 35, 12, '2CH.35.12', 'They set aside the burnt offerings to be given to the divisions of the families of the people to offer to the LORD, as it is written in the Book of Moses. And they did the same with the bulls.'),
('2CH', 35, 13, '2CH.35.13', 'They roasted the Passover animals on the fire according to the regulation, and they boiled the other holy offerings in pots, kettles, and bowls and quickly brought them to all the people.'),
('2CH', 35, 14, '2CH.35.14', 'Afterward, they made preparations for themselves and for the priests, since the priests, the descendants of Aaron, were offering up burnt offerings and fat until nightfall. So the Levites made preparations for themselves and for the priests, the descendants of Aaron.'),
('2CH', 35, 15, '2CH.35.15', 'The singers, the descendants of Asaph, were at their stations according to the command of David, Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun the king’s seer. And the gatekeepers at each gate did not need to leave their posts, because their fellow Levites made preparations for them.'),
('2CH', 35, 16, '2CH.35.16', 'So on that day the entire service of the LORD was carried out for celebrating the Passover and offering burnt offerings on the altar of the LORD, according to the command of King Josiah.'),
('2CH', 35, 17, '2CH.35.17', 'The Israelites who were present also observed the Passover at that time, as well as the Feast of Unleavened Bread for seven days.'),
('2CH', 35, 18, '2CH.35.18', 'No such Passover had been observed in Israel since the days of Samuel the prophet. None of the kings of Israel ever observed a Passover like the one that Josiah observed with the priests, the Levites, all Judah, the Israelites who were present, and the people of Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 35, 19, '2CH.35.19', 'In the eighteenth year of Josiah’s reign, this Passover was observed.'),
('2CH', 35, 20, '2CH.35.20', 'After all this, when Josiah had set the temple in order, Neco king of Egypt marched up to fight at Carchemish by the Euphrates, and Josiah went out to confront him.'),
('2CH', 35, 21, '2CH.35.21', 'But Neco sent messengers to him, saying, “What is the issue between you and me, O king of Judah? I have not come against you today, but I am fighting another dynasty, and God has told me to hurry. So stop opposing God, who is with me, or He will destroy you!”'),
('2CH', 35, 22, '2CH.35.22', 'Josiah, however, did not turn away from him; instead, in order to engage him in battle, he disguised himself. He did not listen to Neco’s words from the mouth of God, but went to fight him on the Plain of Megiddo.'),
('2CH', 35, 23, '2CH.35.23', 'There the archers shot King Josiah, who said to his servants, “Take me away, for I am badly wounded!”'),
('2CH', 35, 24, '2CH.35.24', 'So his servants took him out of his chariot, put him in his second chariot, and brought him to Jerusalem, where he died. And Josiah was buried in the tomb of his fathers, and all Judah and Jerusalem mourned for him.'),
('2CH', 35, 25, '2CH.35.25', 'Then Jeremiah lamented over Josiah, and to this day all the male and female singers recite laments over Josiah. They established them as a statute for Israel, and indeed they are written in the Book of Laments.'),
('2CH', 35, 26, '2CH.35.26', 'As for the rest of the acts of Josiah and his deeds of loving devotion according to what is written in the Law of the LORD—'),
('2CH', 35, 27, '2CH.35.27', 'his acts from beginning to end—they are indeed written in the Book of the Kings of Israel and Judah.'),
('2CH', 36, 1, '2CH.36.1', 'Then the people of the land took Jehoahaz son of Josiah and made him king in Jerusalem in place of his father.'),
('2CH', 36, 2, '2CH.36.2', 'Jehoahaz was twenty-three years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months.'),
('2CH', 36, 3, '2CH.36.3', 'And the king of Egypt dethroned him in Jerusalem and imposed on Judah a levy of a hundred talents of silver and a talent of gold.'),
('2CH', 36, 4, '2CH.36.4', 'Then Neco king of Egypt made Eliakim brother of Jehoahaz king over Judah and Jerusalem, and he changed Eliakim’s name to Jehoiakim. But Neco took Eliakim’s brother Jehoahaz and carried him off to Egypt.'),
('2CH', 36, 5, '2CH.36.5', 'Jehoiakim was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eleven years. And he did evil in the sight of the LORD his God.'),
('2CH', 36, 6, '2CH.36.6', 'Then Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up against Jehoiakim and bound him with bronze shackles to take him to Babylon.'),
('2CH', 36, 7, '2CH.36.7', 'Nebuchadnezzar also took to Babylon some of the articles from the house of the LORD, and he put them in his temple in Babylon.'),
('2CH', 36, 8, '2CH.36.8', 'As for the rest of the acts of Jehoiakim, the abominations he committed, and all that was found against him, they are indeed written in the Book of the Kings of Israel and Judah. And his son Jehoiachin reigned in his place.'),
('2CH', 36, 9, '2CH.36.9', 'Jehoiachin was eighteen years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months and ten days. And he did evil in the sight of the LORD.'),
('2CH', 36, 10, '2CH.36.10', 'In the spring, King Nebuchadnezzar summoned Jehoiachin and brought him to Babylon, along with the articles of value from the house of the LORD. And he made Jehoiachin’s relative Zedekiah king over Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 36, 11, '2CH.36.11', 'Zedekiah was twenty-one years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eleven years.'),
('2CH', 36, 12, '2CH.36.12', 'And he did evil in the sight of the LORD his God and did not humble himself before Jeremiah the prophet, who spoke for the LORD.'),
('2CH', 36, 13, '2CH.36.13', 'He also rebelled against King Nebuchadnezzar, who had made him swear by God. But Zedekiah stiffened his neck and hardened his heart against turning to the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('2CH', 36, 14, '2CH.36.14', 'Furthermore, all the leaders of the priests and the people multiplied their unfaithful deeds, following all the abominations of the nations, and they defiled the house of the LORD, which He had consecrated in Jerusalem.'),
('2CH', 36, 15, '2CH.36.15', 'Again and again the LORD, the God of their fathers, sent word to His people through His messengers because He had compassion on them and on His dwelling place.'),
('2CH', 36, 16, '2CH.36.16', 'But they mocked the messengers of God, despising His words and scoffing at His prophets, until the wrath of the LORD against His people was stirred up beyond remedy.'),
('2CH', 36, 17, '2CH.36.17', 'So He brought up against them the king of the Chaldeans, who put their young men to the sword in the sanctuary, sparing neither young men nor young women, neither elderly nor infirm. God gave them all into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar,'),
('2CH', 36, 18, '2CH.36.18', 'who carried off everything to Babylon—all the articles of the house of God, both large and small, and the treasures of the house of the LORD and of the king and his officials.'),
('2CH', 36, 19, '2CH.36.19', 'Then the Chaldeans set fire to the house of God and broke down the wall of Jerusalem. They burned down all the palaces and destroyed every article of value.'),
('2CH', 36, 20, '2CH.36.20', 'Those who escaped the sword were carried by Nebuchadnezzar into exile in Babylon, and they became servants to him and his sons until the kingdom of Persia came to power.'),
('2CH', 36, 21, '2CH.36.21', 'So the land enjoyed its Sabbath rest all the days of the desolation, until seventy years were completed, in fulfillment of the word of the LORD spoken through Jeremiah.'),
('2CH', 36, 22, '2CH.36.22', 'In the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, to fulfill the word of the LORD spoken through Jeremiah, the LORD stirred the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia to send a proclamation throughout his kingdom and to put it in writing as follows:'),
('2CH', 36, 23, '2CH.36.23', '“This is what Cyrus king of Persia says: ‘The LORD, the God of heaven, who has given me all the kingdoms of the earth, has appointed me to build a house for Him at Jerusalem in Judah. Whoever among you belongs to His people, may the LORD his God be with him, and may he go up.’”'),
('EZR', 1, 1, 'EZR.1.1', 'In the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, to fulfill the word of the LORD spoken through Jeremiah, the LORD stirred the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia to send a proclamation throughout his kingdom and to put it in writing as follows:'),
('EZR', 1, 2, 'EZR.1.2', '“This is what Cyrus king of Persia says: ‘The LORD, the God of heaven, who has given me all the kingdoms of the earth, has appointed me to build a house for Him at Jerusalem in Judah.'),
('EZR', 1, 3, 'EZR.1.3', 'Whoever among you belongs to His people, may his God be with him, and may he go to Jerusalem in Judah and build the house of the LORD, the God of Israel; He is the God who is in Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 1, 4, 'EZR.1.4', 'And let every survivor, wherever he lives, be assisted by the men of that region with silver, gold, goods, and livestock, along with a freewill offering for the house of God in Jerusalem.’”'),
('EZR', 1, 5, 'EZR.1.5', 'So the family heads of Judah and Benjamin, along with the priests and Levites—everyone whose spirit God had stirred—prepared to go up and rebuild the house of the LORD in Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 1, 6, 'EZR.1.6', 'And all their neighbors supported them with articles of silver and gold, with goods and livestock, and with valuables, in addition to all their freewill offerings.'),
('EZR', 1, 7, 'EZR.1.7', 'King Cyrus also brought out the articles belonging to the house of the LORD that Nebuchadnezzar had carried away from Jerusalem and placed in the temple of his gods.'),
('EZR', 1, 8, 'EZR.1.8', 'Cyrus king of Persia had them brought out by the hand of Mithredath the treasurer, who counted them out to Sheshbazzar the prince of Judah.'),
('EZR', 1, 9, 'EZR.1.9', 'This was the inventory: 30 gold dishes, 1,000 silver dishes, 29 silver utensils,'),
('EZR', 1, 10, 'EZR.1.10', '30 gold bowls, 410 matching silver bowls, and 1,000 other articles.'),
('EZR', 1, 11, 'EZR.1.11', 'In all, there were 5,400 gold and silver articles. Sheshbazzar brought all these along when the exiles went up from Babylon to Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 2, 1, 'EZR.2.1', 'Now these are the people of the province who came up from the captivity of the exiles carried away to Babylon by Nebuchadnezzar its king. They returned to Jerusalem and Judah, each to his own town,'),
('EZR', 2, 2, 'EZR.2.2', 'accompanied by Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Seraiah, Reelaiah, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispar, Bigvai, Rehum, and Baanah. This is the count of the men of Israel:'),
('EZR', 2, 3, 'EZR.2.3', 'the descendants of Parosh, 2,172;'),
('EZR', 2, 4, 'EZR.2.4', 'the descendants of Shephatiah, 372;'),
('EZR', 2, 5, 'EZR.2.5', 'the descendants of Arah, 775;'),
('EZR', 2, 6, 'EZR.2.6', 'the descendants of Pahath-moab (through the line of Jeshua and Joab), 2,812;'),
('EZR', 2, 7, 'EZR.2.7', 'the descendants of Elam, 1,254;'),
('EZR', 2, 8, 'EZR.2.8', 'the descendants of Zattu, 945;'),
('EZR', 2, 9, 'EZR.2.9', 'the descendants of Zaccai, 760;'),
('EZR', 2, 10, 'EZR.2.10', 'the descendants of Bani, 642;'),
('EZR', 2, 11, 'EZR.2.11', 'the descendants of Bebai, 623;'),
('EZR', 2, 12, 'EZR.2.12', 'the descendants of Azgad, 1,222;'),
('EZR', 2, 13, 'EZR.2.13', 'the descendants of Adonikam, 666;'),
('EZR', 2, 14, 'EZR.2.14', 'the descendants of Bigvai, 2,056;'),
('EZR', 2, 15, 'EZR.2.15', 'the descendants of Adin, 454;'),
('EZR', 2, 16, 'EZR.2.16', 'the descendants of Ater (through Hezekiah), 98;'),
('EZR', 2, 17, 'EZR.2.17', 'the descendants of Bezai, 323;'),
('EZR', 2, 18, 'EZR.2.18', 'the descendants of Jorah, 112;'),
('EZR', 2, 19, 'EZR.2.19', 'the descendants of Hashum, 223;'),
('EZR', 2, 20, 'EZR.2.20', 'the descendants of Gibbar, 95;'),
('EZR', 2, 21, 'EZR.2.21', 'the men of Bethlehem, 123;'),
('EZR', 2, 22, 'EZR.2.22', 'the men of Netophah, 56;'),
('EZR', 2, 23, 'EZR.2.23', 'the men of Anathoth, 128;'),
('EZR', 2, 24, 'EZR.2.24', 'the descendants of Azmaveth, 42;'),
('EZR', 2, 25, 'EZR.2.25', 'the men of Kiriath-jearim, Chephirah, and Beeroth, 743;'),
('EZR', 2, 26, 'EZR.2.26', 'the men of Ramah and Geba, 621;'),
('EZR', 2, 27, 'EZR.2.27', 'the men of Michmash, 122;'),
('EZR', 2, 28, 'EZR.2.28', 'the men of Bethel and Ai, 223;'),
('EZR', 2, 29, 'EZR.2.29', 'the descendants of Nebo, 52;'),
('EZR', 2, 30, 'EZR.2.30', 'the descendants of Magbish, 156;'),
('EZR', 2, 31, 'EZR.2.31', 'the descendants of the other Elam, 1,254;'),
('EZR', 2, 32, 'EZR.2.32', 'the descendants of Harim, 320;'),
('EZR', 2, 33, 'EZR.2.33', 'the men of Lod, Hadid, and Ono, 725;'),
('EZR', 2, 34, 'EZR.2.34', 'the men of Jericho, 345;'),
('EZR', 2, 35, 'EZR.2.35', 'and the descendants of Senaah, 3,630.'),
('EZR', 2, 36, 'EZR.2.36', 'The priests: The descendants of Jedaiah (through the house of Jeshua), 973;'),
('EZR', 2, 37, 'EZR.2.37', 'the descendants of Immer, 1,052;'),
('EZR', 2, 38, 'EZR.2.38', 'the descendants of Pashhur, 1,247;'),
('EZR', 2, 39, 'EZR.2.39', 'and the descendants of Harim, 1,017.'),
('EZR', 2, 40, 'EZR.2.40', 'The Levites: the descendants of Jeshua and Kadmiel (through the line of Hodaviah), 74.'),
('EZR', 2, 41, 'EZR.2.41', 'The singers: the descendants of Asaph, 128.'),
('EZR', 2, 42, 'EZR.2.42', 'The gatekeepers: the descendants of Shallum, the descendants of Ater, the descendants of Talmon, the descendants of Akkub, the descendants of Hatita, and the descendants of Shobai, 139 in all.'),
('EZR', 2, 43, 'EZR.2.43', 'The temple servants: the descendants of Ziha, the descendants of Hasupha, the descendants of Tabbaoth,'),
('EZR', 2, 44, 'EZR.2.44', 'the descendants of Keros, the descendants of Siaha, the descendants of Padon,'),
('EZR', 2, 45, 'EZR.2.45', 'the descendants of Lebanah, the descendants of Hagabah, the descendants of Akkub,'),
('EZR', 2, 46, 'EZR.2.46', 'the descendants of Hagab, the descendants of Shalmai, the descendants of Hanan,'),
('EZR', 2, 47, 'EZR.2.47', 'the descendants of Giddel, the descendants of Gahar, the descendants of Reaiah,'),
('EZR', 2, 48, 'EZR.2.48', 'the descendants of Rezin, the descendants of Nekoda, the descendants of Gazzam,'),
('EZR', 2, 49, 'EZR.2.49', 'the descendants of Uzza, the descendants of Paseah, the descendants of Besai,'),
('EZR', 2, 50, 'EZR.2.50', 'the descendants of Asnah, the descendants of Meunim, the descendants of Nephusim,'),
('EZR', 2, 51, 'EZR.2.51', 'the descendants of Bakbuk, the descendants of Hakupha, the descendants of Harhur,'),
('EZR', 2, 52, 'EZR.2.52', 'the descendants of Bazluth, the descendants of Mehida, the descendants of Harsha,'),
('EZR', 2, 53, 'EZR.2.53', 'the descendants of Barkos, the descendants of Sisera, the descendants of Temah,'),
('EZR', 2, 54, 'EZR.2.54', 'the descendants of Neziah, and the descendants of Hatipha.'),
('EZR', 2, 55, 'EZR.2.55', 'The descendants of the servants of Solomon: the descendants of Sotai, the descendants of Hassophereth, the descendants of Peruda,'),
('EZR', 2, 56, 'EZR.2.56', 'the descendants of Jaala, the descendants of Darkon, the descendants of Giddel,'),
('EZR', 2, 57, 'EZR.2.57', 'the descendants of Shephatiah, the descendants of Hattil, the descendants of Pochereth-hazzebaim, and the descendants of Ami.'),
('EZR', 2, 58, 'EZR.2.58', 'The temple servants and descendants of the servants of Solomon numbered 392 in all.'),
('EZR', 2, 59, 'EZR.2.59', 'The following came up from Tel-melah, Tel-harsha, Cherub, Addan, and Immer, but they could not prove that their families were descended from Israel:'),
('EZR', 2, 60, 'EZR.2.60', 'the descendants of Delaiah, the descendants of Tobiah, and the descendants of Nekoda, 652 in all.'),
('EZR', 2, 61, 'EZR.2.61', 'And from among the priests: the descendants of Hobaiah, the descendants of Hakkoz, and the descendants of Barzillai (who had married a daughter of Barzillai the Gileadite and was called by their name).'),
('EZR', 2, 62, 'EZR.2.62', 'These men searched for their family records, but they could not find them and so were excluded from the priesthood as unclean.'),
('EZR', 2, 63, 'EZR.2.63', 'The governor ordered them not to eat the most holy things until there was a priest to consult the Urim and Thummim.'),
('EZR', 2, 64, 'EZR.2.64', 'The whole assembly numbered 42,360,'),
('EZR', 2, 65, 'EZR.2.65', 'in addition to their 7,337 menservants and maidservants, as well as their 200 male and female singers.'),
('EZR', 2, 66, 'EZR.2.66', 'They had 736 horses, 245 mules,'),
('EZR', 2, 67, 'EZR.2.67', '435 camels, and 6,720 donkeys.'),
('EZR', 2, 68, 'EZR.2.68', 'When they arrived at the house of the LORD in Jerusalem, some of the heads of the families gave freewill offerings to rebuild the house of God on its original site.'),
('EZR', 2, 69, 'EZR.2.69', 'According to their ability, they gave to the treasury for this work 61,000 darics of gold, 5,000 minas of silver, and 100 priestly garments.'),
('EZR', 2, 70, 'EZR.2.70', 'So the priests, the Levites, the singers, the gatekeepers, and the temple servants, along with some of the people, settled in their own towns; and the rest of the Israelites settled in their towns.'),
('EZR', 3, 1, 'EZR.3.1', 'By the seventh month, the Israelites had settled in their towns, and the people assembled as one man in Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 3, 2, 'EZR.3.2', 'Then Jeshua son of Jozadak and his fellow priests, along with Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel and his associates, began to build the altar of the God of Israel to sacrifice burnt offerings on it, as it is written in the Law of Moses the man of God.'),
('EZR', 3, 3, 'EZR.3.3', 'They set up the altar on its foundation and sacrificed burnt offerings on it to the LORD—both the morning and evening burnt offerings—even though they feared the people of the land.'),
('EZR', 3, 4, 'EZR.3.4', 'They also celebrated the Feast of Tabernacles in accordance with what is written, and they offered burnt offerings daily based on the number prescribed for each day.'),
('EZR', 3, 5, 'EZR.3.5', 'After that, they presented the regular burnt offerings and those for New Moons and for all the appointed sacred feasts of the LORD, as well as all the freewill offerings brought to the LORD.'),
('EZR', 3, 6, 'EZR.3.6', 'On the first day of the seventh month, the Israelites began to offer burnt offerings to the LORD, although the foundation of the temple of the LORD had not been laid.'),
('EZR', 3, 7, 'EZR.3.7', 'They gave money to the masons and carpenters, and food and drink and oil to the people of Sidon and Tyre to bring cedar logs from Lebanon to Joppa by sea, as authorized by Cyrus king of Persia.'),
('EZR', 3, 8, 'EZR.3.8', 'In the second month of the second year after they had arrived at the house of God in Jerusalem, Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel, Jeshua son of Jozadak, and the rest of their associates including the priests, the Levites, and all who had returned to Jerusalem from the captivity, began the work. They appointed Levites twenty years of age or older to supervise the construction of the house of the LORD.'),
('EZR', 3, 9, 'EZR.3.9', 'So Jeshua and his sons and brothers, Kadmiel and his sons (descendants of Yehudah), and the sons of Henadad and their sons and brothers—all Levites—joined together to supervise those working on the house of God.'),
('EZR', 3, 10, 'EZR.3.10', 'When the builders had laid the foundation of the temple of the LORD, the priests in their apparel with trumpets, and the Levites (the sons of Asaph) with cymbals, took their positions to praise the LORD, as David king of Israel had prescribed.'),
('EZR', 3, 11, 'EZR.3.11', 'And they sang responsively with praise and thanksgiving to the LORD: “For He is good; for His loving devotion to Israel endures forever.” Then all the people gave a great shout of praise to the LORD, because the foundation of the house of the LORD had been laid.'),
('EZR', 3, 12, 'EZR.3.12', 'But many of the older priests, Levites, and family heads who had seen the first temple wept loudly when they saw the foundation of this temple. Still, many others shouted joyfully.'),
('EZR', 3, 13, 'EZR.3.13', 'The people could not distinguish the shouts of joy from the sound of weeping, because the people were making so much noise. And the sound was heard from afar.'),
('EZR', 4, 1, 'EZR.4.1', 'When the enemies of Judah and Benjamin heard that the exiles were building a temple for the LORD, the God of Israel,'),
('EZR', 4, 2, 'EZR.4.2', 'they approached Zerubbabel and the heads of the families, saying, “Let us build with you because, like you, we seek your God and have been sacrificing to Him since the time of King Esar-haddon of Assyria, who brought us here.”'),
('EZR', 4, 3, 'EZR.4.3', 'But Zerubbabel, Jeshua, and the other heads of the families of Israel replied, “You have no part with us in building a house for our God, since we alone must build it for the LORD, the God of Israel, as Cyrus king of Persia has commanded us.”'),
('EZR', 4, 4, 'EZR.4.4', 'Then the people of the land set out to discourage the people of Judah and make them afraid to build.'),
('EZR', 4, 5, 'EZR.4.5', 'They hired counselors against them to frustrate their plans throughout the reign of Cyrus king of Persia and down to the reign of Darius king of Persia.'),
('EZR', 4, 6, 'EZR.4.6', 'At the beginning of the reign of Xerxes, an accusation was lodged against the people of Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 4, 7, 'EZR.4.7', 'And in the days of Artaxerxes king of Persia, Bishlam, Mithredath, Tabeel, and the rest of his associates wrote a letter to Artaxerxes. It was written in Aramaic and then translated.'),
('EZR', 4, 8, 'EZR.4.8', 'Rehum the commander and Shimshai the scribe wrote the letter against Jerusalem to King Artaxerxes as follows:'),
('EZR', 4, 9, 'EZR.4.9', 'From Rehum the commander, Shimshai the scribe, and the rest of their associates—the judges and officials over Tripolis, Persia, Erech and Babylon, the Elamites of Susa,'),
('EZR', 4, 10, 'EZR.4.10', 'and the rest of the peoples whom the great and honorable Ashurbanipal deported and settled in the cities of Samaria and elsewhere west of the Euphrates.'),
('EZR', 4, 11, 'EZR.4.11', '(This is the text of the letter they sent to him.) To King Artaxerxes, From your servants, the men west of the Euphrates:'),
('EZR', 4, 12, 'EZR.4.12', 'Let it be known to the king that the Jews who came from you to us have returned to Jerusalem and are rebuilding that rebellious and wicked city. They are restoring its walls and repairing its foundations.'),
('EZR', 4, 13, 'EZR.4.13', 'Let it now be known to the king that if that city is rebuilt and its walls are restored, they will not pay tribute, duty, or toll, and the royal treasury will suffer.'),
('EZR', 4, 14, 'EZR.4.14', 'Now because we are in the service of the palace and it is not fitting for us to allow the king to be dishonored, we have sent to inform the king'),
('EZR', 4, 15, 'EZR.4.15', 'that a search should be made of the record books of your fathers. In these books you will discover and verify that the city is a rebellious city, harmful to kings and provinces, inciting sedition from ancient times. That is why this city was destroyed.'),
('EZR', 4, 16, 'EZR.4.16', 'We advise the king that if this city is rebuilt and its walls are restored, you will have no dominion west of the Euphrates.'),
('EZR', 4, 17, 'EZR.4.17', 'Then the king sent this reply: To Rehum the commander, Shimshai the scribe, and the rest of your associates living in Samaria and elsewhere in the region west of the Euphrates: Greetings.'),
('EZR', 4, 18, 'EZR.4.18', 'The letter you sent us has been translated and read in my presence.'),
('EZR', 4, 19, 'EZR.4.19', 'I issued a decree, and a search was conducted. It was discovered that this city has revolted against kings from ancient times, engaging in rebellion and sedition.'),
('EZR', 4, 20, 'EZR.4.20', 'And mighty kings have ruled over Jerusalem and exercised authority over the whole region west of the Euphrates; and tribute, duty, and toll were paid to them.'),
('EZR', 4, 21, 'EZR.4.21', 'Now, therefore, issue an order for these men to stop, so that this city will not be rebuilt until I so order.'),
('EZR', 4, 22, 'EZR.4.22', 'See that you do not neglect this matter. Why allow this threat to increase and the royal interests to suffer?'),
('EZR', 4, 23, 'EZR.4.23', 'When the text of the letter from King Artaxerxes was read to Rehum, Shimshai the scribe, and their associates, they went immediately to the Jews in Jerusalem and forcibly stopped them.'),
('EZR', 4, 24, 'EZR.4.24', 'Thus the construction of the house of God in Jerusalem ceased, and it remained at a standstill until the second year of the reign of Darius king of Persia.'),
('EZR', 5, 1, 'EZR.5.1', 'Later, the prophets Haggai and Zechariah son of Iddo prophesied to the Jews in Judah and Jerusalem in the name of the God of Israel, who was over them.'),
('EZR', 5, 2, 'EZR.5.2', 'Then Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel and Jeshua son of Jozadak rose up and began to rebuild the house of God in Jerusalem. And the prophets of God were with them, helping them.'),
('EZR', 5, 3, 'EZR.5.3', 'At that time Tattenai the governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and their associates went to the Jews and asked, “Who authorized you to rebuild this temple and restore this structure?”'),
('EZR', 5, 4, 'EZR.5.4', 'They also asked, “What are the names of the men who are constructing this building?”'),
('EZR', 5, 5, 'EZR.5.5', 'But the eye of their God was on the elders of the Jews, so that they were not stopped until a report was sent to Darius and written instructions about this matter were returned.'),
('EZR', 5, 6, 'EZR.5.6', 'This is the text of the letter that Tattenai the governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and their associates, the officials in the region, sent to King Darius.'),
('EZR', 5, 7, 'EZR.5.7', 'The report they sent him read as follows: To King Darius: All peace.'),
('EZR', 5, 8, 'EZR.5.8', 'Let it be known to the king that we went into the province of Judah, to the house of the great God. The people are rebuilding it with large stones and placing timbers in the walls. This work is being carried out diligently and is prospering in their hands.'),
('EZR', 5, 9, 'EZR.5.9', 'So we questioned the elders and asked, “Who authorized you to rebuild this temple and restore this structure?”'),
('EZR', 5, 10, 'EZR.5.10', 'We also asked for their names, so that we could write down the names of their leaders for your information.'),
('EZR', 5, 11, 'EZR.5.11', 'And this is the answer they returned: “We are servants of the God of heaven and earth, and we are rebuilding the temple that was built many years ago, which a great king of Israel built and completed.'),
('EZR', 5, 12, 'EZR.5.12', 'But since our fathers angered the God of heaven, He delivered them into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, the Chaldean who destroyed this temple and carried away the people to Babylon.'),
('EZR', 5, 13, 'EZR.5.13', 'In the first year of his reign, however, Cyrus king of Babylon issued a decree to rebuild this house of God.'),
('EZR', 5, 14, 'EZR.5.14', 'He also removed from the temple of Babylon the gold and silver articles belonging to the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar had taken and carried there from the temple in Jerusalem. King Cyrus gave these articles to a man named Sheshbazzar, whom he appointed governor'),
('EZR', 5, 15, 'EZR.5.15', 'and instructed, ‘Take these articles, put them in the temple in Jerusalem, and let the house of God be rebuilt on its original site.’'),
('EZR', 5, 16, 'EZR.5.16', 'So this Sheshbazzar came and laid the foundation of the house of God in Jerusalem, and from that time until now it has been under construction, but it has not yet been completed.”'),
('EZR', 5, 17, 'EZR.5.17', 'Now, therefore, if it pleases the king, let a search be made of the royal archives in Babylon to see if King Cyrus did indeed issue a decree to rebuild the house of God in Jerusalem. Then let the king send us his decision in this matter.'),
('EZR', 6, 1, 'EZR.6.1', 'Thus King Darius ordered a search of the archives stored in the treasury of Babylon.'),
('EZR', 6, 2, 'EZR.6.2', 'And a scroll was found in the fortress of Ecbatana, in the province of Media, with the following written on it: Memorandum:'),
('EZR', 6, 3, 'EZR.6.3', 'In the first year of King Cyrus, he issued a decree concerning the house of God in Jerusalem: Let the house be rebuilt as a place for offering sacrifices, and let its foundations be firmly laid. It is to be sixty cubits high and sixty cubits wide,'),
('EZR', 6, 4, 'EZR.6.4', 'with three layers of cut stones and one of timbers. The costs are to be paid from the royal treasury.'),
('EZR', 6, 5, 'EZR.6.5', 'Furthermore, the gold and silver articles of the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar took from the temple in Jerusalem and carried to Babylon, must also be returned to the temple in Jerusalem and deposited in the house of God.'),
('EZR', 6, 6, 'EZR.6.6', 'Therefore Darius decreed: To Tattenai governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and your associates and officials in the region: You must stay away from that place!'),
('EZR', 6, 7, 'EZR.6.7', 'Leave this work on the house of God alone. Let the governor and elders of the Jews rebuild this house of God on its original site.'),
('EZR', 6, 8, 'EZR.6.8', 'I hereby decree what you must do for these elders of the Jews who are rebuilding this house of God: The cost is to be paid in full to these men from the royal treasury out of the taxes of the provinces west of the Euphrates, so that the work will not be hindered.'),
('EZR', 6, 9, 'EZR.6.9', 'Whatever is needed—young bulls, rams, and lambs for burnt offerings to the God of heaven, as well as wheat, salt, wine, and oil, as requested by the priests in Jerusalem—must be given to them daily without fail.'),
('EZR', 6, 10, 'EZR.6.10', 'Then they will be able to offer sacrifices of a sweet aroma to the God of heaven and to pray for the lives of the king and his sons.'),
('EZR', 6, 11, 'EZR.6.11', 'I also decree that if any man interferes with this directive, a beam is to be torn from his house and raised up, and he is to be impaled on it. And his own house shall be made a pile of rubble for this offense.'),
('EZR', 6, 12, 'EZR.6.12', 'May God, who has caused His Name to dwell there, overthrow any king or people who lifts a hand to alter this decree or to destroy this house of God in Jerusalem. I, Darius, have issued the decree. Let it be carried out with diligence.'),
('EZR', 6, 13, 'EZR.6.13', 'In response, Tattenai the governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and their associates diligently carried out what King Darius had decreed.'),
('EZR', 6, 14, 'EZR.6.14', 'So the Jewish elders built and prospered through the prophesying of Haggai the prophet and Zechariah son of Iddo. They finished building according to the command of the God of Israel and the decrees of Cyrus, Darius, and Artaxerxes, kings of Persia.'),
('EZR', 6, 15, 'EZR.6.15', 'And this temple was completed on the third day of the month of Adar, in the sixth year of the reign of King Darius.'),
('EZR', 6, 16, 'EZR.6.16', 'Then the people of Israel—the priests, the Levites, and the rest of the exiles—celebrated the dedication of the house of God with joy.'),
('EZR', 6, 17, 'EZR.6.17', 'For the dedication of the house of God they offered a hundred bulls, two hundred rams, four hundred lambs, and a sin offering for all Israel of twelve male goats, one for each tribe of Israel.'),
('EZR', 6, 18, 'EZR.6.18', 'They also appointed the priests by their divisions and the Levites by their groups to the service of God in Jerusalem, according to what is written in the Book of Moses.'),
('EZR', 6, 19, 'EZR.6.19', 'On the fourteenth day of the first month, the exiles kept the Passover.'),
('EZR', 6, 20, 'EZR.6.20', 'All the priests and Levites had purified themselves and were ceremonially clean. And the Levites slaughtered the Passover lamb for all the exiles, for their priestly brothers, and for themselves.'),
('EZR', 6, 21, 'EZR.6.21', 'The Israelites who had returned from exile ate it, together with all who had separated themselves from the uncleanness of the peoples of the land to seek the LORD, the God of Israel.'),
('EZR', 6, 22, 'EZR.6.22', 'For seven days they kept the Feast of Unleavened Bread with joy, because the LORD had made them joyful and turned the heart of the king of Assyria toward them to strengthen their hands in the work on the house of the God of Israel.'),
('EZR', 7, 1, 'EZR.7.1', 'Many years later, during the reign of Artaxerxes king of Persia, Ezra son of Seraiah, the son of Azariah, the son of Hilkiah,'),
('EZR', 7, 2, 'EZR.7.2', 'the son of Shallum, the son of Zadok, the son of Ahitub,'),
('EZR', 7, 3, 'EZR.7.3', 'the son of Amariah, the son of Azariah, the son of Meraioth,'),
('EZR', 7, 4, 'EZR.7.4', 'the son of Zerahiah, the son of Uzzi, the son of Bukki,'),
('EZR', 7, 5, 'EZR.7.5', 'the son of Abishua, the son of Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the chief priest—'),
('EZR', 7, 6, 'EZR.7.6', 'this Ezra came up from Babylon. He was a scribe skilled in the Law of Moses, which the LORD, the God of Israel, had given. The king had granted Ezra all his requests, for the hand of the LORD his God was upon him.'),
('EZR', 7, 7, 'EZR.7.7', 'So in the seventh year of King Artaxerxes, he went up to Jerusalem with some of the Israelites, including priests, Levites, singers, gatekeepers, and temple servants.'),
('EZR', 7, 8, 'EZR.7.8', 'Ezra arrived in Jerusalem in the fifth month of the seventh year of the king.'),
('EZR', 7, 9, 'EZR.7.9', 'He had begun the journey from Babylon on the first day of the first month, and he arrived in Jerusalem on the first day of the fifth month, for the gracious hand of his God was upon him.'),
('EZR', 7, 10, 'EZR.7.10', 'For Ezra had set his heart to study the Law of the LORD, to practice it, and to teach its statutes and ordinances in Israel.'),
('EZR', 7, 11, 'EZR.7.11', 'This is the text of the letter King Artaxerxes had given to Ezra the priest and scribe, an expert in the commandments and statutes of the LORD to Israel:'),
('EZR', 7, 12, 'EZR.7.12', 'Artaxerxes, king of kings. To Ezra the priest, the scribe of the Law of the God of heaven: Greetings.'),
('EZR', 7, 13, 'EZR.7.13', 'I hereby decree that any volunteers among the Israelites in my kingdom, including the priests and Levites, may go up with you to Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 7, 14, 'EZR.7.14', 'You are sent by the king and his seven counselors to evaluate Judah and Jerusalem according to the Law of your God, which is in your hand.'),
('EZR', 7, 15, 'EZR.7.15', 'Moreover, you are to take with you the silver and gold that the king and his counselors have freely offered to the God of Israel, whose dwelling is in Jerusalem,'),
('EZR', 7, 16, 'EZR.7.16', 'together with all the silver and gold you may find in all the province of Babylon, as well as the freewill offerings of the people and priests to the house of their God in Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 7, 17, 'EZR.7.17', 'With this money, therefore, you are to buy as many bulls, rams, and lambs as needed, together with their grain offerings and drink offerings, and offer them on the altar at the house of your God in Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 7, 18, 'EZR.7.18', 'You and your brothers may do whatever seems best with the rest of the silver and gold, according to the will of your God.'),
('EZR', 7, 19, 'EZR.7.19', 'You must deliver to the God of Jerusalem all the articles given to you for the service of the house of your God.'),
('EZR', 7, 20, 'EZR.7.20', 'And if anything else is needed for the house of your God that you may have occasion to supply, you may pay for it from the royal treasury.'),
('EZR', 7, 21, 'EZR.7.21', 'I, King Artaxerxes, decree to all the treasurers west of the Euphrates: Whatever Ezra the priest, the scribe of the Law of the God of heaven, may require of you, it must be provided promptly,'),
('EZR', 7, 22, 'EZR.7.22', 'up to a hundred talents of silver, a hundred cors of wheat, a hundred baths of wine, a hundred baths of olive oil, and salt without limit.'),
('EZR', 7, 23, 'EZR.7.23', 'Whatever is commanded by the God of heaven must be done diligently for His house. For why should wrath fall on the realm of the king and his sons?'),
('EZR', 7, 24, 'EZR.7.24', 'And be advised that you have no authority to impose tribute, duty, or toll on any of the priests, Levites, singers, doorkeepers, temple servants, or other servants of this house of God.'),
('EZR', 7, 25, 'EZR.7.25', 'And you, Ezra, according to the wisdom of your God, which you possess, are to appoint magistrates and judges to judge all the people west of the Euphrates—all who know the laws of your God. And you are to teach these laws to anyone who does not know them.'),
('EZR', 7, 26, 'EZR.7.26', 'If anyone does not keep the law of your God and the law of the king, let a strict judgment be executed against him, whether death, banishment, confiscation of property, or imprisonment.'),
('EZR', 7, 27, 'EZR.7.27', 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of our fathers, who has put into the heart of the king to so honor the house of the LORD in Jerusalem,'),
('EZR', 7, 28, 'EZR.7.28', 'and who has shown me favor before the king, his counselors, and all his powerful officials. And because the hand of the LORD my God was upon me, I took courage and gathered the leaders of Israel to return with me.'),
('EZR', 8, 1, 'EZR.8.1', 'These are the family heads and genealogical records of those who returned with me from Babylon during the reign of King Artaxerxes:'),
('EZR', 8, 2, 'EZR.8.2', 'from the descendants of Phinehas, Gershom; from the descendants of Ithamar, Daniel; from the descendants of David, Hattush'),
('EZR', 8, 3, 'EZR.8.3', 'of the descendants of Shecaniah; from the descendants of Parosh, Zechariah, and with him were registered 150 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 4, 'EZR.8.4', 'from the descendants of Pahath-Moab, Eliehoenai son of Zerahiah, and with him 200 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 5, 'EZR.8.5', 'from the descendants of Zattu, Shecaniah son of Jahaziel, and with him 300 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 6, 'EZR.8.6', 'from the descendants of Adin, Ebed son of Jonathan, and with him 50 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 7, 'EZR.8.7', 'from the descendants of Elam, Jeshaiah son of Athaliah, and with him 70 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 8, 'EZR.8.8', 'from the descendants of Shephatiah, Zebadiah son of Michael, and with him 80 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 9, 'EZR.8.9', 'from the descendants of Joab, Obadiah son of Jehiel, and with him 218 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 10, 'EZR.8.10', 'from the descendants of Bani, Shelomith son of Josiphiah, and with him 160 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 11, 'EZR.8.11', 'from the descendants of Bebai, Zechariah son of Bebai, and with him 28 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 12, 'EZR.8.12', 'from the descendants of Azgad, Johanan son of Hakkatan, and with him 110 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 13, 'EZR.8.13', 'from the later descendants of Adonikam, these were their names: Eliphelet, Jeiel, and Shemaiah, and with them 60 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 14, 'EZR.8.14', 'and from the descendants of Bigvai, both Uthai and Zaccur, and with them 70 men.'),
('EZR', 8, 15, 'EZR.8.15', 'Now I assembled these exiles at the canal that flows to Ahava, and we camped there three days. And when I searched among the people and priests, I found no Levites there.'),
('EZR', 8, 16, 'EZR.8.16', 'Then I summoned the leaders: Eliezer, Ariel, Shemaiah, Elnathan, Jarib, Elnathan, Nathan, Zechariah, and Meshullam, as well as the teachers Joiarib and Elnathan.'),
('EZR', 8, 17, 'EZR.8.17', 'And I sent them to Iddo, the leader at Casiphia, with a message for him and his kinsmen, the temple servants at Casiphia, that they should bring to us ministers for the house of our God.'),
('EZR', 8, 18, 'EZR.8.18', 'And since the gracious hand of our God was upon us, they brought us Sherebiah—a man of insight from the descendants of Mahli son of Levi, the son of Israel—along with his sons and brothers, 18 men;'),
('EZR', 8, 19, 'EZR.8.19', 'also Hashabiah, together with Jeshaiah, from the descendants of Merari, and his brothers and their sons, 20 men.'),
('EZR', 8, 20, 'EZR.8.20', 'They also brought 220 of the temple servants, all designated by name. David and the officials had appointed them to assist the Levites.'),
('EZR', 8, 21, 'EZR.8.21', 'And there by the Ahava Canal I proclaimed a fast, so that we might humble ourselves before our God and ask Him for a safe journey for us and our children, with all our possessions.'),
('EZR', 8, 22, 'EZR.8.22', 'For I was ashamed to ask the king for an escort of soldiers and horsemen to protect us from our enemies on the road, since we had told him, “The hand of our God is gracious to all who seek Him, but His great anger is against all who forsake Him.”'),
('EZR', 8, 23, 'EZR.8.23', 'So we fasted and petitioned our God about this, and He granted our request.'),
('EZR', 8, 24, 'EZR.8.24', 'Then I set apart twelve of the leading priests, together with Sherebiah, Hashabiah, and ten of their brothers,'),
('EZR', 8, 25, 'EZR.8.25', 'and I weighed out to them the contribution of silver and gold and the articles that the king, his counselors, his leaders, and all the Israelites there had offered for the house of our God.'),
('EZR', 8, 26, 'EZR.8.26', 'I weighed out into their hands 650 talents of silver, articles of silver weighing 100 talents, 100 talents of gold,'),
('EZR', 8, 27, 'EZR.8.27', '20 gold bowls valued at 1,000 darics, and two articles of fine polished bronze, as precious as gold.'),
('EZR', 8, 28, 'EZR.8.28', 'Then I told them, “You are holy to the LORD, and these articles are holy. The silver and gold are a freewill offering to the LORD, the God of your fathers.'),
('EZR', 8, 29, 'EZR.8.29', 'Guard them carefully until you weigh them out in the chambers of the house of the LORD in Jerusalem before the leading priests, Levites, and heads of the Israelite families.”'),
('EZR', 8, 30, 'EZR.8.30', 'So the priests and Levites took charge of the silver and gold and sacred articles that had been weighed out to be taken to the house of our God in Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 8, 31, 'EZR.8.31', 'On the twelfth day of the first month we set out from the Ahava Canal to go to Jerusalem, and the hand of our God was upon us to protect us from the hands of the enemies and bandits along the way.'),
('EZR', 8, 32, 'EZR.8.32', 'So we arrived at Jerusalem and rested there for three days.'),
('EZR', 8, 33, 'EZR.8.33', 'On the fourth day, in the house of our God, we weighed out the silver and gold and sacred articles into the hand of Meremoth son of Uriah, the priest. Eleazar son of Phinehas was with him, along with the Levites Jozabad son of Jeshua and Noadiah son of Binnui.'),
('EZR', 8, 34, 'EZR.8.34', 'Everything was verified by number and weight, and the total weight was recorded at that time.'),
('EZR', 8, 35, 'EZR.8.35', 'Then the exiles who had returned from captivity sacrificed burnt offerings to the God of Israel: 12 bulls for all Israel, 96 rams, 77 lambs, and a sin offering of 12 male goats. All this was a burnt offering to the LORD.'),
('EZR', 8, 36, 'EZR.8.36', 'They also delivered the king’s edicts to the royal satraps and governors of the region west of the Euphrates, who proceeded to assist the people and the house of God.'),
('EZR', 9, 1, 'EZR.9.1', 'After these things had been accomplished, the leaders approached me and said, “The people of Israel, including the priests and Levites, have not kept themselves separate from the surrounding peoples whose abominations are like those of the Canaanites, Hittites, Perizzites, Jebusites, Ammonites, Moabites, Egyptians, and Amorites.'),
('EZR', 9, 2, 'EZR.9.2', 'Indeed, the Israelites have taken some of their daughters as wives for themselves and their sons, so that the holy seed has been mixed with the people of the land. And the leaders and officials have taken the lead in this unfaithfulness!”'),
('EZR', 9, 3, 'EZR.9.3', 'When I heard this report, I tore my tunic and cloak, pulled out some hair from my head and beard, and sat down in horror.'),
('EZR', 9, 4, 'EZR.9.4', 'Then everyone who trembled at the words of the God of Israel gathered around me because of the unfaithfulness of the exiles, while I sat there in horror until the evening offering.'),
('EZR', 9, 5, 'EZR.9.5', 'At the evening offering, I got up from my humiliation with my tunic and cloak torn, and I fell on my knees, spread out my hands to the LORD my God,'),
('EZR', 9, 6, 'EZR.9.6', 'and said: “O my God, I am ashamed and embarrassed to lift up my face to You, my God, because our iniquities are higher than our heads, and our guilt has reached the heavens.'),
('EZR', 9, 7, 'EZR.9.7', 'From the days of our fathers to this day, our guilt has been great. Because of our iniquities, we and our kings and priests have been delivered into the hands of the kings of the earth and subjected to the sword and to captivity, to pillage and humiliation, as we are this day.'),
('EZR', 9, 8, 'EZR.9.8', 'But now, for a brief moment, grace has come from the LORD our God to preserve for us a remnant and to give us a stake in His holy place. Even in our bondage, our God has given us new life and light to our eyes.'),
('EZR', 9, 9, 'EZR.9.9', 'Though we are slaves, our God has not forsaken us in our bondage, but He has extended to us grace in the sight of the kings of Persia, giving us new life to rebuild the house of our God and repair its ruins, and giving us a wall of protection in Judah and Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 9, 10, 'EZR.9.10', 'And now, our God, what can we say after this? For we have forsaken the commandments'),
('EZR', 9, 11, 'EZR.9.11', 'that You gave through Your servants the prophets, saying: ‘The land that you are entering to possess is a land polluted by the impurity of its peoples and the abominations with which they have filled it from end to end.'),
('EZR', 9, 12, 'EZR.9.12', 'Now, therefore, do not give your daughters in marriage to their sons or take their daughters for your sons. Never seek their peace or prosperity, so that you may be strong and may eat the good things of the land, leaving it as an inheritance to your sons forever.’'),
('EZR', 9, 13, 'EZR.9.13', 'After all that has come upon us because of our evil deeds and our great guilt (though You, our God, have punished us less than our iniquities deserve and have given us such a remnant as this),'),
('EZR', 9, 14, 'EZR.9.14', 'shall we again break Your commandments and intermarry with the peoples who commit these abominations? Would You not become so angry with us as to wipe us out, leaving no remnant or survivor?'),
('EZR', 9, 15, 'EZR.9.15', 'O LORD, God of Israel, You are righteous! For we remain this day as a remnant. Here we are before You in our guilt, though because of it no one can stand before You.”'),
('EZR', 10, 1, 'EZR.10.1', 'While Ezra prayed and made this confession, weeping and falling facedown before the house of God, a very large assembly of Israelites—men, women, and children—gathered around him, and the people wept bitterly as well.'),
('EZR', 10, 2, 'EZR.10.2', 'Then Shecaniah son of Jehiel, an Elamite, said to Ezra: “We have been unfaithful to our God by marrying foreign women from the people of the land, yet in spite of this, there is hope for Israel.'),
('EZR', 10, 3, 'EZR.10.3', 'So now let us make a covenant before our God to send away all the foreign wives and their children, according to the counsel of my lord and of those who tremble at the command of our God. Let it be done according to the Law.'),
('EZR', 10, 4, 'EZR.10.4', 'Get up, for this matter is your responsibility, and we will support you. Be strong and take action!”'),
('EZR', 10, 5, 'EZR.10.5', 'So Ezra got up and made the leading priests, Levites, and all Israel take an oath to do what had been said. And they took the oath.'),
('EZR', 10, 6, 'EZR.10.6', 'Then Ezra withdrew from before the house of God and walked to the chamber of Jehohanan son of Eliashib. And while he stayed there, he ate no food and drank no water, because he was mourning over the unfaithfulness of the exiles.'),
('EZR', 10, 7, 'EZR.10.7', 'And a proclamation was issued throughout Judah and Jerusalem that all the exiles should gather at Jerusalem.'),
('EZR', 10, 8, 'EZR.10.8', 'Whoever failed to appear within three days would forfeit all his property, according to the counsel of the leaders and elders, and would himself be expelled from the assembly of the exiles.'),
('EZR', 10, 9, 'EZR.10.9', 'So within the three days, all the men of Judah and Benjamin assembled in Jerusalem, and on the twentieth day of the ninth month, all the people sat in the square at the house of God, trembling regarding this matter and because of the heavy rain.'),
('EZR', 10, 10, 'EZR.10.10', 'Then Ezra the priest stood up and said to them, “You have been unfaithful by marrying foreign women, adding to the guilt of Israel.'),
('EZR', 10, 11, 'EZR.10.11', 'Now, therefore, make a confession to the LORD, the God of your fathers, and do His will. Separate yourselves from the people of the land and from your foreign wives.”'),
('EZR', 10, 12, 'EZR.10.12', 'And the whole assembly responded in a loud voice: “Truly we must do as you say!'),
('EZR', 10, 13, 'EZR.10.13', 'But there are many people here, and it is the rainy season. We are not able to stay out in the open. Nor is this the work of one or two days, for we have transgressed greatly in this matter.'),
('EZR', 10, 14, 'EZR.10.14', 'Let our leaders represent the whole assembly. Then let everyone in our towns who has married a foreign woman come at an appointed time, together with the elders and judges of each town, until the fierce anger of our God in this matter is turned away from us.”'),
('EZR', 10, 15, 'EZR.10.15', '(Only Jonathan son of Asahel and Jahzeiah son of Tikvah, supported by Meshullam and Shabbethai the Levite, opposed this plan.)'),
('EZR', 10, 16, 'EZR.10.16', 'So the exiles did as proposed. Ezra the priest selected men who were family heads, each of them identified by name, to represent their families. On the first day of the tenth month they launched the investigation,'),
('EZR', 10, 17, 'EZR.10.17', 'and by the first day of the first month they had dealt with all the men who had married foreign women.'),
('EZR', 10, 18, 'EZR.10.18', 'Among the descendants of the priests who had married foreign women were found these descendants of Jeshua son of Jozadak and his brothers: Maaseiah, Eliezer, Jarib, and Gedaliah.'),
('EZR', 10, 19, 'EZR.10.19', 'They pledged to send their wives away, and for their guilt they presented a ram from the flock as a guilt offering.'),
('EZR', 10, 20, 'EZR.10.20', 'From the descendants of Immer: Hanani and Zebadiah.'),
('EZR', 10, 21, 'EZR.10.21', 'From the descendants of Harim: Maaseiah, Elijah, Shemaiah, Jehiel, and Uzziah.'),
('EZR', 10, 22, 'EZR.10.22', 'From the descendants of Pashhur: Elioenai, Maaseiah, Ishmael, Nethanel, Jozabad, and Elasah.'),
('EZR', 10, 23, 'EZR.10.23', 'Among the Levites: Jozabad, Shimei, Kelaiah (that is, Kelita), Pethahiah, Judah, and Eliezer.'),
('EZR', 10, 24, 'EZR.10.24', 'From the singers: Eliashib. From the gatekeepers: Shallum, Telem, and Uri.'),
('EZR', 10, 25, 'EZR.10.25', 'And among the other Israelites, from the descendants of Parosh: Ramiah, Izziah, Malchijah, Mijamin, Eleazar, Malchijah, and Benaiah.'),
('EZR', 10, 26, 'EZR.10.26', 'From the descendants of Elam: Mattaniah, Zechariah, Jehiel, Abdi, Jeremoth, and Elijah.'),
('EZR', 10, 27, 'EZR.10.27', 'From the descendants of Zattu: Elioenai, Eliashib, Mattaniah, Jeremoth, Zabad, and Aziza.'),
('EZR', 10, 28, 'EZR.10.28', 'From the descendants of Bebai: Jehohanan, Hananiah, Zabbai, and Athlai.'),
('EZR', 10, 29, 'EZR.10.29', 'From the descendants of Bani: Meshullam, Malluch, Adaiah, Jashub, Sheal, and Jeremoth.'),
('EZR', 10, 30, 'EZR.10.30', 'From the descendants of Pahath-moab: Adna, Chelal, Benaiah, Maaseiah, Mattaniah, Bezalel, Binnui, and Manasseh.'),
('EZR', 10, 31, 'EZR.10.31', 'From the descendants of Harim: Eliezer, Isshijah, Malchijah, Shemaiah, Shimeon,'),
('EZR', 10, 32, 'EZR.10.32', 'Benjamin, Malluch, and Shemariah.'),
('EZR', 10, 33, 'EZR.10.33', 'From the descendants of Hashum: Mattenai, Mattattah, Zabad, Eliphelet, Jeremai, Manasseh, and Shimei.'),
('EZR', 10, 34, 'EZR.10.34', 'From the descendants of Bani: Maadai, Amram, Uel,'),
('EZR', 10, 35, 'EZR.10.35', 'Benaiah, Bedeiah, Cheluhi,'),
('EZR', 10, 36, 'EZR.10.36', 'Vaniah, Meremoth, Eliashib,'),
('EZR', 10, 37, 'EZR.10.37', 'Mattaniah, Mattenai, and Jaasu.'),
('EZR', 10, 38, 'EZR.10.38', 'From the descendants of Binnui: Shimei,'),
('EZR', 10, 39, 'EZR.10.39', 'Shelemiah, Nathan, Adaiah,'),
('EZR', 10, 40, 'EZR.10.40', 'Machnadebai, Shashai, Sharai,'),
('EZR', 10, 41, 'EZR.10.41', 'Azarel, Shelemiah, Shemariah,'),
('EZR', 10, 42, 'EZR.10.42', 'Shallum, Amariah, and Joseph.'),
('EZR', 10, 43, 'EZR.10.43', 'And from the descendants of Nebo: Jeiel, Mattithiah, Zabad, Zebina, Jaddai, Joel, and Benaiah.'),
('EZR', 10, 44, 'EZR.10.44', 'All these men had married foreign women, and some of them had children by these wives.'),
('NEH', 1, 1, 'NEH.1.1', 'These are the words of Nehemiah son of Hacaliah: In the month of Chislev, in the twentieth year, while I was in the citadel of Susa,'),
('NEH', 1, 2, 'NEH.1.2', 'Hanani, one of my brothers, arrived with men from Judah. So I questioned them about the remnant of the Jews who had survived the exile, and also about Jerusalem.'),
('NEH', 1, 3, 'NEH.1.3', 'And they told me, “The remnant who survived the exile are there in the province, in great trouble and disgrace. The wall of Jerusalem is broken down, and its gates have been burned with fire.”'),
('NEH', 1, 4, 'NEH.1.4', 'When I heard these words, I sat down and wept. I mourned for days, fasting and praying before the God of heaven.'),
('NEH', 1, 5, 'NEH.1.5', 'Then I said: “O LORD, God of heaven, the great and awesome God who keeps His covenant of loving devotion with those who love Him and keep His commandments,'),
('NEH', 1, 6, 'NEH.1.6', 'let Your eyes be open and Your ears attentive to hear the prayer that I, Your servant, now pray before You day and night for Your servants, the Israelites. I confess the sins that we Israelites have committed against You. Both I and my father’s house have sinned.'),
('NEH', 1, 7, 'NEH.1.7', 'We have behaved corruptly against You and have not kept the commandments, statutes, and ordinances that You gave Your servant Moses.'),
('NEH', 1, 8, 'NEH.1.8', 'Remember, I pray, the word that You commanded Your servant Moses when You said, ‘If you are unfaithful, I will scatter you among the nations,'),
('NEH', 1, 9, 'NEH.1.9', 'but if you return to Me and keep and practice My commandments, then even if your exiles have been banished to the farthest horizon, I will gather them from there and bring them to the place I have chosen as a dwelling for My Name.’'),
('NEH', 1, 10, 'NEH.1.10', 'They are Your servants and Your people. You redeemed them by Your great power and mighty hand.'),
('NEH', 1, 11, 'NEH.1.11', 'O Lord, may Your ear be attentive to my prayer and to the prayers of Your servants who delight to revere Your name. Give Your servant success this day, I pray, and grant him mercy in the sight of this man.” (At that time I was the cupbearer to the king.)'),
('NEH', 2, 1, 'NEH.2.1', 'Now in the month of Nisan, in the twentieth year of King Artaxerxes, when wine was set before him, I took the wine and gave it to the king. I had never been sad in his presence,'),
('NEH', 2, 2, 'NEH.2.2', 'so the king said to me, “Why is your face sad, though you are not ill? This could only be sadness of the heart.” I was overwhelmed with fear'),
('NEH', 2, 3, 'NEH.2.3', 'and replied to the king, “May the king live forever! Why should I not be sad when the city where my fathers are buried lies in ruins, and its gates have been destroyed by fire?”'),
('NEH', 2, 4, 'NEH.2.4', '“What is your request?” replied the king. So I prayed to the God of heaven'),
('NEH', 2, 5, 'NEH.2.5', 'and answered the king, “If it pleases the king, and if your servant has found favor in your sight, I ask that you send me to Judah, to the city where my fathers are buried, so that I may rebuild it.”'),
('NEH', 2, 6, 'NEH.2.6', 'Then the king, with the queen seated beside him, asked me, “How long will your journey take, and when will you return?” So it pleased the king to send me, and I set a time.'),
('NEH', 2, 7, 'NEH.2.7', 'I also said to him, “If it pleases the king, may letters be given to me for the governors west of the Euphrates, so that they will grant me safe passage until I reach Judah.'),
('NEH', 2, 8, 'NEH.2.8', 'And may I have a letter to Asaph, keeper of the king’s forest, so that he will give me timber to make beams for the gates of the citadel to the temple, for the city wall, and for the house I will occupy.” And because the gracious hand of my God was upon me, the king granted my requests.'),
('NEH', 2, 9, 'NEH.2.9', 'Then I went to the governors west of the Euphrates and gave them the king’s letters. The king had also sent army officers and cavalry with me.'),
('NEH', 2, 10, 'NEH.2.10', 'But when Sanballat the Horonite and Tobiah the Ammonite official heard about this, they were deeply disturbed that someone had come to seek the well-being of the Israelites.'),
('NEH', 2, 11, 'NEH.2.11', 'After I had arrived in Jerusalem and had been there three days,'),
('NEH', 2, 12, 'NEH.2.12', 'I set out at night with a few men. I did not tell anyone what my God had laid on my heart to do for Jerusalem. The only animal with me was the one on which I was riding.'),
('NEH', 2, 13, 'NEH.2.13', 'So I went out at night through the Valley Gate toward the Well of the Serpent and the Dung Gate, and I inspected the walls of Jerusalem that had been broken down and the gates that had been destroyed by fire.'),
('NEH', 2, 14, 'NEH.2.14', 'Then I went on to the Fountain Gate and the King’s Pool, but there was no room for the animal under me to get through;'),
('NEH', 2, 15, 'NEH.2.15', 'so I went up the valley by night and inspected the wall. Then I headed back and reentered through the Valley Gate.'),
('NEH', 2, 16, 'NEH.2.16', 'The officials did not know where I had gone or what I was doing, for I had not yet told the Jews or priests or nobles or officials or any other workers.'),
('NEH', 2, 17, 'NEH.2.17', 'Then I said to them, “You see the trouble we are in. Jerusalem lies in ruins, and its gates have been burned down. Come, let us rebuild the wall of Jerusalem, so that we will no longer be a disgrace.”'),
('NEH', 2, 18, 'NEH.2.18', 'I also told them about the gracious hand of my God upon me, and what the king had said to me. “Let us start rebuilding,” they replied, and they set their hands to this good work.'),
('NEH', 2, 19, 'NEH.2.19', 'But when Sanballat the Horonite, Tobiah the Ammonite official, and Geshem the Arab heard about this, they mocked us and ridiculed us, saying, “What is this you are doing? Are you rebelling against the king?”'),
('NEH', 2, 20, 'NEH.2.20', 'So I answered them and said, “The God of heaven is the One who will grant us success. We, His servants, will start rebuilding, but you have no portion, right, or claim in Jerusalem.”'),
('NEH', 3, 1, 'NEH.3.1', 'At the Sheep Gate, Eliashib the high priest and his fellow priests began rebuilding. They dedicated it and installed its doors. After building as far as the Tower of the Hundred and the Tower of Hananel, they dedicated the wall.'),
('NEH', 3, 2, 'NEH.3.2', 'The men of Jericho built next to Eliashib, and Zaccur son of Imri built next to them.'),
('NEH', 3, 3, 'NEH.3.3', 'The Fish Gate was rebuilt by the sons of Hassenaah. They laid its beams and installed its doors, bolts, and bars.'),
('NEH', 3, 4, 'NEH.3.4', 'Next to them, Meremoth son of Uriah, the son of Hakkoz, made repairs. Next to him, Meshullam son of Berechiah, the son of Meshezabel, made repairs; and next to him, Zadok son of Baana made repairs as well.'),
('NEH', 3, 5, 'NEH.3.5', 'Next to him, the Tekoites made repairs, but their nobles did not put their shoulders to the work under their supervisors.'),
('NEH', 3, 6, 'NEH.3.6', 'The Jeshanah Gate was repaired by Joiada son of Paseah and Meshullam son of Besodeiah. They laid its beams and installed its doors, bolts, and bars.'),
('NEH', 3, 7, 'NEH.3.7', 'Next to them, repairs were made by Melatiah the Gibeonite, Jadon the Meronothite, and the men of Gibeon and Mizpah, who were under the authority of the governor of the region west of the Euphrates.'),
('NEH', 3, 8, 'NEH.3.8', 'Next to them, Uzziel son of Harhaiah, one of the goldsmiths, made repairs. And next to him, Hananiah, one of the perfumers, made repairs. They fortified Jerusalem as far as the Broad Wall.'),
('NEH', 3, 9, 'NEH.3.9', 'Next to them, Rephaiah son of Hur, ruler of a half-district of Jerusalem, made repairs;'),
('NEH', 3, 10, 'NEH.3.10', 'next to him, Jedaiah son of Harumaph made repairs across from his house; and next to him, Hattush son of Hashabneiah made repairs.'),
('NEH', 3, 11, 'NEH.3.11', 'Malchijah son of Harim and Hasshub son of Pahath-moab repaired another section, as well as the Tower of the Ovens.'),
('NEH', 3, 12, 'NEH.3.12', 'And next to them, Shallum son of Hallohesh, ruler of the other half-district of Jerusalem, made repairs, with the help of his daughters.'),
('NEH', 3, 13, 'NEH.3.13', 'The Valley Gate was repaired by Hanun and the residents of Zanoah. They rebuilt it, installed its doors, bolts, and bars, and repaired a thousand cubits of the wall as far as the Dung Gate.'),
('NEH', 3, 14, 'NEH.3.14', 'The Dung Gate was repaired by Malchijah son of Rechab, ruler of the district of Beth-haccherem. He rebuilt it and installed its doors, bolts, and bars.'),
('NEH', 3, 15, 'NEH.3.15', 'The Fountain Gate was repaired by Shallun son of Col-hozeh, ruler of the district of Mizpah. He rebuilt it, roofed it, and installed its doors, bolts, and bars. He also repaired the wall of the Pool of Shelah near the king’s garden, as far as the stairs that descend from the City of David.'),
('NEH', 3, 16, 'NEH.3.16', 'Beyond him, Nehemiah son of Azbuk, ruler of a half-district of Beth-zur, made repairs up to a point opposite the tombs of David, as far as the artificial pool and the House of the Mighty.'),
('NEH', 3, 17, 'NEH.3.17', 'Next to him, the Levites made repairs under Rehum son of Bani, and next to him, Hashabiah, ruler of a half-district of Keilah, made repairs for his district.'),
('NEH', 3, 18, 'NEH.3.18', 'Next to him, their countrymen made repairs under Binnui son of Henadad, ruler of the other half-district of Keilah.'),
('NEH', 3, 19, 'NEH.3.19', 'And next to him, Ezer son of Jeshua, ruler of Mizpah, repaired another section opposite the ascent to the armory, near the angle in the wall.'),
('NEH', 3, 20, 'NEH.3.20', 'Next to him, Baruch son of Zabbai diligently repaired another section, from the angle to the doorway of the house of Eliashib the high priest.'),
('NEH', 3, 21, 'NEH.3.21', 'Next to him, Meremoth son of Uriah, the son of Hakkoz, repaired another section, from the doorway of the house of Eliashib to the end of the house.'),
('NEH', 3, 22, 'NEH.3.22', 'And next to him, the priests from the surrounding area made repairs.'),
('NEH', 3, 23, 'NEH.3.23', 'Beyond them, Benjamin and Hasshub made repairs in front of their house, and next to them, Azariah son of Maaseiah, the son of Ananiah, made repairs beside his house.'),
('NEH', 3, 24, 'NEH.3.24', 'After him, Binnui son of Henadad repaired another section, from the house of Azariah to the angle and the corner,'),
('NEH', 3, 25, 'NEH.3.25', 'and Palal son of Uzai made repairs opposite the angle and the tower that juts out from the upper palace of the king near the courtyard of the guard. Next to him, Pedaiah son of Parosh'),
('NEH', 3, 26, 'NEH.3.26', 'and the temple servants living on the hill of Ophel made repairs opposite the Water Gate toward the east and the tower that juts out.'),
('NEH', 3, 27, 'NEH.3.27', 'And next to them, the Tekoites repaired another section, from a point opposite the great tower that juts out to the wall of Ophel.'),
('NEH', 3, 28, 'NEH.3.28', 'Above the Horse Gate, each of the priests made repairs in front of his own house.'),
('NEH', 3, 29, 'NEH.3.29', 'Next to them, Zadok son of Immer made repairs opposite his house, and next to him, Shemaiah son of Shecaniah, the guard of the East Gate, made repairs.'),
('NEH', 3, 30, 'NEH.3.30', 'Next to him, Hananiah son of Shelemiah, as well as Hanun the sixth son of Zalaph, repaired another section. Next to them, Meshullam son of Berechiah made repairs opposite his own quarters.'),
('NEH', 3, 31, 'NEH.3.31', 'Next to him, Malchijah, one of the goldsmiths, made repairs as far as the house of the temple servants and the merchants, opposite the Inspection Gate, and as far as the upper room above the corner.'),
('NEH', 3, 32, 'NEH.3.32', 'And between the upper room above the corner and the Sheep Gate, the goldsmiths and merchants made repairs.'),
('NEH', 4, 1, 'NEH.4.1', 'Now when Sanballat heard that we were rebuilding the wall, he was furious and filled with indignation. He ridiculed the Jews'),
('NEH', 4, 2, 'NEH.4.2', 'before his associates and the army of Samaria, saying, “What are these feeble Jews doing? Can they restore the wall by themselves? Will they offer sacrifices? Will they complete it in a day? Can they bring these burnt stones back to life from the mounds of rubble?”'),
('NEH', 4, 3, 'NEH.4.3', 'Then Tobiah the Ammonite, who was beside him, said, “If even a fox were to climb up on what they are building, it would break down their wall of stones!”'),
('NEH', 4, 4, 'NEH.4.4', 'Hear us, O God, for we are despised. Turn their scorn back upon their own heads, and let them be taken as plunder to a land of captivity.'),
('NEH', 4, 5, 'NEH.4.5', 'Do not cover up their iniquity or let their sin be blotted out from Your sight, for they have provoked the builders.'),
('NEH', 4, 6, 'NEH.4.6', 'So we rebuilt the wall until all of it was joined together up to half its height, for the people had a mind to work.'),
('NEH', 4, 7, 'NEH.4.7', 'When Sanballat and Tobiah, together with the Arabs, Ammonites, and Ashdodites, heard that the repair to the walls of Jerusalem was progressing and that the gaps were being closed, they were furious,'),
('NEH', 4, 8, 'NEH.4.8', 'and all of them conspired to come and fight against Jerusalem and create a hindrance.'),
('NEH', 4, 9, 'NEH.4.9', 'So we prayed to our God and posted a guard against them day and night.'),
('NEH', 4, 10, 'NEH.4.10', 'Meanwhile, the people of Judah said: “The strength of the laborer fails, and there is so much rubble that we will never be able to rebuild the wall.”'),
('NEH', 4, 11, 'NEH.4.11', 'And our enemies said, “Before they know or see a thing, we will come into their midst, kill them, and put an end to the work.”'),
('NEH', 4, 12, 'NEH.4.12', 'At that time the Jews who lived nearby came and told us ten times over, “Wherever you turn, they will attack us.”'),
('NEH', 4, 13, 'NEH.4.13', 'So I stationed men behind the lowest sections of the wall, at the vulnerable areas. I stationed them by families with their swords, spears, and bows.'),
('NEH', 4, 14, 'NEH.4.14', 'After I had made an inspection, I stood up and said to the nobles, the officials, and the rest of the people, “Do not be afraid of them. Remember the Lord, who is great and awesome, and fight for your brothers, your sons and your daughters, your wives and your homes.”'),
('NEH', 4, 15, 'NEH.4.15', 'When our enemies heard that we were aware of their scheme and that God had frustrated it, each of us returned to his own work on the wall.'),
('NEH', 4, 16, 'NEH.4.16', 'And from that day on, half of my servants did the work while the other half held spears, shields, bows, and armor. The officers stationed themselves behind all the people of Judah'),
('NEH', 4, 17, 'NEH.4.17', 'who were rebuilding the wall. The laborers who carried materials worked with one hand and held a weapon with the other.'),
('NEH', 4, 18, 'NEH.4.18', 'And each of the builders worked with his sword strapped at his side. But the trumpeter stayed beside me.'),
('NEH', 4, 19, 'NEH.4.19', 'Then I said to the nobles, the officials, and the rest of the people: “The work is great and extensive, and we are spread out far from one another along the wall.'),
('NEH', 4, 20, 'NEH.4.20', 'Wherever you hear the sound of the horn, rally to us there. Our God will fight for us!”'),
('NEH', 4, 21, 'NEH.4.21', 'So we continued the work, while half of the men held spears from the break of dawn until the stars came out.'),
('NEH', 4, 22, 'NEH.4.22', 'At that time I also said to the people, “Let every man and his servant spend the night inside Jerusalem, so that they can stand guard by night and work by day.”'),
('NEH', 4, 23, 'NEH.4.23', 'So neither I nor my brothers nor my servants nor the guards with me changed out of our clothes; each carried his weapon, even to go for water.'),
('NEH', 5, 1, 'NEH.5.1', 'About that time there was a great outcry from the people and their wives against their fellow Jews.'),
('NEH', 5, 2, 'NEH.5.2', 'Some were saying, “We and our sons and daughters are numerous. We must get grain in order to eat and stay alive.”'),
('NEH', 5, 3, 'NEH.5.3', 'Others were saying, “We are mortgaging our fields, our vineyards, and our homes to get grain during the famine.”'),
('NEH', 5, 4, 'NEH.5.4', 'Still others were saying, “We have borrowed money to pay the king’s tax on our fields and vineyards.'),
('NEH', 5, 5, 'NEH.5.5', 'We and our children are just like our countrymen and their children, yet we are subjecting our sons and daughters to slavery. Some of our daughters are already enslaved, but we are powerless to redeem them because our fields and vineyards belong to others.”'),
('NEH', 5, 6, 'NEH.5.6', 'When I heard their outcry and these complaints, I became extremely angry,'),
('NEH', 5, 7, 'NEH.5.7', 'and after serious thought I rebuked the nobles and officials, saying, “You are exacting usury from your own brothers!” So I called a large assembly against them'),
('NEH', 5, 8, 'NEH.5.8', 'and said, “We have done our best to buy back our Jewish brothers who were sold to foreigners, but now you are selling your own brothers, that they may be sold back to us!” But they remained silent, for they could find nothing to say.'),
('NEH', 5, 9, 'NEH.5.9', 'So I continued, “What you are doing is not right. Shouldn’t you walk in the fear of our God to avoid the reproach of our foreign enemies?'),
('NEH', 5, 10, 'NEH.5.10', 'I, as well as my brothers and my servants, have been lending the people money and grain. Please, let us stop this usury.'),
('NEH', 5, 11, 'NEH.5.11', 'Please restore to them immediately their fields, vineyards, olive groves, and houses, along with the percentage of the money, grain, new wine, and oil that you have been assessing them.”'),
('NEH', 5, 12, 'NEH.5.12', '“We will restore it,” they replied, “and will require nothing more from them. We will do as you say.” So I summoned the priests and required of the nobles and officials an oath that they would do what they had promised.'),
('NEH', 5, 13, 'NEH.5.13', 'I also shook out the folds of my robe and said, “May God likewise shake out of his house and possessions every man who does not keep this promise. May such a man be shaken out and have nothing!” The whole assembly said, “Amen,” and they praised the LORD. And the people did as they had promised.'),
('NEH', 5, 14, 'NEH.5.14', 'Furthermore, from the day King Artaxerxes appointed me to be their governor in the land of Judah, from his twentieth year until his thirty-second year (twelve years total), neither I nor my brothers ate the food allotted to the governor.'),
('NEH', 5, 15, 'NEH.5.15', 'The governors before me had heavily burdened the people, taking from them bread and wine plus forty shekels of silver. Their servants also oppressed the people. But I did not do this, because of my fear of God.'),
('NEH', 5, 16, 'NEH.5.16', 'Instead, I devoted myself to the construction of the wall, and all my servants were gathered there for the work; we did not acquire any land.'),
('NEH', 5, 17, 'NEH.5.17', 'There were 150 Jews and officials at my table, besides the guests from the surrounding nations.'),
('NEH', 5, 18, 'NEH.5.18', 'Each day one ox, six choice sheep, and some fowl were prepared for me, and once every ten days an abundance of all kinds of wine was provided. But I did not demand the food allotted to the governor, because the burden on the people was so heavy.'),
('NEH', 5, 19, 'NEH.5.19', 'Remember me favorably, O my God, for all that I have done for this people.'),
('NEH', 6, 1, 'NEH.6.1', 'When Sanballat, Tobiah, Geshem the Arab, and the rest of our enemies heard that I had rebuilt the wall and not a gap was left—though to that time I had not yet installed the doors in the gates—'),
('NEH', 6, 2, 'NEH.6.2', 'Sanballat and Geshem sent me this message: “Come, let us meet together in one of the villages on the plain of Ono.” But they were planning to harm me.'),
('NEH', 6, 3, 'NEH.6.3', 'So I sent messengers to them, saying, “I am doing a great work and cannot come down. Why should the work stop while I leave it to go down to you?”'),
('NEH', 6, 4, 'NEH.6.4', 'Four times they sent me the same message, and each time I gave the same reply.'),
('NEH', 6, 5, 'NEH.6.5', 'The fifth time, Sanballat sent me this same message by his young servant, who had in his hand an unsealed letter'),
('NEH', 6, 6, 'NEH.6.6', 'that read: “It is reported among the nations—and Geshem agrees—that you and the Jews are plotting to revolt, and this is why you are building the wall. According to these reports, you are to become their king,'),
('NEH', 6, 7, 'NEH.6.7', 'and you have even appointed prophets in Jerusalem to proclaim on your behalf: ‘There is a king in Judah.’ Soon these rumors will reach the ears of the king. So come, let us confer together.”'),
('NEH', 6, 8, 'NEH.6.8', 'Then I sent him this reply: “There is nothing to these rumors you are spreading; you are inventing them in your own mind.”'),
('NEH', 6, 9, 'NEH.6.9', 'For they were all trying to frighten us, saying, “Their hands will be weakened in the work, and it will never be finished.” But now, my God, strengthen my hands.'),
('NEH', 6, 10, 'NEH.6.10', 'Later, I went to the house of Shemaiah son of Delaiah, the son of Mehetabel, who was confined to his house. He said: “Let us meet at the house of God inside the temple. Let us shut the temple doors because they are coming to kill you—by night they are coming to kill you!”'),
('NEH', 6, 11, 'NEH.6.11', 'But I replied, “Should a man like me run away? Should one like me go into the temple to save his own life? I will not go!”'),
('NEH', 6, 12, 'NEH.6.12', 'I realized that God had not sent him, but that he had uttered this prophecy against me because Tobiah and Sanballat had hired him.'),
('NEH', 6, 13, 'NEH.6.13', 'He had been hired to intimidate me so that I would sin by doing as he suggested, so they could give me a bad name in order to discredit me.'),
('NEH', 6, 14, 'NEH.6.14', 'O my God, remember Tobiah and Sanballat for what they have done, and also Noadiah the prophetess and the other prophets who tried to intimidate me.'),
('NEH', 6, 15, 'NEH.6.15', 'So the wall was completed in fifty-two days, on the twenty-fifth of Elul.'),
('NEH', 6, 16, 'NEH.6.16', 'When all our enemies heard about this, all the surrounding nations were afraid and disheartened, for they realized that this task had been accomplished by our God.'),
('NEH', 6, 17, 'NEH.6.17', 'Also in those days, the nobles of Judah sent many letters to Tobiah, and Tobiah’s letters kept coming to them.'),
('NEH', 6, 18, 'NEH.6.18', 'For many in Judah were bound by oath to him, since he was a son-in-law of Shecaniah son of Arah, and his son Jehohanan had married the daughter of Meshullam son of Berechiah.'),
('NEH', 6, 19, 'NEH.6.19', 'Moreover, these nobles kept reporting to me Tobiah’s good deeds, and they relayed my words to him. And Tobiah sent letters to intimidate me.'),
('NEH', 7, 1, 'NEH.7.1', 'When the wall had been rebuilt and I had set the doors in place, the gatekeepers, singers, and Levites were appointed.'),
('NEH', 7, 2, 'NEH.7.2', 'Then I put my brother Hanani in charge of Jerusalem, along with Hananiah the commander of the fortress, because he was a faithful man who feared God more than most.'),
('NEH', 7, 3, 'NEH.7.3', 'And I told them, “Do not open the gates of Jerusalem until the sun is hot. While the guards are on duty, keep the doors shut and securely fastened. And appoint the residents of Jerusalem as guards, some at their posts and some at their own homes.”'),
('NEH', 7, 4, 'NEH.7.4', 'Now the city was large and spacious, but there were few people in it, and the houses had not yet been rebuilt.'),
('NEH', 7, 5, 'NEH.7.5', 'Then my God put it into my heart to assemble the nobles, the officials, and the people to be enrolled by genealogy. I found the genealogical register of those who had first returned, and I found the following written in it:'),
('NEH', 7, 6, 'NEH.7.6', 'These are the people of the province who came up from the captivity of the exiles carried away to Babylon by Nebuchadnezzar its king. They returned to Jerusalem and Judah, each to his own town,'),
('NEH', 7, 7, 'NEH.7.7', 'accompanied by Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Azariah, Raamiah, Nahamani, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispereth, Bigvai, Nehum, and Baanah. This is the count of the men of Israel:'),
('NEH', 7, 8, 'NEH.7.8', 'the descendants of Parosh, 2,172;'),
('NEH', 7, 9, 'NEH.7.9', 'the descendants of Shephatiah, 372;'),
('NEH', 7, 10, 'NEH.7.10', 'the descendants of Arah, 652;'),
('NEH', 7, 11, 'NEH.7.11', 'the descendants of Pahath-moab (through the line of Jeshua and Joab), 2,818;'),
('NEH', 7, 12, 'NEH.7.12', 'the descendants of Elam, 1,254;'),
('NEH', 7, 13, 'NEH.7.13', 'the descendants of Zattu, 845;'),
('NEH', 7, 14, 'NEH.7.14', 'the descendants of Zaccai, 760;'),
('NEH', 7, 15, 'NEH.7.15', 'the descendants of Binnui, 648;'),
('NEH', 7, 16, 'NEH.7.16', 'the descendants of Bebai, 628;'),
('NEH', 7, 17, 'NEH.7.17', 'the descendants of Azgad, 2,322;'),
('NEH', 7, 18, 'NEH.7.18', 'the descendants of Adonikam, 667;'),
('NEH', 7, 19, 'NEH.7.19', 'the descendants of Bigvai, 2,067;'),
('NEH', 7, 20, 'NEH.7.20', 'the descendants of Adin, 655;'),
('NEH', 7, 21, 'NEH.7.21', 'the descendants of Ater (through Hezekiah), 98;'),
('NEH', 7, 22, 'NEH.7.22', 'the descendants of Hashum, 328;'),
('NEH', 7, 23, 'NEH.7.23', 'the descendants of Bezai, 324;'),
('NEH', 7, 24, 'NEH.7.24', 'the descendants of Hariph, 112;'),
('NEH', 7, 25, 'NEH.7.25', 'the descendants of Gibeon, 95;'),
('NEH', 7, 26, 'NEH.7.26', 'the men of Bethlehem and Netophah, 188;'),
('NEH', 7, 27, 'NEH.7.27', 'the men of Anathoth, 128;'),
('NEH', 7, 28, 'NEH.7.28', 'the men of Beth-azmaveth, 42;'),
('NEH', 7, 29, 'NEH.7.29', 'the men of Kiriath-jearim, Chephirah, and Beeroth, 743;'),
('NEH', 7, 30, 'NEH.7.30', 'the men of Ramah and Geba, 621;'),
('NEH', 7, 31, 'NEH.7.31', 'the men of Michmash, 122;'),
('NEH', 7, 32, 'NEH.7.32', 'the men of Bethel and Ai, 123;'),
('NEH', 7, 33, 'NEH.7.33', 'the men of the other Nebo, 52;'),
('NEH', 7, 34, 'NEH.7.34', 'the descendants of the other Elam, 1,254;'),
('NEH', 7, 35, 'NEH.7.35', 'the descendants of Harim, 320;'),
('NEH', 7, 36, 'NEH.7.36', 'the men of Jericho, 345;'),
('NEH', 7, 37, 'NEH.7.37', 'the men of Lod, Hadid, and Ono, 721;'),
('NEH', 7, 38, 'NEH.7.38', 'and the descendants of Senaah, 3,930.'),
('NEH', 7, 39, 'NEH.7.39', 'The priests: the descendants of Jedaiah (through the house of Jeshua), 973;'),
('NEH', 7, 40, 'NEH.7.40', 'the descendants of Immer, 1,052;'),
('NEH', 7, 41, 'NEH.7.41', 'the descendants of Pashhur, 1,247;'),
('NEH', 7, 42, 'NEH.7.42', 'and the descendants of Harim, 1,017.'),
('NEH', 7, 43, 'NEH.7.43', 'The Levites: the descendants of Jeshua (through Kadmiel, through the line of Hodevah), 74.'),
('NEH', 7, 44, 'NEH.7.44', 'The singers: the descendants of Asaph, 148.'),
('NEH', 7, 45, 'NEH.7.45', 'The gatekeepers: the descendants of Shallum, the descendants of Ater, the descendants of Talmon, the descendants of Akkub, the descendants of Hatita, and the descendants of Shobai, 138 in all.'),
('NEH', 7, 46, 'NEH.7.46', 'The temple servants: the descendants of Ziha, the descendants of Hasupha, the descendants of Tabbaoth,'),
('NEH', 7, 47, 'NEH.7.47', 'the descendants of Keros, the descendants of Sia, the descendants of Padon,'),
('NEH', 7, 48, 'NEH.7.48', 'the descendants of Lebanah, the descendants of Hagabah, the descendants of Shalmai,'),
('NEH', 7, 49, 'NEH.7.49', 'the descendants of Hanan, the descendants of Giddel, the descendants of Gahar,'),
('NEH', 7, 50, 'NEH.7.50', 'the descendants of Reaiah, the descendants of Rezin, the descendants of Nekoda,'),
('NEH', 7, 51, 'NEH.7.51', 'the descendants of Gazzam, the descendants of Uzza, the descendants of Paseah,'),
('NEH', 7, 52, 'NEH.7.52', 'the descendants of Besai, the descendants of Meunim, the descendants of Nephushesim,'),
('NEH', 7, 53, 'NEH.7.53', 'the descendants of Bakbuk, the descendants of Hakupha, the descendants of Harhur,'),
('NEH', 7, 54, 'NEH.7.54', 'the descendants of Bazlith, the descendants of Mehida, the descendants of Harsha,'),
('NEH', 7, 55, 'NEH.7.55', 'the descendants of Barkos, the descendants of Sisera, the descendants of Temah,'),
('NEH', 7, 56, 'NEH.7.56', 'the descendants of Neziah, and the descendants of Hatipha.'),
('NEH', 7, 57, 'NEH.7.57', 'The descendants of the servants of Solomon: the descendants of Sotai, the descendants of Sophereth, the descendants of Perida,'),
('NEH', 7, 58, 'NEH.7.58', 'the descendants of Jaala, the descendants of Darkon, the descendants of Giddel,'),
('NEH', 7, 59, 'NEH.7.59', 'the descendants of Shephatiah, the descendants of Hattil, the descendants of Pochereth-hazzebaim, and the descendants of Amon.'),
('NEH', 7, 60, 'NEH.7.60', 'The temple servants and descendants of the servants of Solomon numbered 392 in all.'),
('NEH', 7, 61, 'NEH.7.61', 'The following came up from Tel-melah, Tel-harsha, Cherub, Addon, and Immer, but they could not prove that their families were descended from Israel:'),
('NEH', 7, 62, 'NEH.7.62', 'the descendants of Delaiah, the descendants of Tobiah, and the descendants of Nekoda, 642 in all.'),
('NEH', 7, 63, 'NEH.7.63', 'And from among the priests: the descendants of Hobaiah, the descendants of Hakkoz, and the descendants of Barzillai (who had married a daughter of Barzillai the Gileadite and was called by their name).'),
('NEH', 7, 64, 'NEH.7.64', 'These men searched for their family records, but they could not find them and so were excluded from the priesthood as unclean.'),
('NEH', 7, 65, 'NEH.7.65', 'The governor ordered them not to eat the most holy things until there was a priest to consult the Urim and Thummim.'),
('NEH', 7, 66, 'NEH.7.66', 'The whole assembly numbered 42,360,'),
('NEH', 7, 67, 'NEH.7.67', 'in addition to their 7,337 menservants and maidservants, as well as their 245 male and female singers.'),
('NEH', 7, 68, 'NEH.7.68', 'They had 736 horses, 245 mules,'),
('NEH', 7, 69, 'NEH.7.69', '435 camels, and 6,720 donkeys.'),
('NEH', 7, 70, 'NEH.7.70', 'Some of the heads of the families contributed to the project. The governor gave to the treasury 1,000 darics of gold, 50 bowls, and 530 priestly garments.'),
('NEH', 7, 71, 'NEH.7.71', 'And some of the heads of the families gave to the treasury for the project 20,000 darics of gold and 2,200 minas of silver.'),
('NEH', 7, 72, 'NEH.7.72', 'The rest of the people gave a total of 20,000 darics of gold, 2,000 minas of silver, and 67 priestly garments.'),
('NEH', 7, 73, 'NEH.7.73', 'So the priests, Levites, gatekeepers, singers, and temple servants, along with some of the people and the rest of the Israelites, settled in their own towns. And by the seventh month the Israelites had settled in their towns.'),
('NEH', 8, 1, 'NEH.8.1', 'At that time all the people gathered together in the square before the Water Gate, and they asked Ezra the scribe to bring out the Book of the Law of Moses, which the LORD had commanded for Israel.'),
('NEH', 8, 2, 'NEH.8.2', 'On the first day of the seventh month, Ezra the priest brought the Law before the assembly of men and women and all who could listen and understand.'),
('NEH', 8, 3, 'NEH.8.3', 'So Ezra read it aloud from daybreak until noon as he faced the square before the Water Gate, in front of the men and women and those who could understand. And all the people listened attentively to the Book of the Law.'),
('NEH', 8, 4, 'NEH.8.4', 'Ezra the scribe stood on a high wooden platform built for this occasion. At his right side stood Mattithiah, Shema, Anaiah, Uriah, Hilkiah, and Maaseiah, and at his left were Pedaiah, Mishael, Malchijah, Hashum, Hash-baddanah, Zechariah, and Meshullam.'),
('NEH', 8, 5, 'NEH.8.5', 'Ezra opened the book in full view of all the people, since he was standing above them all, and as he opened it, all the people stood up.'),
('NEH', 8, 6, 'NEH.8.6', 'Then Ezra blessed the LORD, the great God, and with their hands uplifted, all the people said, “Amen, Amen!” Then they bowed down and worshiped the LORD with their faces to the ground.'),
('NEH', 8, 7, 'NEH.8.7', 'The Levites—Jeshua, Bani, Sherebiah, Jamin, Akkub, Shabbethai, Hodiah, Maaseiah, Kelita, Azariah, Jozabad, Hanan, and Pelaiah—instructed the people in the Law as they stood in their places.'),
('NEH', 8, 8, 'NEH.8.8', 'So they read from the Book of the Law of God, explaining it and giving insight, so that the people could understand what was being read.'),
('NEH', 8, 9, 'NEH.8.9', 'Nehemiah the governor, Ezra the priest and scribe, and the Levites who were instructing the people said to all of them, “This day is holy to the LORD your God. Do not mourn or weep.” For all the people were weeping as they heard the words of the Law.'),
('NEH', 8, 10, 'NEH.8.10', 'Then Nehemiah told them, “Go and eat what is rich, drink what is sweet, and send out portions to those who have nothing prepared, since today is holy to our Lord. Do not grieve, for the joy of the LORD is your strength.”'),
('NEH', 8, 11, 'NEH.8.11', 'And the Levites calmed all the people, saying, “Be still, since today is holy. Do not grieve.”'),
('NEH', 8, 12, 'NEH.8.12', 'Then all the people began to eat and drink, to send out portions, and to rejoice greatly, because they understood the words that had been made known to them.'),
('NEH', 8, 13, 'NEH.8.13', 'On the second day of the month, the heads of all the families, along with the priests and Levites, gathered around Ezra the scribe to study the words of the Law.'),
('NEH', 8, 14, 'NEH.8.14', 'And they found written in the Law, which the LORD had commanded through Moses, that the Israelites were to dwell in booths during the feast of the seventh month,'),
('NEH', 8, 15, 'NEH.8.15', 'and that they should proclaim this message and spread it throughout their towns and in Jerusalem, saying, “Go out to the hill country and bring back branches of olive, wild olive, myrtle, palm, and other leafy trees, to make booths, as it is written.”'),
('NEH', 8, 16, 'NEH.8.16', 'And the people went out, brought back branches, and made booths on their own rooftops, in their courtyards, in the courts of the house of God, and in the squares by the Water Gate and by the Gate of Ephraim.'),
('NEH', 8, 17, 'NEH.8.17', 'The whole assembly that had returned from exile made booths and lived in them. From the days of Joshua son of Nun until that day, the Israelites had not celebrated like this. And there was great rejoicing.'),
('NEH', 8, 18, 'NEH.8.18', 'Day after day, from the first day to the last, Ezra read from the Book of the Law of God. The Israelites kept the feast for seven days, and on the eighth day they held an assembly, according to the ordinance.'),
('NEH', 9, 1, 'NEH.9.1', 'On the twenty-fourth day of the same month, the Israelites gathered together, fasting and wearing sackcloth, with dust on their heads.'),
('NEH', 9, 2, 'NEH.9.2', 'Those of Israelite descent separated themselves from all the foreigners, and they stood and confessed their sins and the iniquities of their fathers.'),
('NEH', 9, 3, 'NEH.9.3', 'While they stood in their places, they read from the Book of the Law of the LORD their God for a quarter of the day, and they spent another quarter of the day in confession and worship of the LORD their God.'),
('NEH', 9, 4, 'NEH.9.4', 'And the Levites—Jeshua, Bani, Kadmiel, Shebaniah, Bunni, Sherebiah, Bani, and Chenani—stood on the raised platform and cried out in a loud voice to the LORD their God.'),
('NEH', 9, 5, 'NEH.9.5', 'Then the Levites—Jeshua, Kadmiel, Bani, Hashabneiah, Sherebiah, Hodiah, Shebaniah, and Pethahiah—said, “Stand up and bless the LORD your God from everlasting to everlasting: Blessed be Your glorious name, and may it be exalted above all blessing and praise.'),
('NEH', 9, 6, 'NEH.9.6', 'You alone are the LORD. You created the heavens, the highest heavens with all their host, the earth and all that is on it, the seas and all that is in them. You give life to all things, and the host of heaven worships You.'),
('NEH', 9, 7, 'NEH.9.7', 'You are the LORD, the God who chose Abram, who brought him out of Ur of the Chaldeans and gave him the name Abraham.'),
('NEH', 9, 8, 'NEH.9.8', 'You found his heart faithful before You, and made a covenant with him to give the land of the Canaanites and Hittites, of the Amorites and Perizzites, of the Jebusites and Girgashites—to give it to his descendants. You have kept Your promise, because You are righteous.'),
('NEH', 9, 9, 'NEH.9.9', 'You saw the affliction of our fathers in Egypt; You heard their cry at the Red Sea.'),
('NEH', 9, 10, 'NEH.9.10', 'You performed signs and wonders against Pharaoh, all his officials, and all the people of his land, for You knew they had acted with arrogance against our fathers. You made a name for Yourself that endures to this day.'),
('NEH', 9, 11, 'NEH.9.11', 'You divided the sea before them, and they crossed through it on dry ground. You hurled their pursuers into the depths like a stone into raging waters.'),
('NEH', 9, 12, 'NEH.9.12', 'You led them with a pillar of cloud by day and a pillar of fire by night, to light for them the way in which they should travel.'),
('NEH', 9, 13, 'NEH.9.13', 'You came down on Mount Sinai and spoke with them from heaven. You gave them just ordinances, true laws, and good statutes and commandments.'),
('NEH', 9, 14, 'NEH.9.14', 'You revealed to them Your holy Sabbath and gave them commandments and statutes and laws through Your servant Moses.'),
('NEH', 9, 15, 'NEH.9.15', 'In their hunger You gave them bread from heaven; in their thirst You brought them water from the rock. You told them to go in and possess the land that You had sworn to give them.'),
('NEH', 9, 16, 'NEH.9.16', 'But they and our fathers became arrogant and stiff-necked and did not obey Your commandments.'),
('NEH', 9, 17, 'NEH.9.17', 'They refused to listen and failed to remember the wonders You performed among them. They stiffened their necks and appointed a leader to return them to their bondage in Egypt. But You are a forgiving God, gracious and compassionate, slow to anger and rich in loving devotion, and You did not forsake them.'),
('NEH', 9, 18, 'NEH.9.18', 'Even when they cast for themselves an image of a calf and said, ‘This is your God who brought you up out of Egypt,’ and when they committed terrible blasphemies,'),
('NEH', 9, 19, 'NEH.9.19', 'You in Your great compassion did not forsake them in the wilderness. By day the pillar of cloud never turned away from guiding them on their path; and by the night the pillar of fire illuminated the way they should go.'),
('NEH', 9, 20, 'NEH.9.20', 'You gave Your good Spirit to instruct them. You did not withhold Your manna from their mouths, and You gave them water for their thirst.'),
('NEH', 9, 21, 'NEH.9.21', 'For forty years You sustained them in the wilderness, so that they lacked nothing. Their clothes did not wear out and their feet did not swell.'),
('NEH', 9, 22, 'NEH.9.22', 'You gave them kingdoms and peoples and allotted to them every corner of the land. So they took the land of Sihon king of Heshbon and of Og king of Bashan.'),
('NEH', 9, 23, 'NEH.9.23', 'You multiplied their descendants like the stars of heaven and brought them to the land You had told their fathers to enter and possess.'),
('NEH', 9, 24, 'NEH.9.24', 'So their descendants went in and possessed the land; You subdued before them the Canaanites dwelling in the land. You delivered into their hands the kings and peoples of the land, to do with them as they wished.'),
('NEH', 9, 25, 'NEH.9.25', 'They captured fortified cities and fertile land and took houses full of all goods, wells already dug, vineyards, olive groves, and fruit trees in abundance. So they ate and were filled; they grew fat and delighted in Your great goodness.'),
('NEH', 9, 26, 'NEH.9.26', 'But they were disobedient and rebelled against You; they flung Your law behind their backs. They killed Your prophets, who had admonished them to return to You. They committed terrible blasphemies.'),
('NEH', 9, 27, 'NEH.9.27', 'So You delivered them into the hands of enemies who oppressed them, and in their time of distress they cried out to You. From heaven You heard them, and in Your great compassion You gave them deliverers who saved them from the hands of their enemies.'),
('NEH', 9, 28, 'NEH.9.28', 'But as soon as they had rest, they again did evil in Your sight. So You abandoned them to the hands of their enemies, who had dominion over them. When they cried out to You again, You heard from heaven, and You delivered them many times in Your compassion.'),
('NEH', 9, 29, 'NEH.9.29', 'You admonished them to turn back to Your law, but they were arrogant and disobeyed Your commandments. They sinned against Your ordinances, by which a man will live if he practices them. They turned a stubborn shoulder; they stiffened their necks and would not obey.'),
('NEH', 9, 30, 'NEH.9.30', 'You were patient with them for many years, and Your Spirit admonished them through Your prophets. Yet they would not listen, so You gave them into the hands of the neighboring peoples.'),
('NEH', 9, 31, 'NEH.9.31', 'But in Your great compassion, You did not put an end to them; nor did You forsake them, for You are a gracious and compassionate God.'),
('NEH', 9, 32, 'NEH.9.32', 'So now, our God, the great and mighty and awesome God who keeps His gracious covenant, do not view lightly all the hardship that has come upon us, and upon our kings and leaders, our priests and prophets, our ancestors and all Your people, from the days of the kings of Assyria until today.'),
('NEH', 9, 33, 'NEH.9.33', 'You are just in all that has befallen us, because You have acted faithfully, while we have acted wickedly.'),
('NEH', 9, 34, 'NEH.9.34', 'Our kings and leaders and priests and fathers did not obey Your law or listen to Your commandments and warnings that You gave them.'),
('NEH', 9, 35, 'NEH.9.35', 'For even while they were in their kingdom, with the abundant goodness that You had given them, and in the spacious and fertile land that You had set before them, they would not serve You or turn from their wicked ways.'),
('NEH', 9, 36, 'NEH.9.36', 'So here we are today as slaves in the land You gave our fathers to enjoy its fruit and goodness—here we are as slaves!'),
('NEH', 9, 37, 'NEH.9.37', 'Its abundant harvest goes to the kings You have set over us because of our sins. And they rule over our bodies and our livestock as they please. We are in great distress.'),
('NEH', 9, 38, 'NEH.9.38', 'In view of all this, we make a binding agreement, putting it in writing and sealing it with the names of our leaders, Levites, and priests.”'),
('NEH', 10, 1, 'NEH.10.1', 'Now these were the ones who sealed the document: Nehemiah the governor, son of Hacaliah, and also Zedekiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 2, 'NEH.10.2', 'Seraiah, Azariah, Jeremiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 3, 'NEH.10.3', 'Pashhur, Amariah, Malchijah,'),
('NEH', 10, 4, 'NEH.10.4', 'Hattush, Shebaniah, Malluch,'),
('NEH', 10, 5, 'NEH.10.5', 'Harim, Meremoth, Obadiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 6, 'NEH.10.6', 'Daniel, Ginnethon, Baruch,'),
('NEH', 10, 7, 'NEH.10.7', 'Meshullam, Abijah, Mijamin,'),
('NEH', 10, 8, 'NEH.10.8', 'Maaziah, Bilgai, and Shemaiah. These were the priests.'),
('NEH', 10, 9, 'NEH.10.9', 'The Levites: Jeshua son of Azaniah, Binnui of the sons of Henadad, Kadmiel,'),
('NEH', 10, 10, 'NEH.10.10', 'and their associates: Shebaniah, Hodiah, Kelita, Pelaiah, Hanan,'),
('NEH', 10, 11, 'NEH.10.11', 'Mica, Rehob, Hashabiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 12, 'NEH.10.12', 'Zaccur, Sherebiah, Shebaniah,'),
('NEH', 10, 13, 'NEH.10.13', 'Hodiah, Bani, and Beninu.'),
('NEH', 10, 14, 'NEH.10.14', 'And the leaders of the people: Parosh, Pahath-moab, Elam, Zattu, Bani,'),
('NEH', 10, 15, 'NEH.10.15', 'Bunni, Azgad, Bebai,'),
('NEH', 10, 16, 'NEH.10.16', 'Adonijah, Bigvai, Adin,'),
('NEH', 10, 17, 'NEH.10.17', 'Ater, Hezekiah, Azzur,'),
('NEH', 10, 18, 'NEH.10.18', 'Hodiah, Hashum, Bezai,'),
('NEH', 10, 19, 'NEH.10.19', 'Hariph, Anathoth, Nebai,'),
('NEH', 10, 20, 'NEH.10.20', 'Magpiash, Meshullam, Hezir,'),
('NEH', 10, 21, 'NEH.10.21', 'Meshezabel, Zadok, Jaddua,'),
('NEH', 10, 22, 'NEH.10.22', 'Pelatiah, Hanan, Anaiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 23, 'NEH.10.23', 'Hoshea, Hananiah, Hasshub,'),
('NEH', 10, 24, 'NEH.10.24', 'Hallohesh, Pilha, Shobek,'),
('NEH', 10, 25, 'NEH.10.25', 'Rehum, Hashabnah, Maaseiah,'),
('NEH', 10, 26, 'NEH.10.26', 'Ahijah, Hanan, Anan,'),
('NEH', 10, 27, 'NEH.10.27', 'Malluch, Harim, and Baanah.'),
('NEH', 10, 28, 'NEH.10.28', '“The rest of the people—the priests, Levites, gatekeepers, singers, temple servants, and all who had separated themselves from the people of the land to obey the Law of God—along with their wives and all their sons and daughters who are able to understand,'),
('NEH', 10, 29, 'NEH.10.29', 'hereby join with their noble brothers and commit themselves with a sworn oath to follow the Law of God given through His servant Moses and to obey carefully all the commandments, ordinances, and statutes of the LORD our Lord.'),
('NEH', 10, 30, 'NEH.10.30', 'We will not give our daughters in marriage to the people of the land, and we will not take their daughters for our sons.'),
('NEH', 10, 31, 'NEH.10.31', 'When the people of the land bring merchandise or any kind of grain to sell on the Sabbath day, we will not buy from them on a Sabbath or holy day. Every seventh year we will let the fields lie fallow and will cancel every debt.'),
('NEH', 10, 32, 'NEH.10.32', 'We also place ourselves under the obligation to contribute a third of a shekel yearly for the service of the house of our God:'),
('NEH', 10, 33, 'NEH.10.33', 'for the showbread, for the regular grain offerings and burnt offerings, for the Sabbath offerings, for the New Moons and appointed feasts, for the holy offerings, for the sin offerings to make atonement for Israel, and for all the duties of the house of our God.'),
('NEH', 10, 34, 'NEH.10.34', 'We have cast lots among the priests, Levites, and people for the donation of wood by our families at the appointed times each year. They are to bring it to the house of our God to burn on the altar of the LORD our God, as it is written in the Law.'),
('NEH', 10, 35, 'NEH.10.35', 'We will also bring the firstfruits of our land and of every fruit tree to the house of the LORD year by year.'),
('NEH', 10, 36, 'NEH.10.36', 'And we will bring the firstborn of our sons and our livestock, as it is written in the Law, and will bring the firstborn of our herds and flocks to the house of our God, to the priests who minister in the house of our God.'),
('NEH', 10, 37, 'NEH.10.37', 'Moreover, we will bring to the priests at the storerooms of the house of our God the firstfruits of our dough, of our grain offerings, of the fruit of all our trees, and of our new wine and oil. A tenth of our produce belongs to the Levites, so that they shall receive tithes in all the towns where we labor.'),
('NEH', 10, 38, 'NEH.10.38', 'A priest of Aaron’s line is to accompany the Levites when they collect the tenth, and the Levites are to bring a tenth of these tithes to the storerooms of the treasury in the house of our God.'),
('NEH', 10, 39, 'NEH.10.39', 'For the Israelites and the Levites are to bring the contributions of grain, new wine, and oil to the storerooms where the articles of the sanctuary are kept and where the ministering priests, the gatekeepers, and the singers stay. Thus we will not neglect the house of our God.”'),
('NEH', 11, 1, 'NEH.11.1', 'Now the leaders of the people settled in Jerusalem, and the rest of the people cast lots to bring one out of ten to live in the holy city of Jerusalem, while the remaining nine were to dwell in their own towns.'),
('NEH', 11, 2, 'NEH.11.2', 'And the people blessed all the men who volunteered to live in Jerusalem.'),
('NEH', 11, 3, 'NEH.11.3', 'These are the heads of the provinces who settled in Jerusalem. (In the villages of Judah, however, each lived on his own property in their towns—the Israelites, priests, Levites, temple servants, and descendants of Solomon’s servants—'),
('NEH', 11, 4, 'NEH.11.4', 'while some of the descendants of Judah and Benjamin settled in Jerusalem.) From the descendants of Judah: Athaiah son of Uzziah, the son of Zechariah, the son of Amariah, the son of Shephatiah, the son of Mahalalel, a descendant of Perez;'),
('NEH', 11, 5, 'NEH.11.5', 'and Maaseiah son of Baruch, the son of Col-hozeh, the son of Hazaiah, the son of Adaiah, the son of Joiarib, the son of Zechariah, a descendant of Shelah.'),
('NEH', 11, 6, 'NEH.11.6', 'The descendants of Perez who settled in Jerusalem totaled 468 men of valor.'),
('NEH', 11, 7, 'NEH.11.7', 'From the descendants of Benjamin: Sallu son of Meshullam, the son of Joed, the son of Pedaiah, the son of Kolaiah, the son of Maaseiah, the son of Ithiel, the son of Jeshaiah;'),
('NEH', 11, 8, 'NEH.11.8', 'and his followers Gabbai and Sallai—928 men.'),
('NEH', 11, 9, 'NEH.11.9', 'Joel son of Zichri was the officer over them, and Judah son of Hassenuah was over the Second District of the city.'),
('NEH', 11, 10, 'NEH.11.10', 'From the priests: Jedaiah son of Joiarib; Jachin;'),
('NEH', 11, 11, 'NEH.11.11', 'Seraiah son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, the chief official of the house of God;'),
('NEH', 11, 12, 'NEH.11.12', 'and their associates who did the work at the temple—822 men; Adaiah son of Jeroham, the son of Pelaliah, the son of Amzi, the son of Zechariah, the son of Pashhur, the son of Malchijah;'),
('NEH', 11, 13, 'NEH.11.13', 'and his associates, the leaders of families—242 men; Amashai son of Azarel, the son of Ahzai, the son of Meshillemoth, the son of Immer;'),
('NEH', 11, 14, 'NEH.11.14', 'and his associates—128 mighty men of valor. Zabdiel son of Haggedolim was their overseer.'),
('NEH', 11, 15, 'NEH.11.15', 'From the Levites: Shemaiah son of Hasshub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Bunni;'),
('NEH', 11, 16, 'NEH.11.16', 'Shabbethai and Jozabad, two leaders of the Levites, who supervised the work outside the house of God;'),
('NEH', 11, 17, 'NEH.11.17', 'Mattaniah son of Mica, the son of Zabdi, the son of Asaph, who led in thanksgiving and prayer; Bakbukiah, second among his associates; and Abda son of Shammua, the son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun.'),
('NEH', 11, 18, 'NEH.11.18', 'The Levites in the holy city totaled 284.'),
('NEH', 11, 19, 'NEH.11.19', 'And the gatekeepers: Akkub, Talmon, and their associates, who kept watch at the gates—172 men.'),
('NEH', 11, 20, 'NEH.11.20', 'The rest of the Israelites, with the priests and Levites, were in all the villages of Judah, each on his own inheritance.'),
('NEH', 11, 21, 'NEH.11.21', 'The temple servants lived on the hill of Ophel, with Ziha and Gishpa over them.'),
('NEH', 11, 22, 'NEH.11.22', 'Now the overseer of the Levites in Jerusalem was Uzzi son of Bani, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Mica. He was one of Asaph’s descendants, who were the singers in charge of the service of the house of God.'),
('NEH', 11, 23, 'NEH.11.23', 'For there was a command from the king concerning the singers, an ordinance regulating their daily activities.'),
('NEH', 11, 24, 'NEH.11.24', 'Pethahiah son of Meshezabel, a descendant of Zerah son of Judah, was the king’s agent in every matter concerning the people.'),
('NEH', 11, 25, 'NEH.11.25', 'As for the villages with their fields, some of the people of Judah lived in Kiriath-arba, Dibon, Jekabzeel, and their villages;'),
('NEH', 11, 26, 'NEH.11.26', 'in Jeshua, Moladah, and Beth-pelet;'),
('NEH', 11, 27, 'NEH.11.27', 'in Hazar-shual; in Beersheba and its villages;'),
('NEH', 11, 28, 'NEH.11.28', 'in Ziklag; in Meconah and its villages;'),
('NEH', 11, 29, 'NEH.11.29', 'in En-rimmon, Zorah, Jarmuth,'),
('NEH', 11, 30, 'NEH.11.30', 'Zanoah, Adullam, and their villages; in Lachish and its fields; and in Azekah and its villages. So they settled from Beersheba all the way to the Valley of Hinnom.'),
('NEH', 11, 31, 'NEH.11.31', 'The descendants of Benjamin from Geba lived in Michmash, Aija, and Bethel with its villages;'),
('NEH', 11, 32, 'NEH.11.32', 'in Anathoth, Nob, Ananiah,'),
('NEH', 11, 33, 'NEH.11.33', 'Hazor, Ramah, Gittaim,'),
('NEH', 11, 34, 'NEH.11.34', 'Hadid, Zeboim, Neballat,'),
('NEH', 11, 35, 'NEH.11.35', 'Lod, and Ono; and in the Valley of the Craftsmen.'),
('NEH', 11, 36, 'NEH.11.36', 'And some divisions of the Levites of Judah settled in Benjamin.'),
('NEH', 12, 1, 'NEH.12.1', 'Now these are the priests and Levites who went up with Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel and with Jeshua: Seraiah, Jeremiah, Ezra,'),
('NEH', 12, 2, 'NEH.12.2', 'Amariah, Malluch, Hattush,'),
('NEH', 12, 3, 'NEH.12.3', 'Shecaniah, Rehum, Meremoth,'),
('NEH', 12, 4, 'NEH.12.4', 'Iddo, Ginnethon, Abijah,'),
('NEH', 12, 5, 'NEH.12.5', 'Mijamin, Maadiah, Bilgah,'),
('NEH', 12, 6, 'NEH.12.6', 'Shemaiah, Joiarib, Jedaiah,'),
('NEH', 12, 7, 'NEH.12.7', 'Sallu, Amok, Hilkiah, and Jedaiah. These were the leaders of the priests and their associates in the days of Jeshua.'),
('NEH', 12, 8, 'NEH.12.8', 'The Levites were Jeshua, Binnui, Kadmiel, Sherebiah, Judah, and Mattaniah, who, with his associates, led the songs of thanksgiving.'),
('NEH', 12, 9, 'NEH.12.9', 'Bakbukiah and Unni, their associates, stood across from them in the services.'),
('NEH', 12, 10, 'NEH.12.10', 'Jeshua was the father of Joiakim, Joiakim was the father of Eliashib, Eliashib was the father of Joiada,'),
('NEH', 12, 11, 'NEH.12.11', 'Joiada was the father of Jonathan, and Jonathan was the father of Jaddua.'),
('NEH', 12, 12, 'NEH.12.12', 'In the days of Joiakim, these were the heads of the priestly families: of the family of Seraiah, Meraiah; of Jeremiah, Hananiah;'),
('NEH', 12, 13, 'NEH.12.13', 'of Ezra, Meshullam; of Amariah, Jehohanan;'),
('NEH', 12, 14, 'NEH.12.14', 'of Malluchi, Jonathan; of Shebaniah, Joseph;'),
('NEH', 12, 15, 'NEH.12.15', 'of Harim, Adna; of Meraioth, Helkai;'),
('NEH', 12, 16, 'NEH.12.16', 'of Iddo, Zechariah; of Ginnethon, Meshullam;'),
('NEH', 12, 17, 'NEH.12.17', 'of Abijah, Zichri; of Miniamin and of Moadiah, Piltai;'),
('NEH', 12, 18, 'NEH.12.18', 'of Bilgah, Shammua; of Shemaiah, Jonathan;'),
('NEH', 12, 19, 'NEH.12.19', 'of Joiarib, Mattenai; of Jedaiah, Uzzi;'),
('NEH', 12, 20, 'NEH.12.20', 'of Sallai, Kallai; of Amok, Eber;'),
('NEH', 12, 21, 'NEH.12.21', 'of Hilkiah, Hashabiah; and of Jedaiah, Nethanel.'),
('NEH', 12, 22, 'NEH.12.22', 'In the days of Eliashib, Joiada, Johanan, and Jaddua, during the reign of Darius the Persian, the heads of the families of the Levites and priests were recorded.'),
('NEH', 12, 23, 'NEH.12.23', 'As for the descendants of Levi, the family heads up to the days of Johanan son of Eliashib were recorded in the Book of the Chronicles.'),
('NEH', 12, 24, 'NEH.12.24', 'The leaders of the Levites were Hashabiah, Sherebiah, and Jeshua son of Kadmiel, along with their associates, who stood across from them to give praise and thanksgiving as one section alternated with the other, as prescribed by David the man of God.'),
('NEH', 12, 25, 'NEH.12.25', 'Mattaniah, Bakbukiah, Obadiah, Meshullam, Talmon, and Akkub were gatekeepers who guarded the storerooms at the gates.'),
('NEH', 12, 26, 'NEH.12.26', 'They served in the days of Joiakim son of Jeshua, the son of Jozadak, and in the days of Nehemiah the governor and Ezra the priest and scribe.'),
('NEH', 12, 27, 'NEH.12.27', 'At the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem, the Levites were sought out from all their homes and brought to Jerusalem to celebrate the joyous dedication with thanksgiving and singing, accompanied by cymbals, harps, and lyres.'),
('NEH', 12, 28, 'NEH.12.28', 'The singers were also assembled from the region around Jerusalem, from the villages of the Netophathites,'),
('NEH', 12, 29, 'NEH.12.29', 'from Beth-gilgal, and from the fields of Geba and Azmaveth, for they had built villages for themselves around Jerusalem.'),
('NEH', 12, 30, 'NEH.12.30', 'After the priests and Levites had purified themselves, they purified the people, the gates, and the wall.'),
('NEH', 12, 31, 'NEH.12.31', 'Then I brought the leaders of Judah up on the wall, and I appointed two great thanksgiving choirs. One was to proceed along the top of the wall to the right, toward the Dung Gate.'),
('NEH', 12, 32, 'NEH.12.32', 'Hoshaiah and half the leaders of Judah followed,'),
('NEH', 12, 33, 'NEH.12.33', 'along with Azariah, Ezra, Meshullam,'),
('NEH', 12, 34, 'NEH.12.34', 'Judah, Benjamin, Shemaiah, Jeremiah,'),
('NEH', 12, 35, 'NEH.12.35', 'and some of the priests with trumpets, and also Zechariah son of Jonathan, the son of Shemaiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Micaiah, the son of Zaccur, the son of Asaph,'),
('NEH', 12, 36, 'NEH.12.36', 'and his associates—Shemaiah, Azarel, Milalai, Gilalai, Maai, Nethanel, Judah, and Hanani—with the musical instruments prescribed by David the man of God. Ezra the scribe led the procession.'),
('NEH', 12, 37, 'NEH.12.37', 'At the Fountain Gate they went directly up the steps of the City of David on the ascent to the wall and passed above the house of David to the Water Gate on the east.'),
('NEH', 12, 38, 'NEH.12.38', 'The second thanksgiving choir proceeded to the left, and I followed it with half the people along the top of the wall, past the Tower of the Ovens to the Broad Wall,'),
('NEH', 12, 39, 'NEH.12.39', 'over the Gate of Ephraim, the Jeshanah Gate, the Fish Gate, the Tower of Hananel, and the Tower of the Hundred, as far as the Sheep Gate. And they stopped at the Gate of the Guard.'),
('NEH', 12, 40, 'NEH.12.40', 'The two thanksgiving choirs then stood in the house of God, as did I, along with the half of the officials accompanying me,'),
('NEH', 12, 41, 'NEH.12.41', 'as well as the priests with their trumpets—Eliakim, Maaseiah, Miniamin, Micaiah, Elioenai, Zechariah, and Hananiah—'),
('NEH', 12, 42, 'NEH.12.42', 'and also Maaseiah, Shemaiah, Eleazar, Uzzi, Jehohanan, Malchijah, Elam, and Ezer. Then the choirs sang out under the direction of Jezrahiah.'),
('NEH', 12, 43, 'NEH.12.43', 'On that day they offered great sacrifices, rejoicing because God had given them great joy. The women and children also rejoiced, so that the joy of Jerusalem was heard from afar.'),
('NEH', 12, 44, 'NEH.12.44', 'And on that same day men were appointed over the rooms that housed the supplies, contributions, firstfruits, and tithes. The portions specified by the Law for the priests and Levites were gathered into these storerooms from the fields of the villages, because Judah rejoiced over the priests and Levites who were serving.'),
('NEH', 12, 45, 'NEH.12.45', 'They performed the service of their God and the service of purification, along with the singers and gatekeepers, as David and his son Solomon had prescribed.'),
('NEH', 12, 46, 'NEH.12.46', 'For long ago, in the days of David and Asaph, there were directors for the singers and for the songs of praise and thanksgiving to God.'),
('NEH', 12, 47, 'NEH.12.47', 'So in the days of Zerubbabel and Nehemiah, all Israel contributed the daily portions for the singers and gatekeepers. They also set aside daily portions for the Levites, and the Levites set aside daily portions for the descendants of Aaron.'),
('NEH', 13, 1, 'NEH.13.1', 'At that time the Book of Moses was read aloud in the hearing of the people, and in it they found the passage stating that no Ammonite or Moabite should ever enter the assembly of God,'),
('NEH', 13, 2, 'NEH.13.2', 'because they had not met the Israelites with food and water, but had hired Balaam to call down a curse against them (although our God had turned the curse into a blessing).'),
('NEH', 13, 3, 'NEH.13.3', 'As soon as the people heard this law, they excluded from Israel all of foreign descent.'),
('NEH', 13, 4, 'NEH.13.4', 'Now before this, Eliashib the priest, a relative of Tobiah, had been put in charge of the storerooms of the house of our God'),
('NEH', 13, 5, 'NEH.13.5', 'and had prepared for Tobiah a large room where they had previously stored the grain offerings, the frankincense, the temple articles, and the tithes of grain, new wine, and oil prescribed for the Levites, singers, and gatekeepers, along with the contributions for the priests.'),
('NEH', 13, 6, 'NEH.13.6', 'While all this was happening, I was not in Jerusalem, because I had returned to Artaxerxes king of Babylon in the thirty-second year of his reign. Some time later I obtained leave from the king'),
('NEH', 13, 7, 'NEH.13.7', 'to return to Jerusalem. Then I discovered the evil that Eliashib had done on behalf of Tobiah by providing him a room in the courts of the house of God.'),
('NEH', 13, 8, 'NEH.13.8', 'And I was greatly displeased and threw all of Tobiah’s household goods out of the room.'),
('NEH', 13, 9, 'NEH.13.9', 'Then I ordered that the rooms be purified, and I had the articles of the house of God restored to them, along with the grain offerings and frankincense.'),
('NEH', 13, 10, 'NEH.13.10', 'I also learned that because the portions for the Levites had not been given to them, all the Levites and singers responsible for performing the service had gone back to their own fields.'),
('NEH', 13, 11, 'NEH.13.11', 'So I rebuked the officials and asked, “Why has the house of God been neglected?” Then I gathered the Levites and singers together and stationed them at their posts,'),
('NEH', 13, 12, 'NEH.13.12', 'and all Judah brought a tenth of the grain, new wine, and oil into the storerooms.'),
('NEH', 13, 13, 'NEH.13.13', 'I appointed as treasurers over the storerooms Shelemiah the priest, Zadok the scribe, and Pedaiah of the Levites, with Hanan son of Zaccur, the son of Mattaniah, to assist them, because they were considered trustworthy. They were responsible for distributing the supplies to their fellow Levites.'),
('NEH', 13, 14, 'NEH.13.14', 'Remember me for this, O my God, and do not blot out my deeds of loving devotion for the house of my God and for its services.'),
('NEH', 13, 15, 'NEH.13.15', 'In those days I saw people in Judah treading winepresses on the Sabbath and bringing in grain and loading it on donkeys, along with wine, grapes, and figs. All kinds of goods were being brought into Jerusalem on the Sabbath day. So I warned them against selling food on that day.'),
('NEH', 13, 16, 'NEH.13.16', 'Additionally, men of Tyre who lived there were importing fish and all kinds of merchandise and selling them on the Sabbath to the people of Judah in Jerusalem.'),
('NEH', 13, 17, 'NEH.13.17', 'Then I rebuked the nobles of Judah and asked, “What is this evil you are doing—profaning the Sabbath day?'),
('NEH', 13, 18, 'NEH.13.18', 'Did not your forefathers do the same things, so that our God brought all this disaster on us and on this city? And now you are rekindling His wrath against Israel by profaning the Sabbath!”'),
('NEH', 13, 19, 'NEH.13.19', 'When the evening shadows began to fall on the gates of Jerusalem, just before the Sabbath, I ordered that the gates be shut and not opened until after the Sabbath. I posted some of my servants at the gates so that no load could enter on the Sabbath day.'),
('NEH', 13, 20, 'NEH.13.20', 'Once or twice, the merchants and those who sell all kinds of goods camped outside Jerusalem,'),
('NEH', 13, 21, 'NEH.13.21', 'but I warned them, “Why are you camping in front of the wall? If you do it again, I will lay hands on you.” From that time on, they did not return on the Sabbath.'),
('NEH', 13, 22, 'NEH.13.22', 'Then I instructed the Levites to purify themselves and guard the gates in order to keep the Sabbath day holy. Remember me for this as well, O my God, and show me mercy according to Your abundant loving devotion.'),
('NEH', 13, 23, 'NEH.13.23', 'In those days I also saw Jews who had married women from Ashdod, Ammon, and Moab.'),
('NEH', 13, 24, 'NEH.13.24', 'Half of their children spoke the language of Ashdod or of the other peoples, but could not speak the language of Judah.'),
('NEH', 13, 25, 'NEH.13.25', 'I rebuked them and called down curses on them. I beat some of these men and pulled out their hair. Then I made them take an oath before God and said, “You must not give your daughters in marriage to their sons or take their daughters as wives for your sons or for yourselves!'),
('NEH', 13, 26, 'NEH.13.26', 'Did not King Solomon of Israel sin in matters like this? There was not a king like him among many nations, and he was loved by his God, who made him king over all Israel—yet foreign women drew him into sin.'),
('NEH', 13, 27, 'NEH.13.27', 'Must we now hear that you too are doing all this terrible evil and acting unfaithfully against our God by marrying foreign women?”'),
('NEH', 13, 28, 'NEH.13.28', 'Even one of the sons of Jehoiada son of Eliashib the high priest had become a son-in-law to Sanballat the Horonite. Therefore I drove him away from me.'),
('NEH', 13, 29, 'NEH.13.29', 'Remember them, O my God, because they have defiled the priesthood and the covenant of the priesthood and of the Levites.'),
('NEH', 13, 30, 'NEH.13.30', 'Thus I purified the priests and Levites from everything foreign, and I assigned specific duties to each of the priests and Levites.'),
('NEH', 13, 31, 'NEH.13.31', 'I also arranged for contributions of wood at the appointed times, and for the firstfruits. Remember me, O my God, with favor.'),
('EST', 1, 1, 'EST.1.1', 'This is what happened in the days of Xerxes, who reigned over 127 provinces from India to Cush.'),
('EST', 1, 2, 'EST.1.2', 'In those days King Xerxes sat on his royal throne in the citadel of Susa.'),
('EST', 1, 3, 'EST.1.3', 'In the third year of his reign, Xerxes held a feast for all his officials and servants. The military leaders of Persia and Media were there, along with the nobles and princes of the provinces.'),
('EST', 1, 4, 'EST.1.4', 'And for a full 180 days he displayed the glorious riches of his kingdom and the magnificent splendor of his greatness.'),
('EST', 1, 5, 'EST.1.5', 'At the end of this time, in the garden court of the royal palace, the king held a seven-day feast for all the people in the citadel of Susa, from the least to the greatest.'),
('EST', 1, 6, 'EST.1.6', 'Hangings of white and blue linen were fastened with cords of fine white and purple material to silver rings on the marble pillars. Gold and silver couches were arranged on a mosaic pavement of porphyry, marble, mother-of-pearl, and other costly stones.'),
('EST', 1, 7, 'EST.1.7', 'Beverages were served in an array of goblets of gold, each with a different design, and the royal wine flowed freely, according to the king’s bounty.'),
('EST', 1, 8, 'EST.1.8', 'By order of the king, no limit was placed on the drinking, and every official of his household was to serve each man whatever he desired.'),
('EST', 1, 9, 'EST.1.9', 'Queen Vashti also gave a banquet for the women in the royal palace of King Xerxes.'),
('EST', 1, 10, 'EST.1.10', 'On the seventh day, when the king’s heart was merry with wine, he ordered the seven eunuchs who served him—Mehuman, Biztha, Harbona, Bigtha, Abagtha, Zethar, and Carkas—'),
('EST', 1, 11, 'EST.1.11', 'to bring Queen Vashti before him, wearing her royal crown, to display her beauty to the people and officials. For she was beautiful to behold.'),
('EST', 1, 12, 'EST.1.12', 'Queen Vashti, however, refused to come at the king’s command brought by his eunuchs. And the king became furious, and his anger burned within him.'),
('EST', 1, 13, 'EST.1.13', 'Then the king consulted the wise men who knew the times, for it was customary for him to confer with the experts in law and justice.'),
('EST', 1, 14, 'EST.1.14', 'His closest advisors were Carshena, Shethar, Admatha, Tarshish, Meres, Marsena, and Memucan, the seven princes of Persia and Media who had personal access to the king and ranked highest in the kingdom.'),
('EST', 1, 15, 'EST.1.15', '“According to law,” he asked, “what should be done with Queen Vashti, since she refused to obey the command of King Xerxes delivered by the eunuchs?”'),
('EST', 1, 16, 'EST.1.16', 'And in the presence of the king and his princes, Memucan replied, “Queen Vashti has wronged not only the king, but all the princes and the peoples in all the provinces of King Xerxes.'),
('EST', 1, 17, 'EST.1.17', 'For the conduct of the queen will become known to all women, causing them to despise their husbands and say, ‘King Xerxes ordered Queen Vashti to be brought before him, but she did not come.’'),
('EST', 1, 18, 'EST.1.18', 'This very day the noble women of Persia and Media who have heard about the queen’s conduct will say the same thing to all the king’s officials, resulting in much contempt and wrath.'),
('EST', 1, 19, 'EST.1.19', 'So if it pleases the king, let him issue a royal decree, and let it be recorded in the laws of Persia and Media so that it cannot be repealed, that Vashti shall never again enter the presence of King Xerxes, and that her royal position shall be given to a woman better than she.'),
('EST', 1, 20, 'EST.1.20', 'The edict the king issues will be heard throughout his vast kingdom—and so all women, from the least to the greatest, will honor their husbands.”'),
('EST', 1, 21, 'EST.1.21', 'The king and his princes were pleased with this counsel; so the king did as Memucan advised.'),
('EST', 1, 22, 'EST.1.22', 'He sent letters to all the provinces of the kingdom, to each province in its own script and to each people in their own language, proclaiming that every man should be master of his own household.'),
('EST', 2, 1, 'EST.2.1', 'Some time later, when the anger of King Xerxes had subsided, he remembered Vashti and what she had done, and what had been decreed against her.'),
('EST', 2, 2, 'EST.2.2', 'Then the king’s attendants proposed, “Let a search be made for beautiful young virgins for the king,'),
('EST', 2, 3, 'EST.2.3', 'and let the king appoint commissioners in each province of his kingdom to assemble all the beautiful young women into the harem at the citadel of Susa. Let them be placed under the care of Hegai, the king’s eunuch in charge of the women, and let them be given beauty treatments.'),
('EST', 2, 4, 'EST.2.4', 'Then let the young woman who pleases the king become queen in place of Vashti.” This suggestion pleased the king, and he acted accordingly.'),
('EST', 2, 5, 'EST.2.5', 'Now there was at the citadel of Susa a Jewish man from the tribe of Benjamin named Mordecai son of Jair, the son of Shimei, the son of Kish.'),
('EST', 2, 6, 'EST.2.6', 'He had been carried into exile from Jerusalem by Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon among those taken captive with Jeconiah king of Judah.'),
('EST', 2, 7, 'EST.2.7', 'And Mordecai had brought up Hadassah (that is, Esther), the daughter of his uncle, because she did not have a father or mother. The young woman was lovely in form and appearance, and when her father and mother had died, Mordecai had taken her as his own daughter.'),
('EST', 2, 8, 'EST.2.8', 'When the king’s command and edict had been proclaimed, many young women gathered at the citadel of Susa under the care of Hegai. Esther was also taken to the palace and placed under the care of Hegai, the custodian of the women.'),
('EST', 2, 9, 'EST.2.9', 'And the young woman pleased him and obtained his favor, so he quickly provided her with beauty treatments and the special diet. He assigned to her seven select maidservants from the palace and transferred her with them to the best place in the harem.'),
('EST', 2, 10, 'EST.2.10', 'Esther did not reveal her people or her lineage, because Mordecai had instructed her not to do so.'),
('EST', 2, 11, 'EST.2.11', 'And every day Mordecai would walk back and forth in front of the court of the harem to learn about Esther’s welfare and what was happening to her.'),
('EST', 2, 12, 'EST.2.12', 'In the twelve months before her turn to go to King Xerxes, the harem regulation required each young woman to receive beauty treatments with oil of myrrh for six months, and then with perfumes and cosmetics for another six months.'),
('EST', 2, 13, 'EST.2.13', 'When the young woman would go to the king, she was given whatever she requested to take with her from the harem to the king’s palace.'),
('EST', 2, 14, 'EST.2.14', 'She would go there in the evening, and in the morning she would return to a second harem under the care of Shaashgaz, the king’s eunuch in charge of the concubines. She would not return to the king unless he delighted in her and summoned her by name.'),
('EST', 2, 15, 'EST.2.15', 'Now Esther was the daughter of Abihail, the uncle from whom Mordecai had adopted her as his own daughter. And when it was her turn to go to the king, she did not ask for anything except what Hegai, the king’s trusted official in charge of the harem, had advised. And Esther found favor in the eyes of everyone who saw her.'),
('EST', 2, 16, 'EST.2.16', 'She was taken to King Xerxes in the royal palace in the tenth month, the month of Tebeth, in the seventh year of his reign.'),
('EST', 2, 17, 'EST.2.17', 'And the king loved Esther more than all the other women, and she found grace and favor in his sight more than all of the other virgins. So he placed the royal crown upon her head and made her queen in place of Vashti.'),
('EST', 2, 18, 'EST.2.18', 'Then the king held a great banquet, Esther’s banquet, for all his officials and servants. He proclaimed a tax holiday in the provinces and gave gifts worthy of the king’s bounty.'),
('EST', 2, 19, 'EST.2.19', 'When the virgins were assembled a second time, Mordecai was sitting at the king’s gate.'),
('EST', 2, 20, 'EST.2.20', 'Esther still had not revealed her lineage or her people, just as Mordecai had instructed. She obeyed Mordecai’s command, as she had done under his care.'),
('EST', 2, 21, 'EST.2.21', 'In those days, while Mordecai was sitting at the king’s gate, Bigthan and Teresh, two of the king’s eunuchs who guarded the entrance, grew angry and conspired to assassinate King Xerxes.'),
('EST', 2, 22, 'EST.2.22', 'When Mordecai learned of the plot, he reported it to Queen Esther, and she informed the king on Mordecai’s behalf.'),
('EST', 2, 23, 'EST.2.23', 'After the report had been investigated and verified, both officials were hanged on the gallows. And all this was recorded in the Book of the Chronicles in the presence of the king.'),
('EST', 3, 1, 'EST.3.1', 'After these events, King Xerxes honored Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, elevating him to a position above all the princes who were with him.'),
('EST', 3, 2, 'EST.3.2', 'All the royal servants at the king’s gate bowed down and paid homage to Haman, because the king had commanded that this be done for him. But Mordecai would not bow down or pay homage.'),
('EST', 3, 3, 'EST.3.3', 'Then the royal servants at the king’s gate asked Mordecai, “Why do you disobey the command of the king?”'),
('EST', 3, 4, 'EST.3.4', 'Day after day they warned him, but he would not comply. So they reported it to Haman to see whether Mordecai’s behavior would be tolerated, since he had told them he was a Jew.'),
('EST', 3, 5, 'EST.3.5', 'When Haman saw that Mordecai would not bow down or pay him homage, he was filled with rage.'),
('EST', 3, 6, 'EST.3.6', 'And when he learned the identity of Mordecai’s people, he scorned the notion of laying hands on Mordecai alone. Instead, he sought to destroy all of Mordecai’s people, the Jews, throughout the kingdom of Xerxes.'),
('EST', 3, 7, 'EST.3.7', 'In the twelfth year of King Xerxes, in the first month, the month of Nisan, the Pur (that is, the lot) was cast before Haman to determine a day and month. And the lot fell on the twelfth month, the month of Adar.'),
('EST', 3, 8, 'EST.3.8', 'Then Haman informed King Xerxes, “There is a certain people scattered and dispersed among the peoples of every province of your kingdom. Their laws are different from everyone else’s, and they do not obey the king’s laws. So it is not in the king’s best interest to tolerate them.'),
('EST', 3, 9, 'EST.3.9', 'If it pleases the king, let a decree be issued to destroy them, and I will deposit ten thousand talents of silver into the royal treasury to pay those who carry it out.”'),
('EST', 3, 10, 'EST.3.10', 'So the king removed the signet ring from his finger and gave it to Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, the enemy of the Jews.'),
('EST', 3, 11, 'EST.3.11', '“Keep your money,” said the king to Haman. “These people are given to you to do with them as you please.”'),
('EST', 3, 12, 'EST.3.12', 'On the thirteenth day of the first month, the royal scribes were summoned and the order was written exactly as Haman commanded the royal satraps, the governors of each province, and the officials of each people, in the script of each province and the language of every people. It was written in the name of King Xerxes and sealed with the royal signet ring.'),
('EST', 3, 13, 'EST.3.13', 'And the letters were sent by couriers to each of the royal provinces with the order to destroy, kill, and annihilate all the Jews—young and old, women and children—and to plunder their possessions on a single day, the thirteenth day of Adar, the twelfth month.'),
('EST', 3, 14, 'EST.3.14', 'A copy of the text of the edict was to be issued in every province and published to all the people, so that they would be ready on that day.'),
('EST', 3, 15, 'EST.3.15', 'The couriers left, spurred on by the king’s command, and the edict was issued in the citadel of Susa. Then the king and Haman sat down to drink, but the city of Susa was in confusion.'),
('EST', 4, 1, 'EST.4.1', 'When Mordecai learned of all that had happened, he tore his clothes, put on sackcloth and ashes, and went out into the middle of the city, wailing loudly and bitterly.'),
('EST', 4, 2, 'EST.4.2', 'But he went only as far as the king’s gate, because the law prohibited anyone wearing sackcloth from entering that gate.'),
('EST', 4, 3, 'EST.4.3', 'In every province to which the king’s command and edict came, there was great mourning among the Jews. They fasted, wept, and lamented, and many lay in sackcloth and ashes.'),
('EST', 4, 4, 'EST.4.4', 'When Esther’s maidens and eunuchs came and told her about Mordecai, the queen was overcome with distress. She sent clothes for Mordecai to wear instead of his sackcloth, but he would not accept them.'),
('EST', 4, 5, 'EST.4.5', 'Then Esther summoned Hathach, one of the king’s eunuchs appointed to her, and she dispatched him to Mordecai to learn what was troubling him and why.'),
('EST', 4, 6, 'EST.4.6', 'So Hathach went out to Mordecai in the city square in front of the king’s gate,'),
('EST', 4, 7, 'EST.4.7', 'and Mordecai told him all that had happened to him, including the exact amount of money that Haman had promised to pay into the royal treasury in order to destroy the Jews.'),
('EST', 4, 8, 'EST.4.8', 'Mordecai also gave Hathach a copy of the written decree issued in Susa for the destruction of the Jews, to show and explain to Esther, urging her to approach the king, implore his favor, and plead before him for her people.'),
('EST', 4, 9, 'EST.4.9', 'So Hathach went back and relayed Mordecai’s response to Esther.'),
('EST', 4, 10, 'EST.4.10', 'Then Esther spoke to Hathach and instructed him to tell Mordecai,'),
('EST', 4, 11, 'EST.4.11', '“All the royal officials and the people of the king’s provinces know that one law applies to every man or woman who approaches the king in the inner court without being summoned—that he be put to death. Only if the king extends the gold scepter may that person live. But I have not been summoned to appear before the king for the past thirty days.”'),
('EST', 4, 12, 'EST.4.12', 'When Esther’s words were relayed to Mordecai,'),
('EST', 4, 13, 'EST.4.13', 'he sent back to her this reply: “Do not imagine that because you are in the king’s palace you alone will escape the fate of all the Jews.'),
('EST', 4, 14, 'EST.4.14', 'For if you remain silent at this time, relief and deliverance for the Jews will arise from another place, but you and your father’s house will perish. And who knows if perhaps you have come to the kingdom for such a time as this?”'),
('EST', 4, 15, 'EST.4.15', 'Then Esther sent this reply to Mordecai:'),
('EST', 4, 16, 'EST.4.16', '“Go and assemble all the Jews who can be found in Susa, and fast for me. Do not eat or drink for three days, night or day, and I and my maidens will fast as you do. After that, I will go to the king, even though it is against the law. And if I perish, I perish!”'),
('EST', 4, 17, 'EST.4.17', 'So Mordecai went and did all that Esther had instructed him.'),
('EST', 5, 1, 'EST.5.1', 'On the third day, Esther put on her royal robes and stood in the inner court of the palace across from the king’s quarters. The king was sitting on his royal throne in the royal courtroom, facing the entrance.'),
('EST', 5, 2, 'EST.5.2', 'As soon as the king saw Queen Esther standing in the court, she found favor in his sight. The king extended the gold scepter in his hand toward Esther, and she approached and touched the tip of the scepter.'),
('EST', 5, 3, 'EST.5.3', '“What is it, Queen Esther?” the king inquired. “What is your request? Even up to half the kingdom, it will be given to you.”'),
('EST', 5, 4, 'EST.5.4', '“If it pleases the king,” Esther replied, “may the king and Haman come today to the banquet I have prepared for the king.”'),
('EST', 5, 5, 'EST.5.5', '“Hurry,” commanded the king, “and bring Haman, so we can do as Esther has requested.” So the king and Haman went to the banquet that Esther had prepared.'),
('EST', 5, 6, 'EST.5.6', 'And as they drank their wine, the king said to Esther, “What is your petition? It will be given to you. What is your request? Even up to half the kingdom, it will be fulfilled.”'),
('EST', 5, 7, 'EST.5.7', 'Esther replied, “This is my petition and my request:'),
('EST', 5, 8, 'EST.5.8', 'If I have found favor in the sight of the king, and if it pleases the king to grant my petition and fulfill my request, may the king and Haman come tomorrow to the banquet I will prepare for them. Then I will answer the king’s question.”'),
('EST', 5, 9, 'EST.5.9', 'That day Haman went out full of joy and glad of heart. At the king’s gate, however, he saw Mordecai, who did not rise or tremble in fear at his presence. And Haman was filled with rage toward Mordecai.'),
('EST', 5, 10, 'EST.5.10', 'Nevertheless, Haman restrained himself and went home. And calling for his friends and his wife Zeresh,'),
('EST', 5, 11, 'EST.5.11', 'Haman recounted to them his glorious wealth, his many sons, and all the ways the king had honored and promoted him over the other officials and servants.'),
('EST', 5, 12, 'EST.5.12', '“What is more,” Haman added, “Queen Esther invited no one but me to join the king at the banquet she prepared, and I am invited back tomorrow along with the king.'),
('EST', 5, 13, 'EST.5.13', 'Yet none of this satisfies me as long as I see Mordecai the Jew sitting at the king’s gate.”'),
('EST', 5, 14, 'EST.5.14', 'His wife Zeresh and all his friends told him, “Have them build a gallows fifty cubits high, and ask the king in the morning to have Mordecai hanged on it. Then go to the banquet with the king and enjoy yourself.” The advice pleased Haman, and he had the gallows constructed.'),
('EST', 6, 1, 'EST.6.1', 'That night sleep escaped the king; so he ordered the Book of Records, the Chronicles, to be brought in and read to him.'),
('EST', 6, 2, 'EST.6.2', 'And there it was found recorded that Mordecai had exposed Bigthana and Teresh, two of the eunuchs who guarded the king’s entrance, when they had conspired to assassinate King Xerxes.'),
('EST', 6, 3, 'EST.6.3', 'The king inquired, “What honor or dignity has been bestowed on Mordecai for this act?” “Nothing has been done for him,” replied the king’s attendants.'),
('EST', 6, 4, 'EST.6.4', '“Who is in the court?” the king asked. Now Haman had just entered the outer court of the palace to ask the king to hang Mordecai on the gallows he had prepared for him.'),
('EST', 6, 5, 'EST.6.5', 'So the king’s attendants answered him, “Haman is there, standing in the court.” “Bring him in,” ordered the king.'),
('EST', 6, 6, 'EST.6.6', 'Haman entered, and the king asked him, “What should be done for the man whom the king is delighted to honor?” Now Haman thought to himself, “Whom would the king be delighted to honor more than me?”'),
('EST', 6, 7, 'EST.6.7', 'And Haman told the king, “For the man whom the king is delighted to honor,'),
('EST', 6, 8, 'EST.6.8', 'have them bring a royal robe that the king himself has worn and a horse on which the king himself has ridden—one with a royal crest placed on its head.'),
('EST', 6, 9, 'EST.6.9', 'Let the robe and the horse be entrusted to one of the king’s most noble princes. Let them array the man the king wants to honor and parade him on the horse through the city square, proclaiming before him, ‘This is what is done for the man whom the king is delighted to honor!’”'),
('EST', 6, 10, 'EST.6.10', '“Hurry,” said the king to Haman, “and do just as you proposed. Take the robe and the horse to Mordecai the Jew, who is sitting at the king’s gate. Do not neglect anything that you have suggested.”'),
('EST', 6, 11, 'EST.6.11', 'So Haman took the robe and the horse, arrayed Mordecai, and paraded him through the city square, crying out before him, “This is what is done for the man whom the king is delighted to honor!”'),
('EST', 6, 12, 'EST.6.12', 'Then Mordecai returned to the king’s gate. But Haman rushed home, with his head covered in grief.'),
('EST', 6, 13, 'EST.6.13', 'Haman told his wife Zeresh and all his friends everything that had happened. His advisers and his wife Zeresh said to him, “Since Mordecai, before whom your downfall has begun, is Jewish, you will not prevail against him—for surely you will fall before him.”'),
('EST', 6, 14, 'EST.6.14', 'While they were still speaking with Haman, the king’s eunuchs arrived and rushed him to the banquet that Esther had prepared.'),
('EST', 7, 1, 'EST.7.1', 'So the king and Haman went to dine with Esther the queen,'),
('EST', 7, 2, 'EST.7.2', 'and as they drank their wine on that second day, the king asked once more, “Queen Esther, what is your petition? It will be given to you. What is your request? Even up to half the kingdom, it will be fulfilled.”'),
('EST', 7, 3, 'EST.7.3', 'Queen Esther replied, “If I have found favor in your sight, O king, and if it pleases the king, grant me my life as my petition, and the lives of my people as my request.'),
('EST', 7, 4, 'EST.7.4', 'For my people and I have been sold out to destruction, death, and annihilation. If we had merely been sold as menservants and maidservants, I would have remained silent, because no such distress would justify burdening the king.”'),
('EST', 7, 5, 'EST.7.5', 'Then King Xerxes spoke up and asked Queen Esther, “Who is this, and where is the one who would devise such a scheme?”'),
('EST', 7, 6, 'EST.7.6', 'Esther replied, “The adversary and enemy is this wicked man—Haman!” And Haman stood in terror before the king and queen.'),
('EST', 7, 7, 'EST.7.7', 'In his fury, the king arose from drinking his wine and went to the palace garden, while Haman stayed behind to beg Queen Esther for his life, for he realized that the king was planning a terrible fate for him.'),
('EST', 7, 8, 'EST.7.8', 'Just as the king returned from the palace garden to the banquet hall, Haman was falling on the couch where Esther was reclining. The king exclaimed, “Would he actually assault the queen while I am in the palace?” As soon as the words had left the king’s mouth, they covered Haman’s face.'),
('EST', 7, 9, 'EST.7.9', 'Then Harbonah, one of the eunuchs attending the king, said: “There is a gallows fifty cubits high at Haman’s house. He had it built for Mordecai, who gave the report that saved the king.” “Hang him on it!” declared the king.'),
('EST', 7, 10, 'EST.7.10', 'So they hanged Haman on the gallows he had prepared for Mordecai. Then the fury of the king subsided.'),
('EST', 8, 1, 'EST.8.1', 'That same day King Xerxes awarded Queen Esther the estate of Haman, the enemy of the Jews. And Mordecai entered the king’s presence because Esther had revealed his relation to her.'),
('EST', 8, 2, 'EST.8.2', 'The king removed the signet ring he had recovered from Haman and presented it to Mordecai. And Esther appointed Mordecai over the estate of Haman.'),
('EST', 8, 3, 'EST.8.3', 'And once again, Esther addressed the king. She fell at his feet weeping and begged him to revoke the evil scheme of Haman the Agagite, which he had devised against the Jews.'),
('EST', 8, 4, 'EST.8.4', 'The king extended the gold scepter toward Esther, and she arose and stood before the king.'),
('EST', 8, 5, 'EST.8.5', '“If it pleases the king,” she said, “and if I have found favor in his sight, and the matter seems proper to the king, and I am pleasing in his sight, may an order be written to revoke the letters that the scheming Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, wrote to destroy the Jews in all the king’s provinces.'),
('EST', 8, 6, 'EST.8.6', 'For how could I bear to see the disaster that would befall my people? How could I bear to see the destruction of my kindred?”'),
('EST', 8, 7, 'EST.8.7', 'So King Xerxes said to Esther the Queen and Mordecai the Jew, “Behold, I have given Haman’s estate to Esther, and he was hanged on the gallows because he attacked the Jews.'),
('EST', 8, 8, 'EST.8.8', 'Now you may write in the king’s name as you please regarding the Jews, and seal it with the royal signet ring. For a decree that is written in the name of the king and sealed with the royal signet ring cannot be revoked.”'),
('EST', 8, 9, 'EST.8.9', 'At once the royal scribes were summoned, and on the twenty-third day of the third month (the month of Sivan), they recorded all of Mordecai’s orders to the Jews and to the satraps, governors, and princes of the 127 provinces from India to Cush—writing to each province in its own script, to every people in their own language, and to the Jews in their own script and language.'),
('EST', 8, 10, 'EST.8.10', 'Mordecai wrote in the name of King Xerxes and sealed it with the royal signet ring. He sent the documents by mounted couriers riding on swift horses bred from the royal mares.'),
('EST', 8, 11, 'EST.8.11', 'By these letters the king permitted the Jews in each and every city the right to assemble and defend themselves, to destroy, kill, and annihilate all the forces of any people or province hostile to them, including women and children, and to plunder their possessions.'),
('EST', 8, 12, 'EST.8.12', 'The single day appointed throughout all the provinces of King Xerxes was the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, the month of Adar.'),
('EST', 8, 13, 'EST.8.13', 'A copy of the text of the edict was to be issued in every province and published to all the people, so that the Jews would be ready on that day to avenge themselves on their enemies.'),
('EST', 8, 14, 'EST.8.14', 'The couriers rode out in haste on their royal horses, pressed on by the command of the king. And the edict was also issued in the citadel of Susa.'),
('EST', 8, 15, 'EST.8.15', 'Mordecai went out from the presence of the king in royal garments of blue and white, with a large gold crown and a purple robe of fine linen. And the city of Susa shouted and rejoiced.'),
('EST', 8, 16, 'EST.8.16', 'For the Jews it was a time of light and gladness, of joy and honor.'),
('EST', 8, 17, 'EST.8.17', 'In every province and every city, wherever the king’s edict and decree reached, there was joy and gladness among the Jews, with feasting and celebrating. And many of the people of the land themselves became Jews, because the fear of the Jews had fallen upon them.'),
('EST', 9, 1, 'EST.9.1', 'On the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, the month of Adar, the king’s command and edict were to be executed. On this day the enemies of the Jews had hoped to overpower them, but their plan was overturned and the Jews overpowered those who hated them.'),
('EST', 9, 2, 'EST.9.2', 'In each of the provinces of King Xerxes, the Jews assembled in their cities to attack those who sought to harm them. No man could withstand them, because the fear of them had fallen upon all peoples.'),
('EST', 9, 3, 'EST.9.3', 'And all the officials of the provinces, the satraps, the governors, and the king’s administrators helped the Jews, because the fear of Mordecai had fallen upon them.'),
('EST', 9, 4, 'EST.9.4', 'For Mordecai exercised great power in the palace, and his fame spread throughout the provinces as he became more and more powerful.'),
('EST', 9, 5, 'EST.9.5', 'The Jews put all their enemies to the sword, killing and destroying them, and they did as they pleased to those who hated them.'),
('EST', 9, 6, 'EST.9.6', 'In the citadel of Susa, the Jews killed and destroyed five hundred men,'),
('EST', 9, 7, 'EST.9.7', 'including Parshandatha, Dalphon, Aspatha,'),
('EST', 9, 8, 'EST.9.8', 'Poratha, Adalia, Aridatha,'),
('EST', 9, 9, 'EST.9.9', 'Parmashta, Arisai, Aridai, and Vaizatha.'),
('EST', 9, 10, 'EST.9.10', 'They killed these ten sons of Haman son of Hammedatha, the enemy of the Jews, but they did not lay a hand on the plunder.'),
('EST', 9, 11, 'EST.9.11', 'On that day the number of those killed in the citadel of Susa was reported to the king,'),
('EST', 9, 12, 'EST.9.12', 'who said to Queen Esther, “In the citadel of Susa the Jews have killed and destroyed five hundred men, including Haman’s ten sons. What have they done in the rest of the royal provinces? Now what is your petition? It will be given to you. And what further do you request? It will be fulfilled.”'),
('EST', 9, 13, 'EST.9.13', 'Esther replied, “If it pleases the king, may the Jews in Susa also have tomorrow to carry out today’s edict, and may the bodies of Haman’s ten sons be hanged on the gallows.”'),
('EST', 9, 14, 'EST.9.14', 'So the king commanded that this be done. An edict was issued in Susa, and they hanged the ten sons of Haman.'),
('EST', 9, 15, 'EST.9.15', 'On the fourteenth day of the month of Adar, the Jews in Susa came together again and put to death three hundred men there, but they did not lay a hand on the plunder.'),
('EST', 9, 16, 'EST.9.16', 'The rest of the Jews in the royal provinces also assembled to defend themselves and rid themselves of their enemies. They killed 75,000 who hated them, but they did not lay a hand on the plunder.'),
('EST', 9, 17, 'EST.9.17', 'This was done on the thirteenth day of the month of Adar, and on the fourteenth day they rested, making it a day of feasting and joy.'),
('EST', 9, 18, 'EST.9.18', 'The Jews in Susa, however, had assembled on the thirteenth and the fourteenth days of the month. So they rested on the fifteenth day, making it a day of feasting and joy.'),
('EST', 9, 19, 'EST.9.19', 'This is why the rural Jews, who live in the villages, observe the fourteenth day of the month of Adar as a day of joy and feasting. It is a holiday for sending gifts to one another.'),
('EST', 9, 20, 'EST.9.20', 'Mordecai recorded these events and sent letters to all the Jews in all the provinces of King Xerxes, both near and far,'),
('EST', 9, 21, 'EST.9.21', 'to establish among them an annual celebration on the fourteenth and fifteenth days of the month of Adar'),
('EST', 9, 22, 'EST.9.22', 'as the days on which the Jews gained rest from their enemies and the month in which their sorrow turned to joy and their mourning into a holiday. He wrote that these were to be days of feasting and joy, of sending gifts to one another and to the poor.'),
('EST', 9, 23, 'EST.9.23', 'So the Jews agreed to continue the custom they had started, as Mordecai had written to them.'),
('EST', 9, 24, 'EST.9.24', 'For Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, the enemy of all the Jews, had plotted against the Jews to destroy them and had cast the Pur (that is, the lot) to crush and destroy them.'),
('EST', 9, 25, 'EST.9.25', 'But when it came before the king, he commanded by letter that the wicked scheme which Haman had devised against the Jews should come back upon his own head, and that he and his sons should be hanged on the gallows.'),
('EST', 9, 26, 'EST.9.26', 'Therefore these days are called Purim, from the word Pur. Because of all the instructions in this letter, and because of all they had seen and experienced,'),
('EST', 9, 27, 'EST.9.27', 'the Jews bound themselves to establish the custom that they and their descendants and all who join them should not fail to celebrate these two days at the appointed time each and every year, according to their regulation.'),
('EST', 9, 28, 'EST.9.28', 'These days should be remembered and celebrated by every generation, family, province, and city, so that these days of Purim should not fail to be observed among the Jews, nor should the memory of them fade from their descendants.'),
('EST', 9, 29, 'EST.9.29', 'So Queen Esther daughter of Abihail, along with Mordecai the Jew, wrote with full authority to confirm this second letter concerning Purim.'),
('EST', 9, 30, 'EST.9.30', 'And Mordecai sent letters with words of peace and truth to all the Jews in the 127 provinces of the kingdom of Xerxes,'),
('EST', 9, 31, 'EST.9.31', 'in order to confirm these days of Purim at their appointed time, just as Mordecai the Jew and Queen Esther had established them and had committed themselves and their descendants to the times of fasting and lamentation.'),
('EST', 9, 32, 'EST.9.32', 'So Esther’s decree confirmed these regulations about Purim, which were written into the record.'),
('EST', 10, 1, 'EST.10.1', 'Now King Xerxes imposed tribute throughout the land, even to its farthest shores.'),
('EST', 10, 2, 'EST.10.2', 'And all of Mordecai’s powerful and magnificent accomplishments, together with the full account of the greatness to which the king had raised him, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Media and Persia?'),
('EST', 10, 3, 'EST.10.3', 'For Mordecai the Jew was second only to King Xerxes, preeminent among the Jews and highly favored by his many kinsmen, seeking the good of his people and speaking peace to all his countrymen.'),
('JOB', 1, 1, 'JOB.1.1', 'There was a man in the land of Uz whose name was Job. And this man was blameless and upright, fearing God and shunning evil.'),
('JOB', 1, 2, 'JOB.1.2', 'He had seven sons and three daughters,'),
('JOB', 1, 3, 'JOB.1.3', 'and he owned 7,000 sheep, 3,000 camels, 500 yoke of oxen, 500 female donkeys, and a very large number of servants. Job was the greatest man of all the people of the East.'),
('JOB', 1, 4, 'JOB.1.4', 'Job’s sons would take turns holding feasts in their homes, and they would invite their three sisters to eat and drink with them.'),
('JOB', 1, 5, 'JOB.1.5', 'And when the days of feasting were over, Job would send for his children to purify them, rising early in the morning to offer burnt offerings for all of them. For Job thought, “Perhaps my children have sinned and cursed God in their hearts.” This was Job’s regular practice.'),
('JOB', 1, 6, 'JOB.1.6', 'One day the sons of God came to present themselves before the LORD, and Satan also came with them.'),
('JOB', 1, 7, 'JOB.1.7', '“Where have you come from?” said the LORD to Satan. “From roaming through the earth,” he replied, “and walking back and forth in it.”'),
('JOB', 1, 8, 'JOB.1.8', 'Then the LORD said to Satan, “Have you considered My servant Job? For there is no one on earth like him, a man who is blameless and upright, who fears God and shuns evil.”'),
('JOB', 1, 9, 'JOB.1.9', 'Satan answered the LORD, “Does Job fear God for nothing?'),
('JOB', 1, 10, 'JOB.1.10', 'Have You not placed a hedge on every side around him and his household and all that he owns? You have blessed the work of his hands, and his possessions have increased in the land.'),
('JOB', 1, 11, 'JOB.1.11', 'But stretch out Your hand and strike all that he has, and he will surely curse You to Your face.”'),
('JOB', 1, 12, 'JOB.1.12', '“Very well,” said the LORD to Satan. “Everything he has is in your hands, but you must not lay a hand on the man himself.” Then Satan went out from the presence of the LORD.'),
('JOB', 1, 13, 'JOB.1.13', 'One day, while Job’s sons and daughters were eating and drinking wine in their oldest brother’s house,'),
('JOB', 1, 14, 'JOB.1.14', 'a messenger came and reported to Job: “While the oxen were plowing and the donkeys were grazing nearby,'),
('JOB', 1, 15, 'JOB.1.15', 'the Sabeans swooped down and took them away. They put the servants to the sword, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”'),
('JOB', 1, 16, 'JOB.1.16', 'While he was still speaking, another messenger came and reported: “The fire of God fell from heaven. It burned and consumed the sheep and the servants, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”'),
('JOB', 1, 17, 'JOB.1.17', 'While he was still speaking, another messenger came and reported: “The Chaldeans formed three bands, raided the camels, and took them away. They put the servants to the sword, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”'),
('JOB', 1, 18, 'JOB.1.18', 'While he was still speaking, another messenger came and reported: “Your sons and daughters were eating and drinking wine in their oldest brother’s house,'),
('JOB', 1, 19, 'JOB.1.19', 'when suddenly a mighty wind swept in from the desert and struck the four corners of the house. It collapsed on the young people and they are dead, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”'),
('JOB', 1, 20, 'JOB.1.20', 'Then Job stood up, tore his robe, and shaved his head. He fell to the ground and worshiped,'),
('JOB', 1, 21, 'JOB.1.21', 'saying: “Naked I came from my mother’s womb, and naked I will return. The LORD gave, and the LORD has taken away. Blessed be the name of the LORD.”'),
('JOB', 1, 22, 'JOB.1.22', 'In all this, Job did not sin or charge God with wrongdoing.'),
('JOB', 2, 1, 'JOB.2.1', 'On another day the sons of God came to present themselves before the LORD, and Satan also came with them to present himself before Him.'),
('JOB', 2, 2, 'JOB.2.2', '“Where have you come from?” said the LORD to Satan. “From roaming through the earth,” he replied, “and walking back and forth in it.”'),
('JOB', 2, 3, 'JOB.2.3', 'Then the LORD said to Satan, “Have you considered My servant Job? For there is no one on earth like him, a man who is blameless and upright, who fears God and shuns evil. He still retains his integrity, even though you incited Me against him to ruin him without cause.”'),
('JOB', 2, 4, 'JOB.2.4', '“Skin for skin!” Satan replied. “A man will give up all he owns in exchange for his life.'),
('JOB', 2, 5, 'JOB.2.5', 'But stretch out Your hand and strike his flesh and bones, and he will surely curse You to Your face.”'),
('JOB', 2, 6, 'JOB.2.6', '“Very well,” said the LORD to Satan. “He is in your hands, but you must spare his life.”'),
('JOB', 2, 7, 'JOB.2.7', 'So Satan went out from the presence of the LORD and infected Job with terrible boils from the soles of his feet to the crown of his head.'),
('JOB', 2, 8, 'JOB.2.8', 'And Job took a piece of broken pottery to scrape himself as he sat among the ashes.'),
('JOB', 2, 9, 'JOB.2.9', 'Then Job’s wife said to him, “Do you still retain your integrity? Curse God and die!”'),
('JOB', 2, 10, 'JOB.2.10', '“You speak as a foolish woman speaks,” he told her. “Should we accept from God only good and not adversity?” In all this, Job did not sin in what he said.'),
('JOB', 2, 11, 'JOB.2.11', 'Now when Job’s three friends—Eliphaz the Temanite, Bildad the Shuhite, and Zophar the Naamathite—heard about all this adversity that had come upon him, each of them came from his home, and they met together to go and sympathize with Job and comfort him.'),
('JOB', 2, 12, 'JOB.2.12', 'When they lifted up their eyes from afar, they could barely recognize Job. They began to weep aloud, and each man tore his robe and threw dust in the air over his head.'),
('JOB', 2, 13, 'JOB.2.13', 'Then they sat on the ground with him for seven days and seven nights, but no one spoke a word to him because they saw how intense his suffering was.'),
('JOB', 3, 1, 'JOB.3.1', 'After this, Job opened his mouth and cursed the day of his birth.'),
('JOB', 3, 2, 'JOB.3.2', 'And this is what he said:'),
('JOB', 3, 3, 'JOB.3.3', '“May the day of my birth perish, and the night it was said, ‘A boy is conceived.’'),
('JOB', 3, 4, 'JOB.3.4', 'If only that day had turned to darkness! May God above disregard it; may no light shine upon it.'),
('JOB', 3, 5, 'JOB.3.5', 'May darkness and gloom reclaim it, and a cloud settle over it; may the blackness of the day overwhelm it.'),
('JOB', 3, 6, 'JOB.3.6', 'If only darkness had taken that night away! May it not appear among the days of the year; may it never be entered in any of the months.'),
('JOB', 3, 7, 'JOB.3.7', 'Behold, may that night be barren; may no joyful voice come into it.'),
('JOB', 3, 8, 'JOB.3.8', 'May it be cursed by those who curse the day—those prepared to rouse Leviathan.'),
('JOB', 3, 9, 'JOB.3.9', 'May its morning stars grow dark; may it wait in vain for daylight; may it not see the breaking of dawn.'),
('JOB', 3, 10, 'JOB.3.10', 'For that night did not shut the doors of the womb to hide the sorrow from my eyes.'),
('JOB', 3, 11, 'JOB.3.11', 'Why did I not perish at birth; why did I not die as I came from the womb?'),
('JOB', 3, 12, 'JOB.3.12', 'Why were there knees to receive me, and breasts that I should be nursed?'),
('JOB', 3, 13, 'JOB.3.13', 'For now I would be lying down in peace; I would be asleep and at rest'),
('JOB', 3, 14, 'JOB.3.14', 'with kings and counselors of the earth, who built for themselves cities now in ruins,'),
('JOB', 3, 15, 'JOB.3.15', 'or with princes who had gold, who filled their houses with silver.'),
('JOB', 3, 16, 'JOB.3.16', 'Or why was I not hidden like a stillborn child, like an infant who never sees daylight?'),
('JOB', 3, 17, 'JOB.3.17', 'There the wicked cease from raging, and there the weary find rest.'),
('JOB', 3, 18, 'JOB.3.18', 'The captives enjoy their ease; they do not hear the voice of the oppressor.'),
('JOB', 3, 19, 'JOB.3.19', 'Both small and great are there, and the slave is freed from his master.'),
('JOB', 3, 20, 'JOB.3.20', 'Why is light given to the miserable, and life to the bitter of soul,'),
('JOB', 3, 21, 'JOB.3.21', 'who long for death that does not come, and search for it like hidden treasure,'),
('JOB', 3, 22, 'JOB.3.22', 'who rejoice and greatly exult when they reach the grave?'),
('JOB', 3, 23, 'JOB.3.23', 'Why is life given to a man whose way is hidden, whom God has hedged in?'),
('JOB', 3, 24, 'JOB.3.24', 'I sigh when food is put before me, and my groans pour out like water.'),
('JOB', 3, 25, 'JOB.3.25', 'For the thing I feared has overtaken me, and what I dreaded has befallen me.'),
('JOB', 3, 26, 'JOB.3.26', 'I am not at ease or quiet; I have no rest, for trouble has come.”'),
('JOB', 4, 1, 'JOB.4.1', 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite replied:'),
('JOB', 4, 2, 'JOB.4.2', '“If one ventures a word with you, will you be wearied? Yet who can keep from speaking?'),
('JOB', 4, 3, 'JOB.4.3', 'Surely you have instructed many, and have strengthened their feeble hands.'),
('JOB', 4, 4, 'JOB.4.4', 'Your words have steadied those who stumbled; you have braced the knees that were buckling.'),
('JOB', 4, 5, 'JOB.4.5', 'But now trouble has come upon you, and you are weary. It strikes you, and you are dismayed.'),
('JOB', 4, 6, 'JOB.4.6', 'Is your reverence not your confidence, and the uprightness of your ways your hope?'),
('JOB', 4, 7, 'JOB.4.7', 'Consider now, I plead: Who, being innocent, has ever perished? Or where have the upright been destroyed?'),
('JOB', 4, 8, 'JOB.4.8', 'As I have observed, those who plow iniquity and those who sow trouble reap the same.'),
('JOB', 4, 9, 'JOB.4.9', 'By the breath of God they perish, and by the blast of His anger they are consumed.'),
('JOB', 4, 10, 'JOB.4.10', 'The lion may roar, and the fierce lion may growl, yet the teeth of the young lions are broken.'),
('JOB', 4, 11, 'JOB.4.11', 'The old lion perishes for lack of prey, and the cubs of the lioness are scattered.'),
('JOB', 4, 12, 'JOB.4.12', 'Now a word came to me secretly; my ears caught a whisper of it.'),
('JOB', 4, 13, 'JOB.4.13', 'In disquieting visions in the night, when deep sleep falls on men,'),
('JOB', 4, 14, 'JOB.4.14', 'fear and trembling came over me and made all my bones shudder.'),
('JOB', 4, 15, 'JOB.4.15', 'Then a spirit glided past my face, and the hair on my body bristled.'),
('JOB', 4, 16, 'JOB.4.16', 'It stood still, but I could not discern its appearance; a form loomed before my eyes, and I heard a whispering voice:'),
('JOB', 4, 17, 'JOB.4.17', '‘Can a mortal be more righteous than God, or a man more pure than his Maker?'),
('JOB', 4, 18, 'JOB.4.18', 'If God puts no trust in His servants, and He charges His angels with error,'),
('JOB', 4, 19, 'JOB.4.19', 'how much more those who dwell in houses of clay, whose foundations are in the dust, who can be crushed like a moth!'),
('JOB', 4, 20, 'JOB.4.20', 'They are smashed to pieces from dawn to dusk; unnoticed, they perish forever.'),
('JOB', 4, 21, 'JOB.4.21', 'Are not their tent cords pulled up, so that they die without wisdom?’'),
('JOB', 5, 1, 'JOB.5.1', '“Call out if you please, but who will answer? To which of the holy ones will you turn?'),
('JOB', 5, 2, 'JOB.5.2', 'For resentment kills a fool, and envy slays the simple.'),
('JOB', 5, 3, 'JOB.5.3', 'I have seen a fool taking root, but suddenly his house was cursed.'),
('JOB', 5, 4, 'JOB.5.4', 'His sons are far from safety, crushed in court without a defender.'),
('JOB', 5, 5, 'JOB.5.5', 'The hungry consume his harvest, taking it even from the thorns, and the thirsty pant after his wealth.'),
('JOB', 5, 6, 'JOB.5.6', 'For distress does not spring from the dust, and trouble does not sprout from the ground.'),
('JOB', 5, 7, 'JOB.5.7', 'Yet man is born to trouble as surely as sparks fly upward.'),
('JOB', 5, 8, 'JOB.5.8', 'However, if I were you, I would appeal to God and lay my cause before Him—'),
('JOB', 5, 9, 'JOB.5.9', 'the One who does great and unsearchable things, wonders without number.'),
('JOB', 5, 10, 'JOB.5.10', 'He gives rain to the earth and sends water upon the fields.'),
('JOB', 5, 11, 'JOB.5.11', 'He sets the lowly on high, so that mourners are lifted to safety.'),
('JOB', 5, 12, 'JOB.5.12', 'He thwarts the schemes of the crafty, so that their hands find no success.'),
('JOB', 5, 13, 'JOB.5.13', 'He catches the wise in their craftiness, and sweeps away the plans of the cunning.'),
('JOB', 5, 14, 'JOB.5.14', 'They encounter darkness by day and grope at noon as in the night.'),
('JOB', 5, 15, 'JOB.5.15', 'He saves the needy from the sword in their mouth and from the clutches of the powerful.'),
('JOB', 5, 16, 'JOB.5.16', 'So the poor have hope, and injustice shuts its mouth.'),
('JOB', 5, 17, 'JOB.5.17', 'Blessed indeed is the man whom God corrects; so do not despise the discipline of the Almighty.'),
('JOB', 5, 18, 'JOB.5.18', 'For He wounds, but He also binds; He strikes, but His hands also heal.'),
('JOB', 5, 19, 'JOB.5.19', 'He will rescue you from six calamities; no harm will touch you in seven.'),
('JOB', 5, 20, 'JOB.5.20', 'In famine He will redeem you from death, and in battle from the stroke of the sword.'),
('JOB', 5, 21, 'JOB.5.21', 'You will be hidden from the scourge of the tongue, and will not fear havoc when it comes.'),
('JOB', 5, 22, 'JOB.5.22', 'You will laugh at destruction and famine, and need not fear the beasts of the earth.'),
('JOB', 5, 23, 'JOB.5.23', 'For you will have a covenant with the stones of the field, and the wild animals will be at peace with you.'),
('JOB', 5, 24, 'JOB.5.24', 'You will know that your tent is secure, and find nothing amiss when inspecting your home.'),
('JOB', 5, 25, 'JOB.5.25', 'You will know that your offspring will be many, your descendants like the grass of the earth.'),
('JOB', 5, 26, 'JOB.5.26', 'You will come to the grave in full vigor, like a sheaf of grain gathered in season.'),
('JOB', 5, 27, 'JOB.5.27', 'Indeed, we have investigated, and it is true! So hear it and know for yourself.”'),
('JOB', 6, 1, 'JOB.6.1', 'Then Job replied:'),
('JOB', 6, 2, 'JOB.6.2', '“If only my grief could be weighed and placed with my calamity on the scales.'),
('JOB', 6, 3, 'JOB.6.3', 'For then it would outweigh the sand of the seas—no wonder my words have been rash.'),
('JOB', 6, 4, 'JOB.6.4', 'For the arrows of the Almighty have pierced me; my spirit drinks in their poison; the terrors of God are arrayed against me.'),
('JOB', 6, 5, 'JOB.6.5', 'Does a wild donkey bray over fresh grass, or an ox low over its fodder?'),
('JOB', 6, 6, 'JOB.6.6', 'Is tasteless food eaten without salt, or is there flavor in the white of an egg?'),
('JOB', 6, 7, 'JOB.6.7', 'My soul refuses to touch them; they are loathsome food to me.'),
('JOB', 6, 8, 'JOB.6.8', 'If only my request were granted and God would fulfill my hope:'),
('JOB', 6, 9, 'JOB.6.9', 'that God would be willing to crush me, to unleash His hand and cut me off!'),
('JOB', 6, 10, 'JOB.6.10', 'It still brings me comfort, and joy through unrelenting pain, that I have not denied the words of the Holy One.'),
('JOB', 6, 11, 'JOB.6.11', 'What strength do I have, that I should still hope? What is my future, that I should be patient?'),
('JOB', 6, 12, 'JOB.6.12', 'Is my strength like that of stone, or my flesh made of bronze?'),
('JOB', 6, 13, 'JOB.6.13', 'Is there any help within me now that success is driven from me?'),
('JOB', 6, 14, 'JOB.6.14', 'A despairing man should have the kindness of his friend, even if he forsakes the fear of the Almighty.'),
('JOB', 6, 15, 'JOB.6.15', 'But my brothers are as faithless as wadis, as seasonal streams that overflow,'),
('JOB', 6, 16, 'JOB.6.16', 'darkened because of the ice and the inflow of melting snow,'),
('JOB', 6, 17, 'JOB.6.17', 'but ceasing in the dry season and vanishing from their channels in the heat.'),
('JOB', 6, 18, 'JOB.6.18', 'Caravans turn aside from their routes; they go into the wasteland and perish.'),
('JOB', 6, 19, 'JOB.6.19', 'The caravans of Tema look for water; the travelers of Sheba hope to find it.'),
('JOB', 6, 20, 'JOB.6.20', 'They are confounded because they had hoped; their arrival brings disappointment.'),
('JOB', 6, 21, 'JOB.6.21', 'For now you are of no help; you see terror, and you are afraid.'),
('JOB', 6, 22, 'JOB.6.22', 'Have I ever said, ‘Give me something; offer me a bribe from your wealth;'),
('JOB', 6, 23, 'JOB.6.23', 'deliver me from the hand of the enemy; redeem me from the grasp of the ruthless’?'),
('JOB', 6, 24, 'JOB.6.24', 'Teach me, and I will be silent. Help me understand how I have erred.'),
('JOB', 6, 25, 'JOB.6.25', 'How painful are honest words! But what does your argument prove?'),
('JOB', 6, 26, 'JOB.6.26', 'Do you intend to correct my words, and treat as wind my cry of despair?'),
('JOB', 6, 27, 'JOB.6.27', 'You would even cast lots for an orphan and barter away your friend.'),
('JOB', 6, 28, 'JOB.6.28', 'But now, please look at me. Would I lie to your face?'),
('JOB', 6, 29, 'JOB.6.29', 'Reconsider; do not be unjust. Reconsider, for my righteousness is at stake.'),
('JOB', 6, 30, 'JOB.6.30', 'Is there iniquity on my tongue? Can my mouth not discern malice?'),
('JOB', 7, 1, 'JOB.7.1', '“Is not man consigned to labor on earth? Are not his days like those of a hired hand?'),
('JOB', 7, 2, 'JOB.7.2', 'Like a slave he longs for shade; like a hireling he waits for his wages.'),
('JOB', 7, 3, 'JOB.7.3', 'So I am allotted months of futility, and nights of misery are appointed to me.'),
('JOB', 7, 4, 'JOB.7.4', 'When I lie down I think: ‘When will I get up?’ But the night drags on, and I toss and turn until dawn.'),
('JOB', 7, 5, 'JOB.7.5', 'My flesh is clothed with worms and encrusted with dirt; my skin is cracked and festering.'),
('JOB', 7, 6, 'JOB.7.6', 'My days are swifter than a weaver’s shuttle; they come to an end without hope.'),
('JOB', 7, 7, 'JOB.7.7', 'Remember that my life is but a breath. My eyes will never again see happiness.'),
('JOB', 7, 8, 'JOB.7.8', 'The eye that beholds me will no longer see me. You will look for me, but I will be no more.'),
('JOB', 7, 9, 'JOB.7.9', 'As a cloud vanishes and is gone, so he who goes down to Sheol does not come back up.'),
('JOB', 7, 10, 'JOB.7.10', 'He never returns to his house; his place remembers him no more.'),
('JOB', 7, 11, 'JOB.7.11', 'Therefore I will not restrain my mouth; I will speak in the anguish of my spirit; I will complain in the bitterness of my soul.'),
('JOB', 7, 12, 'JOB.7.12', 'Am I the sea, or the monster of the deep, that You must keep me under guard?'),
('JOB', 7, 13, 'JOB.7.13', 'When I think my bed will comfort me and my couch will ease my complaint,'),
('JOB', 7, 14, 'JOB.7.14', 'then You frighten me with dreams and terrify me with visions,'),
('JOB', 7, 15, 'JOB.7.15', 'so that I would prefer strangling and death over my life in this body.'),
('JOB', 7, 16, 'JOB.7.16', 'I loathe my life! I would not live forever. Leave me alone, for my days are but a breath.'),
('JOB', 7, 17, 'JOB.7.17', 'What is man that You should exalt him, that You should set Your heart upon him,'),
('JOB', 7, 18, 'JOB.7.18', 'that You attend to him every morning, and test him every moment?'),
('JOB', 7, 19, 'JOB.7.19', 'Will You never look away from me, or leave me alone to swallow my spittle?'),
('JOB', 7, 20, 'JOB.7.20', 'If I have sinned, what have I done to You, O watcher of mankind? Why have You made me Your target, so that I am a burden to You?'),
('JOB', 7, 21, 'JOB.7.21', 'Why do You not pardon my transgression and take away my iniquity? For soon I will lie down in the dust; You will seek me, but I will be no more.”'),
('JOB', 8, 1, 'JOB.8.1', 'Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:'),
('JOB', 8, 2, 'JOB.8.2', '“How long will you go on saying such things? The words of your mouth are a blustering wind.'),
('JOB', 8, 3, 'JOB.8.3', 'Does God pervert justice? Does the Almighty pervert what is right?'),
('JOB', 8, 4, 'JOB.8.4', 'When your children sinned against Him, He gave them over to their rebellion.'),
('JOB', 8, 5, 'JOB.8.5', 'But if you would earnestly seek God and ask the Almighty for mercy,'),
('JOB', 8, 6, 'JOB.8.6', 'if you are pure and upright, even now He will rouse Himself on your behalf and restore your righteous estate.'),
('JOB', 8, 7, 'JOB.8.7', 'Though your beginnings were modest, your latter days will flourish.'),
('JOB', 8, 8, 'JOB.8.8', 'Please inquire of past generations and consider the discoveries of their fathers.'),
('JOB', 8, 9, 'JOB.8.9', 'For we were born yesterday and know nothing; our days on earth are but a shadow.'),
('JOB', 8, 10, 'JOB.8.10', 'Will they not teach you and tell you, and speak from their understanding?'),
('JOB', 8, 11, 'JOB.8.11', 'Does papyrus grow where there is no marsh? Do reeds flourish without water?'),
('JOB', 8, 12, 'JOB.8.12', 'While the shoots are still uncut, they dry up more quickly than grass.'),
('JOB', 8, 13, 'JOB.8.13', 'Such is the destiny of all who forget God; so the hope of the godless will perish.'),
('JOB', 8, 14, 'JOB.8.14', 'His confidence is fragile; his security is in a spider’s web.'),
('JOB', 8, 15, 'JOB.8.15', 'He leans on his web, but it gives way; he holds fast, but it does not endure.'),
('JOB', 8, 16, 'JOB.8.16', 'He is a well-watered plant in the sunshine, spreading its shoots over the garden.'),
('JOB', 8, 17, 'JOB.8.17', 'His roots wrap around the rock heap; he looks for a home among the stones.'),
('JOB', 8, 18, 'JOB.8.18', 'If he is uprooted from his place, it will disown him, saying, ‘I never saw you.’'),
('JOB', 8, 19, 'JOB.8.19', 'Surely this is the joy of his way; yet others will spring from the dust.'),
('JOB', 8, 20, 'JOB.8.20', 'Behold, God does not reject the blameless, nor will He strengthen the hand of evildoers.'),
('JOB', 8, 21, 'JOB.8.21', 'He will yet fill your mouth with laughter, and your lips with a shout of joy.'),
('JOB', 8, 22, 'JOB.8.22', 'Your enemies will be clothed in shame, and the tent of the wicked will be no more.”'),
('JOB', 9, 1, 'JOB.9.1', 'Then Job answered:'),
('JOB', 9, 2, 'JOB.9.2', '“Yes, I know that it is so, but how can a mortal be righteous before God?'),
('JOB', 9, 3, 'JOB.9.3', 'If one wished to contend with God, he could not answer Him one time out of a thousand.'),
('JOB', 9, 4, 'JOB.9.4', 'God is wise in heart and mighty in strength. Who has resisted Him and prospered?'),
('JOB', 9, 5, 'JOB.9.5', 'He moves mountains without their knowledge and overturns them in His anger.'),
('JOB', 9, 6, 'JOB.9.6', 'He shakes the earth from its place, so that its foundations tremble.'),
('JOB', 9, 7, 'JOB.9.7', 'He commands the sun not to shine; He seals off the stars.'),
('JOB', 9, 8, 'JOB.9.8', 'He alone stretches out the heavens and treads on the waves of the sea.'),
('JOB', 9, 9, 'JOB.9.9', 'He is the Maker of the Bear and Orion, of the Pleiades and the constellations of the south.'),
('JOB', 9, 10, 'JOB.9.10', 'He does great things beyond searching out, and wonders without number.'),
('JOB', 9, 11, 'JOB.9.11', 'Were He to pass by me, I would not see Him; were He to move, I would not recognize Him.'),
('JOB', 9, 12, 'JOB.9.12', 'If He takes away, who can stop Him? Who dares to ask Him, ‘What are You doing?’'),
('JOB', 9, 13, 'JOB.9.13', 'God does not restrain His anger; the helpers of Rahab cower beneath Him.'),
('JOB', 9, 14, 'JOB.9.14', 'How then can I answer Him or choose my arguments against Him?'),
('JOB', 9, 15, 'JOB.9.15', 'For even if I were right, I could not answer. I could only beg my Judge for mercy.'),
('JOB', 9, 16, 'JOB.9.16', 'If I summoned Him and He answered me, I do not believe He would listen to my voice.'),
('JOB', 9, 17, 'JOB.9.17', 'For He would crush me with a tempest and multiply my wounds without cause.'),
('JOB', 9, 18, 'JOB.9.18', 'He does not let me catch my breath, but overwhelms me with bitterness.'),
('JOB', 9, 19, 'JOB.9.19', 'If it is a matter of strength, He is indeed mighty! If it is a matter of justice, who can summon Him?'),
('JOB', 9, 20, 'JOB.9.20', 'Even if I were righteous, my mouth would condemn me; if I were blameless, it would declare me guilty.'),
('JOB', 9, 21, 'JOB.9.21', 'Though I am blameless, I have no concern for myself; I despise my own life.'),
('JOB', 9, 22, 'JOB.9.22', 'It is all the same, and so I say, ‘He destroys both the blameless and the wicked.’'),
('JOB', 9, 23, 'JOB.9.23', 'When the scourge brings sudden death, He mocks the despair of the innocent.'),
('JOB', 9, 24, 'JOB.9.24', 'The earth is given into the hand of the wicked; He blindfolds its judges. If it is not He, then who is it?'),
('JOB', 9, 25, 'JOB.9.25', 'My days are swifter than a runner; they flee without seeing good.'),
('JOB', 9, 26, 'JOB.9.26', 'They sweep by like boats of papyrus, like an eagle swooping down on its prey.'),
('JOB', 9, 27, 'JOB.9.27', 'If I were to say, ‘I will forget my complaint and change my expression and smile,’'),
('JOB', 9, 28, 'JOB.9.28', 'I would still dread all my sufferings; I know that You will not acquit me.'),
('JOB', 9, 29, 'JOB.9.29', 'Since I am already found guilty, why should I labor in vain?'),
('JOB', 9, 30, 'JOB.9.30', 'If I should wash myself with snow and cleanse my hands with lye,'),
('JOB', 9, 31, 'JOB.9.31', 'then You would plunge me into the pit, and even my own clothes would despise me.'),
('JOB', 9, 32, 'JOB.9.32', 'For He is not a man like me, that I can answer Him, that we can take each other to court.'),
('JOB', 9, 33, 'JOB.9.33', 'Nor is there a mediator between us, to lay his hand upon us both.'),
('JOB', 9, 34, 'JOB.9.34', 'Let Him remove His rod from me, so that His terror will no longer frighten me.'),
('JOB', 9, 35, 'JOB.9.35', 'Then I would speak without fear of Him. But as it is, I am on my own.'),
('JOB', 10, 1, 'JOB.10.1', '“I loathe my own life; I will express my complaint and speak in the bitterness of my soul.'),
('JOB', 10, 2, 'JOB.10.2', 'I will say to God: Do not condemn me! Let me know why You prosecute me.'),
('JOB', 10, 3, 'JOB.10.3', 'Does it please You to oppress me, to reject the work of Your hands and favor the schemes of the wicked?'),
('JOB', 10, 4, 'JOB.10.4', 'Do You have eyes of flesh? Do You see as man sees?'),
('JOB', 10, 5, 'JOB.10.5', 'Are Your days like those of a mortal, or Your years like those of a man,'),
('JOB', 10, 6, 'JOB.10.6', 'that You should seek my iniquity and search out my sin—'),
('JOB', 10, 7, 'JOB.10.7', 'though You know that I am not guilty, and there is no deliverance from Your hand?'),
('JOB', 10, 8, 'JOB.10.8', 'Your hands shaped me and altogether formed me. Would You now turn and destroy me?'),
('JOB', 10, 9, 'JOB.10.9', 'Please remember that You molded me like clay. Would You now return me to dust?'),
('JOB', 10, 10, 'JOB.10.10', 'Did You not pour me out like milk, and curdle me like cheese?'),
('JOB', 10, 11, 'JOB.10.11', 'You clothed me with skin and flesh, and knit me together with bones and sinews.'),
('JOB', 10, 12, 'JOB.10.12', 'You have granted me life and loving devotion, and Your care has preserved my spirit.'),
('JOB', 10, 13, 'JOB.10.13', 'Yet You concealed these things in Your heart, and I know that this was in Your mind:'),
('JOB', 10, 14, 'JOB.10.14', 'If I sinned, You would take note, and would not acquit me of my iniquity.'),
('JOB', 10, 15, 'JOB.10.15', 'If I am guilty, woe to me! And even if I am righteous, I cannot lift my head. I am full of shame and aware of my affliction.'),
('JOB', 10, 16, 'JOB.10.16', 'Should I hold my head high, You would hunt me like a lion, and again display Your power against me.'),
('JOB', 10, 17, 'JOB.10.17', 'You produce new witnesses against me and multiply Your anger toward me. Hardships assault me in wave after wave.'),
('JOB', 10, 18, 'JOB.10.18', 'Why then did You bring me from the womb? Oh, that I had died, and no eye had seen me!'),
('JOB', 10, 19, 'JOB.10.19', 'If only I had never come to be, but had been carried from the womb to the grave.'),
('JOB', 10, 20, 'JOB.10.20', 'Are my days not few? Withdraw from me, that I may have a little comfort,'),
('JOB', 10, 21, 'JOB.10.21', 'before I go—never to return—to a land of darkness and gloom,'),
('JOB', 10, 22, 'JOB.10.22', 'to a land of utter darkness, of deep shadow and disorder, where even the light is like darkness.”'),
('JOB', 11, 1, 'JOB.11.1', 'Then Zophar the Naamathite replied:'),
('JOB', 11, 2, 'JOB.11.2', '“Should this stream of words go unanswered and such a speaker be vindicated?'),
('JOB', 11, 3, 'JOB.11.3', 'Should your babbling put others to silence? Will you scoff without rebuke?'),
('JOB', 11, 4, 'JOB.11.4', 'You have said, ‘My doctrine is sound, and I am pure in Your sight.’'),
('JOB', 11, 5, 'JOB.11.5', 'But if only God would speak and open His lips against you,'),
('JOB', 11, 6, 'JOB.11.6', 'and disclose to you the secrets of wisdom, for true wisdom has two sides. Know then that God exacts from you less than your iniquity deserves.'),
('JOB', 11, 7, 'JOB.11.7', 'Can you fathom the deep things of God or discover the limits of the Almighty?'),
('JOB', 11, 8, 'JOB.11.8', 'They are higher than the heavens—what can you do? They are deeper than Sheol—what can you know?'),
('JOB', 11, 9, 'JOB.11.9', 'Their measure is longer than the earth and wider than the sea.'),
('JOB', 11, 10, 'JOB.11.10', 'If He comes along to imprison you, or convenes a court, who can stop Him?'),
('JOB', 11, 11, 'JOB.11.11', 'Surely He knows the deceit of men. If He sees iniquity, does He not take note?'),
('JOB', 11, 12, 'JOB.11.12', 'But a witless man can no more become wise than the colt of a wild donkey can be born a man!'),
('JOB', 11, 13, 'JOB.11.13', 'As for you, if you direct your heart and lift up your hands to Him,'),
('JOB', 11, 14, 'JOB.11.14', 'if you put away the iniquity in your hand, and allow no injustice to dwell in your tents,'),
('JOB', 11, 15, 'JOB.11.15', 'then indeed you will lift up your face without blemish; you will stand firm and unafraid.'),
('JOB', 11, 16, 'JOB.11.16', 'For you will forget your misery, recalling it only as waters gone by.'),
('JOB', 11, 17, 'JOB.11.17', 'Your life will be brighter than noonday; its darkness will be like the morning.'),
('JOB', 11, 18, 'JOB.11.18', 'You will be secure, because there is hope, and you will look around and lie down in safety.'),
('JOB', 11, 19, 'JOB.11.19', 'You will lie down without fear, and many will court your favor.'),
('JOB', 11, 20, 'JOB.11.20', 'But the eyes of the wicked will fail, and escape will elude them; they will hope for their last breath.”'),
('JOB', 12, 1, 'JOB.12.1', 'Then Job answered:'),
('JOB', 12, 2, 'JOB.12.2', '“Truly then you are the people with whom wisdom itself will die!'),
('JOB', 12, 3, 'JOB.12.3', 'But I also have a mind; I am not inferior to you. Who does not know such things as these?'),
('JOB', 12, 4, 'JOB.12.4', 'I am a laughingstock to my friends, though I called on God, and He answered. The righteous and upright man is a laughingstock.'),
('JOB', 12, 5, 'JOB.12.5', 'The one at ease scorns misfortune as the fate of those whose feet are slipping.'),
('JOB', 12, 6, 'JOB.12.6', 'The tents of robbers are safe, and those who provoke God are secure—those who carry their god in their hands.'),
('JOB', 12, 7, 'JOB.12.7', 'But ask the animals, and they will instruct you; ask the birds of the air, and they will tell you.'),
('JOB', 12, 8, 'JOB.12.8', 'Or speak to the earth, and it will teach you; let the fish of the sea inform you.'),
('JOB', 12, 9, 'JOB.12.9', 'Which of all these does not know that the hand of the LORD has done this?'),
('JOB', 12, 10, 'JOB.12.10', 'The life of every living thing is in His hand, as well as the breath of all mankind.'),
('JOB', 12, 11, 'JOB.12.11', 'Does not the ear test words as the tongue tastes its food?'),
('JOB', 12, 12, 'JOB.12.12', 'Wisdom is found with the elderly, and understanding comes with long life.'),
('JOB', 12, 13, 'JOB.12.13', 'Wisdom and strength belong to God; counsel and understanding are His.'),
('JOB', 12, 14, 'JOB.12.14', 'What He tears down cannot be rebuilt; the man He imprisons cannot be released.'),
('JOB', 12, 15, 'JOB.12.15', 'If He holds back the waters, they dry up, and if He releases them, they overwhelm the land.'),
('JOB', 12, 16, 'JOB.12.16', 'True wisdom and power belong to Him. The deceived and the deceiver are His.'),
('JOB', 12, 17, 'JOB.12.17', 'He leads counselors away barefoot and makes fools of judges.'),
('JOB', 12, 18, 'JOB.12.18', 'He loosens the bonds placed by kings and fastens a belt around their waists.'),
('JOB', 12, 19, 'JOB.12.19', 'He leads priests away barefoot and overthrows the established.'),
('JOB', 12, 20, 'JOB.12.20', 'He deprives the trusted of speech and takes away the discernment of elders.'),
('JOB', 12, 21, 'JOB.12.21', 'He pours out contempt on nobles and disarms the mighty.'),
('JOB', 12, 22, 'JOB.12.22', 'He reveals the deep things of darkness and brings deep shadows into light.'),
('JOB', 12, 23, 'JOB.12.23', 'He makes nations great and destroys them; He enlarges nations, then disperses them.'),
('JOB', 12, 24, 'JOB.12.24', 'He deprives the earth’s leaders of reason and makes them wander in a trackless wasteland.'),
('JOB', 12, 25, 'JOB.12.25', 'They grope in the darkness without light; He makes them stagger like drunkards.'),
('JOB', 13, 1, 'JOB.13.1', '“Indeed, my eyes have seen all this; my ears have heard and understood.'),
('JOB', 13, 2, 'JOB.13.2', 'What you know, I also know; I am not inferior to you.'),
('JOB', 13, 3, 'JOB.13.3', 'Yet I desire to speak to the Almighty and argue my case before God.'),
('JOB', 13, 4, 'JOB.13.4', 'You, however, smear with lies; you are all worthless physicians.'),
('JOB', 13, 5, 'JOB.13.5', 'If only you would remain silent; for that would be your wisdom!'),
('JOB', 13, 6, 'JOB.13.6', 'Hear now my argument, and listen to the plea of my lips.'),
('JOB', 13, 7, 'JOB.13.7', 'Will you speak wickedly on God’s behalf or speak deceitfully for Him?'),
('JOB', 13, 8, 'JOB.13.8', 'Would you show Him partiality or argue in His defense?'),
('JOB', 13, 9, 'JOB.13.9', 'Would it be well when He examined you? Could you deceive Him as you would deceive a man?'),
('JOB', 13, 10, 'JOB.13.10', 'Surely He would rebuke you if you secretly showed partiality.'),
('JOB', 13, 11, 'JOB.13.11', 'Would His majesty not terrify you? Would the dread of Him not fall upon you?'),
('JOB', 13, 12, 'JOB.13.12', 'Your maxims are proverbs of ashes; your defenses are defenses of clay.'),
('JOB', 13, 13, 'JOB.13.13', 'Be silent, and I will speak. Then let come to me what may.'),
('JOB', 13, 14, 'JOB.13.14', 'Why do I put myself at risk and take my life in my own hands?'),
('JOB', 13, 15, 'JOB.13.15', 'Though He slay me, I will hope in Him. I will still defend my ways to His face.'),
('JOB', 13, 16, 'JOB.13.16', 'Moreover, this will be my salvation, for no godless man can appear before Him.'),
('JOB', 13, 17, 'JOB.13.17', 'Listen carefully to my words; let my declaration ring in your ears.'),
('JOB', 13, 18, 'JOB.13.18', 'See now, I have prepared my case; I know that I will be vindicated.'),
('JOB', 13, 19, 'JOB.13.19', 'Can anyone indict me? If so, I will be silent and die.'),
('JOB', 13, 20, 'JOB.13.20', 'Only grant these two things to me, so that I need not hide from You:'),
('JOB', 13, 21, 'JOB.13.21', 'Withdraw Your hand from me, and do not let Your terror frighten me.'),
('JOB', 13, 22, 'JOB.13.22', 'Then call me, and I will answer, or let me speak, and You can reply.'),
('JOB', 13, 23, 'JOB.13.23', 'How many are my iniquities and sins? Reveal to me my transgression and sin.'),
('JOB', 13, 24, 'JOB.13.24', 'Why do You hide Your face and consider me as Your enemy?'),
('JOB', 13, 25, 'JOB.13.25', 'Would You frighten a windblown leaf? Would You chase after dry chaff?'),
('JOB', 13, 26, 'JOB.13.26', 'For You record bitter accusations against me and bequeath to me the iniquities of my youth.'),
('JOB', 13, 27, 'JOB.13.27', 'You put my feet in the stocks and stand watch over all my paths; You set a limit for the soles of my feet.'),
('JOB', 13, 28, 'JOB.13.28', 'So man wastes away like something rotten, like a moth-eaten garment.'),
('JOB', 14, 1, 'JOB.14.1', '“Man, who is born of woman, is short of days and full of trouble.'),
('JOB', 14, 2, 'JOB.14.2', 'Like a flower, he comes forth, then withers away; like a fleeting shadow, he does not endure.'),
('JOB', 14, 3, 'JOB.14.3', 'Do You open Your eyes to one like this? Will You bring him into judgment before You?'),
('JOB', 14, 4, 'JOB.14.4', 'Who can bring out clean from unclean? No one!'),
('JOB', 14, 5, 'JOB.14.5', 'Since his days are determined and the number of his months is with You, and since You have set limits that he cannot exceed,'),
('JOB', 14, 6, 'JOB.14.6', 'look away from him and let him rest, so he can enjoy his day as a hired hand.'),
('JOB', 14, 7, 'JOB.14.7', 'For there is hope for a tree: If it is cut down, it will sprout again, and its tender shoots will not fail.'),
('JOB', 14, 8, 'JOB.14.8', 'If its roots grow old in the ground and its stump dies in the soil,'),
('JOB', 14, 9, 'JOB.14.9', 'at the scent of water it will bud and put forth twigs like a sapling.'),
('JOB', 14, 10, 'JOB.14.10', 'But a man dies and is laid low; he breathes his last, and where is he?'),
('JOB', 14, 11, 'JOB.14.11', 'As water disappears from the sea and a river becomes parched and dry,'),
('JOB', 14, 12, 'JOB.14.12', 'so a man lies down and does not rise. Until the heavens are no more, he will not be awakened or roused from sleep.'),
('JOB', 14, 13, 'JOB.14.13', 'If only You would hide me in Sheol and conceal me until Your anger has passed! If only You would appoint a time for me and then remember me!'),
('JOB', 14, 14, 'JOB.14.14', 'When a man dies, will he live again? All the days of my hard service I will wait, until my renewal comes.'),
('JOB', 14, 15, 'JOB.14.15', 'You will call, and I will answer; You will desire the work of Your hands.'),
('JOB', 14, 16, 'JOB.14.16', 'For then You would count my steps, but would not keep track of my sin.'),
('JOB', 14, 17, 'JOB.14.17', 'My transgression would be sealed in a bag, and You would cover over my iniquity.'),
('JOB', 14, 18, 'JOB.14.18', 'But as a mountain erodes and crumbles and a rock is dislodged from its place,'),
('JOB', 14, 19, 'JOB.14.19', 'as water wears away the stones and torrents wash away the soil, so You destroy a man’s hope.'),
('JOB', 14, 20, 'JOB.14.20', 'You forever overpower him, and he passes on; You change his countenance and send him away.'),
('JOB', 14, 21, 'JOB.14.21', 'If his sons receive honor, he does not know it; if they are brought low, he is unaware.'),
('JOB', 14, 22, 'JOB.14.22', 'He feels only the pain of his own body and mourns only for himself.”'),
('JOB', 15, 1, 'JOB.15.1', 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite replied:'),
('JOB', 15, 2, 'JOB.15.2', '“Does a wise man answer with empty counsel or fill his belly with the hot east wind?'),
('JOB', 15, 3, 'JOB.15.3', 'Should he argue with useless words or speeches that serve no purpose?'),
('JOB', 15, 4, 'JOB.15.4', 'But you even undermine the fear of God and hinder meditation before Him.'),
('JOB', 15, 5, 'JOB.15.5', 'For your iniquity instructs your mouth, and you choose the language of the crafty.'),
('JOB', 15, 6, 'JOB.15.6', 'Your own mouth, not mine, condemns you; your own lips testify against you.'),
('JOB', 15, 7, 'JOB.15.7', 'Were you the first man ever born? Were you brought forth before the hills?'),
('JOB', 15, 8, 'JOB.15.8', 'Do you listen in on the council of God or limit wisdom to yourself?'),
('JOB', 15, 9, 'JOB.15.9', 'What do you know that we do not? What do you understand that is not clear to us?'),
('JOB', 15, 10, 'JOB.15.10', 'Both the gray-haired and the aged are on our side—men much older than your father.'),
('JOB', 15, 11, 'JOB.15.11', 'Are the consolations of God not enough for you, even words spoken gently to you?'),
('JOB', 15, 12, 'JOB.15.12', 'Why has your heart carried you away, and why do your eyes flash,'),
('JOB', 15, 13, 'JOB.15.13', 'so that you turn your spirit against God and pour such words from your mouth?'),
('JOB', 15, 14, 'JOB.15.14', 'What is man, that he should be pure, or one born of woman, that he should be righteous?'),
('JOB', 15, 15, 'JOB.15.15', 'If God puts no trust in His holy ones, if even the heavens are not pure in His eyes,'),
('JOB', 15, 16, 'JOB.15.16', 'how much less man, who is vile and corrupt, who drinks injustice like water?'),
('JOB', 15, 17, 'JOB.15.17', 'Listen to me and I will inform you. I will describe what I have seen,'),
('JOB', 15, 18, 'JOB.15.18', 'what was declared by wise men and was not concealed from their fathers,'),
('JOB', 15, 19, 'JOB.15.19', 'to whom alone the land was given when no foreigner passed among them.'),
('JOB', 15, 20, 'JOB.15.20', 'A wicked man writhes in pain all his days; only a few years are reserved for the ruthless.'),
('JOB', 15, 21, 'JOB.15.21', 'Sounds of terror fill his ears; in his prosperity the destroyer attacks him.'),
('JOB', 15, 22, 'JOB.15.22', 'He despairs of his return from darkness; he is marked for the sword.'),
('JOB', 15, 23, 'JOB.15.23', 'He wanders about as food for vultures; he knows the day of darkness is at hand.'),
('JOB', 15, 24, 'JOB.15.24', 'Distress and anguish terrify him, overwhelming him like a king poised to attack.'),
('JOB', 15, 25, 'JOB.15.25', 'For he has stretched out his hand against God and has vaunted himself against the Almighty,'),
('JOB', 15, 26, 'JOB.15.26', 'rushing headlong at Him with a thick, studded shield.'),
('JOB', 15, 27, 'JOB.15.27', 'Though his face is covered with fat and his waistline bulges with flesh,'),
('JOB', 15, 28, 'JOB.15.28', 'he will dwell in ruined cities, in abandoned houses destined to become rubble.'),
('JOB', 15, 29, 'JOB.15.29', 'He will no longer be rich; his wealth will not endure. His possessions will not overspread the land.'),
('JOB', 15, 30, 'JOB.15.30', 'He will not escape from the darkness; the flame will wither his shoots, and the breath of God’s mouth will carry him away.'),
('JOB', 15, 31, 'JOB.15.31', 'Let him not deceive himself with trust in emptiness, for emptiness will be his reward.'),
('JOB', 15, 32, 'JOB.15.32', 'It will be paid in full before his time, and his branch will not flourish.'),
('JOB', 15, 33, 'JOB.15.33', 'He will be like a vine stripped of its unripe grapes, like an olive tree that sheds its blossoms.'),
('JOB', 15, 34, 'JOB.15.34', 'For the company of the godless will be barren, and fire will consume the tents of bribery.'),
('JOB', 15, 35, 'JOB.15.35', 'They conceive trouble and give birth to evil; their womb is pregnant with deceit.”'),
('JOB', 16, 1, 'JOB.16.1', 'Then Job answered:'),
('JOB', 16, 2, 'JOB.16.2', '“I have heard many things like these; miserable comforters are you all.'),
('JOB', 16, 3, 'JOB.16.3', 'Is there no end to your long-winded speeches? What provokes you to continue testifying?'),
('JOB', 16, 4, 'JOB.16.4', 'I could also speak like you if you were in my place; I could heap up words against you and shake my head at you.'),
('JOB', 16, 5, 'JOB.16.5', 'But I would encourage you with my mouth, and the consolation of my lips would bring relief.'),
('JOB', 16, 6, 'JOB.16.6', 'Even if I speak, my pain is not relieved, and if I hold back, how will it go away?'),
('JOB', 16, 7, 'JOB.16.7', 'Surely He has now exhausted me; You have devastated all my family.'),
('JOB', 16, 8, 'JOB.16.8', 'You have bound me, and it has become a witness; my frailty rises up and testifies against me.'),
('JOB', 16, 9, 'JOB.16.9', 'His anger has torn me and opposed me; He gnashes His teeth at me. My adversary pierces me with His eyes.'),
('JOB', 16, 10, 'JOB.16.10', 'They open their mouths against me and strike my cheeks with contempt; they join together against me.'),
('JOB', 16, 11, 'JOB.16.11', 'God has delivered me to unjust men; He has thrown me to the clutches of the wicked.'),
('JOB', 16, 12, 'JOB.16.12', 'I was at ease, but He shattered me; He seized me by the neck and crushed me. He has set me up as His target;'),
('JOB', 16, 13, 'JOB.16.13', 'His archers surround me. He pierces my kidneys without mercy and spills my gall on the ground.'),
('JOB', 16, 14, 'JOB.16.14', 'He breaks me with wound upon wound; He rushes me like a mighty warrior.'),
('JOB', 16, 15, 'JOB.16.15', 'I have sewn sackcloth over my skin; I have buried my horn in the dust.'),
('JOB', 16, 16, 'JOB.16.16', 'My face is red with weeping, and deep shadows ring my eyes;'),
('JOB', 16, 17, 'JOB.16.17', 'yet my hands are free of violence and my prayer is pure.'),
('JOB', 16, 18, 'JOB.16.18', 'O earth, do not cover my blood; may my cry for help never be laid to rest.'),
('JOB', 16, 19, 'JOB.16.19', 'Even now my witness is in heaven, and my advocate is on high.'),
('JOB', 16, 20, 'JOB.16.20', 'My friends are my scoffers as my eyes pour out tears to God.'),
('JOB', 16, 21, 'JOB.16.21', 'Oh, that a man might plead with God as he pleads with his neighbor!'),
('JOB', 16, 22, 'JOB.16.22', 'For when only a few years are past I will go the way of no return.'),
('JOB', 17, 1, 'JOB.17.1', '“My spirit is broken; my days are extinguished; the grave awaits me.'),
('JOB', 17, 2, 'JOB.17.2', 'Surely mockers surround me, and my eyes must gaze at their rebellion.'),
('JOB', 17, 3, 'JOB.17.3', 'Give me, I pray, the pledge You demand. Who else will be my guarantor?'),
('JOB', 17, 4, 'JOB.17.4', 'You have closed their minds to understanding; therefore You will not exalt them.'),
('JOB', 17, 5, 'JOB.17.5', 'If a man denounces his friends for a price, the eyes of his children will fail.'),
('JOB', 17, 6, 'JOB.17.6', 'He has made me a byword among the people, a man in whose face they spit.'),
('JOB', 17, 7, 'JOB.17.7', 'My eyes have grown dim with grief, and my whole body is but a shadow.'),
('JOB', 17, 8, 'JOB.17.8', 'The upright are appalled at this, and the innocent are stirred against the godless.'),
('JOB', 17, 9, 'JOB.17.9', 'Yet a righteous one holds to his way, and the one with clean hands grows stronger.'),
('JOB', 17, 10, 'JOB.17.10', 'But come back and try again, all of you. For I will not find a wise man among you.'),
('JOB', 17, 11, 'JOB.17.11', 'My days have passed; my plans are broken off—even the desires of my heart.'),
('JOB', 17, 12, 'JOB.17.12', 'They have turned night into day, making light seem near in the face of darkness.'),
('JOB', 17, 13, 'JOB.17.13', 'If I look for Sheol as my home, if I spread out my bed in darkness,'),
('JOB', 17, 14, 'JOB.17.14', 'and say to corruption, ‘You are my father,’ and to the worm, ‘My mother,’ or ‘My sister,’'),
('JOB', 17, 15, 'JOB.17.15', 'where then is my hope? Who can see any hope for me?'),
('JOB', 17, 16, 'JOB.17.16', 'Will it go down to the gates of Sheol? Will we go down together into the dust?”'),
('JOB', 18, 1, 'JOB.18.1', 'Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:'),
('JOB', 18, 2, 'JOB.18.2', '“How long until you end these speeches? Show some sense, and then we can talk.'),
('JOB', 18, 3, 'JOB.18.3', 'Why are we regarded as cattle, as stupid in your sight?'),
('JOB', 18, 4, 'JOB.18.4', 'You who tear yourself in anger—should the earth be forsaken on your account, or the rocks be moved from their place?'),
('JOB', 18, 5, 'JOB.18.5', 'Indeed, the lamp of the wicked is extinguished; the flame of his fire does not glow.'),
('JOB', 18, 6, 'JOB.18.6', 'The light in his tent grows dark, and the lamp beside him goes out.'),
('JOB', 18, 7, 'JOB.18.7', 'His vigorous stride is shortened, and his own schemes trip him up.'),
('JOB', 18, 8, 'JOB.18.8', 'For his own feet lead him into a net, and he wanders into its mesh.'),
('JOB', 18, 9, 'JOB.18.9', 'A trap seizes his heel; a snare grips him.'),
('JOB', 18, 10, 'JOB.18.10', 'A noose is hidden in the ground, and a trap lies in his path.'),
('JOB', 18, 11, 'JOB.18.11', 'Terrors frighten him on every side and harass his every step.'),
('JOB', 18, 12, 'JOB.18.12', 'His strength is depleted, and calamity is ready at his side.'),
('JOB', 18, 13, 'JOB.18.13', 'It devours patches of his skin; the firstborn of death devours his limbs.'),
('JOB', 18, 14, 'JOB.18.14', 'He is torn from the shelter of his tent and is marched off to the king of terrors.'),
('JOB', 18, 15, 'JOB.18.15', 'Fire resides in his tent; burning sulfur rains down on his dwelling.'),
('JOB', 18, 16, 'JOB.18.16', 'The roots beneath him dry up, and the branches above him wither away.'),
('JOB', 18, 17, 'JOB.18.17', 'The memory of him perishes from the earth, and he has no name in the land.'),
('JOB', 18, 18, 'JOB.18.18', 'He is driven from light into darkness and is chased from the inhabited world.'),
('JOB', 18, 19, 'JOB.18.19', 'He has no offspring or posterity among his people, no survivor where he once lived.'),
('JOB', 18, 20, 'JOB.18.20', 'Those in the west are appalled at his fate, while those in the east tremble in horror.'),
('JOB', 18, 21, 'JOB.18.21', 'Surely such is the dwelling of the wicked and the place of one who does not know God.”'),
('JOB', 19, 1, 'JOB.19.1', 'Then Job answered:'),
('JOB', 19, 2, 'JOB.19.2', '“How long will you torment me and crush me with your words?'),
('JOB', 19, 3, 'JOB.19.3', 'Ten times now you have reproached me; you shamelessly mistreat me.'),
('JOB', 19, 4, 'JOB.19.4', 'Even if I have truly gone astray, my error concerns me alone.'),
('JOB', 19, 5, 'JOB.19.5', 'If indeed you would exalt yourselves above me and use my disgrace against me,'),
('JOB', 19, 6, 'JOB.19.6', 'then understand that it is God who has wronged me and drawn His net around me.'),
('JOB', 19, 7, 'JOB.19.7', 'Though I cry out, ‘Violence!’ I get no response; though I call for help, there is no justice.'),
('JOB', 19, 8, 'JOB.19.8', 'He has blocked my way so I cannot pass; He has veiled my paths with darkness.'),
('JOB', 19, 9, 'JOB.19.9', 'He has stripped me of my honor and removed the crown from my head.'),
('JOB', 19, 10, 'JOB.19.10', 'He tears me down on every side until I am gone; He uproots my hope like a tree.'),
('JOB', 19, 11, 'JOB.19.11', 'His anger burns against me, and He counts me among His enemies.'),
('JOB', 19, 12, 'JOB.19.12', 'His troops advance together; they construct a ramp against me and encamp around my tent.'),
('JOB', 19, 13, 'JOB.19.13', 'He has removed my brothers from me; my acquaintances have abandoned me.'),
('JOB', 19, 14, 'JOB.19.14', 'My kinsmen have failed me, and my friends have forgotten me.'),
('JOB', 19, 15, 'JOB.19.15', 'My guests and maidservants count me as a stranger; I am a foreigner in their sight.'),
('JOB', 19, 16, 'JOB.19.16', 'I call for my servant, but he does not answer, though I implore him with my own mouth.'),
('JOB', 19, 17, 'JOB.19.17', 'My breath is repulsive to my wife, and I am loathsome to my own family.'),
('JOB', 19, 18, 'JOB.19.18', 'Even little boys scorn me; when I appear, they deride me.'),
('JOB', 19, 19, 'JOB.19.19', 'All my best friends despise me, and those I love have turned against me.'),
('JOB', 19, 20, 'JOB.19.20', 'My skin and flesh cling to my bones; I have escaped by the skin of my teeth.'),
('JOB', 19, 21, 'JOB.19.21', 'Have pity on me, my friends, have pity, for the hand of God has struck me.'),
('JOB', 19, 22, 'JOB.19.22', 'Why do you persecute me as God does? Will you never get enough of my flesh?'),
('JOB', 19, 23, 'JOB.19.23', 'I wish that my words were recorded and inscribed in a book,'),
('JOB', 19, 24, 'JOB.19.24', 'by an iron stylus on lead, or chiseled in stone forever.'),
('JOB', 19, 25, 'JOB.19.25', 'But I know that my Redeemer lives, and in the end He will stand upon the earth.'),
('JOB', 19, 26, 'JOB.19.26', 'Even after my skin has been destroyed, yet in my flesh I will see God.'),
('JOB', 19, 27, 'JOB.19.27', 'I will see Him for myself; my eyes will behold Him, and not as a stranger. How my heart yearns within me!'),
('JOB', 19, 28, 'JOB.19.28', 'If you say, ‘Let us persecute him, since the root of the matter lies with him,’'),
('JOB', 19, 29, 'JOB.19.29', 'then you should fear the sword yourselves, because wrath brings punishment by the sword, so that you may know there is a judgment.”'),
('JOB', 20, 1, 'JOB.20.1', 'Then Zophar the Naamathite replied:'),
('JOB', 20, 2, 'JOB.20.2', '“So my anxious thoughts compel me to answer, because of the turmoil within me.'),
('JOB', 20, 3, 'JOB.20.3', 'I have heard a rebuke that insults me, and my understanding prompts a reply.'),
('JOB', 20, 4, 'JOB.20.4', 'Do you not know that from antiquity, since man was placed on the earth,'),
('JOB', 20, 5, 'JOB.20.5', 'the triumph of the wicked has been brief and the joy of the godless momentary?'),
('JOB', 20, 6, 'JOB.20.6', 'Though his arrogance reaches the heavens, and his head touches the clouds,'),
('JOB', 20, 7, 'JOB.20.7', 'he will perish forever, like his own dung; those who had seen him will ask, ‘Where is he?’'),
('JOB', 20, 8, 'JOB.20.8', 'He will fly away like a dream, never to be found; he will be chased away like a vision in the night.'),
('JOB', 20, 9, 'JOB.20.9', 'The eye that saw him will see him no more, and his place will no longer behold him.'),
('JOB', 20, 10, 'JOB.20.10', 'His sons will seek the favor of the poor, for his own hands must return his wealth.'),
('JOB', 20, 11, 'JOB.20.11', 'The youthful vigor that fills his bones will lie down with him in the dust.'),
('JOB', 20, 12, 'JOB.20.12', 'Though evil is sweet in his mouth and he conceals it under his tongue,'),
('JOB', 20, 13, 'JOB.20.13', 'though he cannot bear to let it go and keeps it in his mouth,'),
('JOB', 20, 14, 'JOB.20.14', 'yet in his stomach his food sours into the venom of cobras within him.'),
('JOB', 20, 15, 'JOB.20.15', 'He swallows wealth but vomits it out; God will force it from his stomach.'),
('JOB', 20, 16, 'JOB.20.16', 'He will suck the poison of cobras; the fangs of a viper will kill him.'),
('JOB', 20, 17, 'JOB.20.17', 'He will not enjoy the streams, the rivers flowing with honey and cream.'),
('JOB', 20, 18, 'JOB.20.18', 'He must return the fruit of his labor without consuming it; he cannot enjoy the profits of his trading.'),
('JOB', 20, 19, 'JOB.20.19', 'For he has oppressed and forsaken the poor; he has seized houses he did not build.'),
('JOB', 20, 20, 'JOB.20.20', 'Because his appetite is never satisfied, he cannot escape with his treasure.'),
('JOB', 20, 21, 'JOB.20.21', 'Nothing is left for him to consume; thus his prosperity will not endure.'),
('JOB', 20, 22, 'JOB.20.22', 'In the midst of his plenty, he will be distressed; the full force of misery will come upon him.'),
('JOB', 20, 23, 'JOB.20.23', 'When he has filled his stomach, God will vent His fury upon him, raining it down on him as he eats.'),
('JOB', 20, 24, 'JOB.20.24', 'Though he flees from an iron weapon, a bronze-tipped arrow will pierce him.'),
('JOB', 20, 25, 'JOB.20.25', 'It is drawn out of his back, the gleaming point from his liver. Terrors come over him.'),
('JOB', 20, 26, 'JOB.20.26', 'Total darkness is reserved for his treasures. A fire unfanned will consume him and devour what is left in his tent.'),
('JOB', 20, 27, 'JOB.20.27', 'The heavens will expose his iniquity, and the earth will rise up against him.'),
('JOB', 20, 28, 'JOB.20.28', 'The possessions of his house will be removed, flowing away on the day of God’s wrath.'),
('JOB', 20, 29, 'JOB.20.29', 'This is the wicked man’s portion from God, the inheritance God has appointed him.”'),
('JOB', 21, 1, 'JOB.21.1', 'Then Job answered:'),
('JOB', 21, 2, 'JOB.21.2', '“Listen carefully to my words; let this be your consolation to me.'),
('JOB', 21, 3, 'JOB.21.3', 'Bear with me while I speak; then, after I have spoken, you may go on mocking.'),
('JOB', 21, 4, 'JOB.21.4', 'Is my complaint against a man? Then why should I not be impatient?'),
('JOB', 21, 5, 'JOB.21.5', 'Look at me and be appalled; put your hand over your mouth.'),
('JOB', 21, 6, 'JOB.21.6', 'When I remember, terror takes hold, and my body trembles in horror.'),
('JOB', 21, 7, 'JOB.21.7', 'Why do the wicked live on, growing old and increasing in power?'),
('JOB', 21, 8, 'JOB.21.8', 'Their descendants are established around them, and their offspring before their eyes.'),
('JOB', 21, 9, 'JOB.21.9', 'Their homes are safe from fear; no rod of punishment from God is upon them.'),
('JOB', 21, 10, 'JOB.21.10', 'Their bulls breed without fail; their cows bear calves and do not miscarry.'),
('JOB', 21, 11, 'JOB.21.11', 'They send forth their little ones like a flock; their children skip about,'),
('JOB', 21, 12, 'JOB.21.12', 'singing to the tambourine and lyre and making merry at the sound of the flute.'),
('JOB', 21, 13, 'JOB.21.13', 'They spend their days in prosperity and go down to Sheol in peace.'),
('JOB', 21, 14, 'JOB.21.14', 'Yet they say to God: ‘Leave us alone! For we have no desire to know Your ways.'),
('JOB', 21, 15, 'JOB.21.15', 'Who is the Almighty, that we should serve Him, and what would we gain if we pray to Him?’'),
('JOB', 21, 16, 'JOB.21.16', 'Still, their prosperity is not in their own hands, so I stay far from the counsel of the wicked.'),
('JOB', 21, 17, 'JOB.21.17', 'How often is the lamp of the wicked put out? Does disaster come upon them? Does God, in His anger, apportion destruction?'),
('JOB', 21, 18, 'JOB.21.18', 'Are they like straw before the wind, like chaff swept away by a storm?'),
('JOB', 21, 19, 'JOB.21.19', 'It is said that God lays up one’s punishment for his children. Let God repay the man himself, so he will know it.'),
('JOB', 21, 20, 'JOB.21.20', 'Let his eyes see his own destruction; let him drink for himself the wrath of the Almighty.'),
('JOB', 21, 21, 'JOB.21.21', 'For what does he care about his household after him, when the number of his months has run out?'),
('JOB', 21, 22, 'JOB.21.22', 'Can anyone teach knowledge to God, since He judges those on high?'),
('JOB', 21, 23, 'JOB.21.23', 'One man dies full of vigor, completely secure and at ease.'),
('JOB', 21, 24, 'JOB.21.24', 'His body is well nourished, and his bones are rich with marrow.'),
('JOB', 21, 25, 'JOB.21.25', 'Yet another man dies in the bitterness of his soul, having never tasted prosperity.'),
('JOB', 21, 26, 'JOB.21.26', 'But together they lie down in the dust, and worms cover them both.'),
('JOB', 21, 27, 'JOB.21.27', 'Behold, I know your thoughts full well, the schemes by which you would wrong me.'),
('JOB', 21, 28, 'JOB.21.28', 'For you say, ‘Where now is the nobleman’s house, and where are the tents in which the wicked dwell?’'),
('JOB', 21, 29, 'JOB.21.29', 'Have you never asked those who travel the roads? Do you not accept their reports?'),
('JOB', 21, 30, 'JOB.21.30', 'Indeed, the evil man is spared from the day of calamity, delivered from the day of wrath.'),
('JOB', 21, 31, 'JOB.21.31', 'Who denounces his behavior to his face? Who repays him for what he has done?'),
('JOB', 21, 32, 'JOB.21.32', 'He is carried to the grave, and watch is kept over his tomb.'),
('JOB', 21, 33, 'JOB.21.33', 'The clods of the valley are sweet to him; everyone follows behind him, and those before him are without number.'),
('JOB', 21, 34, 'JOB.21.34', 'So how can you comfort me with empty words? For your answers remain full of falsehood.”'),
('JOB', 22, 1, 'JOB.22.1', 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite replied:'),
('JOB', 22, 2, 'JOB.22.2', '“Can a man be of use to God? Can even a wise man benefit Him?'),
('JOB', 22, 3, 'JOB.22.3', 'Does it delight the Almighty that you are righteous? Does He profit if your ways are blameless?'),
('JOB', 22, 4, 'JOB.22.4', 'Is it for your reverence that He rebukes you and enters into judgment against you?'),
('JOB', 22, 5, 'JOB.22.5', 'Is not your wickedness great? Are not your iniquities endless?'),
('JOB', 22, 6, 'JOB.22.6', 'For you needlessly demanded security from your brothers and deprived the naked of their clothing.'),
('JOB', 22, 7, 'JOB.22.7', 'You gave no water to the weary and withheld food from the famished,'),
('JOB', 22, 8, 'JOB.22.8', 'while the land belonged to a mighty man, and a man of honor lived on it.'),
('JOB', 22, 9, 'JOB.22.9', 'You sent widows away empty-handed, and the strength of the fatherless was crushed.'),
('JOB', 22, 10, 'JOB.22.10', 'Therefore snares surround you, and sudden peril terrifies you;'),
('JOB', 22, 11, 'JOB.22.11', 'it is so dark you cannot see, and a flood of water covers you.'),
('JOB', 22, 12, 'JOB.22.12', 'Is not God as high as the heavens? Look at the highest stars, how lofty they are!'),
('JOB', 22, 13, 'JOB.22.13', 'Yet you say: ‘What does God know? Does He judge through thick darkness?'),
('JOB', 22, 14, 'JOB.22.14', 'Thick clouds veil Him so He does not see us as He traverses the vault of heaven.’'),
('JOB', 22, 15, 'JOB.22.15', 'Will you stay on the ancient path that wicked men have trod?'),
('JOB', 22, 16, 'JOB.22.16', 'They were snatched away before their time, and their foundations were swept away by a flood.'),
('JOB', 22, 17, 'JOB.22.17', 'They said to God, ‘Depart from us. What can the Almighty do to us?’'),
('JOB', 22, 18, 'JOB.22.18', 'But it was He who filled their houses with good things; so I stay far from the counsel of the wicked.'),
('JOB', 22, 19, 'JOB.22.19', 'The righteous see it and are glad; the innocent mock them:'),
('JOB', 22, 20, 'JOB.22.20', '‘Surely our foes are destroyed, and fire has consumed their excess.’'),
('JOB', 22, 21, 'JOB.22.21', 'Reconcile now and be at peace with Him; thereby good will come to you.'),
('JOB', 22, 22, 'JOB.22.22', 'Receive instruction from His mouth, and lay up His words in your heart.'),
('JOB', 22, 23, 'JOB.22.23', 'If you return to the Almighty, you will be restored. If you remove injustice from your tents'),
('JOB', 22, 24, 'JOB.22.24', 'and consign your gold to the dust and the gold of Ophir to the stones of the ravines,'),
('JOB', 22, 25, 'JOB.22.25', 'then the Almighty will be your gold and the finest silver for you.'),
('JOB', 22, 26, 'JOB.22.26', 'Surely then you will delight in the Almighty and lift up your face to God.'),
('JOB', 22, 27, 'JOB.22.27', 'You will pray to Him, and He will hear you, and you will fulfill your vows.'),
('JOB', 22, 28, 'JOB.22.28', 'Your decisions will be carried out, and light will shine on your ways.'),
('JOB', 22, 29, 'JOB.22.29', 'When men are brought low and you say, ‘Lift them up!’ then He will save the lowly.'),
('JOB', 22, 30, 'JOB.22.30', 'He will deliver even one who is not innocent, rescuing him through the cleanness of your hands.”'),
('JOB', 23, 1, 'JOB.23.1', 'Then Job answered:'),
('JOB', 23, 2, 'JOB.23.2', '“Even today my complaint is bitter. His hand is heavy despite my groaning.'),
('JOB', 23, 3, 'JOB.23.3', 'If only I knew where to find Him, so that I could go to His seat.'),
('JOB', 23, 4, 'JOB.23.4', 'I would plead my case before Him and fill my mouth with arguments.'),
('JOB', 23, 5, 'JOB.23.5', 'I would learn how He would answer, and consider what He would say.'),
('JOB', 23, 6, 'JOB.23.6', 'Would He contend with me in His great power? No, He would certainly take note of me.'),
('JOB', 23, 7, 'JOB.23.7', 'Then an upright man could reason with Him, and I would be delivered forever from my Judge.'),
('JOB', 23, 8, 'JOB.23.8', 'If I go east, He is not there, and if I go west, I cannot find Him.'),
('JOB', 23, 9, 'JOB.23.9', 'When He is at work in the north, I cannot behold Him; when He turns to the south, I cannot see Him.'),
('JOB', 23, 10, 'JOB.23.10', 'Yet He knows the way I have taken; when He has tested me, I will come forth as gold.'),
('JOB', 23, 11, 'JOB.23.11', 'My feet have followed in His tracks; I have kept His way without turning aside.'),
('JOB', 23, 12, 'JOB.23.12', 'I have not departed from the command of His lips; I have treasured the words of His mouth more than my daily bread.'),
('JOB', 23, 13, 'JOB.23.13', 'But He is unchangeable, and who can oppose Him? He does what He desires.'),
('JOB', 23, 14, 'JOB.23.14', 'For He carries out His decree against me, and He has many such plans.'),
('JOB', 23, 15, 'JOB.23.15', 'Therefore I am terrified in His presence; when I consider this, I fear Him.'),
('JOB', 23, 16, 'JOB.23.16', 'God has made my heart faint; the Almighty has terrified me.'),
('JOB', 23, 17, 'JOB.23.17', 'Yet I am not silenced by the darkness, by the thick darkness that covers my face.'),
('JOB', 24, 1, 'JOB.24.1', '“Why does the Almighty not reserve times for judgment? Why may those who know Him never see His days?'),
('JOB', 24, 2, 'JOB.24.2', 'Men move boundary stones; they pasture stolen flocks.'),
('JOB', 24, 3, 'JOB.24.3', 'They drive away the donkey of the fatherless and take the widow’s ox in pledge.'),
('JOB', 24, 4, 'JOB.24.4', 'They push the needy off the road and force all the poor of the land into hiding.'),
('JOB', 24, 5, 'JOB.24.5', 'Indeed, like wild donkeys in the desert, the poor go to work foraging for food; the wasteland is food for their children.'),
('JOB', 24, 6, 'JOB.24.6', 'They gather fodder in the fields and glean the vineyards of the wicked.'),
('JOB', 24, 7, 'JOB.24.7', 'Without clothing, they spend the night naked; they have no covering against the cold.'),
('JOB', 24, 8, 'JOB.24.8', 'Drenched by mountain rains, they huddle against the rocks for want of shelter.'),
('JOB', 24, 9, 'JOB.24.9', 'The fatherless infant is snatched from the breast; the nursing child of the poor is seized for a debt.'),
('JOB', 24, 10, 'JOB.24.10', 'Without clothing, they wander about naked. They carry the sheaves, but still go hungry.'),
('JOB', 24, 11, 'JOB.24.11', 'They crush olives within their walls; they tread the winepresses, but go thirsty.'),
('JOB', 24, 12, 'JOB.24.12', 'From the city, men groan, and the souls of the wounded cry out, yet God charges no one with wrongdoing.'),
('JOB', 24, 13, 'JOB.24.13', 'Then there are those who rebel against the light, not knowing its ways or staying on its paths.'),
('JOB', 24, 14, 'JOB.24.14', 'When daylight is gone, the murderer rises to kill the poor and needy; in the night he is like a thief.'),
('JOB', 24, 15, 'JOB.24.15', 'The eye of the adulterer watches for twilight. Thinking, ‘No eye will see me,’ he covers his face.'),
('JOB', 24, 16, 'JOB.24.16', 'In the dark they dig through houses; by day they shut themselves in, never to experience the light.'),
('JOB', 24, 17, 'JOB.24.17', 'For to them, deep darkness is their morning; surely they are friends with the terrors of darkness!'),
('JOB', 24, 18, 'JOB.24.18', 'They are but foam on the surface of the water; their portion of the land is cursed, so that no one turns toward their vineyards.'),
('JOB', 24, 19, 'JOB.24.19', 'As drought and heat consume the melting snow, so Sheol steals those who have sinned.'),
('JOB', 24, 20, 'JOB.24.20', 'The womb forgets them; the worm feeds on them; they are remembered no more. So injustice is broken like a tree.'),
('JOB', 24, 21, 'JOB.24.21', 'They prey on the barren and childless, and show no kindness to the widow.'),
('JOB', 24, 22, 'JOB.24.22', 'Yet by His power, God drags away the mighty; though rising up, they have no assurance of life.'),
('JOB', 24, 23, 'JOB.24.23', 'He gives them a sense of security, but His eyes are on their ways.'),
('JOB', 24, 24, 'JOB.24.24', 'They are exalted for a moment, then they are gone; they are brought low and gathered up like all others; they are cut off like heads of grain.'),
('JOB', 24, 25, 'JOB.24.25', 'If this is not so, then who can prove me a liar and reduce my words to nothing?”'),
('JOB', 25, 1, 'JOB.25.1', 'Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:'),
('JOB', 25, 2, 'JOB.25.2', '“Dominion and awe belong to God; He establishes harmony in the heights of heaven.'),
('JOB', 25, 3, 'JOB.25.3', 'Can His troops be numbered? On whom does His light not rise?'),
('JOB', 25, 4, 'JOB.25.4', 'How then can a man be just before God? How can one born of woman be pure?'),
('JOB', 25, 5, 'JOB.25.5', 'If even the moon does not shine, and the stars are not pure in His sight,'),
('JOB', 25, 6, 'JOB.25.6', 'how much less man, who is but a maggot, and the son of man, who is but a worm!”'),
('JOB', 26, 1, 'JOB.26.1', 'Then Job answered:'),
('JOB', 26, 2, 'JOB.26.2', '“How you have helped the powerless and saved the arm that is feeble!'),
('JOB', 26, 3, 'JOB.26.3', 'How you have counseled the unwise and provided fully sound insight!'),
('JOB', 26, 4, 'JOB.26.4', 'To whom have you uttered these words? And whose spirit spoke through you?'),
('JOB', 26, 5, 'JOB.26.5', 'The dead tremble—those beneath the waters and those who dwell in them.'),
('JOB', 26, 6, 'JOB.26.6', 'Sheol is naked before God, and Abaddon has no covering.'),
('JOB', 26, 7, 'JOB.26.7', 'He stretches out the north over empty space; He hangs the earth upon nothing.'),
('JOB', 26, 8, 'JOB.26.8', 'He wraps up the waters in His clouds, yet the clouds do not burst under their own weight.'),
('JOB', 26, 9, 'JOB.26.9', 'He covers the face of the full moon, spreading over it His cloud.'),
('JOB', 26, 10, 'JOB.26.10', 'He has inscribed a horizon on the face of the waters at the boundary between light and darkness.'),
('JOB', 26, 11, 'JOB.26.11', 'The foundations of heaven quake, astounded at His rebuke.'),
('JOB', 26, 12, 'JOB.26.12', 'By His power He stirred the sea; by His understanding He shattered Rahab.'),
('JOB', 26, 13, 'JOB.26.13', 'By His breath the skies were cleared; His hand pierced the fleeing serpent.'),
('JOB', 26, 14, 'JOB.26.14', 'Indeed, these are but the fringes of His ways; how faint is the whisper we hear of Him! Who then can understand the thunder of His power?”'),
('JOB', 27, 1, 'JOB.27.1', 'Job continued his discourse:'),
('JOB', 27, 2, 'JOB.27.2', '“As surely as God lives, who has deprived me of justice—the Almighty, who has embittered my soul—'),
('JOB', 27, 3, 'JOB.27.3', 'as long as my breath is still within me and the breath of God remains in my nostrils,'),
('JOB', 27, 4, 'JOB.27.4', 'my lips will not speak wickedness, and my tongue will not utter deceit.'),
('JOB', 27, 5, 'JOB.27.5', 'I will never say that you are right; I will maintain my integrity until I die.'),
('JOB', 27, 6, 'JOB.27.6', 'I will cling to my righteousness and never let go. As long as I live, my conscience will not accuse me.'),
('JOB', 27, 7, 'JOB.27.7', 'May my enemy be like the wicked and my opponent like the unjust.'),
('JOB', 27, 8, 'JOB.27.8', 'For what is the hope of the godless when he is cut off, when God takes away his life?'),
('JOB', 27, 9, 'JOB.27.9', 'Will God hear his cry when distress comes upon him?'),
('JOB', 27, 10, 'JOB.27.10', 'Will he delight in the Almighty? Will he call upon God at all times?'),
('JOB', 27, 11, 'JOB.27.11', 'I will instruct you in the power of God. I will not conceal the ways of the Almighty.'),
('JOB', 27, 12, 'JOB.27.12', 'Surely all of you have seen it for yourselves. Why then do you keep up this empty talk?'),
('JOB', 27, 13, 'JOB.27.13', 'This is the wicked man’s portion from God—the heritage the ruthless receive from the Almighty.'),
('JOB', 27, 14, 'JOB.27.14', 'Though his sons are many, they are destined for the sword; and his offspring will never have enough food.'),
('JOB', 27, 15, 'JOB.27.15', 'His survivors will be buried by the plague, and their widows will not weep for them.'),
('JOB', 27, 16, 'JOB.27.16', 'Though he heaps up silver like dust and piles up a wardrobe like clay,'),
('JOB', 27, 17, 'JOB.27.17', 'what he lays up, the righteous will wear, and his silver will be divided by the innocent.'),
('JOB', 27, 18, 'JOB.27.18', 'The house he built is like a moth’s cocoon, like a hut set up by a watchman.'),
('JOB', 27, 19, 'JOB.27.19', 'He lies down wealthy, but will do so no more; when he opens his eyes, all is gone.'),
('JOB', 27, 20, 'JOB.27.20', 'Terrors overtake him like a flood; a tempest sweeps him away in the night.'),
('JOB', 27, 21, 'JOB.27.21', 'The east wind carries him away, and he is gone; it sweeps him out of his place.'),
('JOB', 27, 22, 'JOB.27.22', 'It hurls itself against him without mercy as he flees headlong from its power.'),
('JOB', 27, 23, 'JOB.27.23', 'It claps its hands at him and hisses him out of his place.'),
('JOB', 28, 1, 'JOB.28.1', '“Surely there is a mine for silver and a place where gold is refined.'),
('JOB', 28, 2, 'JOB.28.2', 'Iron is taken from the earth, and copper is smelted from ore.'),
('JOB', 28, 3, 'JOB.28.3', 'Man puts an end to the darkness; he probes the farthest recesses for ore in deepest darkness.'),
('JOB', 28, 4, 'JOB.28.4', 'Far from human habitation he cuts a shaft in places forgotten by the foot of man. Far from men he dangles and sways.'),
('JOB', 28, 5, 'JOB.28.5', 'Food may come from the earth, but from below it is transformed as by fire.'),
('JOB', 28, 6, 'JOB.28.6', 'Its rocks are the source of sapphires, containing flecks of gold.'),
('JOB', 28, 7, 'JOB.28.7', 'No bird of prey knows that path; no falcon’s eye has seen it.'),
('JOB', 28, 8, 'JOB.28.8', 'Proud beasts have never trodden it; no lion has ever prowled over it.'),
('JOB', 28, 9, 'JOB.28.9', 'The miner strikes the flint; he overturns mountains at their base.'),
('JOB', 28, 10, 'JOB.28.10', 'He hews out channels in the rocks, and his eyes spot every treasure.'),
('JOB', 28, 11, 'JOB.28.11', 'He stops up the sources of the streams to bring what is hidden to light.'),
('JOB', 28, 12, 'JOB.28.12', 'But where can wisdom be found, and where does understanding dwell?'),
('JOB', 28, 13, 'JOB.28.13', 'No man can know its value, nor is it found in the land of the living.'),
('JOB', 28, 14, 'JOB.28.14', 'The ocean depths say, ‘It is not in me,’ while the sea declares, ‘It is not with me.’'),
('JOB', 28, 15, 'JOB.28.15', 'It cannot be bought with gold, nor can its price be weighed out in silver.'),
('JOB', 28, 16, 'JOB.28.16', 'It cannot be valued in the gold of Ophir, in precious onyx or sapphire.'),
('JOB', 28, 17, 'JOB.28.17', 'Neither gold nor crystal can compare to it, nor jewels of fine gold be exchanged for it.'),
('JOB', 28, 18, 'JOB.28.18', 'Coral and quartz are unworthy of mention; the price of wisdom is beyond rubies.'),
('JOB', 28, 19, 'JOB.28.19', 'Topaz from Cush cannot compare to it, nor can it be valued in pure gold.'),
('JOB', 28, 20, 'JOB.28.20', 'From where, then, does wisdom come, and where does understanding dwell?'),
('JOB', 28, 21, 'JOB.28.21', 'It is hidden from the eyes of every living thing and concealed from the birds of the air.'),
('JOB', 28, 22, 'JOB.28.22', 'Abaddon and Death say, ‘We have heard a rumor about it.’'),
('JOB', 28, 23, 'JOB.28.23', 'But God understands its way, and He knows its place.'),
('JOB', 28, 24, 'JOB.28.24', 'For He looks to the ends of the earth and sees everything under the heavens.'),
('JOB', 28, 25, 'JOB.28.25', 'When God fixed the weight of the wind and measured out the waters,'),
('JOB', 28, 26, 'JOB.28.26', 'when He set a limit for the rain and a path for the thunderbolt,'),
('JOB', 28, 27, 'JOB.28.27', 'then He looked at wisdom and appraised it; He established it and searched it out.'),
('JOB', 28, 28, 'JOB.28.28', 'And He said to man, ‘Behold, the fear of the Lord, that is wisdom, and to turn away from evil is understanding.’”'),
('JOB', 29, 1, 'JOB.29.1', 'And Job continued his discourse:'),
('JOB', 29, 2, 'JOB.29.2', '“How I long for the months gone by, for the days when God watched over me,'),
('JOB', 29, 3, 'JOB.29.3', 'when His lamp shone above my head, and by His light I walked through the darkness,'),
('JOB', 29, 4, 'JOB.29.4', 'when I was in my prime, when the friendship of God rested on my tent,'),
('JOB', 29, 5, 'JOB.29.5', 'when the Almighty was still with me and my children were around me,'),
('JOB', 29, 6, 'JOB.29.6', 'when my steps were bathed in cream and the rock poured out for me streams of oil!'),
('JOB', 29, 7, 'JOB.29.7', 'When I went out to the city gate and took my seat in the public square,'),
('JOB', 29, 8, 'JOB.29.8', 'the young men saw me and withdrew, and the old men rose to their feet.'),
('JOB', 29, 9, 'JOB.29.9', 'The princes refrained from speaking and covered their mouths with their hands.'),
('JOB', 29, 10, 'JOB.29.10', 'The voices of the nobles were hushed, and their tongues stuck to the roofs of their mouths.'),
('JOB', 29, 11, 'JOB.29.11', 'For those who heard me called me blessed, and those who saw me commended me,'),
('JOB', 29, 12, 'JOB.29.12', 'because I rescued the poor who cried out and the fatherless who had no helper.'),
('JOB', 29, 13, 'JOB.29.13', 'The dying man blessed me, and I made the widow’s heart sing for joy.'),
('JOB', 29, 14, 'JOB.29.14', 'I put on righteousness, and it clothed me; justice was my robe and my turban.'),
('JOB', 29, 15, 'JOB.29.15', 'I served as eyes to the blind and as feet to the lame.'),
('JOB', 29, 16, 'JOB.29.16', 'I was a father to the needy, and I took up the case of the stranger.'),
('JOB', 29, 17, 'JOB.29.17', 'I shattered the fangs of the unjust and snatched the prey from his teeth.'),
('JOB', 29, 18, 'JOB.29.18', 'So I thought: ‘I will die in my nest and multiply my days as the sand.'),
('JOB', 29, 19, 'JOB.29.19', 'My roots will spread out to the waters, and the dew will rest nightly on my branches.'),
('JOB', 29, 20, 'JOB.29.20', 'My glory is ever new within me, and my bow is renewed in my hand.’'),
('JOB', 29, 21, 'JOB.29.21', 'Men listened to me with expectation, waiting silently for my counsel.'),
('JOB', 29, 22, 'JOB.29.22', 'After my words, they spoke no more; my speech settled on them like dew.'),
('JOB', 29, 23, 'JOB.29.23', 'They waited for me as for rain and drank in my words like spring showers.'),
('JOB', 29, 24, 'JOB.29.24', 'If I smiled at them, they did not believe it; the light of my countenance was precious.'),
('JOB', 29, 25, 'JOB.29.25', 'I chose their course and presided as chief. So I dwelt as a king among his troops, as a comforter of the mourners.'),
('JOB', 30, 1, 'JOB.30.1', '“But now they mock me, men younger than I am, whose fathers I would have refused to put with my sheep dogs.'),
('JOB', 30, 2, 'JOB.30.2', 'What use to me was the strength of their hands, since their vigor had left them?'),
('JOB', 30, 3, 'JOB.30.3', 'Gaunt from poverty and hunger, they gnawed the dry land, and the desolate wasteland by night.'),
('JOB', 30, 4, 'JOB.30.4', 'They plucked mallow among the shrubs, and the roots of the broom tree were their food.'),
('JOB', 30, 5, 'JOB.30.5', 'They were banished from among men, shouted at like thieves,'),
('JOB', 30, 6, 'JOB.30.6', 'so that they lived on the slopes of the wadis, among the rocks and in holes in the ground.'),
('JOB', 30, 7, 'JOB.30.7', 'They cried out among the shrubs and huddled beneath the nettles.'),
('JOB', 30, 8, 'JOB.30.8', 'A senseless and nameless brood, they were driven off the land.'),
('JOB', 30, 9, 'JOB.30.9', 'And now they mock me in song; I have become a byword among them.'),
('JOB', 30, 10, 'JOB.30.10', 'They abhor me and keep far from me; they do not hesitate to spit in my face.'),
('JOB', 30, 11, 'JOB.30.11', 'Because God has unstrung my bow and afflicted me, they have cast off restraint in my presence.'),
('JOB', 30, 12, 'JOB.30.12', 'The rabble arises at my right; they lay snares for my feet and build siege ramps against me.'),
('JOB', 30, 13, 'JOB.30.13', 'They tear up my path; they profit from my destruction, with no one to restrain them.'),
('JOB', 30, 14, 'JOB.30.14', 'They advance as through a wide breach; through the ruins they keep rolling in.'),
('JOB', 30, 15, 'JOB.30.15', 'Terrors are turned loose against me; they drive away my dignity as by the wind, and my prosperity has passed like a cloud.'),
('JOB', 30, 16, 'JOB.30.16', 'And now my soul is poured out within me; days of affliction grip me.'),
('JOB', 30, 17, 'JOB.30.17', 'Night pierces my bones, and my gnawing pains never rest.'),
('JOB', 30, 18, 'JOB.30.18', 'With great force He grasps my garment; He seizes me by the collar of my tunic.'),
('JOB', 30, 19, 'JOB.30.19', 'He throws me into the mud, and I have become like dust and ashes.'),
('JOB', 30, 20, 'JOB.30.20', 'I cry out to You for help, but You do not answer; when I stand up, You merely look at me.'),
('JOB', 30, 21, 'JOB.30.21', 'You have ruthlessly turned on me; You oppose me with Your strong hand.'),
('JOB', 30, 22, 'JOB.30.22', 'You snatch me up into the wind and drive me before it; You toss me about in the storm.'),
('JOB', 30, 23, 'JOB.30.23', 'Yes, I know that You will bring me down to death, to the place appointed for all the living.'),
('JOB', 30, 24, 'JOB.30.24', 'Yet no one stretches out his hand against a ruined man when he cries for help in his distress.'),
('JOB', 30, 25, 'JOB.30.25', 'Have I not wept for those in trouble? Has my soul not grieved for the needy?'),
('JOB', 30, 26, 'JOB.30.26', 'But when I hoped for good, evil came; when I looked for light, darkness fell.'),
('JOB', 30, 27, 'JOB.30.27', 'I am churning within and cannot rest; days of affliction confront me.'),
('JOB', 30, 28, 'JOB.30.28', 'I go about blackened, but not by the sun. I stand up in the assembly and cry for help.'),
('JOB', 30, 29, 'JOB.30.29', 'I have become a brother of jackals, a companion of ostriches.'),
('JOB', 30, 30, 'JOB.30.30', 'My skin grows black and peels, and my bones burn with fever.'),
('JOB', 30, 31, 'JOB.30.31', 'My harp is tuned to mourning and my flute to the sound of weeping.'),
('JOB', 31, 1, 'JOB.31.1', '“I have made a covenant with my eyes. How then could I gaze with desire at a virgin?'),
('JOB', 31, 2, 'JOB.31.2', 'For what is the allotment of God from above, or the heritage from the Almighty on high?'),
('JOB', 31, 3, 'JOB.31.3', 'Does not disaster come to the unjust and calamity to the workers of iniquity?'),
('JOB', 31, 4, 'JOB.31.4', 'Does He not see my ways and count my every step?'),
('JOB', 31, 5, 'JOB.31.5', 'If I have walked in falsehood or my foot has rushed to deceit,'),
('JOB', 31, 6, 'JOB.31.6', 'let God weigh me with honest scales, that He may know my integrity.'),
('JOB', 31, 7, 'JOB.31.7', 'If my steps have turned from the path, if my heart has followed my eyes, or if impurity has stuck to my hands,'),
('JOB', 31, 8, 'JOB.31.8', 'then may another eat what I have sown, and may my crops be uprooted.'),
('JOB', 31, 9, 'JOB.31.9', 'If my heart has been enticed by my neighbor’s wife, or I have lurked at his door,'),
('JOB', 31, 10, 'JOB.31.10', 'then may my own wife grind grain for another, and may other men sleep with her.'),
('JOB', 31, 11, 'JOB.31.11', 'For that would be a heinous crime, an iniquity to be judged.'),
('JOB', 31, 12, 'JOB.31.12', 'For it is a fire that burns down to Abaddon; it would root out my entire harvest.'),
('JOB', 31, 13, 'JOB.31.13', 'If I have rejected the cause of my manservant or maidservant when they made a complaint against me,'),
('JOB', 31, 14, 'JOB.31.14', 'what will I do when God rises to judge? How will I answer when called to account?'),
('JOB', 31, 15, 'JOB.31.15', 'Did not He who made me in the womb also make them? Did not the same One form us in the womb?'),
('JOB', 31, 16, 'JOB.31.16', 'If I have denied the desires of the poor or allowed the widow’s eyes to fail,'),
('JOB', 31, 17, 'JOB.31.17', 'if I have eaten my morsel alone, not sharing it with the fatherless—'),
('JOB', 31, 18, 'JOB.31.18', 'though from my youth I reared him as would a father, and from my mother’s womb I guided the widow—'),
('JOB', 31, 19, 'JOB.31.19', 'if I have seen one perish for lack of clothing, or a needy man without a cloak,'),
('JOB', 31, 20, 'JOB.31.20', 'if his heart has not blessed me for warming him with the fleece of my sheep,'),
('JOB', 31, 21, 'JOB.31.21', 'if I have lifted up my hand against the fatherless because I saw that I had support in the gate,'),
('JOB', 31, 22, 'JOB.31.22', 'then may my arm fall from my shoulder and be torn from its socket.'),
('JOB', 31, 23, 'JOB.31.23', 'For calamity from God terrifies me, and His splendor I cannot overpower.'),
('JOB', 31, 24, 'JOB.31.24', 'If I have put my trust in gold or called pure gold my security,'),
('JOB', 31, 25, 'JOB.31.25', 'if I have rejoiced in my great wealth because my hand had gained so much,'),
('JOB', 31, 26, 'JOB.31.26', 'if I have beheld the sun in its radiance or the moon moving in splendor,'),
('JOB', 31, 27, 'JOB.31.27', 'so that my heart was secretly enticed and my hand threw a kiss from my mouth,'),
('JOB', 31, 28, 'JOB.31.28', 'this would also be an iniquity to be judged, for I would have denied God on high.'),
('JOB', 31, 29, 'JOB.31.29', 'If I have rejoiced in my enemy’s ruin, or exulted when evil befell him—'),
('JOB', 31, 30, 'JOB.31.30', 'I have not allowed my mouth to sin by asking for his life with a curse—'),
('JOB', 31, 31, 'JOB.31.31', 'if the men of my house have not said, ‘Who is there who has not had his fill?’—'),
('JOB', 31, 32, 'JOB.31.32', 'but no stranger had to lodge on the street, for my door has been open to the traveler—'),
('JOB', 31, 33, 'JOB.31.33', 'if I have covered my transgressions like Adam by hiding my guilt in my heart,'),
('JOB', 31, 34, 'JOB.31.34', 'because I greatly feared the crowds and the contempt of the clans terrified me, so that I kept silent and would not go outside—'),
('JOB', 31, 35, 'JOB.31.35', '(Oh, that I had one to hear me! Here is my signature. Let the Almighty answer me; let my accuser compose an indictment.'),
('JOB', 31, 36, 'JOB.31.36', 'Surely I would carry it on my shoulder and wear it like a crown.'),
('JOB', 31, 37, 'JOB.31.37', 'I would give account of all my steps; I would approach Him like a prince.)—'),
('JOB', 31, 38, 'JOB.31.38', 'if my land cries out against me and its furrows weep together,'),
('JOB', 31, 39, 'JOB.31.39', 'if I have devoured its produce without payment or broken the spirit of its tenants,'),
('JOB', 31, 40, 'JOB.31.40', 'then let briers grow instead of wheat and stinkweed instead of barley.” Thus conclude the words of Job.'),
('JOB', 32, 1, 'JOB.32.1', 'So these three men stopped answering Job, because he was righteous in his own eyes.'),
('JOB', 32, 2, 'JOB.32.2', 'This kindled the anger of Elihu son of Barachel the Buzite, of the family of Ram. He burned with anger against Job for justifying himself rather than God,'),
('JOB', 32, 3, 'JOB.32.3', 'and he burned with anger against Job’s three friends because they had failed to refute Job, and yet had condemned him.'),
('JOB', 32, 4, 'JOB.32.4', 'Now Elihu had waited to speak to Job because the others were older than he.'),
('JOB', 32, 5, 'JOB.32.5', 'But when he saw that the three men had no further reply, his anger was kindled.'),
('JOB', 32, 6, 'JOB.32.6', 'So Elihu son of Barachel the Buzite declared: “I am young in years, while you are old; that is why I was timid and afraid to tell you what I know.'),
('JOB', 32, 7, 'JOB.32.7', 'I thought that age should speak, and many years should teach wisdom.'),
('JOB', 32, 8, 'JOB.32.8', 'But there is a spirit in a man, the breath of the Almighty, that gives him understanding.'),
('JOB', 32, 9, 'JOB.32.9', 'It is not only the old who are wise, or the elderly who understand justice.'),
('JOB', 32, 10, 'JOB.32.10', 'Therefore I say, ‘Listen to me; I too will declare what I know.’'),
('JOB', 32, 11, 'JOB.32.11', 'Indeed, I waited while you spoke; I listened to your reasoning; as you searched for words,'),
('JOB', 32, 12, 'JOB.32.12', 'I paid you full attention. But no one proved Job wrong; not one of you rebutted his arguments.'),
('JOB', 32, 13, 'JOB.32.13', 'So do not claim, ‘We have found wisdom; let God, not man, refute him.’'),
('JOB', 32, 14, 'JOB.32.14', 'But Job has not directed his words against me, and I will not answer him with your arguments.'),
('JOB', 32, 15, 'JOB.32.15', 'Job’s friends are dismayed, with no more to say; words have escaped them.'),
('JOB', 32, 16, 'JOB.32.16', 'Must I wait, now that they are silent, now that they stand and no longer reply?'),
('JOB', 32, 17, 'JOB.32.17', 'I too will answer; yes, I will declare what I know.'),
('JOB', 32, 18, 'JOB.32.18', 'For I am full of words, and my spirit within me compels me.'),
('JOB', 32, 19, 'JOB.32.19', 'Behold, my belly is like unvented wine; it is about to burst like a new wineskin.'),
('JOB', 32, 20, 'JOB.32.20', 'I must speak and find relief; I must open my lips and respond.'),
('JOB', 32, 21, 'JOB.32.21', 'I will be partial to no one, nor will I flatter any man.'),
('JOB', 32, 22, 'JOB.32.22', 'For I do not know how to flatter, or my Maker would remove me in an instant.'),
('JOB', 33, 1, 'JOB.33.1', '“But now, O Job, hear my speech, and listen to all my words.'),
('JOB', 33, 2, 'JOB.33.2', 'Behold, I will open my mouth; my address is on the tip of my tongue.'),
('JOB', 33, 3, 'JOB.33.3', 'My words are from an upright heart, and my lips speak sincerely what I know.'),
('JOB', 33, 4, 'JOB.33.4', 'The Spirit of God has made me, and the breath of the Almighty gives me life.'),
('JOB', 33, 5, 'JOB.33.5', 'Refute me if you can; prepare your case and confront me.'),
('JOB', 33, 6, 'JOB.33.6', 'I am just like you before God; I was also formed from clay.'),
('JOB', 33, 7, 'JOB.33.7', 'Surely no fear of me should terrify you; nor will my hand be heavy upon you.'),
('JOB', 33, 8, 'JOB.33.8', 'Surely you have spoken in my hearing, and I have heard these very words:'),
('JOB', 33, 9, 'JOB.33.9', '‘I am pure, without transgression; I am clean, with no iniquity in me.'),
('JOB', 33, 10, 'JOB.33.10', 'Yet God finds occasions against me; He counts me as His enemy.'),
('JOB', 33, 11, 'JOB.33.11', 'He puts my feet in the stocks; He watches over all my paths.’'),
('JOB', 33, 12, 'JOB.33.12', 'Behold, you are not right in this matter. I will answer you, for God is greater than man.'),
('JOB', 33, 13, 'JOB.33.13', 'Why do you complain to Him that He answers nothing a man asks?'),
('JOB', 33, 14, 'JOB.33.14', 'For God speaks in one way and in another, yet no one notices.'),
('JOB', 33, 15, 'JOB.33.15', 'In a dream, in a vision in the night, when deep sleep falls upon men as they slumber on their beds,'),
('JOB', 33, 16, 'JOB.33.16', 'He opens their ears and terrifies them with warnings'),
('JOB', 33, 17, 'JOB.33.17', 'to turn a man from wrongdoing and keep him from pride,'),
('JOB', 33, 18, 'JOB.33.18', 'to preserve his soul from the Pit and his life from perishing by the sword.'),
('JOB', 33, 19, 'JOB.33.19', 'A man is also chastened on his bed with pain and constant distress in his bones,'),
('JOB', 33, 20, 'JOB.33.20', 'so that he detests his bread, and his soul loathes his favorite food.'),
('JOB', 33, 21, 'JOB.33.21', 'His flesh wastes away from sight, and his hidden bones protrude.'),
('JOB', 33, 22, 'JOB.33.22', 'He draws near to the Pit, and his life to the messengers of death.'),
('JOB', 33, 23, 'JOB.33.23', 'Yet if there is a messenger on his side, one mediator in a thousand, to tell a man what is right for him,'),
('JOB', 33, 24, 'JOB.33.24', 'to be gracious to him and say, ‘Spare him from going down to the Pit; I have found his ransom,’'),
('JOB', 33, 25, 'JOB.33.25', 'then his flesh is refreshed like a child’s; he returns to the days of his youth.'),
('JOB', 33, 26, 'JOB.33.26', 'He prays to God and finds favor; he sees God’s face and shouts for joy, and God restores His righteousness to that man.'),
('JOB', 33, 27, 'JOB.33.27', 'Then he sings before men with these words: ‘I have sinned and perverted what was right; yet I did not get what I deserved.'),
('JOB', 33, 28, 'JOB.33.28', 'He redeemed my soul from going down to the Pit, and I will live to see the light.’'),
('JOB', 33, 29, 'JOB.33.29', 'Behold, all these things God does to a man, two or even three times,'),
('JOB', 33, 30, 'JOB.33.30', 'to bring back his soul from the Pit, that he may be enlightened with the light of life.'),
('JOB', 33, 31, 'JOB.33.31', 'Pay attention, Job, and listen to me; be silent, and I will speak.'),
('JOB', 33, 32, 'JOB.33.32', 'But if you have something to say, answer me; speak up, for I would like to vindicate you.'),
('JOB', 33, 33, 'JOB.33.33', 'But if not, then listen to me; be quiet, and I will teach you wisdom.”'),
('JOB', 34, 1, 'JOB.34.1', 'Then Elihu continued:'),
('JOB', 34, 2, 'JOB.34.2', '“Hear my words, O wise men; give ear to me, O men of learning.'),
('JOB', 34, 3, 'JOB.34.3', 'For the ear tests words as the mouth tastes food.'),
('JOB', 34, 4, 'JOB.34.4', 'Let us choose for ourselves what is right; let us learn together what is good.'),
('JOB', 34, 5, 'JOB.34.5', 'For Job has declared, ‘I am righteous, yet God has deprived me of justice.'),
('JOB', 34, 6, 'JOB.34.6', 'Would I lie about my case? My wound is incurable, though I am without transgression.’'),
('JOB', 34, 7, 'JOB.34.7', 'What man is like Job, who drinks up derision like water?'),
('JOB', 34, 8, 'JOB.34.8', 'He keeps company with evildoers and walks with wicked men.'),
('JOB', 34, 9, 'JOB.34.9', 'For he has said, ‘It profits a man nothing that he should delight in God.’'),
('JOB', 34, 10, 'JOB.34.10', 'Therefore listen to me, O men of understanding. Far be it from God to do wrong, and from the Almighty to act unjustly.'),
('JOB', 34, 11, 'JOB.34.11', 'For according to a man’s deeds He repays him; according to a man’s ways He brings consequences.'),
('JOB', 34, 12, 'JOB.34.12', 'Indeed, it is true that God does not act wickedly, and the Almighty does not pervert justice.'),
('JOB', 34, 13, 'JOB.34.13', 'Who gave Him charge over the earth? Who appointed Him over the whole world?'),
('JOB', 34, 14, 'JOB.34.14', 'If He were to set His heart to it and withdraw His Spirit and breath,'),
('JOB', 34, 15, 'JOB.34.15', 'all flesh would perish together and mankind would return to the dust.'),
('JOB', 34, 16, 'JOB.34.16', 'If you have understanding, hear this; listen to my words.'),
('JOB', 34, 17, 'JOB.34.17', 'Could one who hates justice govern? Will you condemn the just and mighty One,'),
('JOB', 34, 18, 'JOB.34.18', 'who says to kings, ‘You are worthless!’ and to nobles, ‘You are wicked,’'),
('JOB', 34, 19, 'JOB.34.19', 'who is not partial to princes and does not favor rich over poor? For they are all the work of His hands.'),
('JOB', 34, 20, 'JOB.34.20', 'They die in an instant, in the middle of the night. The people convulse and pass away; the mighty are removed without human hand.'),
('JOB', 34, 21, 'JOB.34.21', 'For His eyes are on the ways of a man, and He sees his every step.'),
('JOB', 34, 22, 'JOB.34.22', 'There is no darkness or deep shadow where the workers of iniquity can hide.'),
('JOB', 34, 23, 'JOB.34.23', 'For God need not examine a man further or have him approach for judgment.'),
('JOB', 34, 24, 'JOB.34.24', 'He shatters the mighty without inquiry and sets up others in their place.'),
('JOB', 34, 25, 'JOB.34.25', 'Therefore, He recognizes their deeds; He overthrows them in the night and they are crushed.'),
('JOB', 34, 26, 'JOB.34.26', 'He strikes them for their wickedness in full view,'),
('JOB', 34, 27, 'JOB.34.27', 'because they turned aside from Him and had no regard for any of His ways.'),
('JOB', 34, 28, 'JOB.34.28', 'They caused the cry of the poor to come before Him, and He heard the outcry of the afflicted.'),
('JOB', 34, 29, 'JOB.34.29', 'But when He remains silent, who can condemn Him? When He hides His face, who can see Him? Yet He watches over both man and nation,'),
('JOB', 34, 30, 'JOB.34.30', 'that godless men should not rule or lay snares for the people.'),
('JOB', 34, 31, 'JOB.34.31', 'Suppose someone says to God, ‘I have endured my punishment; I will offend no more.'),
('JOB', 34, 32, 'JOB.34.32', 'Teach me what I cannot see; if I have done wrong, I will not do it again.’'),
('JOB', 34, 33, 'JOB.34.33', 'Should God repay you on your own terms when you have disavowed Him? You must choose, not I; so tell me what you know.'),
('JOB', 34, 34, 'JOB.34.34', 'Men of understanding will declare to me, and the wise men who hear me will say:'),
('JOB', 34, 35, 'JOB.34.35', '‘Job speaks without knowledge; his words lack insight.’'),
('JOB', 34, 36, 'JOB.34.36', 'If only Job were tried to the utmost for answering like a wicked man.'),
('JOB', 34, 37, 'JOB.34.37', 'For he adds rebellion to his sin; he claps his hands among us and multiplies his words against God.”'),
('JOB', 35, 1, 'JOB.35.1', 'And Elihu went on to say:'),
('JOB', 35, 2, 'JOB.35.2', '“Do you think this is just? You say, ‘I am more righteous than God.’'),
('JOB', 35, 3, 'JOB.35.3', 'For you ask, ‘What does it profit me, and what benefit do I gain apart from sin?’'),
('JOB', 35, 4, 'JOB.35.4', 'I will reply to you and to your friends as well.'),
('JOB', 35, 5, 'JOB.35.5', 'Look to the heavens and see; gaze at the clouds high above you.'),
('JOB', 35, 6, 'JOB.35.6', 'If you sin, what do you accomplish against Him? If you multiply your transgressions, what do you do to Him?'),
('JOB', 35, 7, 'JOB.35.7', 'If you are righteous, what do you give Him, or what does He receive from your hand?'),
('JOB', 35, 8, 'JOB.35.8', 'Your wickedness affects only a man like yourself, and your righteousness only a son of man.'),
('JOB', 35, 9, 'JOB.35.9', 'Men cry out under great oppression; they plead for relief from the arm of the mighty.'),
('JOB', 35, 10, 'JOB.35.10', 'But no one asks, ‘Where is God my Maker, who gives us songs in the night,'),
('JOB', 35, 11, 'JOB.35.11', 'who teaches us more than the beasts of the earth and makes us wiser than the birds of the air?’'),
('JOB', 35, 12, 'JOB.35.12', 'There they cry out, but He does not answer, because of the pride of evil men.'),
('JOB', 35, 13, 'JOB.35.13', 'Surely God does not listen to empty pleas, and the Almighty does not take note of it.'),
('JOB', 35, 14, 'JOB.35.14', 'How much less, then, when you say that you do not see Him, that your case is before Him and you must wait for Him,'),
('JOB', 35, 15, 'JOB.35.15', 'and further, that in His anger He has not punished or taken much notice of folly!'),
('JOB', 35, 16, 'JOB.35.16', 'So Job opens his mouth in vain and multiplies words without knowledge.”'),
('JOB', 36, 1, 'JOB.36.1', 'And Elihu continued:'),
('JOB', 36, 2, 'JOB.36.2', '“Bear with me a little longer, and I will show you that there is more to be said on God’s behalf.'),
('JOB', 36, 3, 'JOB.36.3', 'I get my knowledge from afar, and I will ascribe justice to my Maker.'),
('JOB', 36, 4, 'JOB.36.4', 'For truly my words are free of falsehood; one perfect in knowledge is with you.'),
('JOB', 36, 5, 'JOB.36.5', 'Indeed, God is mighty, but He despises no one; He is mighty in strength of understanding.'),
('JOB', 36, 6, 'JOB.36.6', 'He does not keep the wicked alive, but He grants justice to the afflicted.'),
('JOB', 36, 7, 'JOB.36.7', 'He does not take His eyes off the righteous, but He enthrones them with kings and exalts them forever.'),
('JOB', 36, 8, 'JOB.36.8', 'And if men are bound with chains, caught in cords of affliction,'),
('JOB', 36, 9, 'JOB.36.9', 'then He tells them their deeds and how arrogantly they have transgressed.'),
('JOB', 36, 10, 'JOB.36.10', 'He opens their ears to correction and commands that they turn from iniquity.'),
('JOB', 36, 11, 'JOB.36.11', 'If they obey and serve Him, then they end their days in prosperity and their years in happiness.'),
('JOB', 36, 12, 'JOB.36.12', 'But if they do not obey, then they perish by the sword and die without knowledge.'),
('JOB', 36, 13, 'JOB.36.13', 'The godless in heart harbor resentment; even when He binds them, they do not cry for help.'),
('JOB', 36, 14, 'JOB.36.14', 'They die in their youth, among the male shrine prostitutes.'),
('JOB', 36, 15, 'JOB.36.15', 'God rescues the afflicted by their affliction and opens their ears in oppression.'),
('JOB', 36, 16, 'JOB.36.16', 'Indeed, He drew you from the jaws of distress to a spacious and broad place, to a table full of richness.'),
('JOB', 36, 17, 'JOB.36.17', 'But now you are laden with the judgment due the wicked; judgment and justice have seized you.'),
('JOB', 36, 18, 'JOB.36.18', 'Be careful that no one lures you with riches; do not let a large bribe lead you astray.'),
('JOB', 36, 19, 'JOB.36.19', 'Can your wealth or all your mighty effort keep you from distress?'),
('JOB', 36, 20, 'JOB.36.20', 'Do not long for the night, when people vanish from their homes.'),
('JOB', 36, 21, 'JOB.36.21', 'Be careful not to turn to iniquity, for this you have preferred to affliction.'),
('JOB', 36, 22, 'JOB.36.22', 'Behold, God is exalted in His power. Who is a teacher like Him?'),
('JOB', 36, 23, 'JOB.36.23', 'Who has appointed His way for Him, or told Him, ‘You have done wrong’?'),
('JOB', 36, 24, 'JOB.36.24', 'Remember to magnify His work, which men have praised in song.'),
('JOB', 36, 25, 'JOB.36.25', 'All mankind has seen it; men behold it from afar.'),
('JOB', 36, 26, 'JOB.36.26', 'Indeed, God is great—beyond our knowledge; the number of His years is unsearchable.'),
('JOB', 36, 27, 'JOB.36.27', 'For He draws up drops of water which distill the rain from the mist,'),
('JOB', 36, 28, 'JOB.36.28', 'which the clouds pour out and shower abundantly on mankind.'),
('JOB', 36, 29, 'JOB.36.29', 'Furthermore, who can understand how the clouds spread out, how the thunder roars from His pavilion?'),
('JOB', 36, 30, 'JOB.36.30', 'See how He scatters His lightning around Him and covers the depths of the sea.'),
('JOB', 36, 31, 'JOB.36.31', 'For by these He judges the nations and provides food in abundance.'),
('JOB', 36, 32, 'JOB.36.32', 'He fills His hands with lightning and commands it to strike its mark.'),
('JOB', 36, 33, 'JOB.36.33', 'The thunder declares His presence; even the cattle regard the rising storm.'),
('JOB', 37, 1, 'JOB.37.1', '“At this my heart also pounds and leaps from its place.'),
('JOB', 37, 2, 'JOB.37.2', 'Listen closely to the thunder of His voice and the rumbling that comes from His mouth.'),
('JOB', 37, 3, 'JOB.37.3', 'He unleashes His lightning beneath the whole sky and sends it to the ends of the earth.'),
('JOB', 37, 4, 'JOB.37.4', 'Then there comes a roaring sound; He thunders with His majestic voice. He does not restrain the lightning when His voice resounds.'),
('JOB', 37, 5, 'JOB.37.5', 'God thunders wondrously with His voice; He does great things we cannot comprehend.'),
('JOB', 37, 6, 'JOB.37.6', 'For He says to the snow, ‘Fall on the earth,’ and to the gentle rain, ‘Pour out a mighty downpour.’'),
('JOB', 37, 7, 'JOB.37.7', 'He seals up the hand of every man, so that all men may know His work.'),
('JOB', 37, 8, 'JOB.37.8', 'The wild animals enter their lairs; they settle down in their dens.'),
('JOB', 37, 9, 'JOB.37.9', 'The tempest comes from its chamber, and the cold from the driving north winds.'),
('JOB', 37, 10, 'JOB.37.10', 'By the breath of God the ice is formed and the watery expanses are frozen.'),
('JOB', 37, 11, 'JOB.37.11', 'He loads the clouds with moisture; He scatters His lightning through them.'),
('JOB', 37, 12, 'JOB.37.12', 'They swirl about, whirling at His direction, accomplishing all that He commands over the face of all the earth.'),
('JOB', 37, 13, 'JOB.37.13', 'Whether for punishment or for His land, He accomplishes this in His loving devotion.'),
('JOB', 37, 14, 'JOB.37.14', 'Listen to this, O Job; stand still and consider the wonders of God.'),
('JOB', 37, 15, 'JOB.37.15', 'Do you know how God dispatches the clouds or makes the lightning flash?'),
('JOB', 37, 16, 'JOB.37.16', 'Do you understand how the clouds float, those wonders of Him who is perfect in knowledge?'),
('JOB', 37, 17, 'JOB.37.17', 'You whose clothes get hot when the land lies hushed under the south wind,'),
('JOB', 37, 18, 'JOB.37.18', 'can you, like Him, spread out the skies, as strong as a mirror of bronze?'),
('JOB', 37, 19, 'JOB.37.19', 'Teach us what we should say to Him; we cannot draw up our case because of our darkness.'),
('JOB', 37, 20, 'JOB.37.20', 'Should He be told that I want to speak? Would a man ask to be swallowed up?'),
('JOB', 37, 21, 'JOB.37.21', 'Now no one can gaze at the sun when it is bright in the skies after the wind has swept them clean.'),
('JOB', 37, 22, 'JOB.37.22', 'Out of the north He comes in golden splendor; awesome majesty surrounds Him.'),
('JOB', 37, 23, 'JOB.37.23', 'The Almighty is beyond our reach; He is exalted in power! In His justice and great righteousness He does not oppress.'),
('JOB', 37, 24, 'JOB.37.24', 'Therefore, men fear Him, for He is not partial to the wise in heart.”'),
('JOB', 38, 1, 'JOB.38.1', 'Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind and said:'),
('JOB', 38, 2, 'JOB.38.2', '“Who is this who obscures My counsel by words without knowledge?'),
('JOB', 38, 3, 'JOB.38.3', 'Now brace yourself like a man; I will question you, and you shall inform Me.'),
('JOB', 38, 4, 'JOB.38.4', 'Where were you when I laid the foundations of the earth? Tell Me, if you have understanding.'),
('JOB', 38, 5, 'JOB.38.5', 'Who fixed its measurements? Surely you know! Or who stretched a measuring line across it?'),
('JOB', 38, 6, 'JOB.38.6', 'On what were its foundations set, or who laid its cornerstone,'),
('JOB', 38, 7, 'JOB.38.7', 'while the morning stars sang together and all the sons of God shouted for joy?'),
('JOB', 38, 8, 'JOB.38.8', 'Who enclosed the sea behind doors when it burst forth from the womb,'),
('JOB', 38, 9, 'JOB.38.9', 'when I made the clouds its garment and thick darkness its blanket,'),
('JOB', 38, 10, 'JOB.38.10', 'when I fixed its boundaries and set in place its bars and doors,'),
('JOB', 38, 11, 'JOB.38.11', 'and I declared: ‘You may come this far, but no farther; here your proud waves must stop’?'),
('JOB', 38, 12, 'JOB.38.12', 'In your days, have you commanded the morning or assigned the dawn its place,'),
('JOB', 38, 13, 'JOB.38.13', 'that it might spread to the ends of the earth and shake the wicked out of it?'),
('JOB', 38, 14, 'JOB.38.14', 'The earth takes shape like clay under a seal; its hills stand out like the folds of a garment.'),
('JOB', 38, 15, 'JOB.38.15', 'Light is withheld from the wicked, and their upraised arm is broken.'),
('JOB', 38, 16, 'JOB.38.16', 'Have you journeyed to the vents of the sea or walked in the trenches of the deep?'),
('JOB', 38, 17, 'JOB.38.17', 'Have the gates of death been revealed to you? Have you seen the gates of the shadow of death?'),
('JOB', 38, 18, 'JOB.38.18', 'Have you surveyed the extent of the earth? Tell Me, if you know all this.'),
('JOB', 38, 19, 'JOB.38.19', 'Where is the way to the home of light? Do you know where darkness resides,'),
('JOB', 38, 20, 'JOB.38.20', 'so you can lead it back to its border? Do you know the paths to its home?'),
('JOB', 38, 21, 'JOB.38.21', 'Surely you know, for you were already born! And the number of your days is great!'),
('JOB', 38, 22, 'JOB.38.22', 'Have you entered the storehouses of snow or observed the storehouses of hail,'),
('JOB', 38, 23, 'JOB.38.23', 'which I hold in reserve for times of trouble, for the day of war and battle?'),
('JOB', 38, 24, 'JOB.38.24', 'In which direction is the lightning dispersed, or the east wind scattered over the earth?'),
('JOB', 38, 25, 'JOB.38.25', 'Who cuts a channel for the flood or clears a path for the thunderbolt,'),
('JOB', 38, 26, 'JOB.38.26', 'to bring rain on a barren land, on a desert where no man lives,'),
('JOB', 38, 27, 'JOB.38.27', 'to satisfy the parched wasteland and make it sprout with tender grass?'),
('JOB', 38, 28, 'JOB.38.28', 'Does the rain have a father? Who has begotten the drops of dew?'),
('JOB', 38, 29, 'JOB.38.29', 'From whose womb does the ice emerge? Who gives birth to the frost from heaven,'),
('JOB', 38, 30, 'JOB.38.30', 'when the waters become hard as stone and the surface of the deep is frozen?'),
('JOB', 38, 31, 'JOB.38.31', 'Can you bind the chains of the Pleiades or loosen the belt of Orion?'),
('JOB', 38, 32, 'JOB.38.32', 'Can you bring forth the constellations in their seasons or lead out the Bear and her cubs?'),
('JOB', 38, 33, 'JOB.38.33', 'Do you know the laws of the heavens? Can you set their dominion over the earth?'),
('JOB', 38, 34, 'JOB.38.34', 'Can you command the clouds so that a flood of water covers you?'),
('JOB', 38, 35, 'JOB.38.35', 'Can you send the lightning bolts on their way? Do they report to you, ‘Here we are’?'),
('JOB', 38, 36, 'JOB.38.36', 'Who has put wisdom in the heart or given understanding to the mind?'),
('JOB', 38, 37, 'JOB.38.37', 'Who has the wisdom to count the clouds? Or who can tilt the water jars of the heavens'),
('JOB', 38, 38, 'JOB.38.38', 'when the dust hardens into a mass and the clods of earth stick together?'),
('JOB', 38, 39, 'JOB.38.39', 'Can you hunt the prey for a lioness or satisfy the hunger of young lions'),
('JOB', 38, 40, 'JOB.38.40', 'when they crouch in their dens and lie in wait in the thicket?'),
('JOB', 38, 41, 'JOB.38.41', 'Who provides food for the raven when its young cry out to God as they wander about for lack of food?'),
('JOB', 39, 1, 'JOB.39.1', '“Do you know when mountain goats give birth? Have you watched the doe bear her fawn?'),
('JOB', 39, 2, 'JOB.39.2', 'Can you count the months they are pregnant? Do you know the time they give birth?'),
('JOB', 39, 3, 'JOB.39.3', 'They crouch down and bring forth their young; they deliver their newborn.'),
('JOB', 39, 4, 'JOB.39.4', 'Their young ones thrive and grow up in the open field; they leave and do not return.'),
('JOB', 39, 5, 'JOB.39.5', 'Who set the wild donkey free? Who released the swift donkey from the harness?'),
('JOB', 39, 6, 'JOB.39.6', 'I made the wilderness his home and the salt flats his dwelling.'),
('JOB', 39, 7, 'JOB.39.7', 'He scorns the tumult of the city and never hears the shouts of a driver.'),
('JOB', 39, 8, 'JOB.39.8', 'He roams the mountains for pasture, searching for any green thing.'),
('JOB', 39, 9, 'JOB.39.9', 'Will the wild ox consent to serve you? Will he stay by your manger at night?'),
('JOB', 39, 10, 'JOB.39.10', 'Can you hold him to the furrow with a harness? Will he plow the valleys behind you?'),
('JOB', 39, 11, 'JOB.39.11', 'Can you rely on his great strength? Will you leave your hard work to him?'),
('JOB', 39, 12, 'JOB.39.12', 'Can you trust him to bring in your grain and gather it to your threshing floor?'),
('JOB', 39, 13, 'JOB.39.13', 'The wings of the ostrich flap joyfully, but cannot match the pinions and feathers of the stork.'),
('JOB', 39, 14, 'JOB.39.14', 'For she leaves her eggs on the ground and lets them warm in the sand.'),
('JOB', 39, 15, 'JOB.39.15', 'She forgets that a foot may crush them, or a wild animal may trample them.'),
('JOB', 39, 16, 'JOB.39.16', 'She treats her young harshly, as if not her own, with no concern that her labor was in vain.'),
('JOB', 39, 17, 'JOB.39.17', 'For God has deprived her of wisdom; He has not endowed her with understanding.'),
('JOB', 39, 18, 'JOB.39.18', 'Yet when she proudly spreads her wings, she laughs at the horse and its rider.'),
('JOB', 39, 19, 'JOB.39.19', 'Do you give strength to the horse or adorn his neck with a mane?'),
('JOB', 39, 20, 'JOB.39.20', 'Do you make him leap like a locust, striking terror with his proud snorting?'),
('JOB', 39, 21, 'JOB.39.21', 'He paws in the valley and rejoices in his strength; he charges into battle.'),
('JOB', 39, 22, 'JOB.39.22', 'He laughs at fear, frightened of nothing; he does not turn back from the sword.'),
('JOB', 39, 23, 'JOB.39.23', 'A quiver rattles at his side, along with a flashing spear and lance.'),
('JOB', 39, 24, 'JOB.39.24', 'Trembling with excitement, he devours the distance; he cannot stand still when the ram’s horn sounds.'),
('JOB', 39, 25, 'JOB.39.25', 'At the blast of the horn, he snorts with fervor. He catches the scent of battle from afar, the shouts of captains and the cry of war.'),
('JOB', 39, 26, 'JOB.39.26', 'Does the hawk take flight by your understanding and spread his wings toward the south?'),
('JOB', 39, 27, 'JOB.39.27', 'Does the eagle soar at your command and make his nest on high?'),
('JOB', 39, 28, 'JOB.39.28', 'He dwells on a cliff and lodges there; his stronghold is on a rocky crag.'),
('JOB', 39, 29, 'JOB.39.29', 'From there he spies out food; his eyes see it from afar.'),
('JOB', 39, 30, 'JOB.39.30', 'His young ones feast on blood; and where the slain are, there he is.”'),
('JOB', 40, 1, 'JOB.40.1', 'And the LORD said to Job:'),
('JOB', 40, 2, 'JOB.40.2', '“Will the faultfinder contend with the Almighty? Let him who argues with God give an answer.”'),
('JOB', 40, 3, 'JOB.40.3', 'Then Job answered the LORD:'),
('JOB', 40, 4, 'JOB.40.4', '“Behold, I am insignificant. How can I reply to You? I place my hand over my mouth.'),
('JOB', 40, 5, 'JOB.40.5', 'I have spoken once, but I have no answer—twice, but I have nothing to add.”'),
('JOB', 40, 6, 'JOB.40.6', 'Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind and said:'),
('JOB', 40, 7, 'JOB.40.7', '“Now brace yourself like a man; I will question you, and you shall inform Me.'),
('JOB', 40, 8, 'JOB.40.8', 'Would you really annul My justice? Would you condemn Me to justify yourself?'),
('JOB', 40, 9, 'JOB.40.9', 'Do you have an arm like God’s? Can you thunder with a voice like His?'),
('JOB', 40, 10, 'JOB.40.10', 'Then adorn yourself with majesty and splendor, and clothe yourself with honor and glory.'),
('JOB', 40, 11, 'JOB.40.11', 'Unleash the fury of your wrath; look on every proud man and bring him low.'),
('JOB', 40, 12, 'JOB.40.12', 'Look on every proud man and humble him; trample the wicked where they stand.'),
('JOB', 40, 13, 'JOB.40.13', 'Bury them together in the dust; imprison them in the grave.'),
('JOB', 40, 14, 'JOB.40.14', 'Then I will confess to you that your own right hand can save you.'),
('JOB', 40, 15, 'JOB.40.15', 'Look at Behemoth, which I made along with you. He feeds on grass like an ox.'),
('JOB', 40, 16, 'JOB.40.16', 'See the strength of his loins and the power in the muscles of his belly.'),
('JOB', 40, 17, 'JOB.40.17', 'His tail sways like a cedar; the sinews of his thighs are tightly knit.'),
('JOB', 40, 18, 'JOB.40.18', 'His bones are tubes of bronze; his limbs are rods of iron.'),
('JOB', 40, 19, 'JOB.40.19', 'He is the foremost of God’s works; only his Maker can draw the sword against him.'),
('JOB', 40, 20, 'JOB.40.20', 'The hills yield him their produce, while all the beasts of the field play nearby.'),
('JOB', 40, 21, 'JOB.40.21', 'He lies under the lotus plants, hidden among the reeds of the marsh.'),
('JOB', 40, 22, 'JOB.40.22', 'The lotus plants conceal him in their shade; the willows of the brook surround him.'),
('JOB', 40, 23, 'JOB.40.23', 'Though the river rages, Behemoth is unafraid; he remains secure, though the Jordan surges to his mouth.'),
('JOB', 40, 24, 'JOB.40.24', 'Can anyone capture him as he looks on, or pierce his nose with a snare?'),
('JOB', 41, 1, 'JOB.41.1', '“Can you pull in Leviathan with a hook or tie down his tongue with a rope?'),
('JOB', 41, 2, 'JOB.41.2', 'Can you put a cord through his nose or pierce his jaw with a hook?'),
('JOB', 41, 3, 'JOB.41.3', 'Will he beg you for mercy or speak to you softly?'),
('JOB', 41, 4, 'JOB.41.4', 'Will he make a covenant with you to take him as a slave for life?'),
('JOB', 41, 5, 'JOB.41.5', 'Can you pet him like a bird or put him on a leash for your maidens?'),
('JOB', 41, 6, 'JOB.41.6', 'Will traders barter for him or divide him among the merchants?'),
('JOB', 41, 7, 'JOB.41.7', 'Can you fill his hide with harpoons or his head with fishing spears?'),
('JOB', 41, 8, 'JOB.41.8', 'If you lay a hand on him, you will remember the battle and never repeat it!'),
('JOB', 41, 9, 'JOB.41.9', 'Surely hope of overcoming him is false. Is not the sight of him overwhelming?'),
('JOB', 41, 10, 'JOB.41.10', 'No one is so fierce as to rouse Leviathan. Then who is able to stand against Me?'),
('JOB', 41, 11, 'JOB.41.11', 'Who has given to Me that I should repay him? Everything under heaven is Mine.'),
('JOB', 41, 12, 'JOB.41.12', 'I cannot keep silent about his limbs, his power and graceful form.'),
('JOB', 41, 13, 'JOB.41.13', 'Who can strip off his outer coat? Who can approach him with a bridle?'),
('JOB', 41, 14, 'JOB.41.14', 'Who can open his jaws, ringed by his fearsome teeth?'),
('JOB', 41, 15, 'JOB.41.15', 'His rows of scales are his pride, tightly sealed together.'),
('JOB', 41, 16, 'JOB.41.16', 'One scale is so near to another that no air can pass between them.'),
('JOB', 41, 17, 'JOB.41.17', 'They are joined to one another; they clasp and cannot be separated.'),
('JOB', 41, 18, 'JOB.41.18', 'His snorting flashes with light, and his eyes are like the rays of dawn.'),
('JOB', 41, 19, 'JOB.41.19', 'Firebrands stream from his mouth; fiery sparks shoot forth!'),
('JOB', 41, 20, 'JOB.41.20', 'Smoke billows from his nostrils as from a boiling pot over burning reeds.'),
('JOB', 41, 21, 'JOB.41.21', 'His breath sets coals ablaze, and flames pour from his mouth.'),
('JOB', 41, 22, 'JOB.41.22', 'Strength resides in his neck, and dismay leaps before him.'),
('JOB', 41, 23, 'JOB.41.23', 'The folds of his flesh are tightly joined; they are firm and immovable.'),
('JOB', 41, 24, 'JOB.41.24', 'His chest is as hard as a rock, as hard as a lower millstone!'),
('JOB', 41, 25, 'JOB.41.25', 'When Leviathan rises up, the mighty are terrified; they withdraw before his thrashing.'),
('JOB', 41, 26, 'JOB.41.26', 'The sword that reaches him has no effect, nor does the spear or dart or arrow.'),
('JOB', 41, 27, 'JOB.41.27', 'He regards iron as straw and bronze as rotten wood.'),
('JOB', 41, 28, 'JOB.41.28', 'No arrow can make him flee; slingstones become like chaff to him.'),
('JOB', 41, 29, 'JOB.41.29', 'A club is regarded as straw, and he laughs at the sound of the lance.'),
('JOB', 41, 30, 'JOB.41.30', 'His undersides are jagged potsherds, spreading out the mud like a threshing sledge.'),
('JOB', 41, 31, 'JOB.41.31', 'He makes the depths seethe like a cauldron; he makes the sea like a jar of ointment.'),
('JOB', 41, 32, 'JOB.41.32', 'He leaves a glistening wake behind him; one would think the deep had white hair!'),
('JOB', 41, 33, 'JOB.41.33', 'Nothing on earth is his equal—a creature devoid of fear!'),
('JOB', 41, 34, 'JOB.41.34', 'He looks down on all the haughty; he is king over all the proud.”'),
('JOB', 42, 1, 'JOB.42.1', 'Then Job replied to the LORD:'),
('JOB', 42, 2, 'JOB.42.2', '“I know that You can do all things and that no plan of Yours can be thwarted.'),
('JOB', 42, 3, 'JOB.42.3', 'You asked, ‘Who is this who conceals My counsel without knowledge?’ Surely I spoke of things I did not understand, things too wonderful for me to know.'),
('JOB', 42, 4, 'JOB.42.4', 'You said, ‘Listen now, and I will speak. I will question you, and you shall inform Me.’'),
('JOB', 42, 5, 'JOB.42.5', 'My ears had heard of You, but now my eyes have seen You.'),
('JOB', 42, 6, 'JOB.42.6', 'Therefore I despise myself, and I repent in dust and ashes.”'),
('JOB', 42, 7, 'JOB.42.7', 'After the LORD had spoken these words to Job, He said to Eliphaz the Temanite, “My wrath is kindled against you and your two friends. For you have not spoken about Me accurately, as My servant Job has.'),
('JOB', 42, 8, 'JOB.42.8', 'So now, take seven bulls and seven rams, go to My servant Job, and sacrifice a burnt offering for yourselves. Then My servant Job will pray for you, for I will accept his prayer and not deal with you according to your folly. For you have not spoken accurately about Me, as My servant Job has.”'),
('JOB', 42, 9, 'JOB.42.9', 'So Eliphaz the Temanite, Bildad the Shuhite, and Zophar the Naamathite went and did as the LORD had told them; and the LORD accepted Job’s prayer.'),
('JOB', 42, 10, 'JOB.42.10', 'After Job had prayed for his friends, the LORD restored his prosperity and doubled his former possessions.'),
('JOB', 42, 11, 'JOB.42.11', 'All his brothers and sisters and prior acquaintances came and dined with him in his house. They consoled him and comforted him over all the adversity that the LORD had brought upon him. And each one gave him a piece of silver and a gold ring.'),
('JOB', 42, 12, 'JOB.42.12', 'So the LORD blessed Job’s latter days more than his first. He owned 14,000 sheep, 6,000 camels, 1,000 yoke of oxen, and 1,000 female donkeys.'),
('JOB', 42, 13, 'JOB.42.13', 'And he also had seven sons and three daughters.'),
('JOB', 42, 14, 'JOB.42.14', 'He named his first daughter Jemimah, his second Keziah, and his third Keren-happuch.'),
('JOB', 42, 15, 'JOB.42.15', 'No women as beautiful as Job’s daughters could be found in all the land, and their father granted them an inheritance among their brothers.'),
('JOB', 42, 16, 'JOB.42.16', 'After this, Job lived 140 years and saw his children and their children to the fourth generation.'),
('JOB', 42, 17, 'JOB.42.17', 'And so Job died, old and full of years.'),
('PSA', 1, 1, 'PSA.1.1', 'Blessed is the man who does not walk in the counsel of the wicked, or set foot on the path of sinners, or sit in the seat of mockers.'),
('PSA', 1, 2, 'PSA.1.2', 'But his delight is in the Law of the LORD, and on His law he meditates day and night.'),
('PSA', 1, 3, 'PSA.1.3', 'He is like a tree planted by streams of water, yielding its fruit in season, whose leaf does not wither, and who prospers in all he does.'),
('PSA', 1, 4, 'PSA.1.4', 'Not so the wicked! For they are like chaff driven off by the wind.'),
('PSA', 1, 5, 'PSA.1.5', 'Therefore the wicked will not stand in the judgment, nor sinners in the assembly of the righteous.'),
('PSA', 1, 6, 'PSA.1.6', 'For the LORD guards the path of the righteous, but the way of the wicked will perish.'),
('PSA', 2, 1, 'PSA.2.1', 'Why do the nations rage and the peoples plot in vain?'),
('PSA', 2, 2, 'PSA.2.2', 'The kings of the earth take their stand and the rulers gather together, against the LORD and against His Anointed One:'),
('PSA', 2, 3, 'PSA.2.3', '“Let us break Their chains and cast away Their cords.”'),
('PSA', 2, 4, 'PSA.2.4', 'The One enthroned in heaven laughs; the Lord taunts them.'),
('PSA', 2, 5, 'PSA.2.5', 'Then He rebukes them in His anger, and terrifies them in His fury:'),
('PSA', 2, 6, 'PSA.2.6', '“I have installed My King on Zion, upon My holy mountain.”'),
('PSA', 2, 7, 'PSA.2.7', 'I will proclaim the decree spoken to Me by the LORD: “You are My Son; today I have become Your Father.'),
('PSA', 2, 8, 'PSA.2.8', 'Ask Me, and I will make the nations Your inheritance, the ends of the earth Your possession.'),
('PSA', 2, 9, 'PSA.2.9', 'You will break them with an iron scepter; You will shatter them like pottery.”'),
('PSA', 2, 10, 'PSA.2.10', 'Therefore be wise, O kings; be admonished, O judges of the earth.'),
('PSA', 2, 11, 'PSA.2.11', 'Serve the LORD with fear, and rejoice with trembling.'),
('PSA', 2, 12, 'PSA.2.12', 'Kiss the Son, lest He be angry and you perish in your rebellion, when His wrath ignites in an instant. Blessed are all who take refuge in Him.'),
('PSA', 3, 1, 'PSA.3.1', 'A Psalm of David, when he fled from his son Absalom. O LORD, how my foes have increased! How many rise up against me!'),
('PSA', 3, 2, 'PSA.3.2', 'Many say of me, “God will not deliver him.” Selah'),
('PSA', 3, 3, 'PSA.3.3', 'But You, O LORD, are a shield around me, my glory, and the One who lifts my head.'),
('PSA', 3, 4, 'PSA.3.4', 'To the LORD I cry aloud, and He answers me from His holy mountain. Selah'),
('PSA', 3, 5, 'PSA.3.5', 'I lie down and sleep; I wake again, for the LORD sustains me.'),
('PSA', 3, 6, 'PSA.3.6', 'I will not fear the myriads set against me on every side.'),
('PSA', 3, 7, 'PSA.3.7', 'Arise, O LORD! Save me, O my God! Strike all my enemies on the jaw; break the teeth of the wicked.'),
('PSA', 3, 8, 'PSA.3.8', 'Salvation belongs to the LORD; may Your blessing be on Your people. Selah'),
('PSA', 4, 1, 'PSA.4.1', 'For the choirmaster. With stringed instruments. A Psalm of David. Answer me when I call, O God of my righteousness! You have relieved my distress; show me grace and hear my prayer.'),
('PSA', 4, 2, 'PSA.4.2', 'How long, O men, will my honor be maligned? How long will you love vanity and seek after lies? Selah'),
('PSA', 4, 3, 'PSA.4.3', 'Know that the LORD has set apart the godly for Himself; the LORD hears when I call to Him.'),
('PSA', 4, 4, 'PSA.4.4', 'Be angry, yet do not sin; on your bed, search your heart and be still. Selah'),
('PSA', 4, 5, 'PSA.4.5', 'Offer the sacrifices of the righteous and trust in the LORD.'),
('PSA', 4, 6, 'PSA.4.6', 'Many ask, “Who can show us the good?” Shine the light of Your face upon us, O LORD.'),
('PSA', 4, 7, 'PSA.4.7', 'You have filled my heart with more joy than when grain and new wine abound.'),
('PSA', 4, 8, 'PSA.4.8', 'I will lie down and sleep in peace, for You alone, O LORD, make me dwell in safety.'),
('PSA', 5, 1, 'PSA.5.1', 'For the choirmaster, to be accompanied by flutes. A Psalm of David. Give ear to my words, O LORD; consider my groaning.'),
('PSA', 5, 2, 'PSA.5.2', 'Attend to the sound of my cry, my King and my God, for to You I pray.'),
('PSA', 5, 3, 'PSA.5.3', 'In the morning, O LORD, You hear my voice; at daybreak I lay my plea before You and wait in expectation.'),
('PSA', 5, 4, 'PSA.5.4', 'For You are not a God who delights in wickedness; no evil can dwell with You.'),
('PSA', 5, 5, 'PSA.5.5', 'The boastful cannot stand in Your presence; You hate all workers of iniquity.'),
('PSA', 5, 6, 'PSA.5.6', 'You destroy those who tell lies; the LORD abhors the man of bloodshed and deceit.'),
('PSA', 5, 7, 'PSA.5.7', 'But I will enter Your house by the abundance of Your loving devotion; in reverence I will bow down toward Your holy temple.'),
('PSA', 5, 8, 'PSA.5.8', 'Lead me, O LORD, in Your righteousness because of my enemies; make straight Your way before me.'),
('PSA', 5, 9, 'PSA.5.9', 'For not a word they speak can be trusted; destruction lies within them. Their throats are open graves; their tongues practice deceit.'),
('PSA', 5, 10, 'PSA.5.10', 'Declare them guilty, O God; let them fall by their own devices. Drive them out for their many transgressions, for they have rebelled against You.'),
('PSA', 5, 11, 'PSA.5.11', 'But let all who take refuge in You rejoice; let them ever shout for joy. May You shelter them, that those who love Your name may rejoice in You.'),
('PSA', 5, 12, 'PSA.5.12', 'For surely You, O LORD, bless the righteous; You surround them with the shield of Your favor.'),
('PSA', 6, 1, 'PSA.6.1', 'For the choirmaster. With stringed instruments, according to Sheminith. A Psalm of David. O LORD, do not rebuke me in Your anger or discipline me in Your wrath.'),
('PSA', 6, 2, 'PSA.6.2', 'Be merciful to me, O LORD, for I am frail; heal me, O LORD, for my bones are in agony.'),
('PSA', 6, 3, 'PSA.6.3', 'My soul is deeply distressed. How long, O LORD, how long?'),
('PSA', 6, 4, 'PSA.6.4', 'Turn, O LORD, and deliver my soul; save me because of Your loving devotion.'),
('PSA', 6, 5, 'PSA.6.5', 'For there is no mention of You in death; who can praise You from Sheol?'),
('PSA', 6, 6, 'PSA.6.6', 'I am weary from groaning; all night I flood my bed with weeping and drench my couch with tears.'),
('PSA', 6, 7, 'PSA.6.7', 'My eyes fail from grief; they grow dim because of all my foes.'),
('PSA', 6, 8, 'PSA.6.8', 'Depart from me, all you workers of iniquity, for the LORD has heard my weeping.'),
('PSA', 6, 9, 'PSA.6.9', 'The LORD has heard my cry for mercy; the LORD accepts my prayer.'),
('PSA', 6, 10, 'PSA.6.10', 'All my enemies will be ashamed and dismayed; they will turn back in sudden disgrace.'),
('PSA', 7, 1, 'PSA.7.1', 'A Shiggaion of David, which he sang to the LORD concerning the words of Cush, a Benjamite. O LORD my God, I take refuge in You; save me and deliver me from all my pursuers,'),
('PSA', 7, 2, 'PSA.7.2', 'or they will shred my soul like a lion and tear me to pieces with no one to rescue me.'),
('PSA', 7, 3, 'PSA.7.3', 'O LORD my God, if I have done this, if injustice is on my hands,'),
('PSA', 7, 4, 'PSA.7.4', 'if I have rewarded my ally with evil, if I have plundered my foe without cause,'),
('PSA', 7, 5, 'PSA.7.5', 'then may my enemy pursue me and overtake me; may he trample me to the ground and leave my honor in the dust. Selah'),
('PSA', 7, 6, 'PSA.7.6', 'Arise, O LORD, in Your anger; rise up against the fury of my enemies. Awake, my God, and ordain judgment.'),
('PSA', 7, 7, 'PSA.7.7', 'Let the assembled peoples gather around You; take Your seat over them on high.'),
('PSA', 7, 8, 'PSA.7.8', 'The LORD judges the peoples; vindicate me, O LORD, according to my righteousness and integrity.'),
('PSA', 7, 9, 'PSA.7.9', 'Put an end to the evil of the wicked, but establish the righteous, O righteous God who searches hearts and minds.'),
('PSA', 7, 10, 'PSA.7.10', 'My shield is with God, who saves the upright in heart.'),
('PSA', 7, 11, 'PSA.7.11', 'God is a righteous judge and a God who feels indignation each day.'),
('PSA', 7, 12, 'PSA.7.12', 'If one does not repent, God will sharpen His sword; He has bent and strung His bow.'),
('PSA', 7, 13, 'PSA.7.13', 'He has prepared His deadly weapons; He ordains His arrows with fire.'),
('PSA', 7, 14, 'PSA.7.14', 'Behold, the wicked man travails with evil; he conceives trouble and births falsehood.'),
('PSA', 7, 15, 'PSA.7.15', 'He has dug a hole and hollowed it out; he has fallen into a pit of his own making.'),
('PSA', 7, 16, 'PSA.7.16', 'His trouble recoils on himself, and his violence falls on his own head.'),
('PSA', 7, 17, 'PSA.7.17', 'I will thank the LORD for His righteousness and sing praise to the name of the LORD Most High.'),
('PSA', 8, 1, 'PSA.8.1', 'For the choirmaster. According to Gittith. A Psalm of David. O LORD, our Lord, how majestic is Your name in all the earth! You have set Your glory above the heavens.'),
('PSA', 8, 2, 'PSA.8.2', 'From the mouths of children and infants You have ordained praise on account of Your adversaries, to silence the enemy and avenger.'),
('PSA', 8, 3, 'PSA.8.3', 'When I behold Your heavens, the work of Your fingers, the moon and the stars, which You have set in place—'),
('PSA', 8, 4, 'PSA.8.4', 'what is man that You are mindful of him, or the son of man that You care for him?'),
('PSA', 8, 5, 'PSA.8.5', 'You made him a little lower than the angels; You crowned him with glory and honor.'),
('PSA', 8, 6, 'PSA.8.6', 'You made him ruler of the works of Your hands; You have placed everything under his feet:'),
('PSA', 8, 7, 'PSA.8.7', 'all sheep and oxen, and even the beasts of the field,'),
('PSA', 8, 8, 'PSA.8.8', 'the birds of the air and the fish of the sea, all that swim the paths of the seas.'),
('PSA', 8, 9, 'PSA.8.9', 'O LORD, our Lord, how majestic is Your name in all the earth!'),
('PSA', 9, 1, 'PSA.9.1', 'For the choirmaster. To the tune of “The Death of the Son.” A Psalm of David. I will give thanks to the LORD with all my heart; I will recount all Your wonders.'),
('PSA', 9, 2, 'PSA.9.2', 'I will be glad and rejoice in You; I will sing praise to Your name, O Most High.'),
('PSA', 9, 3, 'PSA.9.3', 'When my enemies retreat, they stumble and perish before You.'),
('PSA', 9, 4, 'PSA.9.4', 'For You have upheld my just cause; You sit on Your throne judging righteously.'),
('PSA', 9, 5, 'PSA.9.5', 'You have rebuked the nations; You have destroyed the wicked; You have erased their name forever and ever.'),
('PSA', 9, 6, 'PSA.9.6', 'The enemy has come to eternal ruin, and You have uprooted their cities; the very memory of them has vanished.'),
('PSA', 9, 7, 'PSA.9.7', 'But the LORD abides forever; He has established His throne for judgment.'),
('PSA', 9, 8, 'PSA.9.8', 'He judges the world with justice; He governs the people with equity.'),
('PSA', 9, 9, 'PSA.9.9', 'The LORD is a refuge for the oppressed, a stronghold in times of trouble.'),
('PSA', 9, 10, 'PSA.9.10', 'Those who know Your name trust in You, for You, O LORD, have not forsaken those who seek You.'),
('PSA', 9, 11, 'PSA.9.11', 'Sing praises to the LORD, who dwells in Zion; proclaim His deeds among the nations.'),
('PSA', 9, 12, 'PSA.9.12', 'For the Avenger of bloodshed remembers; He does not ignore the cry of the afflicted.'),
('PSA', 9, 13, 'PSA.9.13', 'Be merciful to me, O LORD; see how my enemies afflict me! Lift me up from the gates of death,'),
('PSA', 9, 14, 'PSA.9.14', 'that I may declare all Your praises—that within the gates of Daughter Zion I may rejoice in Your salvation.'),
('PSA', 9, 15, 'PSA.9.15', 'The nations have fallen into a pit of their making; their feet are caught in the net they have hidden.'),
('PSA', 9, 16, 'PSA.9.16', 'The LORD is known by the justice He brings; the wicked are ensnared by the work of their hands. Higgaion Selah'),
('PSA', 9, 17, 'PSA.9.17', 'The wicked will return to Sheol—all the nations who forget God.'),
('PSA', 9, 18, 'PSA.9.18', 'For the needy will not always be forgotten; nor the hope of the oppressed forever dashed.'),
('PSA', 9, 19, 'PSA.9.19', 'Rise up, O LORD, do not let man prevail; let the nations be judged in Your presence.'),
('PSA', 9, 20, 'PSA.9.20', 'Lay terror upon them, O LORD; let the nations know they are but men. Selah'),
('PSA', 10, 1, 'PSA.10.1', 'Why, O LORD, do You stand far off? Why do You hide in times of trouble?'),
('PSA', 10, 2, 'PSA.10.2', 'In pride the wicked pursue the needy; let them be caught in the schemes they devise.'),
('PSA', 10, 3, 'PSA.10.3', 'For the wicked man boasts in the cravings of his heart; he blesses the greedy and reviles the LORD.'),
('PSA', 10, 4, 'PSA.10.4', 'In his pride the wicked man does not seek Him; in all his schemes there is no God.'),
('PSA', 10, 5, 'PSA.10.5', 'He is secure in his ways at all times; Your lofty judgments are far from him; he sneers at all his foes.'),
('PSA', 10, 6, 'PSA.10.6', 'He says to himself, “I will not be moved; from age to age I am free of distress.”'),
('PSA', 10, 7, 'PSA.10.7', 'His mouth is full of cursing, deceit, and violence; trouble and malice are under his tongue.'),
('PSA', 10, 8, 'PSA.10.8', 'He lies in wait near the villages; in ambush he slays the innocent; his eyes watch in stealth for the helpless.'),
('PSA', 10, 9, 'PSA.10.9', 'He lies in wait like a lion in a thicket; he lurks to seize the oppressed; he catches the lowly in his net.'),
('PSA', 10, 10, 'PSA.10.10', 'They are crushed and beaten down; the helpless fall prey to his strength.'),
('PSA', 10, 11, 'PSA.10.11', 'He says to himself, “God has forgotten; He hides His face and never sees.”'),
('PSA', 10, 12, 'PSA.10.12', 'Arise, O LORD! Lift up Your hand, O God! Do not forget the helpless.'),
('PSA', 10, 13, 'PSA.10.13', 'Why has the wicked man renounced God? He says to himself, “You will never call me to account.”'),
('PSA', 10, 14, 'PSA.10.14', 'But You have regarded trouble and grief; You see to repay it by Your hand. The victim entrusts himself to You; You are the helper of the fatherless.'),
('PSA', 10, 15, 'PSA.10.15', 'Break the arm of the wicked and evildoer; call him to account for his wickedness until none is left to be found.'),
('PSA', 10, 16, 'PSA.10.16', 'The LORD is King forever and ever; the nations perish from His land.'),
('PSA', 10, 17, 'PSA.10.17', 'You have heard, O LORD, the desire of the humble; You will strengthen their hearts. You will incline Your ear,'),
('PSA', 10, 18, 'PSA.10.18', 'to vindicate the fatherless and oppressed, that the men of the earth may strike terror no more.'),
('PSA', 11, 1, 'PSA.11.1', 'For the choirmaster. Of David. In the LORD I take refuge. How then can you say to me: “Flee like a bird to your mountain!'),
('PSA', 11, 2, 'PSA.11.2', 'For behold, the wicked bend their bows. They set their arrow on the string to shoot from the shadows at the upright in heart.'),
('PSA', 11, 3, 'PSA.11.3', 'If the foundations are destroyed, what can the righteous do?”'),
('PSA', 11, 4, 'PSA.11.4', 'The LORD is in His holy temple; the LORD is on His heavenly throne. His eyes are watching closely; they examine the sons of men.'),
('PSA', 11, 5, 'PSA.11.5', 'The LORD tests the righteous and the wicked; His soul hates the lover of violence.'),
('PSA', 11, 6, 'PSA.11.6', 'On the wicked He will rain down fiery coals and sulfur; a scorching wind will be their portion.'),
('PSA', 11, 7, 'PSA.11.7', 'For the LORD is righteous; He loves justice. The upright will see His face.'),
('PSA', 12, 1, 'PSA.12.1', 'For the choirmaster. According to Sheminith. A Psalm of David. Help, O LORD, for the godly are no more; the faithful have vanished from among men.'),
('PSA', 12, 2, 'PSA.12.2', 'They lie to one another; they speak with flattering lips and a double heart.'),
('PSA', 12, 3, 'PSA.12.3', 'May the LORD cut off all flattering lips and every boastful tongue.'),
('PSA', 12, 4, 'PSA.12.4', 'They say, “With our tongues we will prevail. We own our lips—who can be our master?”'),
('PSA', 12, 5, 'PSA.12.5', '“For the cause of the oppressed and for the groaning of the needy, I will now arise,” says the LORD. “I will bring safety to him who yearns.”'),
('PSA', 12, 6, 'PSA.12.6', 'The words of the LORD are flawless, like silver refined in a furnace, like gold purified sevenfold.'),
('PSA', 12, 7, 'PSA.12.7', 'You, O LORD, will keep us; You will forever guard us from this generation.'),
('PSA', 12, 8, 'PSA.12.8', 'The wicked wander freely, and vileness is exalted among men.'),
('PSA', 13, 1, 'PSA.13.1', 'For the choirmaster. A Psalm of David. How long, O LORD? Will You forget me forever? How long will You hide Your face from me?'),
('PSA', 13, 2, 'PSA.13.2', 'How long must I wrestle in my soul, with sorrow in my heart each day? How long will my enemy dominate me?')
) as x(osis, chapter, verse, ref, body)
join public.books b on b.osis_code = x.osis
join public.bible_versions v on v.id = b.version_id and v.code = 'BSB'
join public.chapters c on c.book_id = b.id and c.number = x.chapter
on conflict (chapter_id, number) do update set osis_ref = excluded.osis_ref, text = excluded.text;
